hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19520","(19514) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar narrated from 'Asim ibn Sulayman from al-Sha'bi from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with both of them: that a slave of Banu Bayadah cupped the Messenger of Allah, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him and his family, so he gave him his wages. Had it been unlawful, he would not have given it to him. And he ordered his masters to reduce his tax. Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. [Authentic. Agreed upon.]"
"19521","(19515) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated to us — Khālid narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, underwent cupping (ḥijāmah) and gave the cupper (ḥajjām) his fee. Had he known it to be impure (khabīth), he would not have given it to him.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"
"19522","(19516) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us — Khālid narrated from ʿIkrimah and Muḥammad, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Messenger of Allah, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, underwent cupping and gave the cupper his fee. Had it been impure (khabīth), he would not have given it to him.\n\nIt was also narrated by Ayyūb from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Ibn ʿAbbās, and the narration of Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Ibn ʿAbbās is mursal (disconnected). [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"
"19523","(19517) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed him — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, that is al-Aṣamm, narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us from Ayyūb.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, underwent cupping and gave him (the cupper) his fee. Had it been ḥarām (unlawful), he would not have given it to him. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"
"19524","(19518) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — al-Ḥajjāj and Sulaymān said — Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn said: I was informed that Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of Allah, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, underwent cupping and gave the cupper his fee. Had he considered it harmful (biʾs), he would not have given it to him. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"
"19525","(19519) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Sufyān informed me — Ibrāhīm ibn Maysarah narrated from Ṭāwūs: The Messenger of Allah, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, underwent cupping and said to the cupper: \Give him a gift (or reward).\"" [Ḍaʿīf (weak)]"""
"19526","(19520) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Warqāʾ narrated from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Abī Jamīlah, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, underwent cupping and commanded me, so I gave the cupper his fee. This is more appropriate and more akin to what has preceded regarding the narration of ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī from ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḍamrah from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him: \The earnings of the cupper are from the suḥṭ (unlawful gain).\"" [Munkar (objectionable)]"""
"19527","(19521) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās, that is al-Aṣamm, narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: And it has been narrated that a man who was a relative of ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, came to him and asked about his livelihood. He mentioned to him the revenue of a public bath (ḥammām) and the earnings of a cupper or two cuppers. He (ʿUthmān) said: \Indeed"," your earnings are vile (wasakh)\"" — or he said \""foul (danis)\"" — or \""repugnant (danīʾ)\"" — or a word resembling these. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19528","(19522) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād informed me from his father, who said: The trustworthy narrator informed me that the Quraysh used to consider the earnings of the cupper beneath their dignity in the Jāhiliyyah (pre-Islamic period). Had it been ḥarām (unlawful), the Messenger of Allah, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, would not have said to the Anṣārī: \Put it in the fodder of the orphan's camel.\"" [Ḍaʿīf (weak)]"""
"19529","(19523) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb informed me — ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Bukayr narrated to him that ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah narrated to him that Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with him, visited al-Muqannaʿ (a man with a covered head) and said: \I shall not leave until you undergo cupping"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," saying: 'Indeed"," in it there is healing (shifāʾ).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Talid"," and Muslim narrated it from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf and Abī al-Ṭāhir"," all of them from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"19530","(19524) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Bakr al-Sahmī narrated to us — Ḥumayd narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, said: \The most exemplary of the remedies with which you treat yourselves — or the best of the remedies with which you treat yourselves — is cupping (ḥijāmah) and Indian costus (qusts al-baḥrī). And do not torment your children by pressing (ghamz) on their uvulas.\""\n\nBoth (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) recorded it in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections as previously noted. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"19531","(19525) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Haytham al-Sha'rānī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Muḥammad ibn 'Amr from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Abū Hind performed cupping on the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) on the crown of his head due to an ailment he was suffering from. And he (the Prophet) said: \If there is any healing in the medicines you use"," then it is in cupping.\"" [Weak]"""
"19532","(19526) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad ibn Sufyān informed us, 'Abd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb informed us, Jarīr narrated from 'Abd al-Malik, who is Ibn 'Umayr, from Ḥuṣayn ibn Abī Ḥurr from Samurah ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family). He called for the cupper"," who had cupping horns with him"," and he (the cupper) made incisions with a razor. Then a Bedouin from Banī Fazārah came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what is this that is cutting your skin?' He said: 'This is cupping (al-ḥajm).' He asked: 'What is cupping?' He replied: 'It is among the best of remedies by which people treat themselves.'\"" [Authentic]"""
"19533","(19527) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Wazīr al-Dimashqī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān informed us, 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Mawālī informed us, Fā'id, the freed slave of 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Alī ibn Abī Rāfi', narrated from his master 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Alī ibn Abī Rāfi' from his grandmother Salmay (may Allah be pleased with her), the servant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family), who said: \No one ever complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) of a headache except that he said: 'Perform cupping.' Nor of a pain in his feet except that he said: 'Dye them (with henna).'\"" [Authentic]"""
"19534","(19528) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us, Abū Qalābah 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī al-Baṣrī narrated in Baghdad, Abū 'Āmir informed us, 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Mawālī narrated from Ayyūb ibn Ḥasan from his grandmother Salmay, who said: \I never heard anyone complain to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) of a headache except that he commanded him to perform cupping"," nor of a pain in his feet except that he commanded him to dye them with henna.\""\n\nAyyūb ibn Ḥasan is Ibn 'Alī ibn Abī Rāfi'"," and there has been a difference of opinion regarding him on the authority of Ibn Abī al-Mawālī. [Authentic]"""
"19535","(19529) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Tājir informed us, Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Rāzī informed us, al-Anṣārī informed us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān informed us, 'Ikrimah narrated from Ibn 'Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) performed cupping while he was in the state of iḥrām"," on his head"," due to a headache or a strain he was suffering from. And he performed cupping at a place called Laḥy Jamal.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Anṣārī"," and he also reported it from the ḥadīth of 'Abd Allāh ibn Buḥaynah (may Allah be pleased with him) with the same meaning"," and it has already been mentioned in the Book of Ḥajj. [Authentic"," agreed upon]"""
"19536","(19530) Al-Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-'Alawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū al-Azhar al-Salīṭī informed us, 'Abd al-Razzāq informed us, Ma'mar narrated from Qatādah from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) performed cupping on the top of his foot while he was in the state of iḥrām.\n\nThus it is in this narration: \on the top of his foot.\"" And in the narration of Ibn Buḥaynah and Ibn 'Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," it is \""on his head.\"" The majority is more deserving of being preserved than the single narrator"," unless he did it twice while in the state of iḥrām"," and Allah knows best. [Authentic]"""
"19537","(19531) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq and Abū Muslim both said, Muslim informed us, Hishām narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) performed cupping on his hip due to a strain he was suffering from.\n\nThus said Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm: \on his hip.\"" [Authentic]"""
"19538","(19532) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Hishām narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) performed cupping while he was in the state of iḥrām due to a strain in his hip, or he said, on his back, as though he (the Prophet) performed cupping on his head while in the state of iḥrām due to a strain or a headache he was suffering from, as we have narrated in the ḥadīth of Ibn 'Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them both). [Authentic]"
"19539","(19533) Abū al-Khayr Jāmi' ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Wakīl informed us, Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Mazzakī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdūs al-'Anazī informed us; both said, 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd informed us, 'Alī ibn 'Uthmān al-Lāḥiqī informed us, Jarīr, who is Ibn Ḥāzim, narrated from Qatādah from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) used to have cupping done three times: two on the two jugular veins and one on the upper back (al-kāhil).\"" [Authentic]"""
"19540","(19534) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Ismā'īl ibn al-Faḍl informed us, Ibn Muṣaffā informed me, al-Walīd, who is Ibn Muslim, informed me, Ibn Thawbān narrated from his father from Abū Kabshah al-Anmārī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he narrated to him that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) used to have cupping done on the crown of his head and between his shoulders, and he would say: \Whoever has let this blood"," it will not harm him if he does not treat himself with anything.\"" I think he said: \""for anything.\"" [Weak]"""
"19541","(19535) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū Tawbah, al-Rabīʿ ibn Nāfiʿ, narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Jumaḥī narrated from Suhayl from his father from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Whoever performs cupping on the seventeenth"," the nineteenth"," and the twenty-first"," it shall be a cure from every ailment.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19542","(19536) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \The best days upon which you perform cupping are the seventeenth"," the nineteenth"," and the twenty-first.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by al-Zuhrī from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) as a mursal narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19543","(19537) And Salām ibn Salm al-Ṭawīl — who is matrūk (abandoned) — narrated from Zayd al-ʿAmmī from Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah from Maʿqil ibn Yasār (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family), who said: \Whoever performs cupping on Tuesday"," the seventeenth of the month"," it shall be a remedy for the ailments of the entire year.\""\n\nAbū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us of it; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Khalīfah narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us; Salām al-Ṭawīl narrated it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19544","(19538) And it was narrated from Zayd, as ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥulwānī informed us; Abū Maʿmar narrated to us; Hushaym narrated from Zayd al-ʿAmmī from Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who raised it (as a marfūʿ narration), saying: \Whoever performs cupping on Tuesday"," the seventeenth of the month"," Allah will remove from him the ailment of the entire year.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19545","(19539) And Abū Jazī — Naṣr ibn Ṭarīf — narrated it through two of his chains from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) as a marfūʿ narration, and he is matrūk (abandoned); it is not appropriate to mention it.\n\nʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Tamtām narrated to us; Abū Salamah narrated to us. And Hishām ibn ʿAlī al-Sīrāfī informed us; Abū Salamah al-Minqarī narrated to us. And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl — and he is Abū Salamah — informed me; Abū Bakrah, Bakkār ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, informed me; my aunt — and she is Kabshah bint Abī Bakrah — informed me that her father used to forbid his family from cupping on Tuesday, and he asserted, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family), that Tuesday is the day of blood, and in it there is an hour in which the blood does not clot.\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū Dāwūd, and the narration of Ibn ʿAbdān carries the same meaning. The prohibition mentioned in it is mawqūf (stopped at the companion) and not marfūʿ (raised to the Prophet), and its chain is not strong. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"19546","(19540) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us orally; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ayyūb ibn Māsī informed us; Abū Muslim al-Kajjī informed us; Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl informed us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Sulaymān ibn Arqam from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Whoever performs cupping on Wednesday and Saturday and sees a rash (waḍaḥ)"," let no one blame but himself.\"" Sulaymān ibn Arqam is weak (ḍaʿīf).\n\nIt was also narrated from Ibn Samʿān and Sulaymān ibn Yazīd from al-Zuhrī likewise as a mawsūl (connected) narration"," and it is also weak. And it was narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ṣalt from Ibn al-Musayyib from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) as a marfūʿ narration"," and it is also weak. What is preserved (maḥfūẓ) from al-Zuhrī is from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) as a munqaṭiʿ (disconnected) narration. And Allah knows best. [Munkar]"""
"19547","(19541) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us; Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdawayh ibn Sahl al-Marwazī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥammād al-Āmulī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; ʿAṭṭāf ibn Khālid narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Indeed"," on Friday there is an hour in which no one performs cupping except that an affliction befalls him from which he will not be cured.\"" ʿAṭṭāf ibn Khālid is weak (ḍaʿīf).\n\nAnd Yaḥyā ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Rāzī — who is matrūk (abandoned) — narrated through his chain from al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī a marfūʿ ḥadīth regarding it"," and it is nothing (of significance). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19548","(19542) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us orally; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ayyūb ibn Māsī informed us; Abū Muslim al-Kajjī informed us; Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl informed us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Sulaymān ibn Arqam from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \If there is any good in your medicines"," then it is in the incision of the cupper"," a drink of honey"," or a branding with fire"," but I do not like branding (cauterization).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19549","(19543) And ʿAlī informed us; Aḥmad informed us; ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ghayṣil narrated to us; ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah narrated, saying: Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) came to our house and narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \If there is any good in your medicines — or in that with which you treat yourselves — then it is in the incision of a cupper"," a drink of honey"," or a branding with fire that coincides with an ailment"," but I do not like branding (cauterization).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd"," and Muslim narrated it through another route from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"19550","(19544) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me; Abū Ḥāmid Muḥammad ibn Hārūn al-Ḥaḍramī informed us; Abū Yaḥyā Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm informed us; Surayj ibn Yūnus narrated from Marwān ibn Shuʿjāʿ from Sālim al-Afṭas from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Cure is in three things: in the incision of a cupper"," a drink of honey"," or a branding with fire"," and I forbid my ummah from cauterization (al-kayy).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"19551","(19545) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Saffar al-Isbahani — recited to us — Abu Yahya Ahmad ibn 'Isam ibn 'Abd al-Majid al-Ansari al-Isbahani informed us: Ruh ibn 'Ubaydah al-Qaysi informed us: Shu'bah said: I heard Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman say: I was sitting with Sa'id ibn Jubayr when he said, \At such-and-such hour last night"," was it such-and-such?\"" I said"," \""Such-and-such","\"" and he supposed I was praying. I said"," \""I was stung last night.\"" He said"," \""Did you not perform ruqyah?\"" I said"," \""I heard al-Sha'bi narrating from Buraydah ibn Husayb that he said"," 'There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a venomous bite.'\"" Sa'id ibn Jubayr then narrated from Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," that the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""Seventy thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise without being taken to account.\"" He said"," \""Who are they?\"" He replied"," \""Those who do not perform ruqyah"," do not seek omens"," and do not get themselves cauterized — and upon their Lord they place their trust.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq from Ruh"," and Muslim recorded it through another chain from Husayn.\n\n[Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"19552","(19546) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar in Baghdad informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: al-Thawri informed me: Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir from Mujahid, from 'Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \Whoever gets himself cauterized or has ruqyah performed has absolved himself of tawakkul (reliance upon Allah).\""\n\nIt was also narrated from him from Mujahid from Hassan ibn Abi Wajza' from 'Aqqar. Mujahid heard the hadith from 'Aqqar but did not memorize it precisely"," so he instructed Hassan"," who preserved it on his behalf. This was stated by Jarir from Mansur.\n\n[Hasan]"""
"19553","(19547) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Yunus ibn Habib informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade us from cauterization, so we got ourselves cauterized — and we did not prosper nor succeed.\n\n[Sahih]"
"19554","(19548) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Isma'il ibn Qutaybah informed us: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us: Abu Mu'awiyah from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, sent a physician to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who cut a vein and then cauterized it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya.\n\n[Sahih — Muslim (2207)]"
"19555","(19549) Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan in Baghdad informed us: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr informed us: 'Abbas ibn Muhammad informed us: Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd informed us: al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, fell ill, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, sent a physician to him, who cauterized him on his vein.\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Sahih through various chains from al-A'mash.\n\n[Sahih]"
"19556","(19550) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: Ahmad ibn Yunus informed us: Zuhayr —\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed us: Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Imam informed us: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us: Abu Khaythamah from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Sa'd ibn Mu'adh was struck by an arrow in his vein, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, cauterized it with his own hand. It swelled again, so he cauterized it a second time.\n\nThe wording is from the hadith of Yahya. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Yunus.\n\n[Sahih — Muslim (2208)]"
"19557","(19551) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisi both informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Matar informed us: Ibrahim ibn 'Ali informed us: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us: Yazid ibn Zura'i from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, cauterized As'ad ibn Zurarah for a thorn wound.\n\n[Munkar]"
"19558","(19552) Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A group of people came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," our companion is ailing — shall we cauterize him?\"" He remained silent for a while"," then said"," \""If you wish"," cauterize him; and if you wish"," leave him\"" — meaning with heated stones.\n\nAl-Thawri also narrated it from Abu Ishaq with the same meaning"," saying: \""Leave him with heated stones (bi-l-radf).\""\n\n[Sahih]"""
"19559","(19553) Abu Mansur al-Dhufur ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-'Alawi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Abu Ja'far ibn Duham informed us: Ahmad ibn Hazim informed us: Qabisah informed us: Sufyan from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man from the Ansar complained of an illness, and his pain intensified. Cauterization was suggested for him, so they came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and asked him. He remained silent three times, then said, \If you wish"," cauterize him; and if you wish"," cauterize him with heated stones (bi-l-radf).\""\n\n[Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"19560","(19554) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah informed us: Rayhan ibn Sa'id informed us: 'Abbad ibn Mansur from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, gave permission to a household of the Ansar to perform ruqyah for the effects of a venomous bite, and he gave permission for ruqyah against the evil eye and the evil spirit. Anas said, \I was cauterized for a pleurisy-like ailment while the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," was still alive"," and Abu Talhah"," Anas ibn al-Nadir"," Zayd ibn Thabit"," and Abu Talhah witnessed my cauterization.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari said: And 'Abbad ibn Mansur narrated this hadith after the hadith of 'Arim from Hammad from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Anas"," that Abu Talhah and Anas ibn al-Nadir cauterized him"," and Abu Talhah cauterized him with his own hand.\n\n[Sahih — without the mention of \""and the evil spirit\"" (wa-l-nafs)]"""
"19561","(19555) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Jarīr read letters of Abū Qilābah. Ayyūb said: \I heard it from Abū Qilābah"," from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: 'I was cauterized for pleurisy"," and Anas ibn al-Naḍr and Abū Ṭalḥah were present when I was cauterized.'\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19562","(19556) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) was cauterized for facial paralysis and cauterized his son Wāqid. And Ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he was cauterized for facial paralysis and sought treatment through incantation (ruqyah) for a scorpion sting.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"19563","(19557) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us, Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated from ʿUmar ibn Saʿīd, from ʬAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family), who said: \Allah did not send down any disease except that He sent down for it a cure.\""\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," from Abū Aḥmad.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5678.]"""
"19564","(19558) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from ʿAbd Rabbih ibn Saʿīd, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family), that he said: \For every disease there is a cure. When the cure for the disease is administered"," the patient recovers"," by the permission of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\""\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf and others"," from Ibn Wahb.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2204.]"""
"19565","(19559) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥurfī informed us in Baghdād, Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from Ziyād ibn ʿIlāqah, from Usāmah ibn Sharīk (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family)"," and his Companions were as though birds were sitting upon their heads (i.e."," in perfect stillness and reverence). I greeted them and sat down. Then the Bedouins came from here and there and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," should we seek medical treatment?' He said: 'Seek medical treatment"," for Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," did not place any disease except that He placed for it a cure"," except one: old age.' He (the narrator) said: 'They asked him about certain things that were of no harm: 'Is there any restriction upon us in such and such?' He said: 'Servants of Allah"," Allah has removed restriction"," except for a person who wrongfully wrongs another—that is the one who is restricted and destroyed.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what is the best thing that people are given?' He said: 'Good character.'\""\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar up to his words \""old age.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"19566","(19560) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn Shaybān informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʬAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), reaching the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family): \Allah did not send down any disease except that He sent down for it a cure. He who knew it"," knew it"," and he who was ignorant of it"," was ignorant of it.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"19567","(19561) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us, Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān al-Madanī narrated to us, Ayyūb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Anṣārī informed me, from Yaʿqūb ibn Abī Yaʿqūb, from Umm Mubashshir al-Anṣāriyyah, who was among the maternal aunts of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family). She said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) came to me"," and with him was ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who was recovering from an illness. In the house there was a cluster of dates hanging. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) stood and took from it. ʿAlī began to take from it"," so he said: 'Leave it"," for it does not suit you—you are recovering (nāqih).' She said: 'So I got up to some barley and beetroot and cooked it. I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family)"," and he said: 'Eat from this"," for it is more beneficial for you.' Thus said Umm Mubashshir. And thus also said Isḥāq al-Ḥanẓalī from Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb.\""\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"19568","(19562) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us, Fulayḥ narrated from Ayyūb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ṣaʿṣaʿah, from Yaʿqūb ibn Abī Yaʿqūb, from Umm al-Mundhir bint Qays al-Anṣāriyyah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) came to me"," and with him was ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)","\"" and she mentioned its meaning. And thus also said Abū Dāwūd and Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān from Fulayḥ"," and likewise al-Muʿāfā ibn Sulaymān from Fulayḥ. And in the narration of Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb there is a doubt (wahm).\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"19569","(19563) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Abī Khalaf ibn Aḥmad al-Ṣūfī al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us there, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Yazdād ibn Masʿūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Sahl ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ziyād ibn Ṣuhayb, from his father, from his grandfather Ṣuhayb, who said: \I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) as an emigrant"," and before him were dates. He said: 'Come"," eat.' He said: 'So I began eating the dates.' He said: 'Are you eating dates while you have an eye ailment?' He said: 'I said: 'I am chewing them from the other side.' He said: 'So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) smiled.'\""\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"19570","(19564) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār said: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, from Abī al-Mutawakkil, from Abī Saʿīd, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) and said: \My brother's stomach has become loose (i.e."," he has diarrhea).\"" He said: \""Give him honey to drink.\"" So he came back and said: \""I gave him honey to drink"," but it only increased his looseness.\"" He said: \""Give him honey to drink.\"" On the third or fourth occasion"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: \""Allah has spoken the truth"," and your brother's stomach has lied. Give him honey to drink.\"" So he gave him honey to drink"," and he recovered.\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Mathnā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19571","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafid informed me; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sufyan narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Salamah al-Labqi narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Hold fast to the two cures: honey and the Qur'an.\""\n\nIts raising (as a marfu' hadith) is not established; the correct version is mawquf (a statement of the Companion). Waki' also narrated it from Sufyan as a mawquf hadith. [Munkar]"""
"19572","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us; Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl informed us. (In another chain:) Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us in Baghdad; Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas informed us; al-'Abbas al-Dawri narrated to us; 'Ubayd Allah, i.e. ibn Musa, narrated to us; Isra'il narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \There are two cures in the Qur'an: the Qur'an and honey. The Qur'an is a cure for what is in the breasts"," and honey is a cure for every disease.\""\n\nThis is the correct version"," and it is mawquf. It was also narrated by al-A'mash from Khaythamah"," and by al-Aswad from 'Abd Allah"," as a mawquf hadith. [Sahih]"""
"19573","Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani narrated to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Hassan al-Qattan informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar ibn Rashid narrated from al-Zuhri; Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed me from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) say about the shuniz (black seed): \Hold fast to this black seed"," for in it is a cure for every disease\"" — or he said \""everything\"" — \""except death.\"" By \""al-sam\"" he meant death.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd ibn Humayd from 'Abd al-Razzaq"," and al-Bukhari reported it through another chain from al-Zuhri. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"19574","Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from 'Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn 'Amr ibn Nufayl (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family), who said: \The truffle is from the manna"," and its water is a cure for the eye.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ibn Abi 'Umar from Sufyan"," and both al-Bukhari and Muslim reported it through other chains from 'Abd al-Malik. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"19575","Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran narrated to us; Abu 'Ali Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Munadi narrated to us; Abu Badr Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Hashim ibn Hashim narrated from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, that Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Whoever eats seven dates of 'ajwah in the morning"," no poison or sorcery will harm him that day.\"" [Sahih. Agreed upon]\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from Abu Badr"," and both al-Bukhari and Muslim reported it through other chains from Hashim."""
"19576","It was also narrated by Abu Tuwalah 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Whoever eats seven dates from between its two walls (labatayha) when he wakes in the morning"," no poison will harm him until he reaches the evening.\"" Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us of this; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Daybuli narrated to us in Makkah; Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Zayd al-Sa'ig narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman"," and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it from al-Qa'nabi. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"19577","Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us by dictation; Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Fakihi informed us in Makkah; Abu Yahya ibn Abi Masrah narrated to us; Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us; al-Mas'udi narrated from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," did not send down any disease without appointing a cure for it"," except death (al-sam). So consume cows' milk"," for it grazes from every tree.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19578","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Abu al-Nadr narrated to us; Abu Khaythamah narrated from a woman of his family, from Mulaikah bint 'Amr al-Ju'fiyyah, who said to her: \Use cow's ghee — from the throat area or from the two humps — for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: 'Its milk — or its milk is a cure"," its ghee is a medicine"," and its meat — or its meats — is a disease.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"19579","Abu 'Amr al-Adib narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us; al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Dawri and 'Abd Allah ibn Salih informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us; I heard my father say: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak informed us from Yunus, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she used to recommend talbinah (a broth made from barley) for the sick and the grieved one who has lost a loved one, and she would say: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) say: 'Talbinah soothes the heart of the sick person and removes some of the grief.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Hibban from Ibn al-Mubarak in this manner"," and both al-Bukhari and Muslim reported it from the hadith of al-Layth from 'Uqayl. It has already been mentioned in the Book of Funerals. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"19580","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Maymuni narrated to us; Ruh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us; Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to me; Fatimah bint Abi Layth narrated to me from Umm Kulthum bint 'Amr ibn Abi 'Aqrab, who said: I heard 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) say: \You should take the beneficial"," disliked talbinah. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," it cleanses the stomach of one of you just as one of you washes his face with water from dirt.\"" She also said: \""When any member of his household fell ill"," the cooking pot would remain on the fire until one of two things happened\"" — meaning until the patient either recovered or passed away. [Da'if]"""
"19581","(19575) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Umm Qays bint Miḥsan, sister of ʿUkkāshah ibn Miḥsan al-Asadiyyah, who said: I came to the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) with a son of mine upon whom I had pressed — or he said, I had pressed him — due to a throat ailment. He said: \What is this that you press your children's throats with on account of this ailment? You should use this Indian aloe-wood (al-ʿūd al-hindī)"," for indeed in it are seven remedies. It is administered as a snuff (suʿiṭa bihi) for the throat ailment"," and it is given by way of ladūd for pleurisy (dhāt al-janb).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Ibn Abī ʿUmar and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"19582","(19576) Sufyān said regarding it: Ibn Abī ʿUmar mentioned al-qusṭ (costus), and that is in what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us, Sufyān narrated, and he mentioned it and said: \For indeed in it are remedies.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19583","(19577) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ ibn al-Ḥammāmiyy informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Maymūn Abī ʿAbd Allāh, from Zayd ibn Arqam (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \Treat pleurisy (dhāt al-janb) with olive oil and sea costus (al-qusṭ al-baḥrī).\""\n\nIt was also narrated by ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maymūn from his father"," from Zayd ibn Arqam (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu)"," who said: \""The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) prescribed for us for pleurisy (dhāt al-janb) wars (a type of resin)"," olive oil"," and costus.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19584","(19578) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, al-Layth narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn Thawbān al-Hamdānī, from Qays ibn Rāfiʿ al-Ashjaʿī, that the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \What is there in the two bitter things of remedy? Aloes (al-ṣabr) and colocynth (al-thuffāʾ).\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd cited it among the Marāsīl. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19585","(19579) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us, Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to us, Zakariyyā narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \The best of remedies are the snuff (saʿūṭ)"," the ladūd (medicine given to the side of the mouth)"," cupping (ḥijāmah)"," the purgative drink (mashiyy)"," and the application of leeches (ʿalaq).\"" This is a mursal narration. Abū Dāwūd cited it among the Marāsīl.\n\nIt was also narrated by ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā)"," who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \""The best of what you treat with are the snuff"," the ladūd"," cupping"," and the purgative drink.\""\n\nAnd it was narrated to us previously from Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā) that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \""Use kohl (al-ithmid)"," for indeed it clarifies the vision and causes the hair to grow.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19586","(19580) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated from ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Taymī, from Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) asked me: \What do you use as a laxative?\"" I said: \""Shubrum (a type of purgative plant).\"" He said: \""It is hot.\"" She said: Then I said: \""I used senna (sanā) as a laxative.\"" He said: \""If there were anything that could serve as a remedy against death"," it would be in senna.\""\n\nThis is how Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated it from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar.\n\nAbū Usāmah contradicted him in its chain"," saying: from Zurʿah ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bayāḍī al-Anṣārī — and it was said: Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — from a mawlā of Maʿmar al-Taymī"," from Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19587","(19581) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Zurʿah al-Dimashqī narrated to me, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to me, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Fazārī narrated to me: I heard Shaddād ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from the descendants of Shaddād ibn Aws, narrate to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī ʿAblah narrated to me, saying: I set out with Ibn al-Daylamī until we came to Abū Ubayy al-Anṣārī (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu), and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) say: \Senna (sanā) and sanūt — in both of them is a remedy for every ailment.\"" He said: It was said to Ibrāhīm: \""And what is sanūt?\"" He said: \""Have you not heard the poet's verse:\n\n'They are the fat (samn) with sanūt"," there is no deceit in them","\nAnd they protect the neighbour from being humbled.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by ʿAmr ibn Bakr ibn Tamīm from Ibrāhīm ibn Abī ʿAblah"," and he added in it: \""Except death (al-sām).\"" And ʿAmr explained sanūt in this hadith as honey. As for in the rare speech of the Arabs"," it is the cream of a skin of ghee (samn) that emerges as black streaks upon the ghee. Then he mentioned the poetry and explained his words \""there is no deceit in them\"" — he said: \""There is no dishonesty in them.\"" And his words \""from being humbled\"" — meaning: \""Their neighbour is not abased.\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"19588","(19582) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dabarī informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Baḥīr ibn Raysān, who said: One who heard Furwah ibn Maysik (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) narrated to me, saying: I said: \O Messenger of Allāh"," indeed we have a land called Arḍ Abʾan; it is our fertile land and our source of provision"," but it is a land of epidemic — or he said"," its epidemic is severe.\"" The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \""Leave it"," for indeed from proximity to epidemic comes destruction (talaf).\"" Al-Qutaybī said: \""Al-qarf means proximity to epidemic and disease.\""\n\nAbū Sulaymān said: \""This is from the category of medicine"," for indeed the corruption of air is among the most harmful and swiftest things in causing bodily illness"," according to the physicians.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (raḥimahullāh taʿālā) said: \""And this is analogous to his statement (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam): 'When you hear of it in a land"," do not approach it.' And all of that is by the will and permission of Allāh"," and there is no power and no strength except with Allāh.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19589","(19583) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, from the village of Ḥaddādah, narrated to us. They both said: Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Bakr ibn Yūnus narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUlayy ibn Rabāḥ, from his father, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \Do not compel your sick to eat and drink"," for indeed Allāh feeds them and gives them drink.\""\n\nThe wording of Abū Naṣr's hadith"," both chain and text"," is singular. Bakr ibn Yūnus ibn Bukayr is alone in narrating it from Mūsā ibn ʿUlayy"," and he is denounced in hadith"," as stated by al-Bukhārī.\n\nIt was narrated by ʿAlī ibn Qutaybah al-Rifāʿī and Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd al-Yashkurī from Mālik"," from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā)"," as a marfūʿ narration"," and it is baseless"," having no origin in the hadith of Mālik.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19590","(19584) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us, Sulaymān al-Shaybānī narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad, from his father, that he said: I asked ʿĀʾishah (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā) about ruqyah (incantation) for fever (ḥummā). She said: \The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) permitted ruqyah for every type of fever.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid"," and Muslim narrated it through another route from al-Shaybānī.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us"," Abū al-Muthannā informed us"," Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us"," Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated to me"," Maʿbad ibn Khālid narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaddād"," from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā)"," who said: \""The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) commanded me to perform ruqyah against the evil eye (al-ʿayn).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," and Muslim narrated it through another route from Sufyān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19591","(19585) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Wahb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, al-Zubaydī narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) saw in her house a young girl whose face had a yellowish mark, so he said: \Perform ruqyah for her"," for she has been afflicted by the evil eye.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"19592","(19586) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Bishr ibn Marwān informed us, Abū al-Rabīʿ Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥarb narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd al-Zubaydī narrated with a similar chain of narration, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said regarding a young girl in the house of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family): he saw on her face a yellowish mark and said: \She has been afflicted by the evil eye; perform ruqyah for her.\"" That is"," on her face there was yellowness.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Khālid from Muḥammad ibn Wahb ibn ʿAṭiyyah al-Dimashqī"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"19593","(19587) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from Ayyūb, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿUrwah ibn ʿĀmir, from ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah, from Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," the children of Jaʿfar are afflicted by the evil eye; shall I perform ruqyah for them?\"" He said: \""Yes. If there were anything that could precede destiny (al-qadar)"," it would be the evil eye.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19594","(19588) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us orally, Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdawayh ibn Sahl al-Marwazī informed us, Maḥmūd ibn Ādam al-Marwazī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿUrwah ibn ʿĀmir, from ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah al-Zuraqī, that Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \O Messenger of Allah…\"" and he mentioned it with a similar narration"," except that he said: \""al-Qaḍāʾ\"" (Decree) instead of \""al-Qadar\"" (Destiny). [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"19595","(19589) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us, Ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Zakariyyā narrated from Ḥuṣayn.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd al-Ṣayrafī and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated to us, Ṭalq ibn Ghannām narrated to me, Mālik ibn Miḥwal narrated from Ḥuṣayn, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: \There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a ḥummah (poisonous sting/bite).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: That is"," and Allah knows best"," these two are most deserving of ruqyah because of the increased harm in them. And al-ḥummah is the venom of venomous creatures. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19596","(19590) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us, Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyābī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from ʢĀṣim, from Yūsuf ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) gave permission for ruqyah in cases of al-laqwah (facial paralysis), al-namlah (a type of ulcerous swelling), and al-ḥummah (poisonous sting/bite). In my copy it is al-laqwah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"19597","(19591) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Sufyān narrated it with his chain of narration, and he said: \From al-ʿayn (the evil eye)\"" instead of \""al-laqwah (facial paralysis).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\nAnd Abū ʿUbayd said: al-Aṣmaʿī said: Al-namlah is a type of ulcerous swelling that emerges on the side and elsewhere. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19598","(19592) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, Ibn Jurayj narrated from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) gave permission to Banū ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm to perform ruqyah for the bite of a snake. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2199]"
"19599","(19593) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Sahl Muḥammad ibn Naṣrūyah al-Marwazī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khunb informed us, Abū Bakr Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Ibn Jurayj narrated from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said to Asmāʾ: \Why do I see the bodies of my brother's children so emaciated? Is some need afflicting them?\"" She said: \""No"," but the evil eye takes effect upon them quickly. Shall I perform ruqyah for them?\"" He said: \""With what?\"" She then recited to him some words that were unobjectionable"," and he said: \""Yes"," perform ruqyah for them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ"," incorporated within the first narration from Abī ʿĀṣim from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as mentioned previously]"""
"19600","(19594) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh and Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Naḍrūwī informed us, saying: al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah informed us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: A scorpion stung one of our men while we were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family). A man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," shall I perform ruqyah for him?\"" He said: \""Whoever among you is able to benefit his brother"," let him do so.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim from Rūḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2199]"""
"19601","(19595) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abū Sufyān from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) prohibited ruqyah (incantations). The family of ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm had a ruqyah that they used for scorpion stings. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," you have prohibited ruqyah"," yet we have a ruqyah that we use for scorpion stings.\"" He said"," \""Present it to me.\"" So they presented it to him"," and he said"," \""There is no harm in it. Whoever among you is able to benefit his brother"," let him do so.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb from Abū Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim]"""
"19602","(19596) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Rajāʾ informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr from his father from ʿAwf ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We used to perform ruqyah during the Jāhiliyyah (pre-Islamic period of ignorance). We said, \O Messenger of Allah"," what do you say about that?\"" He said"," \""Present your ruqyahs to me. There is no harm in ruqyah so long as it does not involve shirk (associating partners with Allah).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2200]"""
"19603","(19597) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Mashshāṭ informed us, both saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān from Abū Bakr ibn Sulaymān ibn Abī Ḥathmah from al-Shifāʾ (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) came to Ḥafṣah while I was with her. He said to me, \Will you not teach her the ruqyah for ant stings"," just as you taught her writing?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19604","(19598) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith and Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me from Ibn Shihāb that Abū Khizāmah narrated to him that his father narrated to him that he said, \O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think of medicines we use for treatment"," ruqyahs we seek"," and precautions we take — do any of these repel anything from the decree of Allah?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said"," \""They are from the decree of Allah.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19605","(19599) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Fārisī informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Ṣāliḥ informed me: al-Layth informed me: Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb who informed me: Abū Khizāmah, one of the Banī al-Ḥārith ibn Saʿd, informed me that his father informed him that he asked, and he mentioned it similarly. Yaʿqūb said: Abū Khizāmah is Ibn Maʿmar al-Saʿdī; Saʿd is Hudhaym, a Qudaʿī. [Same as the preceding hadith]"
"19606","(19600) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī al-Qāḍī informed us: Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā narrated from Yūnus from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Khizāmah Zayd ibn al-Ḥārith from his father that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) — thus he said, and the first narration is more accurate, and Allah knows best. The Shaykh said: It has also been narrated from Maʿmar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq from al-Zuhrī from Ibn Abī Khizāmah from his father, and the first is more accurate."
"19607","(19601) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf said: Sufyān mentioned from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from ʿAmrah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to her while a Jewish woman was performing ruqyah on her. He said, \Perform ruqyah on her with the Book of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — without the statement \""a Jewish woman\""]"""
"19608","(19602) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ said: I asked al-Shāfiʿī about ruqyah. He said, \There is no harm in a man performing ruqyah with the Book of Allah or with that which is known as dhikr (remembrance) of Allah.\"" I said"," \""Can the People of the Book perform ruqyah on Muslims?\"" He said"," \""Yes"," provided they perform ruqyah with what is known from the Book of Allah or the dhikr of Allah.\"" I said"," \""What is the evidence for that?\"" He said"," \""It is not based on a specific evidence"," but rather on the narration of our companion and your companion"," for Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to ʿĀʾishah while she was complaining of an ailment and a Jewish woman was performing ruqyah on her. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," 'Perform ruqyah on her with the Book of Allah.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The narrations regarding what the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) performed ruqyah with"," what was used for his ruqyah"," what he treated with"," and what he commanded treatment with are numerous. I have extracted some of what has been transmitted regarding ruqyah in the book al-Daʿawāt (Supplications)"," and success is through Allah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19609","(19603) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us: al-Aʿmash narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah from Yaḥyā ibn al-Jazzār from the brother of Zaynab, the wife of ʿAbdullāh — meaning Ibn Masʿūd — from Zaynab, the wife of ʿAbdullāh, from ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) say, \Indeed"," ruqyah"," tamāʾim (amulets)"," and tiwalah (charms to cause love) are shirk.\"" She said"," \""I said"," 'Why do you say this? By Allah"," my eye used to discharge"," and I would go to so-and-so"," a Jewish man"," who would perform ruqyah on me"," and when he performed ruqyah on me"," it would settle.'\"" ʿAbdullāh said"," \""That was only the work of Satan. He used to poke it with his hand"," and when he performed ruqyah on it"," he would desist from it. It would have been sufficient for you to say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) used to say: 'Adhhib al-bāsa"," Rabb al-nās"," ishfa"," anta al-Shāfī"," lā shifāʾa illā shifāuka"," shifāʾan lā yughādir saqaman (Remove the affliction"," Lord of mankind. Cure"," for You are the Healer. There is no cure except Your cure — a cure that leaves no illness behind).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — without the story]"""
"19610","(19604) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī both informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar said: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Jarīr narrated from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabīʿ ibn ʿUmaylah from al-Qāsim ibn Ḥassān from his paternal uncle ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥarmalah from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) disliked ten things: wearing a gold ring, letting the garment drag below the ankles, ṣufrah (meaning khalūq — a type of perfume or dye), altering grey hair, ruqyah except with the Muʿawwidhāt (the last three sūrahs of the Qurʾān), tying amulets, playing with dice (kʿāb), displaying adornment outside its proper place, diverting water from its proper place (i.e., coitus interruptus), and corrupting a child other than one's own through one's ḥarām relations. [Munkar]\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: As for tiwalah, it is with a kasrah on the tāʾ, and it refers to that by which a woman is made beloved to her husband, and it is from sorcery, and that is not permissible. As for ruqyah and tamāʾim, ʿAbdullāh only intended that which is not in the Arabic language and whose meaning is not known.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Tamīmah (amulet) is said to be a bead or beads that they would hang, believing that they would ward off afflictions from them. It is also said to be a necklace in which protective charms (ʿūdh) are placed."
"19611","(19605) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan — both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Haywa ibn Shurayh informed me that Khalid ibn Ubayd al-Ma'afiri narrated to him from Abu al-Mus'ab Mushrih ibn Ha'an that he heard him say: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \Whoever hangs a tamimah (amulet)"," may Allah not complete his affair"," and whoever hangs a wad'ah (charm)"," may Allah not grant him peace.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: This also refers in meaning to what Abu 'Ubayd said. It may also be that this and similar narrations constitute a prohibition and disapproval directed at one who hangs such things while believing that complete recovery and the removal of illness come from them"," as the people of the Jahiliyyah used to do. As for one who hangs them seeking blessing through the remembrance of Allah"," the Most High"," knowing that there is no remover of affliction except Allah and no defender besides Him"," then there is no harm in that"," if Allah wills. [Da'if]"""
"19612","(19606) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak from Talhah ibn Abi Sa'id from Bukayr ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The tamimah is not what is hung before the affliction. Rather"," the tamimah is what is hung after the affliction so that through it the decrees may be repelled.\"" [Sahih]"""
"19613","(19607) 'Abd narrated it from Ibn al-Mubarak and said in its text that she said: \The tama'im (amulets) are what is hung before the descent of affliction"," and what is hung after the descent of affliction is not a tamimah.\""\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah informed me through ijazah: al-Hasan ibn Halim informed me: Abu al-Muwajjih informed us: 'Abd informed us: 'Abd Allah mentioned it. And this is more authentic. [Da'if]"""
"19614","(19608) Abu Zakariyya and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me from Bukayr ibn 'Abd Allah from al-Qasim Muhammad from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that she said: \That which is hung after the affliction has befallen is not a tamimah.\""\n\nAnd this indicates the soundness of the narration of 'Abd. [Sahih]"""
"19615","(19609) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami from his original, and Abu Bakr al-Qadi, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us: Abu 'Amir al-Khazzaz narrated from al-Hasan from 'Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, while he had a ring of copper around his neck. He said: \What is this?\"" He said: \""It is for weakness.\"" He said: \""Would you like to be entrusted to it? Remove it and throw it away.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19616","(19610) Al-Faqih Abu Ishaq — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tusi narrated to us: Abu al-Walid — Hassan ibn Muhammad al-Faqih narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us: Waki' narrated from Ibn Abi Layla from his brother from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Ukaym, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Whoever hangs a 'ilah (charm) shall be entrusted to it.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19617","(19611) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas narrated to us: Harun narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from Shu'bah from Qatadah from Waq' ibn Suhban from Usayr ibn Jabir who said: 'Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Whoever hangs something shall be entrusted to it.\""\n\nHe said: And 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Jarir ibn Hazim who said: I heard al-Hasan say: The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""Whoever hangs something shall be entrusted to it.\""\n\nHe said: And 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Shu'bah from al-Hajjaj from Fudayl that Sa'id ibn Jubayr used to write protective invocations (al-ma'adhah) for his sons.\n\nHe said: And I asked 'Ata'"," and he said: \""We did not dislike them except for something that came to us from your direction.\"" [Hasan"," Mawquf]"""
"19618","(19612) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Nafi' ibn Yazid informed me that he asked Yahya ibn Sa'id about ruqyah (incantation) and the hanging of written verses, and he said: \Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab used to command the hanging of Qur'anic verses and said: 'There is no harm in it.'\""\n\nThe Sheikh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: All of this refers to what we have stated — that if one is treated with a ruqyah whose contents are unknown"," or with something resembling what the people of the Jahiliyyah did by attributing healing to the ruqyah itself"," then it is not permissible. But if one is treated with the Book of Allah or with known forms of remembrance of Allah"," seeking blessing through them"," while believing that healing descends from Allah"," the Most High"," then there is no harm in it. And success is through Allah. [Sahih]"""
"19619","(19613) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: 'Aqil ibn Ma'qil said: I heard Wahb ibn Munabbih narrate from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was asked about al-nushrah (counter-spell), and he said: \It is from the work of Satan.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: It has also been narrated from the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," in a mursal form"," and despite its being mursal it is more authentic. The ruling regarding what is disliked of al-nushrah and what is not disliked is the same as the ruling regarding ruqyah"," which we have already mentioned. [Da'if]"""
"19620","(19614) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us.\n\nHe said: And Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us. Both said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Wuhaib narrated from Ibn Tawus from his father from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \The evil eye is real. And if there were anything that could precede the divine decree"," the evil eye would precede it. And when you are asked to perform ghusl (ritual washing)"," then perform it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi and Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir and Ahmad ibn Khirash from Muslim ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih. Muslim 2188]"""
"19621","(19615) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Jarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The one who casts the evil eye (al-ʿāʾin) would be commanded to perform wuḍūʾ, and the one affected by the evil eye (al-maʿīn) would be washed with that water. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"19622","(19616) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Abī Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf, who said: ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah passed by Sahl ibn Ḥunayf while he was bathing and said: \I have not seen the like of today"," nor the skin of a concealed young woman.\"" It was not long before he collapsed. He was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) and it was said to him: \""Help Sahl—he has fallen unconscious.\"" He asked: \""Whom do you suspect?\"" They said: \""ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah.\"" He said: \""Why would one of you kill his brother? When he sees something that impresses him"," let him invoke blessing.\"" And he commanded him to perform wuḍūʾ—to wash his face"," his hands up to the elbows"," his knees"," and the inner edge of his lower garment—and to pour the water over him.\n\nMaʿmar said: al-Zuhrī said: \""And the vessel should be tipped over behind him.\"" Sufyān said: Maʿmar narrated this ḥadīth to me and added this in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19623","(19617) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated from Ibn Shihāb; Abī Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf informed me, and he mentioned the meaning of this ḥadīth, except that he said: So he called ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah and rebuked him, saying to him: \Why would one of you kill his brother? Will you not invoke blessing? Bathe for him.\"" So ʿĀmir bathed for him"," and Sahl departed with the caravan.\n\nIbn Shihāb said: The bathing (ghusl) that we learned from our scholars"," as they describe it"," is that the man who casts the evil eye upon his companion is brought a vessel containing water. It is held up from the ground for him. The one who casts the evil eye inserts his right hand into the water and pours a single handful upon his face into the vessel. Then he inserts his left hand into the water and washes his right hand up to the elbow with his left hand"," a single handful into the vessel. Then he inserts his right hand and washes his left hand"," a single handful"," up to the elbow into the vessel. Then he inserts both hands together into the water"," a single handful into the vessel. Then he inserts his hand and rinses his mouth"," then spits it out into the vessel. Then he inserts his left hand and scoops water and pours it upon the back of his right palm"," a single handful into the vessel. Then he inserts his left hand and pours upon the elbow of his right hand"," a single handful into the vessel"," while raising his hand up to his neck. Then he does the like of that for the elbow of his left hand. Then he does that for the top of his right foot from near the fingers"," and likewise for the left. Then he inserts his left hand and pours upon his right knee"," then does likewise for the left. Then he dips the inner edge of his right lower garment into the water. Then the one holding the vessel stands with it and pours it upon the head of the one afflicted by the evil eye from behind him"," then tips the vessel face-down upon the ground behind him.\n\n(T) Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated it from al-Zuhrī and said: The man who casts the evil eye is brought a vessel; he inserts his palm into it and rinses his mouth"," then spits it out into the vessel. Then he washes his face in the vessel. Then he inserts his left hand and pours upon his right palm. Then he inserts his right hand and pours upon his left palm. Then he inserts his left hand and pours upon his right elbow. Then he inserts his right hand and pours upon his left elbow. Then he inserts his left hand and pours upon his right foot. Then he inserts his right hand and pours upon his left foot. Then he inserts his left hand and pours upon his right knee. Then he inserts his right hand and pours upon his left knee. Then he washes the inner edge of his lower garment"," and the vessel is not placed upon the ground. Then it is poured upon the head of the man who was afflicted by the evil eye from behind him"," a single handful.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: By \""the inner edge of his lower garment\"" (dākhilat izārih) he means the inner edge of his lower garment that is adjacent to his body. Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated it from al-Zuhrī and added in it: Then that vessel is given to the man who was afflicted before it is placed upon the ground"," so that he may drink from it"," rinse his mouth"," and pour it upon his face. Then it is poured upon his head"," and the vessel is turned upside down upon its face. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was narrated before.]"""
"19624","(19618) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAliyy ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī informed us in Baghdād; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān al-Naysābūrī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Ibn Abī Uways informed me; Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās, from Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith (may Allah be pleased with her): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee and died. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Remove it and what is around it"," and eat your ghee.\"" This is the wording of Muḥammad's ḥadīth. In the narration of al-Qāḍī it states: \""Remove it and what is around it of the ghee"," and discard it.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19625","(19619) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us; Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), from Maymūnah (may Allah be pleased with her): The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee and died in it. He said: \Remove it and what is around it"," and eat it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19626","(19620) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us; al-Ḥumaydī informed us; Sufyān informed us; al-Zuhrī informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us that he heard Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrate from Maymūnah (may Allah be pleased with her): A mouse fell into ghee and died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) was asked about it. He said: \Remove it and what is around it"," and eat.\"" It was said to Sufyān: \""Maʿmar narrates it from al-Zuhrī"," from Saʿīd"," from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" Sufyān said: \""I did not hear al-Zuhrī narrate it except from ʿUbaydullāh"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from Maymūnah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family). And indeed"," I heard it from him many times.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19627","(19621) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ and al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAliyy informed us, and the wording is that of al-Ḥasan. They said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \If a mouse falls into ghee"," if it is solid"," remove it and what is around it; if it is liquid"," do not go near it.\"" al-Ḥasan said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: And sometimes Maʿmar would narrate it from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from Maymūnah"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family). And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUmar informed me that Maʿmar also narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbaydullāh"," from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," from Maymūnah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Munkar]"""
"19628","(19622) ʿAliyy ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī informed us; Musaddad informed us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, who is Ibn Ziyād, informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee. He said: \If it is solid"," it and what is around it are taken and discarded; if it is melted or liquid"," it is not to be eaten.\"" [Munkar]"""
"19629","(19623) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAliyy ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us; from Abū ʿUbayd; Hushaym narrated from Maʿmar ibn Abān, from Rāshid, the client of Quraysh, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both): He was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee. He said: \If it is liquid"," discard all of it; if it is solid (jāmis)"," discard the mouse and what is around it"," and eat what remains.\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""Jāmis\"" means \""jāmid\"" (solid). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19630","(19624) ʿAliyy ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ibn Minhāl informed us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us; Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated from Barakah, Abī al-Walīd, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) was in the mosque. He raised his gaze toward the sky and smiled, and said: \May Allah curse the Jews! May Allah curse the Jews! May Allah curse the Jews! Indeed"," Allah forbade them the fats"," so they sold them and consumed their prices. Indeed"," when Allah forbids a people the eating of a thing"," He forbids them its price as well.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19631","(19625) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and others narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn ʿUmar informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from his father, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee (clarified butter). He said: \Throw it away along with what is around it"," and eat what remains.\"" It was said: \""O Prophet of Allah"," what if the ghee is liquid?\"" He said: \""Make use of it"," but do not eat it.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn ʿUmar is not relied upon as a narrator. It is also narrated from Ibn Jurayj"," from Ibn Shihāb"," in this manner"," but the chain leading to him is not strong. [Weak]"""
"19632","(19626) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdad, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shuʿayb ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) was asked about a mouse that falls into ghee or fat. He said: \Throw it away along with what is around it"," if it is solid.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what if it is liquid?\"" He said: \""Make use of it"," but do not eat it.\""\n\nThe authentic narration from Ibn ʿUmar is his own statement"," stopped at him (mawqūf)"," and not raised to the Prophet (marfūʿ). [Weak]"""
"19633","(19627) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us, Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, regarding a mouse that fell into oil. He said: \Use it for lighting (your lamps) and anoint your skins with it.\"" [Weak]"""
"19634","(19628) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Rāshid al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Barqī narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Bashīr, from Abī Hārūn, from Abī Saʿīd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) was asked about a mouse that falls into ghee or oil. He said: \Use it for lighting"," but do not eat it.\"" Or something similar to that.\n\nʿAlī said: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Abī Hārūn as a stopped statement (mawqūf) from Abī Saʿīd. [Weak]"""
"19635","(19629) Abū Bakr informed us, ʿAlī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Dāwūd narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb and Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim said: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us, from Abī Hārūn al-ʿAbdī, from Abī Saʿīd, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said regarding a mouse that falls into ghee or oil: \Make use of it"," but do not eat it.\"" The Shaykh said: This is the preserved narration"," and it is stopped (mawqūf). [Weak]"""
"19636","(19630) By way of evidence, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazīd, that is Ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) say during the Year of the Conquest, while he was in Makkah: \Indeed"," Allah and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of intoxicants"," carrion"," swine"," and idols.\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what about the fat of carrion? For ships are caulked with it"," skins are anointed with it"," and people use it for lighting.\"" He said: \""No"," it is unlawful.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said at that time: \""May Allah fight the Jews. When Allah forbade them their fats"," they melted them down and then sold them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Authentic. Agreed upon.]"""
"19637","(19631) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Usāmah ibn Zayd informed me, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) say during the Year of the Conquest, while he was in Makkah: \Indeed"," Allah and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of intoxicants"," carrion"," swine"," and idols.\"" It was said to him at that time: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what about the fat of carrion? For water-skins and skins are anointed with it"," and people use it for lighting.\"" He said: \""No"," it is unlawful.\"" Then he said at that time: \""May Allah fight the Jews. When Allah forbade them their fats"," they melted them down and then sold them and consumed their price.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Among the scholars are those who distinguished between carrion and that which becomes impure by the occurrence of an impurity in it"," permitting the use of that which becomes incidentally impure"," but not carrion"," in accordance with the narrations regarding both"," and because the impurity of carrion is more severe while the impurity of oil is lighter. And with Allah lies success. [Authentic through other chains.]"""
"19638","(19632) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Dhakwān, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Whoever kills himself with an iron blade"," his blade will be in his hand"," and he will thrust it into his belly in the Fire of Hell"," abiding therein forever and ever. And whoever kills himself with poison"," his poison will be in his hand"," and he will sip it in the Fire of Hell"," abiding therein forever and ever. And whoever throws himself from a mountain and kills himself"," he will be throwing himself into the Fire of Hell"," abiding therein forever and ever.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Authentic. Agreed upon.]"""
"19639","(19633) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Mayṣarah narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated to us, Shuraḥbīl ibn Yazīd al-Maʿāfirī narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ al-Tanūkhī, who said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with both of them, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) say: \I care not what I come upon"," if I were to drink a theriac (antidote)"," or hang an amulet"," or recite poetry of my own accord.\""\n\nIt is narrated from Ibn Sīrīn that he used to dislike theriac because snake flesh is used in its preparation.\n\nImām Aḥmad said: It is for this meaning that al-Shāfiʿī disliked it"," saying: \""It is not permissible to consume theriac made with the flesh of snakes except in a state of necessity"," in which carrion is permitted.\"" [Weak]"""
"19640","(19634) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdad, Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us, from Simāk, from Jābir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A mule—or he said a she-camel—died belonging to a man, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) to seek a legal ruling. Jābir claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said to its owner: \Do you not have something that suffices you from it?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Go and eat it.\"" [Weak]"""
"19641","(19635) Abu al-Rudhbari narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Hammad, i.e. ibn Salamah, narrated to us — from Simak ibn Harb — from Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man descended upon a rocky tract with his family and children. A man said to him: \A she-camel of mine has gone astray; if you find it"," keep it.\"" He found it but could not find its owner. Then it fell ill. His wife said: \""Slaughter it.\"" He refused. It died. She said: \""Skin it so that we may dry its fat and meat and eat it.\"" He said: \""I shall ask the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him.\"" So he came to him and asked him. He said: \""Do you have wealth that would suffice you?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then eat it.\"" When its owner came and was informed of the matter"," he said: \""Why did you not slaughter it?\"" He replied: \""I felt shy before you.\""\n\nSharik ibn Abd Allah followed them both from Simak ibn Harb. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"19642","(19636) And in what Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali narrated — from al-Walid ibn Muslim — from al-Awza'i, who said: Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to me — from Ibn Murtada, or Abu Murtada — from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: They said: \O Messenger of Allah"," we are in a land where severe hunger afflicts us. What of the carrion is lawful for us?\"" He said: \""If you do not have a morning meal"," or an evening meal"," or gather any herbage"," then deal with it as you wish.\""\n\nAbu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed me by licence that Abu al-Hasan ibn Sabih had informed them — that Abd Allah ibn Shirwayh had informed them — that Ishaq had narrated it"," mentioning it. [Sahih (Authentic)]"""
"19643","(19637) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Harun al-Zahid narrated to us — Sahl ibn Ammar al-Ataki narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us — al-Awza'i narrated — from Hassan ibn Atiyyah — from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We said: \O Messenger of Allah"," severe hunger afflicts us. What of the carrion is permissible for us?\"" He said: \""If you do not have a morning meal"," or an evening meal"," or gather herbage"," then deal with it as you wish.\"" [Sahih (Authentic). Previously cited.]"""
"19644","(19638) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us — Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Karizi narrated to us — Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us — from Abu Ubayd — Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us — from al-Awza'i — from Hassan ibn Atiyyah — from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," we are in a land where severe hunger afflicts us. When does carrion become lawful for us?\"" He said: \""So long as you do not have a morning meal"," or an evening meal"," or gather herbage from it"," then deal with it as you wish.\""\n\nAbu Ubayd said: Abu Ubaydah said: \""Al-hafa' is the moist"," white"," fresh palm-shoot"," which is eaten.\"" He interpreted the words 'or gather herbage' as meaning: \""So long as you do not uproot this specific plant and eat it.\""\n\nAbu Ubayd said: Mu'adh narrated to us — from Ibn Awn"," who said: \""I saw with al-Hasan the books of Samurah for his sons"," stating that what suffices in a state of necessity or dire need is a morning meal or an evening meal.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: This tafsir (exegesis) which Abu Ubayd"," may Allah have mercy on him"," provided is correct"," based on what he transmitted from the book of Samurah. As for the marfu' (elevated) hadith"," it has been said that it is possible that what is intended by it — and Allah knows best — is that carrion is made lawful for them so long as they have no morning meal"," evening meal"," or herbage by which they sustain themselves. This is what is appropriate to their question in the narration of Abu Ubayd: \""When does carrion become lawful for us?\"" and by His words: \""or gather herbage from it.\"" [Sahih (Authentic)]"""
"19645","(19639) Abu Ja'far Kamil ibn Ahmad al-Mustamli narrated to us — Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Mihrajan narrated to us — Dawud ibn al-Husayn al-Bayhaqi narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us — Kharijah narrated — from Thawr — from Rashid ibn Sa'd, and he gave me a book — from Samurah ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When you give your family an evening drink of milk"," then avoid what Allah has forbidden you of carrion.\""\n\nThis corroborates what came before"," and Allah knows best. What Abu Ubayd interpreted is the most well-known among the scholars of knowledge and most appropriate to his words: \""What of the carrion is lawful for us?\"" in the narration of al-Walid ibn Muslim. Abu Abd Allah al-Halimi"," may Allah have mercy on him"," mentioned it in his book and said: \""He clarified that if they do not eat it as they eat permissible food"," there is no sin upon them regarding it. Eating permissible food means that one does not seek a state of dire necessity in which one fears for one's life. Rather"," the one who finds something with which to have a morning meal becomes independent of anything else until nightfall — meaning that it suffices him for his needs. When evening comes"," he partakes of what he left during the day"," even if there is not a severe necessity. He may add to it herbage or other things"," either as additional food or as something pleasant. This is not the way of carrion. Rather"," carrion is only permitted in the amount that sustains life and meets the pressing need that calls for it. It does not occur at a specific time of morning or evening"," nor is it eaten for pleasure"," with herbage or the like added to it.\"" Thus the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," clarified that if they do not eat it as they eat permissible food"," there is no sin upon them regarding it. And Allah knows best. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"19646","(19640) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abu Dawud informed us — Harun ibn Abd Allah informed us — al-Fadl ibn Dukayn informed us — Uqbah ibn Wahb ibn Uqbah al-Amiri informed us, saying: I heard my father narrating from al-Fujay' al-Amiri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: He came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \What of the carrion is lawful for us?\"" He said: \""What is your food?\"" We said: \""We have an evening drink and a morning drink.\""\n\nAbu Nu'aym said: Uqbah explained it to me as a vessel in the morning and a vessel in the evening. He said: \""That"," and hunger is what makes it so.\"" So he made carrion lawful for them in this state. Abu Dawud said: \""Al-ghabuq (evening drink) is at the end of the day.\"" Others narrated from Abu Nu'aym"," saying: \""That is the abode of hunger.\"" In this hadith is the indication that he permitted them to consume carrion along with what sustains life and preserves the soul — a morning drink and an evening drink — when neither nourishes the body nor satisfies fully. And Allah knows best.\n\nThere is room for consideration regarding the establishment of these hadiths"," and the hadith of Jabir ibn Samurah is the most authentic among them. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"19647","(19641) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Sa'id Isma'il ibn Ahmad al-Jurjani informed us — Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asqalani informed us — Harmalah ibn Yahya informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Amr ibn al-Harith informed me — from Sa'd ibn Abi Hilal — from Utban, i.e. ibn Abi Hakim — from Nafi' ibn Jubayr — from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, who said: It was said to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: \Narrate to us about the matter of the hour of hardship.\"" Umar said: \""We went out to Tabuk in intense heat. We halted at a place where thirst afflicted us so severely that we thought our necks would be severed. A man would go out seeking water and not return until he thought his neck would be cut off. A man would slaughter his camel"," squeeze its dung"," and drink it"," and place what remained upon his liver. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," Allah has accustomed you to goodness in supplication. Supplicate for us.' He said: 'Would you like that?' He said: 'Yes.' So he raised his hands and did not lower them until the sky gave shade"," then poured down rain. They filled what they had with them. We then went to look and found that it had not gone beyond the army.\"" [Hasan (Good)]"""
"19648","(19642) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran informed us — Isma'il al-Saffar informed us — Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us — Abd al-Razzaq informed us — from Ma'mar — from al-A'mash — from Abu al-Duha — from Masruq, who said: Whoever is compelled to carrion, blood, and the flesh of swine, and does not eat or drink until he dies, shall enter the Fire.\n\nAnd from Ma'mar — from Qatadah, who said: \Let him eat of carrion what suffices him"," but let him not gorge himself upon it.\"" Ma'mar said: \""And I did not hear any concession regarding wine.\"" [Sahih (Authentic)]"""
"19649","(19643) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed us — Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi informed us — al-Qa'nabi informed us, reciting to Malik, who said: And Abu Nasr Umar informed us — Muhammad ibn Amr al-Harashi informed us — Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, saying: I recited to Malik — from Nafi' — from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Let no one milk the livestock of another without his permission.\"" Would any of you like to be brought his vessel of food and have its contents overturned and his food carried away? For the udders of their livestock store their sustenance for them. Let no one milk the livestock of another without his permission.\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Yahya. In the narration of al-Qa'nabi: \""and have it overturned.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih (Authentic). Agreed upon (muttafaq alayh).]"""
"19650","(19644) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan al-Amiri al-Kufi informed us — Abu Usamah informed us — from Ubayd Allah — from Nafi' — from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade that livestock be milked without the permission of their owners. He said: \Would any of you like to be brought his vessel in which is his food and have what is in it overturned? For the udders of their livestock are like what is in their drinking vessels.\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in al-Sahih from the hadith of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar. He also extracted it from the hadith of al-Layth"," Ayyub"," Musa ibn Uqbah"," and Isma'il ibn Umayyah — all from Nafi' — from Ibn Umar"," may Allah be pleased with both of them — from the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him. [Sahih (Authentic). Agreed upon (muttafaq alayh).]"""
"19651","(19645) Abū al-Qāsim — ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Mu'adhdhin — informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb narrated to us; Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, on the authority of Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, on the authority of Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, on the authority of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿīd, on the authority of Abī Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \It is not permissible for a person to take the staff of his brother without his goodwill.\"" That is because of the severity with which Allah has forbidden the wealth of a Muslim to another Muslim.\n\nIbn Wahb also narrated it on the authority of Sulaymān ibn Bilāl"," on the authority of Suhayl"," on the authority of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd"," on the authority of Abī Ḥumayd. And ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Ḥasan narrated it on the authority of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Saʿīd"," on the authority of ʿUmārah ibn Ḥārithah al-Ḍamrī"," on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Yathribī al-Ḍamrī"," on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family). This has already been mentioned in the Book of Usurpation. And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd ibn Mālik is Ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," as stated by al-Bukhārī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19652","(19646) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī narrated to us; Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us; ʿIkramah — that is, Ibn ʿAmmār — narrated to us, on the authority of Yaḥyā, who said: A freed client of mine belonging to Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated to me, saying: We were with Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him) when we came upon a valley containing palm trees that had reached maturity. Saʿd gave me two dirhams and said: \Buy us fodder and dates.\"" So I went but found no one among the palm trees. I returned to him and informed him. He said to me: \""If it pleases you to be a true believer"," then do not eat any fruit from the palm trees.\"" He said: \""So we spent the night"," and our she-camel"," hungry.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19653","(19647) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū ʿUtbah narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us, on the authority of Shuʿbah, on the authority of Ayyūb, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, on the authority of Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), that he was asked about what falls from the palm tree — may he eat from it? He said: \No"," not even a single date.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19654","(19648) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \Whoever passes by a man's crop"," or fruit"," or livestock"," or any other part of his wealth"," it is not permissible for him to take anything from it without his permission. This is because there is neither a text from the Book nor an established Sunnah permitting it. Thus"," it is forbidden to its owner except with his permission. And Allah knows best.\"" He said: \""And it has been said: 'Whoever passes by a garden"," let him eat and not take a bundle in his garment.'\""\n\nA hadith has been narrated on this matter; were its like to be established with us"," we would not contradict it. For the Book and the established hadith confirm that it is not permissible to consume the wealth of anyone except with his permission.\n\nThe Shaykh said: As for the one who stated this opinion"," it is ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19655","(19649) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us; Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Manṣūr narrated to us, on the authority of Mujāhid, on the authority of Abī ʿIyāḍ, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whoever among you passes by a garden"," let him eat to fill his belly"," but let him not take a bundle in his garment.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"19656","(19650) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān both informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, on the authority of al-Aʿmash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When you are three"," appoint one of you as your leader. And when you pass by a shepherd of camels"," call out: 'O shepherd of the camels!' If he responds to you"," then ask him for water. If he does not respond"," then go to the she-camels"," milk them"," drink"," and then tie up their udders.\""\n\nThis narration from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) is authentic through both its chains of narration. With us"," it is understood to apply in a state of necessity. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19657","(19651) As for the hadith that has been narrated, Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated it on the authority of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), on the authority of Nāfiʿ, on the authority of Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Whoever enters a garden"," let him eat and not take a bundle in his garment.\""\n\nʿUmar ibn Aḥmad informed us; Abū ʿAmr al-Sulamī narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-Jawwāz al-Makkī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19658","(19652) Abū Muḥammad al-Sukkari informed us; Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us; al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Ghassān narrated to us, saying: It was mentioned to Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn — the hadith of Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym al-Ṭāʾifī on the authority of ʿUbayd Allāh, regarding a man who passes by a garden and eats from it. He said: \This is an error.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: \""I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl about this hadith"," and he said: 'Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrates hadiths from ʿUbayd Allāh in which he makes errors.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has also been narrated through other routes"," none of which are strong. [Ṣaḥīḥ — according to Ibn Maʿīn]"""
"19659","(19653) Among them is what Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated to us, on the authority of al-Walīd ibn Kathīr, who narrated to me: ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: \I heard a man from Muzaynah asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) — and I was listening — about lost property. He mentioned the hadith. Then he asked him about fruits that a man takes. He said: 'What he takes in its sheaths — that is"," the heads of the palm trees — and carries away"," then its price and the like of it along with it"," and a disciplinary punishment. And what is in its clusters"," and he takes it"," then for it there is amputation"," if that reaches the price of a shield. But if he eats from it with his mouth and does not take anything or carry a bundle in his garment"," then there is nothing upon him.'\""\n\nThis"," if authentic"," is understood to mean that there is no amputation upon him when he did not remove it from its place of safekeeping. [Ḥasan]"""
"19660","(19654) Among them is what Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAyāsh ibn al-Walīd al-Raqqām narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us; Saʿīd narrated to us, on the authority of Qatādah, on the authority of al-Ḥasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \When one of you comes upon livestock"," if its owner is among them"," let him seek his permission. If he grants him permission"," let him milk and drink. If the owner is not among them"," let him call out three times. If someone responds to him"," let him seek his permission. Otherwise"," let him milk and drink"," but let him not carry any away.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The hadiths of al-Ḥasan from Samurah are not established by some of the ḥuffāẓ"," who claim that they are from a book other than the hadith of al-ʿAqīqah"," in which he mentioned having heard directly. If it is authentic"," then it is understood to apply in a state of necessity. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19661","(19655) And among them is what Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us — al-Jurayrī narrated from Abī Naḍrah, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam, who said: \When one of you comes upon a herdsman"," let him call out 'O herdsman of the camels!' three times. If he responds"," [well and good]; otherwise"," let him milk and drink"," and let him not carry [any away]. And when one of you comes upon a walled garden"," let him call out three times"," 'O owner of the garden!' If he responds"," [well and good]; otherwise"," let him eat"," and let him not carry [any away].\""\n\nSaʿīd ibn Iyās al-Jurayrī is the sole narrator of this ḥadīth"," and he is among the trustworthy narrators (al-thiqāt)"," except that he became confused (ikhtalaṭa) in the latter part of his life"," and the hearing of Yazīd ibn Hārūn from him occurred after his confusion.\n\nIt was also narrated by Ḥammād ibn Salamah from al-Jurayrī"," but he is not strong (bi-l-qawī).\n\nAnd it has also been narrated from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," from the Prophet"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," with a different wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19662","(19656) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed him — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārīzī informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us — from Abī ʿUbayd, Sharīk narrated to us — from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀṣim, who said: I heard Abā Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: \It is not permissible for anyone to untie the teat-strap (ṣirār) of a she-camel except with the permission of its owners"," for indeed the seal of its owners is upon it.\""\n\nIt was said to Sharīk: \""Did you raise it (rafaʿahu)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: This is consistent with the established ḥadīth from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," from the Prophet"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," regarding the prohibition of that"," which has already been mentioned earlier in this chapter. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19663","(19657) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārīzī informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, who said: Abū ʿUbayd said: \This ḥadīth — meaning the ḥadīth of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and then the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb regarding the concession (al-rukhṣah) — he permitted it for the starving"," desperate person who has nothing with which to purchase [food]. This is explained in another ḥadīth which al-Anṣārī Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us — from Ibn Jurayj"," from ʿAṭāʾ"," who said: 'The Messenger of Allah"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," permitted the starving"," desperate person"," when he passes by a garden"," to eat from it and not to take provisions (khubnah) from it.'\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""And that which clarifies this is the ḥadīth of ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," regarding the Anṣār who passed by a tribe of the Arabs and asked for hospitality (al-qirā)"," but they refused. They then asked for the right to buy food (al-shirā)"," but they refused. So they restrained them and overpowered them"," and they came to ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and mentioned that to him. He intended to punish the Bedouins and said: 'The wayfarer (ibn al-sabīl) has a greater right to water than the one settled upon it.'\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""And Ḥajjāj narrated it to us — from Shuʿbah"," from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Thaqafī"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," from ʿUmar.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: \""This is its explanation — it is only for one who is unable to obtain hospitality or to purchase food. And similarly"," in the first ḥadīth"," it says: 'Let him call out"," O herdsman of the camels"," three times' — so that it constitutes a request for hospitality beforehand.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And in this context"," ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Tamtām narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād al-Makkī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Makhzūmī said: I heard al-Qāsim ibn Makhwal al-Bahzī saying: I heard my father saying: I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," we come upon camels and we are in need of them"," while their milk is withheld (muṣarrārah).\"" He said: \""Call out"," O owner of the camels"," three times. If he responds to you"," [well and good]; otherwise"," milk"," and then leave for the milk its vessels (lawāhiqahu).\"" Another narrator added: \""Then milk"," and then leave for the milk its vessels.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19664","(19658) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to me — my father narrated to me — from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh, from Salīṭ ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Tamīmī, from Dhuhayl ibn ʿAwf ibn Shammākh, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \We were with the Prophet"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," when [we saw] camels with their udders tied"," gnawing at the branches of trees. People went to milk them"," but the Prophet"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," called them and said: 'Have you considered if people were to take provisions for you and then seize what is in your provision bags — would they have betrayed you?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'These are the households of a Muslim; what is in their udders is like what is in your provision bags.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," then what is permissible for a man from the wealth of his brother?' He said: 'That he eats and does not carry [away]"," and drinks and does not carry [away].'\""\n\nThis is an unknown (majhūl) chain of narration — no proof is established by such a chain. And al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh is not relied upon (ghayr muḥtāj bihi).\n\nIt has also been narrated from another direction from al-Ḥajjāj"," indicating that it pertains to the one in desperate need (al-muḍṭarr). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19665","(19659) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed him — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us — ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī narrated — from al-Ḥajjāj, from Salīṭ ibn ʿAbdullāh, from Dhuhayl ibn ʿAwf ibn Shammākh, who said: Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, saying: \While we were with the Prophet"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," we saw camels with their udders tied"," gnawing at the branches of trees.\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth. We said: \""Have you considered if we are in need of food and drink?\"" He said: \""Eat and do not carry [away]"," and drink and do not carry [away].\""\n\nSharīk al-Qāḍī also narrated it from al-Ḥajjāj"," but he differed in its chain of narration from those who came before. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19666","(19660) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Abū ʿAbdullāh Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥajarī al-Kūfī narrated to us — my father narrated to us — Sharīk narrated — from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh, from Salīṭ al-Tamīmī, from Abī Salamah, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Prophet"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," was asked about what is permissible for a man from the wealth of his brother. He said: 'He eats until he is full"," if he is hungry"," and drinks until he is quenched.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]\n\nThe Shaykh al-Muzakkī"," Abū al-Qāsim Manṣūr ibn ʿAbd al-Munʿim ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Farāwī"," informed us — Abū al-Maʿālī Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī informed us — the Imām al-Ḥāfiẓ Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Bayhaqī informed us"," and other than one of our shaykhs informed us — from Zāhir ibn Ṭāhir al-Shaḥāmī"," who said: The Imām al-Ḥāfiẓ Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," informed us —"""
"19667","(19661) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated — from Abī Bishr, from ʿAbbād ibn Sharḥabīl, who said: \I arrived in Madīnah while I was stricken with severe hunger. I entered a garden and took a stalk of grain"," ate from it"," and placed some in my garment. The owner of the garden came and struck me and took what was in my garment. We went to the Prophet"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," said: 'You did not teach him when he was ignorant"," nor did you feed him when he was hungry.' He then commanded that I be given half a wasq of barley.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ṭayālisī narrated it.]"""
"19668","(19662) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Abī Khalaf al-Ṣūfī al-Isfarāʾīnī therein narrated to us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Yazdād ibn Masʿūd narrated to us — Muḥammad narrated — from Ayyūb ibn Yaḥyā al-Rāzī, who informed us — Muʿādh ibn Asad al-Khurāsānī informed us — al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā informed us — Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Jubayr narrated from his father, from Rāfiʿ ibn ʿAmr, who said: \I was throwing stones at the date-palms of the Anṣār"," so they seized me and brought me to the Messenger of Allah"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," and said: 'This man is throwing stones at our date-palms.' He said: 'O Rāfiʿ"," why are you throwing stones at their date-palms?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I am hungry.' He said: 'Do not throw stones"," and eat of what falls — may Allah satiate you and quench your thirst.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19669","(19663) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Munādī narrated to us — ʿUmar ibn ʿUthmān, the brother of ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim's father, narrated to us — Abū Tumaylah narrated — from Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Jubayr, the freed slave of al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAmr al-Ghifārī, from his father, who said: \Some of the people of Madīnah complained to the Messenger of Allah"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam"," that a young man from Banī Ghifār was throwing stones at their date-palms. He said: 'Seize him and bring him to me.' And it was Rāfiʿ ibn ʿAmr"," the brother of al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAmr. He mentioned its meaning.\""\n\nThis chain is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ)"," and that has also been narrated through another chain from Rāfiʿ ibn ʿAmr al-Ghifārī. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-ʿIlal al-Tirmidhī 340]"""
"19670","(19664) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us — Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Munādī narrated to us — ʿUmar ibn ʿUthmān, the brother of ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim's father, narrated to us — Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān said: I heard Ibn Abī al-Ḥakam al-Ghifārī saying: My grandmother narrated to me from my father's brother, Rāfiʿ ibn ʿAmr al-Ghifārī, who said: \While I was a young man"," I was throwing stones at the date-palms of the Anṣār. It was said to the Prophet"," ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam: 'Here is a young man who is throwing stones at our date-palms.' He said: 'Seize him and bring him to me.' He said: 'O young man"," why are you throwing stones at their date-palms?' He said: 'I wish to eat.' He said: 'Do not throw stones at their date-palms"," and eat of what is at their bases.'\"" He said: \""And he wiped the head of the young man and said: 'O Allah"," satiate his belly.'\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from Abī Bakr and ʿUthmān"," the two sons of Abī Shaybah"," from Muʿtamir"," with its meaning. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19671","(19665) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī — narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr — narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ — narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq — from his father — from ʿUmayr, the freedman of Abī al-Laḥm, who said:\n\nI came with my masters, intending to emigrate, until when we drew near to Madīnah, they placed me behind them and entered Madīnah. I was then afflicted with severe hunger. He said: A man who was leaving Madīnah passed by me and said: \If only you would enter Madīnah and take from the fruits of its gardens.\"" So I entered one of the gardens of Madīnah and cut down two clusters of dates. The owner of the garden came while the two clusters were with me"," and he took me to the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam). He asked me about my affair"," and I informed him. He said: \""Which of the two is better?\"" I pointed to one of them. He said: \""Take it.\"" And he commanded the owner of the garden to take the other"," and he let me go.\n\nThese reports"," if established"," indicate — along with others — the permissibility of eating from another's property in a state of necessity"," followed by the obligation of compensation. This is derived from the evidences that establish the prohibition of consuming another's property without their goodwill. And success is by Allah.\n\nSome of our companions have cited what we mentioned in the Book of Purification from the ḥadīth of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn"," that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) on a journey"," he and his companions"," and they were afflicted with severe thirst. He sent for the woman who had with her a camel carrying two water-skins"," until she was brought"," and they drank from her water"," while the two water-skins remained as they were"," nay"," they only increased in fullness. Then he commanded his companions"," and they came with provisions from their supplies until they filled her garment for her."""
"19672","(19666) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī — narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd — narrated to us that Abū al-Ashhab — narrated to us from Abū Naḍrah — from Abū Saʿīd (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu), who said:\n\nWe were with the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) on a journey when a man came upon a riding camel, turning it right and left. The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \Whoever has surplus riding mounts"," let him give them to those who have no mount; and whoever has surplus provisions"," let him give them to those who have no provisions.\"" He continued enumerating the categories of wealth until we thought that none of us had any right to surplus.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Shaybān"," from Abū al-Ashhab. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1728]"""
"19673","(19667) Abū Saʿd al-Zāhid — informed us orally — that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sirāj — informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī — narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Kathīr — informed us that Sufyān al-Thawrī — narrated to us from Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir — from Abū Wāʾil — from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu), who said:\n\nThe Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \Feed the hungry"," visit the sick"," and free the captive.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 7353]"""
"19674","(19668) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl — in Baghdād — informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr — narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām — narrated to us that Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān — informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī — narrated to us that Ibn Abī Maryam — narrated to us that al-Firyābī — narrated to us; both saying: Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Bashīr — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Misāwir, who said:\n\nI heard Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) — while he was reproaching Ibn al-Zubayr for miserliness — saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) say: \He is not a believer who eats his fill while his neighbor beside him goes hungry.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Aḥmad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Without the story of reproaching Ibn al-Zubayr]"""
"19675","(19669) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm — narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān — narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam — narrated to us that Shuʿbah — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī — narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd — narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb — narrated to us that Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj — narrated to us from Abū ʿAwn al-Thaqafī — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said:\n\nA group of the Anṣār traveled and ran out of provisions. They came upon a tribe of the Bedouins and asked them for hospitality or for something to buy, but they refused. So they seized them and took from them by force. The Bedouins went to ʿUmar (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu), and the Anṣār feared the consequences. ʿUmar (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) intended to punish them and said: \You withhold from the wayfarer what Allah replenishes in the udders of camels and sheep by night and by day? The wayfarer has a greater right to the water than the one settled upon it.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Sulaymān. In the narration of Yaḥyā ibn Ādam: A group of the Anṣār ran out of provisions and passed by a group of Bedouins. They asked them to sell them something"," but they refused. They asked them for hospitality"," but they refused. So they seized them and milked their animals. ʿUmar said: \""You withhold from the wayfarer what Allah replenishes in the udders of livestock by night and by day?\"" Then he said: \""The wayfarer has a greater right to the water than the one settled upon it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19676","(19670) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm — narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī — narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam — narrated to us that Ibn Wāqid al-Madanī — narrated to us from Kathīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh — from his father — from his grandfather — from ʿUmar, who said:\n\n\The wayfarer has a greater right to the water and the shade than the one settled upon it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19677","(19671) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān — informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān — narrated to us that Yaḥyā, who is Ibn Ādam — narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd — narrated to us from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd and Hishām ibn Ḥassān — from al-Ḥasan, that:\n\nA man came to the people of a water source and asked them for water, but they gave him nothing until he died of thirst. So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) made them pay his blood-money. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"19678","(19672) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib — informed us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ — informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim — narrated to us from al-Ḥasan, with the meaning of this (previous narration). Ismāʿīl said: And al-Ḥasan used to say: \If they refuse to feed him and he fears for his life"," he should fight them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19679","(19673) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī (raḥimahullāh) — informed us that Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī — narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr — narrated to us that Sālim ibn Nūḥ — narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn ʿĀmir — narrated to us from Qatādah — from Anas, that:\n\nThe Prophet of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) commanded the ʿUraynīs to drink the milk and urine of camels. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī and Muslim]"
"19680","(19674) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh — narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb — narrated to us that Abū Salamah — narrated to us that Hammām — narrated to us from Qatādah — from Anas, that:\n\nA group from ʿUraynah came to the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) and said: \We have found Madīnah uncongenial; our bellies have swollen and our limbs have become inflamed.\"" The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) commanded them to join the shepherd of the camels and drink from their milk and urine. So they joined the shepherd and drank from their urine and milk until their bellies and bodies were restored. Then they killed the shepherd and drove away the camels. This reached the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa ālihi wa sallam)"," so he sent in pursuit of them. They were brought"," and he cut off their hands and eyes and gouged out their eyes.\n\nQatādah said: Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated to me that this was before the ḥudūd were revealed.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Salamah"," and Muslim narrated it from Hudbah ibn Khālid"," from Hammām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"19681","(19675) Abū Sa'd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn 'Adiyy narrated to us, Mūsā ibn 'Ubayd Allāh al-Muqri' and Ṭarīf ibn 'Ubayd Allāh both said: 'Alī ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Isrā'īl informed me, from Thawrī, from a shaykh of the people of Qubā', from his father, who was among the Companions of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam), that he asked the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) about drinking the milk of she-donkeys, and he said: \There is no harm in it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""This is not strong.\"" [Weak]"""
"19682","(19676) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr both informed us, saying: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from 'Alqamah ibn Wā'il, from his father, that Ṭāriq ibn Suwayd — or Suwayd ibn Ṭāriq — a man from Ju'fī, asked the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) about wine. He forbade its production, so he said: \It is a remedy.\"" The Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: \""It is not a remedy; rather"," it is a disease.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ghundar"," from Shu'bah"," and he said: \""Indeed Ṭāriq ibn Suwayd asked…\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1984]"""
"19683","(19677) The Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-'Alawī (raḥimahullāh) informed us, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, al-'Abbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī and Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī both said: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated from Mūsā ibn Jubayr, from Nāfi', the mawlā of 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar, from 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) say:\n\n\When Allāh sent Adam ('alayhi al-salām) down to the earth"," the angels said: 'O our Lord! Will You place therein one who will spread corruption therein and shed blood"," while we glorify You with praise and sanctify You?' He said: 'Indeed"," I know what you do not know.' [Al-Baqarah 30]\n\nThey said: 'Our Lord"," we are more obedient to You than the children of Adam.' So Allāh said to the angels: 'Bring Me two angels from among the angels"," so that I may send them down to the earth and see how you act.' They said: 'Our Lord"," Hārūt and Mārūt.' So they were sent down to the earth"," and al-Zahrah (Venus) was presented to them in the form of the most beautiful of human women. She came to them"," and they asked her for herself (i.e."," for sexual intimacy). She said: 'No"," by Allāh"," unless you utter this word of shirk.' They said: 'No"," by Allāh"," we will never associate anything with Allāh.' So she left them.\n\nThen she returned carrying a child. They asked her for herself"," and she said: 'No"," by Allāh"," unless you kill this child.' They said: 'No"," by Allāh"," we will never kill him.' So she left.\n\nThen she returned carrying a cup of wine. They asked her for herself"," and she said: 'No"," by Allāh"," unless you drink this wine.' So they drank and became intoxicated. Then they fell upon her (committing adultery) and killed the child. When they regained consciousness"," the woman said: 'By Allāh"," you did not refuse me anything I asked of you except that you did it when you were intoxicated.' At that point"," they were given the choice between the punishment of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter"," and they chose the punishment of this world.\""\n\nZuhayr ibn Muḥammad is alone in narrating this from Mūsā ibn Jubayr from Nāfi'. And Mūsā ibn 'Uqbah narrated it from Nāfi'"," from Ibn 'Umar"," from Ka'b"," who said: \""The angels mentioned the deeds of the children of Adam…\"" and he narrated part of this story. And this is more likely. [Munkar. al-'Ilal al-Dārquṭnī 2792]"""
"19684","(19678) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Sa'dān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from 'Amr — who is ibn Dīnār — from Yaḥyā ibn Ja'dah, who said: 'Uthmān ibn 'Affān (raḍiyallāhu 'anhu) said:\n\n\Beware of wine"," for it is the key to every evil. A man was brought and it was said to him: 'Either burn this book"," or kill this child"," or commit adultery with this woman"," or drink this cup"," or prostrate to this cross.' He saw nothing easier among these matters than drinking the cup. So when he drank it"," he prostrated to the cross"," killed the child"," committed adultery with the woman"," and burned the book.\""\n\nWe have also narrated it in the Book of Drinks from the ḥadīth of 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith"," from 'Uthmān ibn 'Affān (raḍiyallāhu 'anhu). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited under no. 8/17339/17340]"""
"19685","(19679) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Ḥasan ibn Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Abū Ma'mar al-Qaṭī'ī narrated to us, Jarīr narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī, from Ḥassān ibn Mukhāriq, from Umm Salamah, who said:\n\n\I prepared nabīdh (fermented drink) in a vessel. The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) entered while it was boiling. He said: 'What is this?' I said: 'A daughter of mine is unwell"," so I prepared this for her.' The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said: 'Indeed"," Allāh has not placed your cure in that which He has forbidden for you.'\""\n\nKhālid al-Wāsiṭī also narrated it from al-Shaybānī"," from Ḥassān"," that Umm Salamah said: \""The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) entered upon me…\"" and he mentioned its meaning. [Weak]"""
"19686","(19680) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr both informed us, saying: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from al-A'mash, from Ḥabīb ibn Ḥassān, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, who said:\n\n\A man among us complained of his stomach"," and yellow fluid (i.e."," jaundice) was found in it. He was brought to 'Abd Allāh"," and he said: 'I have been prescribed an intoxicant (sakar) for my stomach ailment.' 'Abd Allāh said: 'Indeed"," Allāh has not placed your cure in that which He has forbidden for you.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19687","(19681) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn 'Ubādah al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ismā'īl ibn 'Ayyāsh narrated from Tha'labah ibn Muslim, from Abī 'Imrān al-Anṣārī, from Umm al-Dardā', from Abī al-Dardā', who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) said:\n\n\Indeed"," Allāh"," the Mighty and Majestic"," sent down the disease and the cure"," and He made for every disease a cure. So seek treatment"," but do not seek treatment with that which is forbidden.\"" [Weak]"""
"19688","(19682) And Abū 'Alī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Hārūn ibn 'Abd Allāh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated from Mujāhid, from Abī Hurayrah, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) forbade foul (khabīth) medicine.\""\n\nThese two aḥādīth"," if they are authentic"," are interpreted as referring to the prohibition of treating with intoxicants"," or as referring to the prohibition of treating with anything forbidden in a situation other than one of dire necessity"," so as to reconcile between them and the ḥadīth of the 'Uraynīs. And Allāh knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Sijistānī 3870]"""
"19689","(19683) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both informed us, saying: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, 'Amr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that 'Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'īd narrated to him that he heard Nāfi' saying:\n\n\Whenever Ibn 'Umar called a physician to treat a member of his household"," he stipulated upon him that he should not treat with anything that Allāh"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has forbidden.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19690","(19684) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Mūsā al-Balkhī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from 'Amr ibn Manṣūr, from al-Sha'bī, from Ibn 'Umar (raḍiyallāhu 'anhumā), who said:\n\n\A piece of cheese was brought to the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa ālihi wa sallam) during the expedition of Tabūk. He called for a knife"," pronounced the name of Allāh"," and cut it.\"" [Weak. Abū Dāwūd 3819–54]"""
"19691","(19685) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us that 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us that Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us that Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us that Sharik narrated from Jabir from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) conquered Makkah, he saw cheese and said: \What is this?\"" It was said: \""This is a food prepared in the land of the non-Arabs.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \""Cut it with a knife"," mention the name of Allah"," and eat.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19692","(19686) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us that Abu 'Amr ibn Matar and Abu al-Hasan al-Sarraj both said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Marwazi narrated to us that 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us that Shu'bah narrated from Abu Ishaq who said: I heard Qurazah narrating from Kathir ibn Shahab who said: I asked 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) about cheese. He said: \Cheese is made from milk and fat"," so eat it"," mention the name of Allah over it"," and let not the enemies of Allah deceive you.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19693","(19687) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us that Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us that Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us that Muslim narrated from Habbah from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: \When you intend to eat cheese"," place the knife in it"," mention the name of Allah"," and eat.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated through another chain from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and also from Salman al-Farisi. [Da'if]"""
"19694","(19688) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both informed us that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated from his father from Abu Bakr, meaning ibn al-Munkadir, who said: A woman from among us asked 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family), about eating cheese. 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \If you do not wish to eat it"," then give it to me and I will eat it.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19695","(19689) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-'Adl informed us that Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us that 'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us that my father narrated to us that Shu'bah narrated from Abu Ishaq from Tamlik from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family), that she said regarding cheese: \Eat it and mention the name of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19696","(19690) The noble Abu al-Fath al-'Umari informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman al-Shurayhi narrated to us that Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi narrated to us that 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd informed us that Shu'bah narrated from a man from Banu 'Uqayl from his paternal uncle who said: A letter of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was read to us: \Eat cheese that has been made by the People of the Book.\"" The Sheikh said: He is Ibrahim al-'Uqayli"," and his paternal uncle is Thawr ibn Qudamah"," from whom al-Thawri narrated it. [Da'if]"""
"19697","(19691) Abu Bakr al-Ardastani informed us that Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us that Sufyan al-Jawhari narrated to us that 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali narrated to us that 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us that Sufyan narrated to me that Ibrahim al-'Uqayli narrated to me that my paternal uncle Thawr ibn Qudamah said: A letter of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us: \Do not eat cheese except that which has been made by the People of the Book.\"" [Da'if. Preferring the previous narration.]"""
"19698","(19692) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub dictated in the year thirty-seven that Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from Sufyan and Shu'bah from Mansur from 'Ubayd ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Qays ibn Sakan who said: 'Abdullah, meaning ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), said: \Eat cheese that has been made by the Muslims and the People of the Book.\"" [Hasan]"""
"19699","(19693) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz informed us that 'Ali ibn 'Abbas informed us that Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us that Shu'bah narrated from Qatadah from 'Ali al-Bariqi that he asked Ibn 'Umar about cheese. He said: \Eat that which has been made by the Muslims and the People of the Book.\""\n\nAnd a similar narration has been transmitted from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas and Anas ibn Malik.\n\nThis is because the young goats are slaughtered and the rennet is extracted from them with which cheese is made. If it comes from the slaughter of the Magus or the idolaters"," it is not permissible. Similarly"," if the young goat dies and the rennet is extracted from it"," it is not permissible. [Hasan]"""
"19700","(19694) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us that Abu 'Uthman al-Basri informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us that Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us that Sufyan narrated from Jabalah ibn Suhaym who said: Ibn 'Umar was asked about cheese and ghee. He said: \Mention the name and eat.\"" It was said: \""What if there is a carcass in it?\"" He said: \""If you know that there is a carcass in it"," then do not eat it.\""\n\n(Q) Some of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) would not ask about it"," giving precedence to the presumption of purity. We have received this from Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) and others. And some of them would ask about it as a precaution. We have received from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari that he said: \""That I be delayed from this palace is more beloved to me than that I eat cheese about which I do not ask.\"" And from al-Hasan al-Basri who said: \""The Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) would ask about cheese but would not ask about ghee.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19701","(19695) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, who is al-Aṣamm, informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Khalīl ibn Murrah informed me, from Abān ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \We used to eat cheese during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and after that"," and we would not ask about it. And Anas would not eat [cheese] except that which was made by the Muslims and the People of the Book.\"" Abān ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh is abandoned (matrūk). [Weak]"""
"19702","(19696) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās, who is al-Aṣamm, narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us: Abū Khaythamah narrated to us: ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated to us, from Kathīr ibn Jumḥān, who said: \I said"," 'O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān' — meaning Ibn ʿUmar — or someone else said: 'I passed by a dead hen and stepped upon it"," and an egg came out of its rear. May I eat it?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," I passed by a dead hen and pressed upon it"," and an egg came out of its rear"," and I hatched it and it produced a chick. May I eat it?' He said: 'From whom are you?' He said: 'I said: I am from the people of Iraq.'\"" [Weak]"""
"19703","(19697) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah al-Bashīrī informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Harawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Two dead animals and two types of blood have been made lawful for us. As for the two dead animals"," they are locusts and fish (sea creatures). As for the two types of blood"," they are the spleen and the liver.'\"" ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and his brothers narrated it from their father"," and others narrated it as a stopped (mawqūf) report from Ibn ʿUmar"," and that is the correct view. [Denounced (Munkar); see no. 1196]"""
"19704","(19698) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn al-Baghdādī al-Harawī informed us through it: Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us: Bishr ibn Ādam narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I used to eat the spleen"," not out of any need for it"," but so that my household would know that there is nothing wrong with it.\"" [Authentic]"""
"19705","(19699) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muʿādh narrated to us: Bishr narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ʿIkrimah, who said: \A man asked Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," saying: 'May I eat the spleen?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Most of it is blood.' He said: 'Only the flowing blood (al-dam al-masfūḥ) is forbidden.'\"" [Weak]"""
"19706","(19700) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh informed me: Yazīd ibn al-Haytham informed me that Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth narrated to them: al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us, from Sufyān, from al-Awzāʿī, from Wāṣil ibn Abī Jamīl, from Mujāhid, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to dislike seven things from the sheep: blood"," the gallbladder"," the testicles"," the two kidneys"," the urinary bladder"," the lymph glands"," and the bladder.\"" He said: \""And the front portion of the sheep was most beloved to him (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" This is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ). [Weak]"""
"19707","(19701) ʿUmar ibn Mūsā ibn Wajīh, who is weak, narrated it from Wāṣil ibn Abī Jamīl, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to dislike eating seven things from the sheep, and he mentioned the hadith. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Waqqār ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Raqqī narrated to us: Ayyūb al-Wazzān narrated to us: Fihr ibn Bashīr narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Mūsā narrated it, and he mentioned it as a connected (mawṣūl) narration, but its being connected is not authentic. Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī said, as it reached me from him: \Blood is forbidden by consensus"," and the majority of the things mentioned along with it are disliked (makrūh) but not forbidden.\"" [Weak]"""
"19708","(19702) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: al-Thawrī informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-Muthannā informed us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that Isrāʾīl (Yaʿqūb, peace be upon him) was afflicted with the sciatica (ʿirq al-nasā), and he would spend the night crying out in pain. He said: \If Allah heals me"," I will never eat meat containing tendons.\"" So the Jews made it unlawful for themselves"," and the verse was revealed: {All food was lawful to the Children of Israel"," except what Israel had made unlawful for himself before the Torah was revealed. Say"," \""Bring the Torah and recite it"," if you are truthful\""} [Āl ʿImrān 93]"," meaning that this was before the Torah. ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: Sufyān said: \""Zuqāʾan means 'crying out in pain (ṣiyāḥ).'\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," said: {And for the wrongdoing of the Jews"," We made unlawful for them certain good foods which had been lawful for them} [al-Nisāʾ 160]. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And they — and Allah knows best — are good foods that had been made lawful for them.\"" And He said: {And upon the Jews We forbade every animal with claws; and of the cattle and sheep We forbade them their fats"," except what adheres to their backs"," or the entrails"," or what is mixed with bone} [al-Anʿām 146]. Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""Al-ḥawāyā (the entrails) are what encloses food and drink in the belly.\"" [Weak]"""
"19709","(19703) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding His words {every animal with claws} [al-Anʿām 146]: he said: \It refers to the camel and the ostrich.\"" And regarding His words {except what adheres to their backs} [al-Anʿām 146]: \""It means the fat attached to the back"," or the entrails"," which is the al-mabʿar (the cud receptacle).\"" Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated something similar from Mujāhid"," from his own words"," regarding the interpretation of \""every animal with claws\"" and \""the entrails.\"" And it has previously been established in the authentic hadith from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and others from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: \""May Allah curse the Jews; fats were made unlawful for them"," so they melted them down and sold them and consumed their prices.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""What Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," made unlawful upon the Children of Israel — the Jews specifically"," and others generally — remained forbidden from the time He made it so"," until Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," sent Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and commanded faith in him"," and informed His creation that his religion is Islam"," by which He abrogated every religion before it. He said: {Indeed"," the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam} [Āl ʿImrān 19]. And He revealed regarding the People of the Book among the polytheists: {Say"," \""O People of the Book"," come to a word that is equitable between us and between you\""} [Āl ʿImrān 164]"," the verse. And He commanded fighting them until they pay the jizyah if they do not embrace Islam. And He revealed regarding them: {Those who follow the Messenger"," the unlettered Prophet"," whom they find written in their possession in the Torah and the Gospel. He commands them to what is right and forbids them from what is wrong. He makes lawful for them the good things and makes unlawful for them the impure things. And he relieves them of their burden and the shackles that were upon them} [al-Aʿrāf 157].\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And it is said — and Allah knows best — that 'their burden' (awzārahum) refers to what they were prevented from due to their innovations before the religion of Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was legislated.\"" [Weak]"""
"19710","(19704) Abū Zakariyyā informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \It is what Allah took from them in the covenant regarding what He had made unlawful for them — that He would remove that from them.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""There has remained no rational creation — neither jinn nor human — since Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," sent Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him)"," to whom his call has reached"," except that the proof of Allah has been established upon him by following his religion. And it has become obligatory upon every one of them to regard as forbidden what Allah has declared forbidden upon the tongue of His Prophet"," and to regard as lawful what He has declared lawful upon the tongue of Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" [Weak]"""
"19711","(19705) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed me; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Abū Muʿāwiya —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiya narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Sufyān, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nAn-Nuʿmān ibn Qawqal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," tell me — if I perform the obligatory prayers"," regard the ḥarām as ḥarām and the ḥalāl as ḥalāl"," shall I enter Paradise?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: \""Yes.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 15]"""
"19712","(19706) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī informed us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Ḥumayd narrated from Abī al-Malīḥ, from Maʿqil ibn Yasār (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: \Act upon the Qurʾān; regard its ḥalāl as ḥalāl and its ḥarām as ḥarām. Follow its guidance and do not reject anything from it. Whatever is ambiguous to you of it"," refer it back to Allah and to those of knowledge after me"," as they will inform you. Believe in the Torah"," the Gospel"," the Psalms"," and whatever the Prophets were given from their Lord. Let the Qurʾān and the clarity therein suffice you"," for it is an intercessor whose intercession will be accepted and a truthful confirmor. Beware! Every verse shall have a light on the Day of Resurrection. I have been given Sūrat al-Baqarah from the First Remembrance"," and I have been given Ṭāhā"," the Ṭawāsīn"," and the Ḥawāmīm from the Tablets of Mūsā"," and I have been given the Opening of the Book from beneath the Throne.\""\n\n(Ḥ) ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Ḥumayd — scholars have spoken about him. Al-Shāfiʿī said: Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," made the food of the People of the Book ḥalāl"," and the exegetes understood this to include their slaughtered animals without exception. However"," the slaughter of a Person of the Book is not permissible if there is anything in the slaughter that is forbidden upon every Muslim — that which was forbidden upon the People of the Book before Muḥammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19713","(19707) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us; Abū al-Aḥraz Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Jamīl al-Ṭūsī informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Marwazī al-Ḥarbī narrated to us; Saʿdawayh narrated to us; Sulaymān — that is, ibn al-Mughīra — narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nOn the day of Khaybar, a bag of fat was lowered down. I embraced it and said, \I shall not give anyone anything from it.\"" I turned around and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family)"," smiling.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī and Muslim]"""
"19714","(19708) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; al-Faḍl ibn Ḥubāb informed me; Abū al-Walīd informed us; Shuʿbah narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal, who said:\n\nA bag of fat was lowered down on the day of Khaybar. I clung to it and said, \This is mine; I shall not give anyone anything from it.\"" I turned around and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family)"," smiling"," and I felt shy before him.\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs as previously mentioned. In this hadith there is evidence that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) permitted the fat from the slaughter of the People of the Book"," and in that there is evidence supporting the statement of al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him). [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously cited]"""
"19715","(19709) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; my father and Shuʿbayh said: al-Layth informed us from Ibn al-Hād, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nI heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) say: \I saw ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir al-Khuzāʿī dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to set free the Sāʾibah animals.\""\n\nSaʿīd said: \""The Sāʾibah is the animal that is set free so that nothing is carried upon it. The Baḥīrah is the animal whose milk is withheld for the idols"," so no one milks it. The Waṣīlah is the she-camel that gives birth first to a female in the first litter of camels"," and then gives birth again to a female. They would set it free for the idols"," calling it the Waṣīlah"," if one was joined to the other. And the Ḥām is the male camel that impregnates ten camels. When he had finished his breeding"," they would cut his nose for the idols and spare him from carrying anything"," and they called him the Ḥām.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān and others from Ibn Shihāb. Al-Bukhārī said: Ibn al-Hād also narrated it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19716","(19710) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdad by dictation and recitation; Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ al-Jushamī, from his father, who said:\n\nThe Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) saw me wearing tattered garments. He said: \Do you have any wealth?\"" He said: \""I said: 'Yes.'\"" He said: \""What kind of wealth?\"" He said: \""I said: 'Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has given me from sheep and camels.'\"" He said: \""Then let the blessing of Allah and His generosity be visible upon you.\"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: \""Do your camels give birth with their ears intact?\"" He said: \""And do they give birth except in that manner?\"" He had not yet accepted Islam at that time. He said: \""Perhaps you take your blade and cut the ear of some of them and say: 'This is a Baḥīrah","' and tear the ear of another and say: 'This is a Ṣuram.'\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Do not do that"," for everything that Allah has given you is ḥalāl. And the blade of Allah is sharper"," and the Hand of Allah is stronger.\"" He said: \""O Muḥammad"," tell me — if I pass by a man and he does not host me and does not offer me hospitality"," and then he later comes to me"," should I repay him or should I host him?\"" He said: \""Rather"," host him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19717","(19711) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the words of the Most High: \And they assign to Allah a share of what He has produced of crops and livestock"," and they say: 'This is for Allah' — by their assertion — 'and this is for our partners'\"" [al-Anʿām 136].\n\nHe said: \""They assigned a share for Allah from their fruits and their wealth"," and a share for the Shayṭān and the idols. If something fell from the fruit they had designated for Allah into the share of the Shayṭān"," they would leave it. And if something fell from what they had designated for the Shayṭān into the share of Allah"," they would pick it up"," preserve it"," and return it to the share of the Shayṭān. And so it was with the watering of water. As for what they designated for the Shayṭān from livestock"," that is in the words of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: 'Allah has not made the Baḥīrah"," nor the Sāʾibah"," nor the Waṣīlah"," nor the Ḥām'\"" [al-Anʿām 136].\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And it is said that regarding them was revealed: 'Say: Bring forward your witnesses who testify that Allah has forbidden this. So if they testify"," do not testify with them'\"" [al-Anʿām 150]. He refuted them regarding what they had forbidden upon themselves"," and He informed them that He had not forbidden it upon them. He mentioned the rest of the verses that were revealed concerning that matter. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19718","(19712) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq and ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad said: Hannād ibn al-Sarī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ narrated to us. He said: I heard Rabīʿah ibn Yazīd al-Dimashqī say: Abū Idrīs ʿĀʾidhullāh informed me. He said: I heard Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī (may Allah be pleased with him) say:\n\nI came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," we are in a land of a People of the Book — we eat from their vessels — and a land of game. I hunt with my bow and I hunt with my trained dog and with my dog that is not trained. Tell me"," what is permissible for us from that?\""\n\nHe said: \""As for what you mentioned — that you are in a land of a People of the Book and eat from their vessels — if you find other than their vessels"," do not eat from them. And if you do not find any"," then wash them and eat from them. As for what you mentioned — that you are in a land of game — whatever you strike with your bow"," mention the name of Allah and eat. And whatever you catch with your trained dog"," mention the name of Allah and eat. And whatever you catch with your dog that is not trained"," if you reach it while it is still alive and slaughter it"," then eat.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hannād ibn al-Sarī"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another chain from Ibn al-Mubārak. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19719","(19713) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dimashqī — his nickname being Duḥaym — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir narrated from ʿUmayr ibn Hānʾ, who informed him from Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nI came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I shoot with my bow. Some of the game I catch and slaughter"," and some I do not catch. What is permissible for me and what is forbidden upon me? We are in a land of the People of the Book — they eat pork in their vessels and drink wine in them. So should we eat and drink from them?\""\n\nHe said: \""Whatever your bow returns to you and you have mentioned the name of Allah"," eat. And if you find independence from the vessels of the People of the Book"," do not eat from them. And if you do not find independence from them"," then wash them vigorously with water"," and then eat from them.\""\n\nIn this there is evidence that the command to wash was given only when their impurity was known. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19720","(19714) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā and Ismāʿīl narrated from Burd ibn Sinān, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nWe used to go on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family), and we would acquire the vessels and drinking containers of the polytheists. We would make use of them, and that was not considered blameworthy upon us. [Ḥasan]"
"19721","(19715) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us — Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us — Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us — Sufyān, from Burd, from ʤābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We used to go on military expeditions and eat from the vessels of the polytheists and drink from their water-skins.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said in the narration of Ḥarmalah: A Jewish woman presented the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with a roasted sheep in which she had poisoned its arm. He (peace and blessings be upon him) ate from it, as did others. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The morsel that I ate from the sheep has continued to cause me pain until this moment"," when my aorta has been severed.\"" [Hasan. It was mentioned before.]"""
"19722","(19716) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabīb ibn ʿArabī narrated to us — Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us — Shuʿbah, from Hishām ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), that a Jewish woman brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a poisoned sheep, and he ate from it. She was then brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he asked her about that. She said: \I intended to kill you.\"" He said: \""Allah would not have given you power over that\"" — or he said"," \""over me.\"" They said: \""Shall we not kill him?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""I continued to recognize its effect in the throat of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabīb"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from al-Ḥajabī from Khālid. And we narrated the ḥadīth of Jābir and others on this subject in the book of Injuries (al-Jirāḥ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19723","(19717) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ashqar narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Mūsā al-Marwarrūdhī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us — ʿAnbasah narrated to us — Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUrwah said that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say during his illness in which he passed away: \O ʿĀʾishah"," I still feel pain from the food that I ate at Khaybar"," and this is the time when my aorta has been severed from that poison.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""And Yūnus said…\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19724","(19718) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥurḍī al-Naysābūrī narrated to us — Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Harawī al-Raffāʾ narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dimashqī, Abū Ayyūb, narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Marwān, who was regarded as trustworthy, a Damascene, narrated to us — from Ibn Jurayj, from ʤābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with both of them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever becomes engrossed in eating clay has indeed aided himself (towards his own destruction).\""\n\nʿAbd Allāh ibn Marwān is unknown (majhūl). [Weak.]"""
"19725","(19719) Its meaning was narrated through another chain of unknown narrators. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us — Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī Maʿshar narrated to us — al-Musayyab ibn Wāḍiḥ narrated to us — Baqiyyah, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Mihrān, from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever eats clay is as though he has aided in killing himself.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: \""I do not know anyone other than this ʿAbd al-Malik who narrated it from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ"," and he is unknown (majhūl).\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""Even if this were authentic"," it would not indicate prohibition; rather"," it indicates the dislike (karāhah) of excessive consumption of it. Excessive consumption of it or of anything else that harms the body is forbidden. And Allah knows best.\"" [Weak. See what the author said.]"""
"19726","(19720) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Jarrāḥī in Marw narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Shāsawayh narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Sukkariyy narrated to us — Wahb ibn Zamʿah narrated to us — Sufyān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, who said: It was mentioned to ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn al-Mubārak, that eating clay is ḥarām, and he rejected it and said: \Had I known that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said it"," I would have accepted it with my head"," my eyes"," my hearing"," and my obedience.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. For Ibn al-Mubārak.]"""
"19727","(19721) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — Aṣbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb, from Mālik, who said: He was asked about the sale of clay that people eat, and he said: \I do not like that one should sell what harms people in their religion and their worldly life.\"" Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: **\""They ask you what is lawful for them. Say: Lawful for you are the good things (al-ṭayyibāt)\""** [Al-Māʾidah: 4]. Mālik said: \""And I think the market authority should prevent them from selling it and forbid it.\"" Mālik also said: \""It is also from the category of foolishness (safah).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik.]"""
"19728","(19722) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdad — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Bishr ibn Mūsā, Abū ʿAlī, narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — from Sufyān, narrated to us — Sulaymān, from Abū ʿUthmān, from Salmān (may Allah be pleased with him), and he (the narrator) thought he raised it (to the Prophet), who said: \Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has made lawful what is lawful and forbidden what is forbidden. So what He has made lawful is lawful"," and what He has forbidden is forbidden"," and what He has remained silent about is pardon (forgiven).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ as a mawqūf narration.]"""
"19729","(19723) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī narrated to us — Abū Maʿmar narrated to us — Sayf ibn Hārūn, who was among the best of Allah's creation, one of the most devout of people, and whom Sufyān al-Thawrī used to hold in great esteem, and he was above his brother — narrated to us — Sulaymān al-Taymī, from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, from Salmān al-Fārisī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about clarified butter, cheese, and the flesh of the wild ass. He said: \The lawful is that which Allah has made lawful in His Book"," and the unlawful is that which Allah has made unlawful in His Book"," and that about which He has remained silent is pardon (forgiven).\""\n\nAnd we narrated this previously through another chain from Salmān as a marfūʿ narration. And it was narrated on this subject from Ibn ʿAbbās and Abū al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with them all). [Ṣaḥīḥ. As a mawqūf narration"," it was mentioned before.]"""
"19730","(19724) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Shaybānī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim al-Ghifārī narrated to us — Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us — ʿĀṣim ibn Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah, from his father, from Abū al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with him), who raised the ḥadīth (to the Prophet), saying: \What Allah has made lawful in His Book is lawful"," and what He has forbidden is unlawful"," and what He has remained silent about is pardon (ʿāfiyah). So accept from Allah His pardon"," for Allah was never forgetful.\"" Then he recited this verse: **\""And your Lord is never forgetful\""** [Maryam: 64]."""
"19731","(19725) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us from Dāwūd — who is ibn Abī Hind — from Makḥūl, from Abū Thaʿlabah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Indeed"," Allah has prescribed obligations"," so do not neglect them; He has set boundaries"," so do not transgress them; He has prohibited certain things"," so do not violate them; and He has remained silent regarding certain things as a concession for you"," not out of forgetfulness"," so do not seek them out.\"" This is a mawqūf narration. [Munkar. Al-Dāraquṭnī said in al-ʿIlal"," 1170.]"""
"19732","(19726) Our shaykh Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me of it in al-Mustadrak, through an ijāzah that was not read back to him, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated to us from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from Makḥūl, from Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said…\"" and he mentioned it with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the commentary preceding it.]"""
"19733","(19727) Abū al-Qāsim Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ṣaqr narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to me, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Khālid al-Ājurrī narrated to me. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me, Abū Yaʿlá narrated to us, both saying: Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me from Abū ʿAlī Thumāmah ibn Shufayy, who heard ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was upon the pulpit saying: {'And prepare against them whatever you are able of power' [al-Anfāl:60] — verily"," power is archery! Verily"," power is archery! Verily"," power is archery!}\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1917.]"""
"19734","(19728) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me from Abū ʿAlī al-Hamdānī, who heard ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Lands will be conquered for you"," and Allah will spare you the burden"," so let none of you be negligent with his arrows.'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1918.]"""
"19735","(19729) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn Milḥān narrated to us, Yaḥyā — who is ibn Bukayr — narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, al-Ḥārith ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to me, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shumāsah informed me that Faqīm al-Lakhmī said to ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir: \You alternate between these two targets"," and you are an elderly man for whom that is difficult.\"" ʿUqbah said: \""Had it not been for words I heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," I would never have assisted him in it.\"" Al-Ḥārith said: Ibn Shumāsah said"," \""And what is that?\"" He said: \""Whoever learns archery and then abandons it is not of us"," or he has disobeyed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1919.]"""
"19736","(19730) Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ from al-Layth, except that he said: Al-Ḥārith said, \I said to Ibn Shumāsah"," 'And what is that?' He said: 'Whoever learns archery and then abandons it is not of us"," or he has disobeyed.'\"" Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me of it"," Abū al-Walīd informed me"," al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us"," Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ narrated to us"," al-Layth narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the narration preceding it.]"""
"19737","(19731) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd al-Bayrūtī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir narrated to us, Abū Salām al-Aswad narrated to us, from Khālid ibn Zayd, who said: \I was a man who practiced archery"," and I would shoot with ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir. One day he passed by me and said"," 'O Khālid"," come out with us to shoot.' I delayed in responding to him"," so he said"," 'O Khālid"," come"," I shall narrate to you what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) narrated to me","' or he said"," 'I shall tell you as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," will admit three persons into Paradise by virtue of a single arrow: its maker"," who intends goodness in its manufacture; the one who hands it to the archer; and the one who shoots it. Shoot and ride"," and I love for you to shoot more than to ride. There are only three things that constitute permissible diversion: a man's training of his horse"," his playful interaction with his wife"," and his shooting with his arrows from his bow. And whoever learns archery and then abandons it has been ungrateful for the blessing.'\"" Ibn al-Mubārak"," al-Walīd ibn Muslim"," and al-Walīd ibn Mazīd also narrated it from Ibn Jābir. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"19738","(19732) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Hishām narrated to us, from Yaḥyā — who is ibn Abī Kathīr — from Abū Salām, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd al-Azraq, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: 'Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," will admit three persons into Paradise by virtue of a single arrow: its maker"," who intends goodness in its manufacture; the one who shoots it; and the one who assists with it.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"19739","(19733) Through this same chain of narration from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Shoot and ride"," and I love for you to shoot more than to ride. Every form of diversion in which a man engages is vain"," except a man's shooting with his bow"," his training of his horse"," or his playful interaction with his wife"," for these are of the truth. And whoever abandons archery after having learned it has disbelieved in that which he learned.'\"" In my copy it is \""Ibn Yazīd","\"" while another authority said \""ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. See the narration preceding it.]"""
"19740","(19734) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Khalaf ibn ʿAmr al-ʿUkburī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to me, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sālim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUwaym ibn Sāʿidah narrated to me from his father, from his grandfather, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw a man with a Persian bow"," so he said"," 'Cast it aside.' Then he pointed to the Arab bow and said"," 'With this and with spears of qanā"," Allah will grant you victory over the lands and will grant you victory over your enemies.'\"" Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah is the sole narrator of this"," and there is a break (inqiṭāʿ) in the chain"," as ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUwaym did not have companionship (ṣuḥbah). [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"19741","(19735) It was narrated in this chain, as Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Hamid al-Muqri' informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn Salim ibn 'Utbah ibn 'Uwaym ibn Sa'idah narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw a Persian bow and said: \Cursed"," cursed is the one who carries it. Hold fast to this\"" — and he pointed to the Arab bow — \""and to spears of qana (bamboo shafts)"," for through these Allah will establish you in the lands and grant you victory over your enemies.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari said: 'Utbah ibn 'Uwaym — his hadith is not authentic. [Weak. Previously mentioned.]"""
"19742","(19736) Abu Bakr ibn Furak, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated to us, informing us that 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Ash'ath ibn Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Busr narrated to us, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turbaned me on the Day of Ghadir Khumm with a turban"," letting its end hang behind me"," and then said: 'Indeed"," Allah supported me on the days of Badr and Hunayn with angels wearing this type of turban.' And he said: 'Indeed"," the turban is a barrier between disbelief and faith.' And he saw a man shooting with a Persian bow and said: 'Shoot with it.' Then he looked at an Arab bow and said: 'Hold fast to this and the like of it"," and to spears of qana (bamboo shafts)"," for through these Allah will establish you in the lands and grant you aid in victory.'\""\n\nAl-Ash'ath is Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman"," and he is not strong. (T) Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash contradicted him"," narrating this from 'Abdullah ibn Busr"," from 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn 'Adi al-Bahrani"," from his brother 'Abd al-A'la"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," with a disconnected chain. And 'Abdullah ibn Busr is not strong"," as stated by Abu Dawud al-Sijistani and others.\n\n[Weak. Previously mentioned.]"""
"19743","(19737) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Abu 'Abdillah al-Bushanjiyy narrated to us, and Abu 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn 'A'ishah said: \The scholars of hadith stated that the prohibition of the Persian bow was because when its string breaks"," its owner cannot benefit from it"," whereas when the string of the Arab bow breaks"," it becomes a staff with which he can walk. And they had wooden spears"," so when a man was struck with one"," the one struck would seize it and break it. So he (the Prophet ﷺ) commanded them to use spears of qana (bamboo shafts)"," so that when a man struck with one and the one struck seized it"," it would bend and not break. These were brought from al-Bahrayn.\""\n\n[Hasan]"""
"19744","(19738) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahmuyah al-'Askariyy narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisiyy narrated to us, Abu Adam ibn Iyas narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated from al-Ahwal, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdiyy, who said: \The letter of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us while we were with 'Utbah ibn Farqad in Adharbayjan. He wrote: 'After greetings: Wear the waist-wrap"," put on sandals"," drape the cloak"," and discard the light shoes and trousers. Clothe yourselves in the garment of your father Isma'il. Beware of luxury and the attire of the non-Arabs. Hold fast to the sun"," for it is the bathhouse of the Arabs. Be manly"," be rugged"," be hopeful"," cut the knees (of your garments short)"," leap upon horses in leaping"," shoot at targets"," and walk between them.' And he mentioned the rest of the hadith.\""\n\n[Sahih]"""
"19745","(19739) It was narrated to us in the book of al-Fara'id from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that he wrote to Abu 'Ubaydah (may Allah be pleased with him): \Teach your boys swimming and teach your fighters archery.\"" And they were practicing between targets when a stray arrow came and struck a boy"," killing him. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith.\n\nIt was narrated to us by 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan"," who informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid narrated to us"," Muhammad ibn Rabbah al-Bazzaz narrated to us"," Abu Nu'aym narrated to us"," Sufyan ibn 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn 'Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah narrated from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn 'Abbad ibn Hunayf"," from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf"," who said: \""'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Abu 'Ubaydah","\"" and he mentioned it.\n\n[Hasan for other reasons. Previously mentioned under no. 6/12207.]"""
"19746","(19740) Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Sa'd al-Harawiyy, who came to us, informed us that Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Haririyy narrated to us in Baghdad, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Baghandyy narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Ma'bad al-Harraniyy narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \My love is obligatory upon the one who strives between the two targets with my bow — not with the bow of Kisra (the Persian emperor).\"""""
"19747","(19741) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Farqad al-Firyabiyy narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Yahya, Abu al-Asbagh, narrated to us, Muhammad — meaning Ibn Salamah al-Jazariyy — narrated from Abu 'Abd ar-Rahim, from 'Abd al-Wahhab — meaning Ibn Bukht — from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, who said: \I saw Jabir ibn 'Abdillah and Jabir ibn 'Umayr al-Ansariyyayn (may Allah be pleased with both of them) practicing archery. One of them grew weary and sat down"," so his companion said to him: 'Have you sat down? Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""Everything that is not from the remembrance of Allah is heedlessness and idle amusement"," except four things: a man's walking between the two targets"," his training of his horse"," his learning of swimming"," and his playful interaction with his family.\""'\""\n\nIshaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzaliyy followed him in narrating from Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Jazariyy. [Hasan]"""
"19748","(19742) Abu al-Qasim 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sarraj narrated to us by dictation, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus al-Tara'ifiyy informed us, 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yazid ibn 'Abd Rabbih narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated from 'Isa ibn Ibrahim, from al-Zuhriyy, from Abu Sulayman, the freed slave of Abu Rafi', from Abu Rafi', who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," does the child have rights over us just as we have rights over them?' He said: 'Yes. The right of the child over the parent is that he teach him writing"," swimming"," and archery"," and that he leave him a good inheritance.'\""\n\nThis hadith is weak. 'Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Hashimiyy is among the shaykhs of Baqiyyah; he is denounced in hadith. Yahya ibn Ma'in and al-Bukhari and others declared him weak. [Hasan]"""
"19749","(19743) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad, Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us, Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated — and Shabib ibn Ghurqadah heard 'Urwah say: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — or I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.'\""\n\nSufyan said: \""Mujalid added in it"," from al-Sha'bi"," from 'Urwah al-Bariqiyy: 'And reward and booty.'\""\n\n[Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"19750","(19744) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Shayban narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Shabib ibn Ghurqadah, from 'Urwah al-Bariqiyy.\n\nAnd from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Urwah al-Bariqiyy, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) said","\"" and he mentioned something similar to it.\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in the Sahih from the hadith of Sufyan from Shabib"," as previously mentioned."""
"19751","(19745) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us — from what he read to Mālik — from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Sammān, from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Horses are of three types: for one man they are a reward"," for another a shield"," and upon another a burden. As for the one that is a reward: a man ties it for the sake of Allah"," keeping it long-reined in a meadow or garden. Whatever it eats from that meadow or garden within the length of its rope"," it will be counted as good deeds for him. Even if it breaks its rope and gallops over one or two elevated places"," its tracks and its dung will be good deeds for him. And if it passes by a river and drinks from it"," though he did not intend to water it"," that too will be good deeds for him. And a man ties it out of self-sufficiency"," chastity"," and as a means of covering himself"," and he does not neglect the right of Allah regarding its back or its neck — it is for him a shield. And a man ties it out of pride"," showing off"," and to cause harm to the people of Islam — it is upon him a burden.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about donkeys"," and he said: \""Nothing has been revealed to me concerning them except this comprehensive and unique verse: {Whoever does an atom's weight of good shall see it"," and whoever does an atom's weight of evil shall see it} [al-Zalzalah 7–8].\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Zayd ibn Aslam. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"19752","(19746) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤud al-Ḥakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ṭalḥah ibn Abī Saʿīd narrated to us that Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated to him, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm narrated to us, Abū al-Muwajjah narrated to us, ʿAbdān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Ṭalḥah ibn Abī Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: I heard Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrating that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever keeps a horse for the sake of Allah"," in faith in Allah and in confirmation of His promise"," its satiation"," its drinking"," its urine"," and its dung will be good deeds in his scale on the Day of Resurrection.\"" In the narration of Ibn Wahb: \""In faith and in confirmation of the promise of Allah.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥafṣ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"19753","(19747) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us, Nāfiʿ ibn Abī Nāfiʿ informed us, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no competition except in camel-racing"," horse-racing"," or arrow-shooting.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19754","(19748) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Baghdādī informed us in it that ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Qurashī narrated to us. Both said: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us, Nāfiʿ ibn Abī Nāfiʿ narrated to us, saying: I heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no competition except in arrow-shooting"," horse-racing"," or camel-racing.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously mentioned]"""
"19755","(19749) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from Nāfiʿ ibn Abī Nāfiʿ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no competition except in arrow-shooting"," horse-racing"," or camel-racing.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19756","(19750) He said, and Ibn Abī Fudayk informed us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from ʿAbbād ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There is no competition except in horse-racing or camel-racing.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said in al-Tārīkh: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shaybah told me"," Ibn Abī al-Fudayk informed me"," and he mentioned the hadith of ʿAbbād ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ and said: \""Except in arrow-shooting"," horse-racing"," or camel-racing.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19757","(19751) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Hishām ibn Abī al-Dumayk narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Ziyād Sabalān narrated to us, ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbbād al-Muhallabī narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from Abū al-Ḥakam, the client of the Laythīs, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no competition except in camel-racing or horse-racing.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn ʿAmr said: \""They say: 'or arrow-shooting.'\"" Yazīd ibn Hārūn followed him in narrating from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr"," and it is narrated from Abū ʿAbd Allāh"," the client of the Jandaʿīs"," from Abū Hurayrah"," similarly. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously mentioned]"""
"19758","(19752) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us. And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik ibn Anas, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) held a race with horses that had been trained and conditioned, from al-Ḥafyāʾ to Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ, and he held a race with horses that had not been conditioned, from al-Thaniyyah to the Mosque of Banī Zuraq. And Ibn ʿUmar was among those who raced with them. The wording is from the hadith of Yaḥyā. It was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"19759","(19753) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ʿAbdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Rāzī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us, Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated to us, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a she-camel called al-ʿAḍbāʾ that could never be outrun. Then a Bedouin came upon his camel and outran it. This distressed the Muslims. When he saw what was on their faces, one said: \O Messenger of Allah"," al-ʿAḍbāʾ has been outrun!\"" He said: \""It is a right upon Allah that nothing be raised in this world except that He brings it low.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from Ḥumayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 2871]"""
"19760","(19754) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us. And Abū Saʿd al-Zāhid informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Bundār al-Ṣūfī narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Ḥubāb al-Jumaḥī narrated to us, saying: Musaddad narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd, Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came upon a group of the Banī Aslam who were practicing archery in the marketplace. He said: \Shoot"," O Banī Ismāʿīl"," for your father was an archer. And I am with the sons of so-and-so\"" — one of the two parties. So they held back their hands. He said: \""What is the matter with you?\"" They said: \""Shoot!\"" He said: \""What is the matter with you?\"" They said: \""How can we shoot while you are with the sons of so-and-so?\"" He said: \""Shoot"," and I am with all of you.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 2899"," 3373"," 3807]"""
"19761","(19755) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣabbāghī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to me from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥarmalah from Muḥammad ibn Iyās ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some people of the tribe of Aslam who were practising archery. He said — and al-Ḥasan said: \Good is this pastime\"" — twice: \""Shoot"," for you had a father who used to shoot. Shoot"," and I am with Ibn al-Adraʿ.\"" The narrator said: The people held back their hands. He said: \""What is the matter with you?\"" They said: \""By Allah"," we shall not shoot while you are with him"," O Messenger of Allah"," for he will outshoot us.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Shoot"," and I am with all of you.\"" The narrator said: They shot for most of that day"," then they dispersed on equal terms"," none of them having outshot the others. [Weak]"""
"19762","(19756) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: While the Abyssinians were playing with their spears in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ʿUmar entered and reached for the pebbles, striking them with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Leave them"," O ʿUmar.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"19763","(19757) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated to us, ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār al-Yamāmī narrated to us from Iyās ibn Salamah from his father who said: We went on an expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — and he mentioned the hadith — he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted me behind him on al-ʿAḍbāʾ, and I set out towards Madīnah. While we was travelling, a man from the Anṣār who could not be outrun in a sprint kept saying: \Is there anyone who will race to Madīnah? Is there any competitor?\"" He repeated this several times. When I heard his words"," I said to him: \""Do you not honour a noble person nor show respect to one of high standing?\"" He said: \""No"," unless it be the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," by my father and my mother"," permit me to race the man.\"" He said: \""If you wish.\"" I said: I leapt down"," then I ran one or two hillocks"," then I overtook him and struck him between his shoulders"," saying: \""By Allah"," I have outrun you.\"" He said: \""I think he said\"" — and I outran him to Madīnah. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Agreed upon]"""
"19764","(19758) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān who said: ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, informed me that she was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey while she was a young girl. He said to his companions: \Go ahead.\"" So they went ahead. Then he said: \""Come"," let me race you.\"" So I raced him and I outran him on foot. Then later I went out with him again on a journey. He said to his companions: \""Go ahead.\"" Then he said: \""Come"," let me race you.\"" But I had forgotten what had happened before"," and I had now gained weight. I said: \""How can I race you"," O Messenger of Allah"," in this state?\"" He said: \""You certainly shall.\"" So I raced him and he outran me. He said: \""This is in return for that race.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19765","(19759) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Anṭākī Maḥbūb ibn Mūsā informed us that Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father and from Abū Salamah from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. She raced him and outran him on foot. When she had gained weight, she raced him and he outran her. He said: \This is in return for that race.\""\n\nAbū Usāmah narrated it from Hishām from a man from Abū Salamah from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. And Jarīr narrated it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated previously]"""
"19766","(19760) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Harawī narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar al-Anṣārī narrated to us from his father from Samurah ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to test the boys of the Anṣār every year and would enlist those among them who were found fit. He said: I was presented one year and a boy was enlisted while I was turned away. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you have enlisted him and turned me away. Had I wrestled him"," I would have thrown him.\"" He said: \""Then wrestle him.\"" So I wrestled him and threw him"," and he enlisted me. [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated previously"," 9/17810]"""
"19767","(19761) Abū Dāwūd narrated it in al-Marāsīl from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at al-Baṭḥāʾ when Yazīd ibn Rukānah — or Rukānah ibn Yazīd — came to him with some goats he owned. He said: \O Muhammad"," will you wrestle me?\"" He said: \""What will you offer if I defeat you?\"" He said: \""A sheep from my flock.\"" So he wrestled him and threw him"," and took a sheep. Rukānah said: \""Will you go again?\"" He said: \""What will you offer if I defeat you?\"" He said: \""Another one.\"" He mentioned this several times. Then he said: \""O Muhammad"," by Allah"," no one has ever laid my side upon the ground"," yet you are the one who threw me\"" — meaning he accepted Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned his goats to him.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Muḥammad informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us"," Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us"," Abū Dāwūd narrated it. It is a good mursal narration"," and it has also been narrated through another chain as a connected narration"," though it is weak. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"19768","(19762) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man chasing a pigeon and said: \A devil chasing a she-devil.\""\n\n(T) Sharik contradicted him in what was narrated from him"," saying: from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr from Abū Salamah from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. The hadith of Ḥammād is more authentic"," and Allah knows best. ʿUmar ibn Ḥamzah narrated from Ḥuṣayn ibn Muṣʿab who said: Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," disapproved of betting on two pigeons. [Weak]"""
"19769","(19763) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us.\n\n(H) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us. Both said: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a race among the horses that had been conditioned, sending them from al-Ḥafyāʾ, their finishing point being Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ. And he held a race among the horses that had not been conditioned, their course being from al-Thaniyyah to the Mosque of Banī Zuraq. And ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, used to race with them.\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Qatādah, and the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh regarding the horses that had not been conditioned does not mention what preceded it. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"19770","(19764) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Fārayābī narrated to us, Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it with its chain, identical to it in its entirety.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus in abridged form, and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated previously]"
"19771","(19765) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, he said: Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, Qabīṣah narrated to us, Sufyān from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Prophet ﷺ raced the horses that had been conditioned for racing from al-Ḥafiyāʾ to Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ, and he raced those that had not been conditioned from Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ to the Mosque of Banū Zuraq.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously referenced.]"
"19772","(19766) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq — Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Fawāris — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conditioned the horses for racing and sent them from al-Ḥafiyāʾ; and those among them that were not conditioned, he sent from Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ to the Mosque of Banū Zuraq.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah, from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously referenced.]"
"19773","(19767) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us by dictation, Abū Muslim narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Sulaymān al-ʿAtakī informed us; both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a horse race; he made the goal for the conditioned horses from al-Ḥafiyāʾ to Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ, and those that were not conditioned, from Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ to the Mosque of Banū Zuraq. Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \I came forward as a competitor"," and the horse carried me past the mosque.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Ḥarb. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān al-ʿAtakī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously referenced.]"""
"19774","(19768) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad — he is al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us, Abū ʿArūbah narrated to us, al-Musayyib ibn Wāḍiḥ narrated to us, Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī narrated to us, from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a race among the horses that had been conditioned, and he sent them from al-Ḥafiyāʾ, their furthest point being Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ. I said to Mūsā: \And how far was that?\"" He said: \""Six or seven miles.\"" And he held a race among the horses that had not been conditioned"," and he sent them from Thaniyyat al-Wadāʿ"," their furthest point being the Mosque of Banū Zuraq. I said: \""And how far was that?\"" He said: \""A mile or thereabout.\"" He said: \""And Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was among those who competed in it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad"," from Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr"," from Abū Isḥāq. And Muslim extracted it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj"," from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah. He also extracted it from the ḥadīth of Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah and Usāmah ibn Zayd"," from Nāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19775","(19769) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-ʿAbd al-Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, Sahl ibn ʿAmmār al-ʿAtakī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Sulaymān narrated to him, from al-ʿUmarī, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the horses used to be raced over six miles, and then a competition would be held, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would give the prize to the winner. Ḥammād ibn Sulaymān — he is unknown (majhūl). [Ḍaʿīf. See what the author stated.]"
"19776","(19770) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Ḥuṣayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever enters a horse between two other horses"," while he is secure from being overtaken"," it is gambling (qimār). And whoever enters a horse between two other horses while he is not secure from being overtaken"," then it is not gambling.\""\n\n[Munkar. Kitāb al-Umm 5/342.]"""
"19777","(19771) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Qāsim ibn al-Layth al-Rasʿanī, ʿUmar ibn Sinān, and Ibn Duḥaym said: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Bashīr narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever enters a horse between two other horses while he does not fear being overtaken"," it is gambling. And whoever enters a horse between two other horses while he does fear being overtaken"," then it is not gambling.\"" Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn and Saʿīd ibn Bashīr are the only ones who narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," and both Abū Dāwūd extracted it in Kitāb al-Sunan. [Ḍaʿīf. Previously referenced.]"""
"19778","(19772) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, that he heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib saying: \There is no harm in wagering on horses when a *muḥallil* (a third horse entered with no stake) is included. If it wins"," it takes the prize; and if it is overtaken"," there is nothing incumbent upon him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"19779","(19773) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashīr narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us, from his father, from the jurists whose word is authoritative among the people of Madīnah, who used to say: \Wagering on horses is permissible when a *muḥallil* is included: if it wins"," it takes the prize; and if it is overtaken"," it owes nothing. And it is befitting that the *muḥallil* be comparable to the horses in speed and quality.\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"19780","(19774) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrīt, from Abī Labīd, who said: \Al-Ḥakam ibn Ayyūb sent forth the horses one day. We said: 'If we were to come to Anas ibn Mālik.' So we came to him and asked him: 'Did you used to wager in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes. Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wagered on a horse of his called *Sabḥah*"," and it came in first"," and he was delighted and pleased by that.'\"" In meaning"," Yazīd ibn Hārūn and ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Zayd. [Ḥasan.]"""
"19781","(19775) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd — or Saʿīd ibn Zayd — from Wāṣil, the freedman of Abū ʿUyaynah, Mūsā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to me, saying: I was in the Ḥijr after we had performed the morning prayer. When the light had spread, we found ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — among us. He began asking each one of us individually, saying, \Where did you pray"," O so-and-so?\"" The person would reply"," \""Here"," here.\"" This continued until he came to me and said"," \""Where did you pray"," O Ibn ʿUbayd?\"" I said"," \""Here.\"" He said"," \""Excellent"," excellent! We know of no prayer more excellent in the sight of Allah than the Fajr prayer performed in congregation on the day of Jumuʿah.\"" They asked him"," saying"," \""O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," did you used to place wagers during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He said"," \""Yes. He ﷺ wagered on a horse of his called Subḥah"," and it came in first.\"" Ismāʿīl said: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated this hadith to us from Ḥammād ibn Zayd"," and then he said after that"," \""Ḥammād ibn Zayd or Saʿīd ibn Zayd.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated it from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb from Ḥammād ibn Zayd without any doubt"," and Asad ibn Mūsā narrated it from Ḥammād ibn Zayd.\n\nThe Shaykh said: If this is sound"," then what is meant — and Allah knows best — is that when one of the two riders outpaces his companion"," the victory belongs to him alone"," not to his companion. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"19782","(19776) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Ibn Bashshār both said: Ghundar narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Simāk, who said: I heard ʿIyāḍ al-Ashʿarī say: Abū ʿUbaydah said, \Who will wager against me?\"" A young man said"," \""I will"," if you do not become angry.\"" So he raced against him and defeated him. He said: I saw the two braids of Abū ʿUbaydah bouncing behind him while he was mounted on an Arabian horse. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19783","(19777) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us, al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir Shādhān narrated to us, Sharīk narrated to us, from al-Rukayn, from al-Qāsim ibn Ḥassān, from Ibn Masʿūd — may Allah be pleased with him — who attributed it to the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \Horses are three: a horse for the Most Merciful"," a horse for Satan"," and a horse for man. As for the horse of the Most Merciful"," it is the one that is tied in the cause of Allah — its dung and its urine will be in his scale. As for the horse of Satan"," it is the one upon which wagers are placed. As for the horse of man"," it is the one that he ties up"," seeking to fill his belly out of fear of poverty.\"" If this is established"," then what is meant by it — and Allah knows best — is that both parties put up the stakes from their own side and do not introduce a third party as a muhallil (an intermediary)"," in which case it would be gambling and would not be permissible. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"19784","(19778) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ḥumayd.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Khalaf narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us, ʿAnbasah — all of them — narrated from al-Ḥasan, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn — may Allah be pleased with him — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \There is no jalab and no janab in a race (al-rihān).\"" This is the wording of the hadith of ʿAnbasah. In the narration of Ḥumayd it is: \""There is no janab"," no jalab"," and no shighār in Islam.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ"," without the phrase \""al-rihān\""]"""
"19785","(19779) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, who said: \Al-jalab and al-janab in a race (al-rihān) are not permitted.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19786","(19780) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Mālik was asked, \What is the explanation of that?\"" He said: \""As for al-jalab"," it is that a horse falls behind in the race"," and something is moved behind it to urge it on so that it overtakes — that is al-jalab. As for al-janab"," it is that another horse is kept alongside the horse that is being raced"," so that when it draws near"," the rider switches to the horse that was kept alongside and takes the prize.\"" [Weak]"""
"19787","(19781) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Shabīb narrated to us, and I heard Muḥammad ibn Ṣadrān al-Sulamī say: ʿAbdullāh ibn Maymūn al-Marāʾī narrated to us, ʿAwf narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan — or Khilās — from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him. Ibn Maymūn was uncertain. The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him: \O ʿAlī"," I have entrusted this race (al-sabqah) to you among the people.\"" So ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — went out and called Surāqah ibn Mālik"," saying"," \""O Surāqāh"," I have entrusted to you what the Prophet ﷺ placed upon my neck regarding this race — I have placed it upon your neck. When you reach the miṭār\"" — Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \""And the miṭār is the point from which they are sent to the farthest limit\"" — \""then line up the horses and call out: 'Is there anyone who has fastened a bridle"," or is carrying a boy"," or has thrown down a weapon?' If no one answers you"," then say 'Allāhu Akbar' three times"," and at the third time release them. May Allah grant success in the race to whomever He wills among His creation.\"" ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — used to sit at the farthest limit and draw a line"," stationing two men facing each other at the edge of the line"," the edge of the line between the big toes of their feet. The horses would pass between the two men"," and he would say to them: \""When one of the two horses outpaces its companion by the tip of its ear"," or an ear"," or a cheek-strap"," then award the race to it. If you are uncertain"," then make their race a tie. When you couple two things"," then set the limit from the limit of the smaller of the two things. And there is no jalab"," no janab"," and no shighār in Islam.\"" This is a weak chain of narration. [Weak]"""
"19788","(19782) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥaḍramī Muṭayyin narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, from Quṭbah, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Yaḥyā, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade inciting animals against one another (al-taḥrīsh).\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ. Similarly"," it was narrated from Sharīk from al-Aʿmash. Ziyād ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Bakkāʾī narrated it from al-Aʿmash"," from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr"," from Mujāhid"," from Ibn ʿAbbās. Manṣūr ibn Abī al-Aswad narrated it from al-Aʿmash"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — from the Prophet ﷺ. And Layth ibn Abī Sulaym narrated it from Mujāhid"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from the Prophet ﷺ. [Munkar. ʿIlal al-Tirmidhī 511]"""
"19789","(19783) What is preserved is what Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī narrated to us in Kūfah, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us, Wakīʿ narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Mujāhid, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade inciting animals against one another (al-taḥrīsh).\"" And this is a mursal narration. [Weak]"""
"19790","(19784) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us, Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazīd — meaning Ibn Abī Ḥabīb — from Abū al-Khayr, from Ibn Zurayr, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \A mule was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he rode it. ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — said"," 'If we were to crossbreed donkeys with horses"," we would have something like this.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Only those who have no knowledge do that.'\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from Qutaybah"," from Layth ibn Saʿd"," likewise. Similarly"," Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr and others narrated it from Layth. ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated it from Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik"," from Layth. And Ibn Lahīʿah narrated it from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19791","(19785) Shu'ayb ibn Ayyub al-Sarifini narrated it from Abu al-Walid, as Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Shawdhb al-Wasiti narrated to us — Shu'ayb ibn Ayyub narrated to us — Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Habib — from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah — from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani — from 'Abdullah ibn Zurayr — from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A mule was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and it pleased us. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," should we not breed our donkeys upon our horses so that we may obtain the like of this?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""Only those who have no knowledge do that.\"" Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar likewise narrated it from Yazid ibn Abi Habib. [Sahih; narrated previously.]"""
"19792","(19786) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us — Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil al-Khuza'i informed us — Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us — 'Ali ibn 'Abdullah al-Madini narrated to us — 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Habib — from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah — from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani — from 'Abdullah ibn Zurayr — from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the ruler of Ayla or Farwa presented the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with his white mule, I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," if we were to breed donkeys upon purebred horses"," we would obtain the like of this.\"" He said: \""Only those who have no knowledge do that.\"" That has also been narrated through another chain from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). [Sahih; narrated previously.]"""
"19793","(19787) 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us — Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'faranī narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us — Sharik narrated from 'Uthman ibn Abi Zur'ah.\n\n(Reference) And Abu Bakr ibn Furak narrated to us — 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Sharik narrated from 'Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, who is Ibn Abi Zur'ah — from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd — from 'Ali ibn 'Alqamah — from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace be upon him): \Shall we breed the donkey upon the mare?\"" He said: \""Only those who have no knowledge do that.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Dawud. In the narration of Ibn al-Sabbah"," he said: A mule or a she-mule was gifted to the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is this?\"" He said: \""A mule or a she-mule — the donkey is bred upon the mare"," and this comes forth from between the two of them.\"" So I said: \""Should we breed so-and-so (a donkey) upon so-and-so (a mare)?\"" He said: \""Only those who have no knowledge do that.\"" [Sahih; narrated previously.]"""
"19794","(19788) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Maymuni narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Kathir al-'Abdi narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from Abu Jahdam Musa ibn Salim — from 'Ubayd Allah, a descendant of al-'Abbas — from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded us to perform the wudu thoroughly, and he forbade us — and I do not say he forbade you — from eating charity (sadaqah), and from breeding a donkey upon a mare. Thus said al-Thawri in this isnad: 'Ubayd Allah. And thus said Hammad ibn Salamah in what he narrated from him, as transmitted by al-Tayalisi. However, the correct name is 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas.\n\nAnd likewise Hammad ibn Zayd, al-Warith ibn Sa'id, and Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated it from Abu Jahdam. The hadith of Sufyan contains an error, as stated by al-Bukhari and others. [Sahih.]"
"19795","(19789) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — 'Abd al-Warith narrated from Musa ibn Salim — 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubaydullah narrated. He said: I visited Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) among a group of young men from Banu Hashim, and Ibn 'Abbas said, in a hadith he mentioned from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): \He did not single us out over the people in anything except in three matters: He commanded us to perform the wudu thoroughly"," that we should not eat charity (sadaqah)"," and that we should not breed a donkey upon a mare.\"" [Sahih; narrated previously.]"""
"19796","(19790) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Dawri narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us — Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated from al-Zuhri — from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah — from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade the confinement of living creatures (sabr al-ruh) and the castration of animals.\n\nAl-'Abbas said: No one narrated it except 'Ubayd Allah, and it is considered unusual (mustaghrab) from him.\n\nThe Sheikh said: Thus al-'Abbas narrated it. [Sahih, without his words \and the castration of animals.\""]"""
"19797","(19791) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki informed us — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, mentioning his chain of narration, except that he said: \…from the confinement of living creatures and the castration of animals — a severe confinement.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: His statement \""and the castration of animals is a severe confinement\"" is an analogy based on what was forbidden regarding the confinement of living creatures"," and it is from the words of al-Zuhri. Others besides 'Ubayd Allah narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhi'b as a mursal narration"," and they attributed the words regarding castration to al-Zuhri. [Sahih"," without his words \""and the castration of animals.\""]"""
"19798","(19792) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Bakhtari narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-'Awwam narrated to us — Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us — Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated. He said: I asked al-Zuhri about castration. He said: \'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah narrated to me"," saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade the confinement of living creatures (sabr al-ruh).\"" Al-Zuhri said: \""And castration is a severe confinement.\"" Likewise"," Yunus and Ma'mar narrated it from al-Zuhri as a mursal narration. Ma'mar also mentioned castration from al-Zuhri"," as Ibn Abi Dhi'b did. The preserved version in this report is what al-'Aqadi narrated from Ibn Abi Dhi'b"," due to the corroboration of Ma'mar and Yunus. And Allah knows best.\n\nIt has also been narrated in this regard through another chain from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," but the chain contains weakness. [Sahih"," without his words \""and the castration of animals.\""]"""
"19799","(19793) Abu al-Hasan ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us — Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us — Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us — al-Nadr ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us — Ibn Luha'ah narrated from 'Ata' — from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \There is no castration in Islam"," and no building of churches.\"" [Da'if (Weak).]"""
"19800","(19794) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran in Baghdad narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us — 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar — from Nafi' — from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he used to dislike the castration of animals and would say: \Do not alter the creation of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\"" This is the correct version"," as a mawquf narration. It has also been narrated as a marfu' narration. [Hasan.]"""
"19801","(19795) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ, Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Ṣaḥḥāf narrated to us, saying: Jubārah ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, saying: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the castration of camels, cattle, sheep, and horses, and he said: \Indeed"," increase (in numbers) is through offspring.\"" (T) And Yaḥyā ibn Yamān similarly narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh. And other than Jubārah narrated it from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar: \""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade…\"" And Jubārah also narrated it from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ"," from his father"," from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them)"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). And other than Jubārah narrated it from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus. And this matn with this isnād is more likely"," though ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ is weak in it"," which is consistent with raising mawqūf narrations. And Allah knows best. And it was narrated from Mūsā ibn Yasār"," from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," as marfūʿ. But the correct version is mawqūf. And ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated it from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," from Ibn ʿUmar: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to forbid the castration of animals and would say: \""Is increase not only through the males?\"" And it was narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn al-Muhājir"," who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him): \""Do not castrate a horse"," and do not race a horse beyond two hundred.\"" And this is munqaṭiʿ. And the narrations of ʿĀṣim in this regard are weak. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"19802","(19796) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, saying: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār, from Ibn ʿAbbās. (Ḥ) And he said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Qatādah, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), regarding His statement: \And I will surely command them"," so they will alter the creation of Allah\"" [al-Nisāʾ: 119]. He said: It means the castration of animals. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19803","(19797) He said: And Ādam narrated to us, saying: Warqāʾ narrated to us from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, who said: \He means the fitrah","\"" i.e."," the religion. [Weak]"""
"19804","(19798) He said: And Ādam narrated to us, saying: Warqāʾ narrated to us from Mughīrah, from Ibrāhīm, who said: \He means the religion of Allah.\"" And we have narrated from al-Ḥasan"," Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," and Qatādah a statement similar to that of Ibrāhīm. And from Bashīr"," who said: \""ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ordered me to castrate a mule for him during his caliphate.\"" And from al-Ḥasan"," that he was asked about castration and said: \""There is no harm in it.\"" And from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"," that he castrated a mule for himself. And from Ibn Sīrīn"," who said: \""There is no harm in castrating horses. If the stallions were left alone"," some of them would eat others.\"" And from ʬAṭāʾ: \""If there is fear of its biting and bad temperament"," there is no harm in it.\"" (Q) And the statement of Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them) is more deserving in light of the narrated Sunnah"," and with Allah is the success. And it may be permissible if there is a valid purpose connected to it"," as we have narrated from the Successors. And we have narrated in the Book of Sacrifices that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sacrificed two castrated rams"," and that is because of the improvement of the meat. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19805","(19799) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr al-Sahmī narrated to us, saying: Ḥumayd narrated from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was called al-ʿAḍbāʾ, and it was never outrun. Then a Bedouin came upon his camel and outran it, and that distressed the Muslims. When he saw what was in their faces, they said: \O Messenger of Allah"," al-ʿAḍbāʾ has been outrun!\"" He said: \""Indeed"," it is a right upon Allah that He does not raise anything of this world except that He will bring it down.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from various routes from Ḥumayd"," and it has already been mentioned in the Book of Ḥajj from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him) in the story of the Ḥajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): then he mounted al-Qaṣwāʾ until he reached the stopping place"," and he placed the belly of his she-camel al-Qaṣwāʾ against the rocks. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2871"," 2872"," 6501]"""
"19806","(19800) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd al-Jurmī narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿUmar al-Bisṭāmī informed us, saying: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, saying: ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us. They both said: Maʿn ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, saying: Ubayy ibn al-ʿAbbās ibn Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had a horse in our garden called al-Luḥayf. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm. And in the narration of al-Jurmī: al-Lukhayf with a khāʾ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿn with a ḥāʾ, then he said: \And some of them said: al-Lukhayf with a khāʾ.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Bukhārī 2855]"""
"19807","(19801) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd al-Jurmī narrated to us, saying: Maʿn narrated to me, saying: Ubayy ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated from his brother Muṣaddiq ibn al-ʿAbbās, from his father. He said thus: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had with them a horse called al-Ẓarib, and another called al-Lizāz."
"19808","(19802) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Baḥr narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Muhaymin ibn ʿAbbās ibn Sahl narrated from his father, from Sahl ibn Saʿd: that there were three horses of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with Saʿd ibn Abī Sahl, which he used to feed, and their names were al-Lizāz, al-Luḥayf, and al-Ẓarib. [Weak]"
"19809","(19803) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us, saying: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us, saying: Ādam narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) say: There was an alarm in Madīnah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) borrowed a horse from Abū Ṭalḥah called al-Manḍūb and rode it. When he returned, he said: \We did not see anything"," and indeed we found it to be a sea (i.e."," extremely swift).\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and Muslim narrated it from two other routes from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19810","(19804) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on a donkey called ʿUfayr, and he mentioned the ḥadīth. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another route from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ. [Weak]"
"19811","(19805) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us that Ḥibbān ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, from Idrīs al-Awdī, from al-Ḥakam, from Yaḥyā ibn al-Jazzār, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The horse of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was called al-Murtajiz; his mule was called Duldul; his donkey was called ʿUfayr; his sword was called Dhū al-Fiqār; his coat of mail was Dhāt al-Fuḍūl; and his she-camel was al-Qaṣwāʾ. [Weak]"
"19812","(19806) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf said: Sufyān mentioned, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, who said: The she-camel of the Prophet (peace be upon him) was called al-ʿAḍbāʾ; his mule was al-Shahbāʾ; his donkey was Yaʿfūr; and his maidservant was Khaḍirah. This has also been narrated in the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) left behind nothing except his white mule, his weapons, and a piece of land which he designated as charity. [Weak]"
"19813","(19807) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān al-Marwazī narrated to us that Khalaf ibn Hishām narrated to us. Both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ghaylān ibn Jarīr, from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) as part of a delegation from the Ashʿarīs, requesting mounts. He said: \By Allah"," I cannot provide you with mounts"," and I have nothing upon which to mount you.\"" We remained for as long as Allah willed. Then camels were brought to him"," and he ordered that three white-humped she-camels be given to us. When we departed"," we said—or some of us said to others—\""May Allah not bless us! We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) requesting mounts"," and he swore that he would not mount us"," yet then he provided mounts for us.\"" So we went back to him and informed him. He said: \""It is not I who mounted you"," but Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," mounted you. By Allah"," if Allah wills"," I do not swear an oath upon something and then see something better than it without expiating my oath and doing that which is better.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Khalaf ibn Hishām"," and the ḥadīth of al-Ṭayālisī carries the same meaning.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Nuʿmān and Qutaybah"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Khalaf ibn Hishām and others"," all of them from Ḥammād ibn Zayd. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"19814","(19808) ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that a solar eclipse occurred during the time of the Prophet (peace be upon him). [The ḥadīth is long, and at the end he (peace be upon him) said:] \By Allah"," if you knew what I know"," you would laugh little and weep much.\"""""
"19815","(19809) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us that ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)—the ḥadīth—until she said: He said: \By Allah"," if you knew what I know"," you would laugh little and weep much.\"" It was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad from ʿAbdah.\n\nAnd Muslim narrated it through another chain from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. [Sound — agreed upon"," without the wording of the oath]"""
"19816","(19810) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us that Maʿmar narrated to us, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \By the One in whose Hand is my soul"," if you knew what I know"," you would weep much and laugh little.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ through another chain from Maʿmar. [Sound — Bukhārī 6630]"""
"19817","(19811) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr narrated to us that Aḥmad narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated to us, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muḥammad"," if I had gold equal to Mount Uḥud"," I would not love that it remain with me for three nights"," except a dinar that I would find someone to accept from me"," except something I set aside for a debt owed by me.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Weak]"""
"19818","(19812) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us that Wakīʿ narrated to us that ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us, from ʢāsim ibn Shumaykh, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made a determined oath, he would say: \No"," by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Abū al-Qāsim.\""\n\nAbū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī in Kūfah and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī in Naysābūr both informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Wakīʿ narrated to us"," from al-Aʿmash"," from al-Maʿrūr ibn Suwayd"," from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was sitting in the shade of the Kaʿbah. When he saw me"," he said: \""They are the most losers"," by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!\"" I came until I sat down"," but I could not remain still"," so I stood up and said: \""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you"," O Messenger of Allah"," who are they?\"" He said: \""They are those with the most wealth"," except one who says with his wealth thus and thus and thus—in front of him"," behind him"," to his right"," and to his left—but they are few.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Wakīʿ. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"19819","(19813) Al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ, from his father, from al-Aʿmash, from al-Maʿrūr ibn Suwayd, from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I came to him while he was saying in the shade of the Kaʿbah: \They are the most losers"," by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!\"" I said: \""What is the matter with me? Does he see something in me?\"" I sat down while he was speaking"," but I could not remain silent"," and there came over me what Allah willed. I said: \""Who are they"," may my father and mother be sacrificed for you"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Those with the most wealth"," except one who says thus and thus and thus.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us that al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us that my father narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Sound — as previously cited]"""
"19820","(19814) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us that Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṭṭār narrated to us that Abū Usāmah informed us that Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated to us, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to me: \Indeed I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry with me.\"" She said: I said: \""How do you know that"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""When you are pleased with me"," you say"," 'No"," by the Lord of Muḥammad","' and when you are angry with me"," you say"," 'No"," by the Lord of Ibrāhīm.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Abū Kurayb"," both from Abū Usāmah. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"19821","(19815) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqba from Sālim from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) had an oath by which he would swear: \No"," by the Turner of Hearts.\"""""
"19822","(19816) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī both said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalīy al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us — Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamza narrated to us from his father from Abī al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abī Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Verily"," Allah has ninety-nine names — one hundred minus one. Whoever enumerates them shall enter Paradise. He is the One (al-Witr) and He loves the odd (al-witr).\"""""
"19823","(19817) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatāda al-Bashīrī informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl al-Khuzāʿī informed us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Mustafād al-Firyābī narrated to us — Ṣafwān ibn Ṣāliḥ, Abū ʿAbd al-Malik al-Dimashqī, in the year two hundred and thirty-two, narrated to us — al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us — Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamza narrated to us from Abī al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abī Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Verily"," Allah has ninety-nine names — one hundred minus one. Whoever enumerates them shall enter Paradise. He is the One and He loves the odd. He is Allah"," besides Whom there is no deity — the Most Merciful"," the Bestower of Mercy"," the Sovereign"," the Most Holy"," the Source of Peace"," the Granter of Security"," the Watcher over"," the Almighty"," the Compeller"," the Supreme"," the Creator"," the Originator"," the Fashioner"," the Repeatedly Forgiving"," the Subduing"," the Bestower"," the Provider"," the Opener"," the All-Knowing"," the Constrictor"," the Expander"," the Abaser"," the Exalter"," the Honorer"," the Humiliator"," the All-Hearing"," the All-Seeing"," the Judge"," the Just"," the Subtle"," the All-Aware"," the Forbearing"," the Magnificent"," the Repeatedly Relenting"," the Appreciative"," the Most High"," the Most Great"," the Guardian"," the Sustainer"," the Reckoner"," the Majestic"," the Noble"," the Watchful"," the Responsive"," the All-Encompassing"," the All-Wise"," the Loving"," the Glorious"," the Resurrector"," the Witness"," the Truth"," the Trustee"," the Strong"," the Firm"," the Protecting Friend"," the Praiseworthy"," the Counter"," the Restorer"," the Restorer"," the Giver of Life"," the Taker of Life"," the Ever-Living"," the Self-Subsisting"," the Finder"," the Illustrious"," the One"," the Self-Sufficient"," the All-Powerful"," the Predominant"," the Bringer Forward"," the Deferrer"," the First"," the Last"," the Manifest"," the Hidden"," the Governor"," the Most Exalted"," the Source of Goodness"," the Acceptor of Repentance"," the Avenger"," the Pardoner"," the Tender"," the Owner of the Kingdom"," the Lord of Majesty and Honor"," the Equitable"," the Gatherer"," the Self-Sufficient"," the Enricher"," the Withholder"," the Distressor"," the Benefactor"," the Light"," the Guide"," the Originator"," the Everlasting"," the Inheritor"," the Guide to the Right Path"," the Patient.\"""""
"19824","(19818) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said — al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \Whoever swears by Allah or by any of the names of Allah and then breaks his oath"," upon him is the expiation (kaffāra).\"""""
"19825","(19819) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, and al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Dārimī informed me — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanẓalī, narrated to me — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to me, saying: I heard al-Shāfiʿī saying: \Whoever swears by any of the names of Allah and then breaks his oath"," upon him is the expiation"," because the name of Allah is not a created thing. But whoever swears by the Kaʿba"," or by al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa"," there is no expiation upon him"," for they are created things"," and that which is not created is other than that which is created.\"""""
"19826","(19820) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Bazzāz narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī from Sālim from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) saying, \By my father"," by my father","\"" and he said: \""Verily"," Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers.\"" ʿUmar said: \""By Allah"," I have not sworn by them"," neither deliberately nor in transmission.\"""""
"19827","(19821) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Sufyān narrated to us — al-Zuhrī informed me — Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated from his father, saying: The Prophet (ﷺ) heard ʿUmar swearing by his father, and he said: \Beware! Verily"," Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""By Allah"," I have not sworn by them after that"," neither deliberately nor in transmission.\"""""
"19828","(19822) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī in Baghdad informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Sālim from Ibn ʿUmar from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), saying: The Prophet (ﷺ) heard me while I was swearing, saying, \By my father","\"" and he said: \""Verily"," Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers.\"" ʿUmar said: \""I have not sworn by them"," neither deliberately nor in transmission.\"""""
"19829","(19823) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us — Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Abū Yaḥyā Jaʿfar ibn Hāshim al-Simsār narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslama al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — al-Qaʿnabī, from what he read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came upon ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb while he was traveling in a caravan, swearing by his father, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Beware! Verily"," Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers. Whoever must let him swear by Allah"," or let him remain silent.\"""""
"19830","(19824) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyayna narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayya from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came upon ʿUmar during one of his journeys while he was saying, \By my father"," by my father","\"" and he said: \""Verily"," Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers. Whoever must let him swear by Allah"," or let him remain silent.\"""""
"19831","(19825) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us, saying: Abū Usāmah narrated to us, from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr, who said: Nāfiʿ, the freedman of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, narrated to me that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came upon ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was among a caravan, swearing by his father. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard him, he said: \Hold back! Indeed"," Allah has forbidden you to swear by your fathers. Whoever swears an oath"," let him swear by Allah"," or let him remain silent.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb"," from Abū Usāmah. Likewise"," al-Layth ibn Saʿd"," Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī"," and al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān narrated it from Nāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above.]"""
"19832","(19826) It was narrated with a difference regarding ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ. It was said from him thus, and it was also said from him, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ). Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdad, saying: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, saying: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, saying: Nāfiʿ narrated to me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came upon him while he was among a caravan, swearing by his father. He said: \Indeed"," Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Let the one who swears an oath swear by Allah"," or let him remain silent.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above.]"""
"19833","(19827) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Narsī narrated to us, saying: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, saying: Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not swear by your fathers"," nor by the ṭawāghīt (false deities).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1648.]"""
"19834","(19828) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: Tamtām and Abū Jaʿfar al-Tirmidhī both narrated to us, saying: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: ʿAwf narrated to us, from Muḥammad — that is, Ibn Sīrīn — from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Do not swear by your fathers"," nor by your mothers.\"" Tamtām added: \""Nor by the andād (rival deities). And do not swear except by Allah"," and do not swear except while you are truthful.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh in its entirety. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"19835","(19829) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī narrated to us in al-Kūfah, saying: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah al-Ghifārī informed us, saying: Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, saying: Masʿūd ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, who said: Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard a man swearing by the Kaʿbah. He said: \Do not swear by the Kaʿbah"," for indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Whoever swears by other than Allah has committed disbelief (kufr) or associated partners with Him (shirk).'\"" And this is among the things that Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah did not hear directly from Ibn ʿUmar. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"19836","(19830) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to me, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to me, from Manṣūr, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, who said: I was with ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) when I stood up and left a man from Kindah with him. I went to Saʿid ibn al-Musayyab. He said: Then the Kindī came in a state of alarm and said: \A man came to Ibn ʿUmar and said: 'Shall I swear by the Kaʿbah?' He said: 'No"," but swear by the Lord of the Kaʿbah"," for ʿUmar used to swear by his father"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Do not swear by your father"," for indeed whoever swears by other than Allah has associated partners with Him (shirk).\""'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Preceded above.]"""
"19837","(19831) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us, saying: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿĀmir Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us, saying: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, who narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) raced against me and I beat him. I said: \I have beaten you"," by the Kaʿbah!\"" Then he raced against me and beat me. He said: \""I have beaten you"," by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!\"" When he dismounted"," he intended to strike me and said: \""Do you swear by the Kaʿbah?\""\n\nAs for what we have narrated in the book of Ṣalāh"," from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbayd Allāh"," in the story of the Bedouin"," that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""He shall prosper"," by his father"," if he is truthful\"" — it is possible that this statement of his was made before the prohibition; and it is possible that it was a customary expression that flowed upon the tongue without the intention of making an oath"," similar to the inadvertent oath (laghw al-yamīn) for which there is no sin; and it is possible that the prohibition applies specifically when it is done in a manner of veneration and exalting the right of the one sworn by"," as opposed to what is not of that nature — and that was not done in a manner of exaltation"," but rather in a manner of emphasis; and it is possible that he (ﷺ) suppressed the name of Allah"," exalted be He"," as if he said: \""No"," by the Lord of his father","\"" whereas others do not suppress it but rather intend the exaltation of their father. [Ḥasan.]"""
"19838","(19832) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated to us that he heard Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is to swear an oath"," let him not swear except by Allah.\"" And the Quraysh used to swear by their fathers"," so he said: \""Do not swear by your fathers.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another route from ʿAbd Allāh"," in an abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19839","(19833) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdad, saying: Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Mukram narrated to us, saying: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to us, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf informed me that Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever among you swears an oath and says in his oath"," 'By al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā","' let him say: 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh (There is no deity but Allah).' And whoever says to his companion"," 'Come"," let me gamble with you","' let him give in charity.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr"," and they both narrated it from other routes from Ibn Shihāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19840","(19834) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, saying: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, saying: Abū Dāwūd informed us, saying: Hishām narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abī Qilābah, who said: Thābit ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There is no vow (nadhr) upon the believer regarding that which he does not possess. Cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever swears by a religion other than Islam while lying"," then he is as he said.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hishām al-Dastawāʾī"," and they both narrated it from another route from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19841","(19835) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us — Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us — Husayn ibn Waqid narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever swears that he is free of Islam"," if he is truthful"," he will not return to Islam safely; and if he is lying"," then he is as he said.\"" [Hasan]"""
"19842","(19836) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us — Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Baghdadi narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us — Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us — al-Walid ibn Tha'labah narrated from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever swears an oath of betrayal is not of us"," and whoever deceives the wife of a man or his slave is not of us.\"" [Sahih]"""
"19843","(19837) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Asbahani informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us — Abu 'Amir Musa ibn 'Amir narrated to us — al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, who said: Sa'id said — and Qatadah and al-Hasan used to say: \There is no expiation (kaffarah) for one who swears by Judaism or Christianity and then breaks his oath.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19844","(19838) As for the hadith which Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Asbahani informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us — Zayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Mawsili narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Harrani narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Sulayman — (h) — and Ibn Hayyan informed us — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan and 'Ali ibn Siraj both said — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ayyashun narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to me — my father narrated to me — from al-Zuhri — from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who says, 'I am a Jew or a Christian or free from Islam,' in an oath upon which he swears and then breaks it. He ﷺ said: \The expiation of an oath.\"" This has no basis from the hadith of al-Zuhri or any other. Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud al-Harrani is alone in narrating it"," and he is denounced (munkar al-hadith); the Imams declared him weak and abandoned him. [Munkar]"""
"19845","(19839) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us — Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Hayyan narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Musa al-Hulwani narrated to us — Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us — Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us — Bashshar ibn Kidam narrated from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \An oath is either a violation or a cause of regret.\"" Thus did Bashshar ibn Kidam narrate it"," and he is the brother of Mis'ar ibn Kidam. [Da'if]"""
"19846","(19840) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisi informed us — Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah al-Asbahani narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Faris narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari said — Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us — 'Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd said: I heard my father saying: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \An oath is sinful or a cause of regret.\"" Al-Bukhari said: And the hadith of 'Umar is more deserving. [Da'if]"""
"19847","(19841) Sayyid Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us — Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hafiz dictated to us from memory in the year three hundred and twenty-five — Abu 'Ali Sakhawayh ibn Mazayar narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Sadusi narrated to us — Sulayman al-Taymi narrated from al-Hasan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O 'Abd al-Rahman"," do not ask for authority (imarah)"," for if you are given it after asking"," you will be entrusted with it; and if you are given it without asking"," you will be aided therein. And if you swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better"," then do that which is better and expiate your oath.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from the hadith of Sulayman al-Taymi regarding the oath but not the imarah; and he narrated it through other chains from al-Hasan. [Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"19848","(19842) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr al-Saffar narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq, that is al-Saghani, narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak Abu Bakr narrated to us — al-Sa'q ibn Hazn narrated to us — Matar al-Warraq narrated from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: I entered upon Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was eating chicken meat. He said: \Come near and eat.\"" I said: \""I have sworn an oath that I will not eat it.\"" He said: \""Come near and eat"," and I will inform you about this oath of yours.\"" So I drew near and ate. He said: \""We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among a group of Ash'ari men"," seeking mounts. He ﷺ said: 'No"," by Allah"," I will not carry you"," and I have nothing to carry you upon.' We did not leave until camels of the highest quality came"," and he ﷺ commanded that we be given mounts. We had only gone a short distance when we said: 'What have we done? We have made the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forget his oath. By Allah"," we shall not prosper.' So we returned to him. He ﷺ said: 'What brought you back?' They said: 'You swore that you would not carry us"," and we feared that there would be no blessing for us"," and feared that we had made you forget your oath.' He ﷺ said: 'By Allah"," I did not forget it. Rather"," whoever swears an oath and then sees something other than it that is better"," let him do that which is better and let him expiate his oath.'\""\n\n[Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"19849","(19843) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ala' narrated to us — Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us — al-Sa'q ibn Hazn narrated, and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Shayban. [Sahih — previously mentioned]"
"19850","(19844) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud informed us — Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Hamdawayh ibn Sahl al-Marwazi narrated to us — Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Ma'bad al-Sanji narrated to us — Yazid ibn Harun informed us — Sulayman al-Taymi narrated from Abi al-Salil, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking mounts. He ﷺ said: \By Allah"," I will not carry you"," and I have nothing to carry you upon.\"" When we departed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to us three camels. I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you swore that you would not carry us"," yet you have carried us.\"" He ﷺ said: \""I did not carry you; rather"," Allah carried you. By Allah"," I do not swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better except that I do it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih through another chain from Sulayman.\n\nThe Shaykh said: al-Taymi fell short in it and did not mention the expiation (kaffarah). [Sahih — previously mentioned]"""
"19851","(19845) We have narrated it from the hadith of Abu Qilabah and al-Qasim ibn 'Asim from Zahdam al-Jarmi from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace be upon him), that in this hadith he said: \By Allah"," if Allah wills"," I shall not take an oath upon something and then see something else better than it except that I shall do that which is better and expiate my oath.\""\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'quob narrated to us; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Zahdam al-Jarmi. Ayyub said: and al-Qasim al-Kalbi narrated it to me from Zahdam"," and he mentioned it. [Sahih. Previously cited.]"""
"19852","(19846) Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa narrated it from his father, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), in this hadith: \By Allah"," I shall not take an oath upon something and then see something else better than it except that I shall expiate my oath and do that which is better.\""\n\nAbu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us; Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us from Abu Burdah from his father"," and he mentioned it.\n\nHe (the compiler) recorded it in al-Sahih"," as has preceded. [Sahih. Previously cited.]"""
"19853","(19847) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Zurarah narrated to us; Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Yazid ibn Kaisan al-Yashkuri narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man stayed late at night with the Prophet (peace be upon him), then he returned to his family and found that the children had fallen asleep. His family brought him food, but he swore that he would not eat because of his children. Then it seemed preferable to him, so he ate. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever takes an oath upon something and then sees something else better than it"," let him do that which is better and let him expiate his oath.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb from Marwan. [Sahih. Muslim 1650.]"""
"19854","(19848) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us; 'Ali ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil informed us; Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' from Tamim ibn Tarafah, who said: A man came to 'Adiyy ibn Hatim and asked him for an expenditure or for the price of a servant. 'Adiyy said to him: I have nothing except my coat of mail and my helmet. I shall write to my family and they will give it to you. He said: The man was not pleased. 'Adiyy became angry and swore that he would not give him anything. The man said: Then he was pleased. He said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: \Whoever takes an oath upon something and sees the avoidance of it to be better"," let him adopt taqwa (i.e."," let him abandon his oath for the sake of piety)\"" — I would not have broken my oath.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Qutaybah from Jarir. [Sahih. Muslim 1651.]"""
"19855","(19849) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' from Tamim al-Ta'i from 'Adiyy ibn Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever takes an oath upon something and then sees something else better than it"," let him do that which is better and let him leave it (i.e."," leave his oath).\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in al-Sahih from the hadith of Mu'adh al-'Anbari from Shu'bah"," and he said: \""and let him leave his oath.\"" And al-A'mash narrated it from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' from Tamim al-Ta'i from 'Adiyy"," who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""When one of you takes an oath upon something and then sees something better than it"," let him expiate it and do that which is better.\"" [Sahih. Previously cited.]\n\n(b) Mu'adh al-'Anbari narrated from Shu'bah that he said: \""and let him leave his oath.\""\n\n(c) 'Adiyy (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: \""When one of you takes an oath upon something and then sees something better than it"," let him expiate his oath and do that which is better.\"""""
"19856","(19850) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Bukhari informed me; Salih ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us from al-A'mash, and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn Fudayl. And he recorded it from the hadith of al-Shaybani from 'Abd al-'Aziz with the mention of expiation in it. And Simak ibn Harb narrated it from Tamim ibn Tarafah, and he mentioned expiation in one of the two narrations from him, and he did not mention it in the other narration. [Sahih. Previously cited.]"
"19857","(19851) Others besides Tamim narrated it from 'Adiyy, and they mentioned expiation in it. Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us of it; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Murrah informed me; he heard 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, the freed slave of al-Hasan ibn 'Ali, narrating that 'Adiyy ibn Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked, and he swore that he would not give, but then he gave. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: \Whoever takes an oath upon something and then sees something else better than it"," let him do that which is better and let him expiate his oath.\"" [Sahih. Without mention of expiation.]"""
"19858","(19852) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar narrated to us from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \By Allah"," if one of you persists in his oath concerning his family"," it is more sinful for him before Allah than that he give the expiation that Allah has ordained.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi'"," both from 'Abd al-Razzaq. [Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"19859","(19853) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; Ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us; Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us; Mu'awiyah ibn Salam narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from 'Ikrimah from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \When a man persists in his oath concerning his family"," it is a greater sin. Expiation does not avail him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Yahya ibn Salih. [Sahih. Previously cited.]"""
"19860","(19854) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me by way of ijazah; Ibrahim ibn Isma'il al-Qari' narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us; Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, and he mentioned it with his chain of narration, except that he said: \Whoever persists in his oath concerning his family"," it is a greater sin.\"" [Sahih. Previously cited.]"""
"19861","(19855) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abu al-Hasan al-Tara'ifi narrated to us that 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us that 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And do not make Allah an obstacle for your oaths} [Al-Baqarah 224]. He said: \Do not make Me an obstacle for your oath so that you refrain from doing good. Rather"," expiate your oath and do good.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19862","(19856) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, both saying that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us that Ruh ibn 'Ubadah narrated from Sa'id from Qatadah from al-Hasan regarding His words: {And do not make Allah an obstacle for your oaths} [Al-Baqarah 224]. He said: \Do not use Allah as an excuse"," so that none of you says: 'I have sworn that I will not maintain ties of kinship"," nor strive for reconciliation"," nor give charity from my wealth.' Rather"," expiate your oath and fulfill that which you have sworn to do.\"" This is the statement of Qatadah. [Hasan]"""
"19863","(19857) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ma'ruf al-Faqih al-Isfara'ini narrated to us there that Abu Sahl Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfara'ini informed us that Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Nasr al-Hadda' narrated to us that 'Abdullah ibn al-Madini narrated to us that Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us that Habib, the teacher, narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from Sa'id al-Musayyib that two brothers from the Ansar had an inheritance between them. One of them asked his brother for the division of the estate, and the other said: \If you ever ask me again for the division"," I will never speak to you as long as I live"," and all my wealth shall be dedicated to the maintenance of the Ka'bah.\"" 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""The Ka'bah has no need of your wealth. Expiate your oath and speak to your brother"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'There is no oath or vow in that which displeases the Lord"," nor in severing ties of kinship"," nor in that which one does not possess.'\"" The ruling of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding expiation is evidence that the meaning of the hadith is that there is no oath which one is commanded to uphold and maintain fidelity to when it involves disobedience to Allah — not that expiation is not required for breaking it. [Sahih]"""
"19864","(19858) And this is also the intended meaning of what Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, both saying that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us that Abu Usamah narrated from al-Walid ibn Kathir that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith narrated to me from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from his father from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever divorces that which he does not possess"," there is no divorce for him; and who frees that which he does not possess"," there is no emancipation for him; and who makes a vow regarding that which he does not possess"," there is no vow for him; and who swears an oath in disobedience to Allah"," there is no oath for him; and who swears an oath to sever ties of kinship"," there is no oath for him.\"" An additional narration has been reported in this hadith that contradicts the authentic narrations from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). [Da'if. Previously referenced under number 14870/14871]"""
"19865","(19859) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us that 'Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us that 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no vow and no oath in that which the son of Adam does not possess"," nor in disobedience to Allah"," nor in severing ties of kinship. And whoever swears an oath and then sees something other than it that is better"," let him leave it and do that which is better"," for leaving it is its expiation.\"" [Munkar]"""
"19866","(19860) And this has been narrated from another chain, weaker than this one. Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani informed us that Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us that Hamid ibn Shu'aib narrated to us that Sura narrated to us that Hushaym narrated from Yahya ibn 'Ubaydullah from his father from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Whoever swears an oath and then sees something other than it that is better"," let him do that which is better"," for that is its expiation.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19867","(19861) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, and he said that Abu Dawud said: All the hadiths from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) state: \Let him expiate his oath","\"" except for that which is insignificant. Abu Dawud said: I said to Ahmad ibn Hanbal: \""Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated from Yahya ibn 'Ubaydullah.\"" He said: \""He abandoned him after that"," though he was qualified for it.\"" Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: \""His hadiths are munkar (rejected)"," and his father is unknown.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad]"""
"19868","(19862) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us that Salim ibn Nuh narrated from al-Jurayri from Abu 'Uthman from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, who said: \Guests came to us"," and my father used to converse with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at night. He departed and said: 'Attend to your guests.' When I came in the evening with their meal"," they refused and said: 'Until the master of our house comes and eats with us.' I said: 'He is a stern man"," and if you do not do so"," I fear he may harm me.' They refused. When my father came"," he did not begin with anything and said: 'Have you attended to your guests?' They said: 'No"," by Allah"," we have not.' He said: 'Did I not command 'Abd al-Rahman?' I stepped aside and he said: 'O Ghunthar! I swear by Allah"," if you can hear my voice"," you must respond.' I came and said: 'By Allah"," I have no fault. These are your guests — ask them. I came to them with their meal"," but they refused to eat until you came.' He said: 'Why do you not accept our hospitality from us?' By Allah"," I will not eat it tonight.' They said: 'By Allah"," we will not eat it until you eat.' He said: 'It is an evil thing since this night that you do not accept our hospitality from us.' Then he said: 'As for the first matter"," it was from Satan. Bring your meal.' In the morning"," he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," they were righteous and I broke my oath.' He informed him"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Rather"," you are the most righteous and the best of them.' He said: 'No expiation reached me.'\"" Muslim narrated this in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna. The statement of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) — \""As for the first matter"," it was from Satan\"" — is evidence that swearing an oath to abstain from food is disliked (makruh)"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not command him with expiation. If he did not command it"," it may be because he knew of his awareness of its obligation"," or it may be that this was before the revelation of the expiation ruling"," and the former is more likely. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"19869","(19863) For Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Halim al-Marwazi informed us that Abu al-Muwajjah informed us that 'Abdan informed us that 'Abdullah narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) never broke an oath until Allah revealed the expiation of oaths, and he said: \I will not swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better without doing that which is better and expiating my oath.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Muqatil from 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak. [Sahih. Bukhari 6621]"""
"19870","(19864) And the Shaykh Abu al-Fath informed us that Abu al-Hasan ibn Faras narrated to us that Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us that 'Abd al-Humid ibn Subayh narrated to us that Sufyan narrated from Sulayman al-Ahwal from Abu Ma'bad from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \Whoever swears an oath regarding his property that he will not divide it"," its expiation is to leave it"," and along with the expiation there is a good deed.\"" [Sahih]"""
"19871","(19865) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Sakan narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated from Shuʿbah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in Baghdād that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us that Abū ʿUmar narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ashʿath ibn Sulaym from Muʿāwiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with seven things and prohibited us from seven. He prohibited us from wearing a gold ring or gold bangles"," from using silver vessels"," and from wearing silk"," brocade"," istabraq (a type of silk)"," mītharah (a silk cushion)"," and qassī (a garment made of silk mixed with wool). And he commanded us with seven: he commanded us to visit the sick"," to follow funeral greetings"," to return the greeting of salām"," to say yarḥamuk Allāh to one who sneezes"," to accept the invitation of the one who invites"," to help the oppressed"," and to fulfil an oath.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Khwārizmī"," and the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdillāh carries the same meaning.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd and Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon.]"""
"19872","(19866) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that Abū ʿĀmir Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us that Ḥarīz informed me from Shuraḥbīl ibn Shuʿfah from Nāṣij al-Ḥaḍramī, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by two men who were swearing oaths over a sale"," one of them saying"," 'By Allah"," I will not lower the price for you","' and the other saying"," 'By Allah"," I will not increase it for you.' Then he saw that the sheep had been purchased"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," 'One of them has made it obligatory' — meaning the sin and the expiation.\"" Ḥarīz ibn ʿUthmān is alone in narrating this with this chain"," and Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19873","(19867) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Maymūnī narrated to us that Rūḥ narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Abū al-Fayḍ, who said: \I heard ʿAbdullāh"," a man from the people of Ḥimṣ"," say: 'I saw Abū al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with him) bargaining with a man over some sheep. The man swore that he would not sell them"," but then later said"," \""I will sell them.\"" So Abū al-Dardāʾ refused to buy them"," saying"," \""I would not like to lead you into sin","\"" but the man refused to sell to anyone else.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19874","(19868) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us that Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Sābiq, narrated to us that Shaybān narrated from Firās from ʿĀmir from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said"," 'What are the major sins?' He said"," 'Associating partners with Allah (shirk).' He said"," 'Then what?' He said"," 'Then disobedience to parents (ʿuqūq al-wālidayn).' He said"," 'Then what?' He said"," 'Then the oath that plunges one into sin (al-yamīn al-ghamūs).'\"" He said: \""I asked ʿĀmir"," 'What is al-yamīn al-ghamūs?' He said"," 'It is when a person seizes the wealth of a Muslim by means of his oath while he is lying therein.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 6675"," 6920]"""
"19875","(19869) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Shaybān narrated it with his chain, except that he did not mention ʿuqūq (disobedience to parents). It was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn from ʿAbdullāh ibn Mūsā. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously mentioned.]"
"19876","(198670) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ḥīrī narrated to us by dictation that ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Masarrah narrated to us that al-Muqriʾ narrated from Abū Ḥanīfah from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Mujāhid and ʿIkrimah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is nothing in which obedience to Allah is rewarded more swiftly than the joining of the ties of kinship (ṣilat al-raḥm)"," and there is nothing punished more swiftly than transgression (al-baghy)"," severing the ties of kinship (qaṭīʿat al-raḥm)"," and the sinful oath (al-yamīn al-fājirah)"," which leaves homes desolate.\"" This is how ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated it from Abū Ḥanīfah.\n\n(T) And Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān"," ʿAlī ibn Ẓabyān"," and al-Qāsim ibn al-Ḥakam contradicted him"," narrating it from Abū Ḥanīfah from Nāṣiḥ ibn ʿAbdillāh from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet ﷺ. And it was also said that Yaḥyā narrated it from Abū Salamah from his father. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19877","(19871) The ḥadīth is well-known through irsāl (a broken chain). Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, who narrated it, saying: \There are three things — whoever has them will see their consequences before his death.\"" He mentioned them"," and at the end of them he said: \""And the sinful oath (al-yamīn al-fājirah) which leaves homes desolate.\"" [Ḍaʿīf — as previously mentioned.]"""
"19878","(19872) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from the original of his book that Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Abū al-ʿAlāʾ from Makhūl, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," the most swiftly rewarded good deed is the joining of the ties of kinship (ṣilat al-raḥm)"," and the most swiftly punished evil is transgression (al-baghy) and the sinful"," patient oath (al-yamīn al-ṣabr al-fājirah) which leaves homes desolate.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Whoever deliberately swears a false oath"," saying"," 'By Allah"," such-and-such happened","' when it did not"," has committed a sin and must offer expiation"," and he has done wrong by deliberately swearing by Allah falsely.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""If someone asks"," 'What is the evidence that he must offer expiation when he intended falsehood?' it is said: 'The closest proof is the statement of the Prophet ﷺ: \""Let him do that which is better and offer expiation for his oath.\"" For he commanded him to break his oath.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19879","(19873) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil ibn Khalaf al-Qāḍī narrated to us in Baghdād that Abū Qilābah narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī and Ashhal ibn Ḥātim said that Ibn ʿAwn narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ḥasan from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Jamīl al-Azdī narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham al-Baldī narrated to us that Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us that Hushaym narrated to us that Yūnus ibn ʿUbayb, Manṣūr ibn Zādhān, and Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from al-Ḥasan, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When you swear an oath…\"" And in the narration of Ibn ʿAwn: \""When you swear an oath upon something and you see something other than it that is better"," then do that which is better and offer expiation for your oath.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr from Hushaym"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another route from Ibn ʿAwn"," then he said: \""And Ashhal followed him from Ibn ʿAwn.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon.]\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And the statement of Allah: {And let not those of virtue and wealth among you swear not to give to their relatives} [al-Nūr: 22] was revealed concerning a man who swore not to benefit a certain person"," so Allah commanded him to benefit him.\"""""
"19880","(19874) The Shaykh said: \This is in the story of al-Ifk (the Incident of the Slander)"," and that is in what Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us that al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Yūnus ibn Yazīd from Ibn Shihāb"," who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"," Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," ʿAlqamah ibn Waqqāṣ"," and ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah narrated to me from the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," when the people of al-Ifk said what they said about her. Allah declared her innocent of what they said"," and each of them narrated to me a portion of the ḥadīth"," some of their narrations confirming others"," even though some of them had better memories than others.\"" He then mentioned the ḥadīth at length"," and in it he said: \""Then Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: {Indeed"," those who came with the slander are a group among you} [al-Nūr: 11] — the ten verses that Allah revealed concerning my innocence.\"" Abū Bakr said: \""He used to spend on Misṭaḥ ibn Uthāthah on account of his kinship to him and his poverty"," and he swore"," 'By Allah"," I will never spend anything on Misṭaḥ again after what he said about ʿĀʾishah.' So Allah revealed: {And let not those of virtue and wealth among you swear not to give to their relatives"," the needy"," and the emigrants in the cause of Allah. And let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving"," Merciful} [al-Nūr: 22].\"" Abū Bakr said: \""Yes"," by Allah"," indeed I love that Allah should forgive me.\"" So he restored to Misṭaḥ the maintenance that he used to provide him and said: \""By Allah"," I will never withdraw it from him.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it through another route from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon.]"""
"19881","(19875) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, that ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us, that Ibn Abī Maryam informed us, that Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us, that Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father, from ʿĀ'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to provide for Misṭaḥ ibn Uthāthah. When Misṭaḥ said about ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) what he said, Abū Bakr swore by Allah that he would never benefit him again. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: *\Let not those among you who possess grace and abundance swear not to give to the kindred"," the poor"," and those who emigrated in the cause of Allah\""* [An-Nūr 22]. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Yes"," indeed"," by Allah"," I love that Allah forgive me.\"" So he resumed providing for Misṭaḥ and expiated his oath.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: Allah the Most High said: *\""Indeed"," they utter a hateful word and a lie\""* [Al-Mujādalah 2]"," and then Allah made expiation obligatory therein.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: The obligation of expiation in this is established by the explicit text"," and the reports concerning it have preceded in the chapter on Ẓihār."""
"19882","(19876) As for the ḥadīth which Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, that Ḥammād informed us, that ʿAṭā' ibn al-Sā'ib narrated from Abū Yaḥyā, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that two men came to the Prophet ﷺ disputing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked the claimant for proof, but he had no proof. So he asked the defendant to take an oath, and he swore by Allah, there is no deity but He. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \You have done so"," but you have been forgiven through the sincerity of your saying *Lā ilāha illā Allāh*.\"" Thus did Ḥammād ibn Salamah"," ʿAbd al-Wārith"," al-Thawrī"," Jarīr"," and Sharīk narrate it from ʿAṭā'."""
"19883","(19877) And Shuʿbah narrated it from ʿAṭā' ibn al-Sā'īb, as Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Abū al-Muthannā narrated to me, that my father narrated to me, that my father narrated from Shuʿbah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, that Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAṭā', from Abī al-Bakhtarī, from ʿUbaydah, from Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet ﷺ, that a man swore by Allah, there is no deity but He — or he said: he swore by Allah falsely — and he was forgiven, meaning for his sincerity in declaring *Lā ilāha illā Allāh*. This is a mistake on the part of Shuʿbah. The correct narration is that of the group. And ʿUbaydah died before Ibn al-Zubayr, as the people of history claim, by nine years, so his narration from him is far-fetched. And Allah knows best. ʿAṭā' al-Sā'īb is alone in narrating it, along with the disagreement regarding its chain of narration."
"19884","(19878) It is narrated from the ḥadīth of Thābit from Anas, though it is not strong. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, that Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, that Abū Qudāmah narrated to us, that Thābit al-Bunānī narrated from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: \O so-and-so"," did you do such and such?\"" He said: \""No"," by Allah"," there is no deity but He"," I did not do it","\"" while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew that he had done it. He repeated this to him several times"," and each time he swore. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Allah has forgiven your lie through your sincerity in saying *Lā ilāha illā Allāh*.\"""""
"19885","(19879) And it is said from Thābit, from Ibn ʿUmar. Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed it to us by way of ijāzah, that Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣabīḥ informed them, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shīrūyah narrated to us, that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Thābit al-Bunānī, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: \Did you do such and such?\"" He said: \""No"," by Allah"," there is no deity but He.\"" Then Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came to him and said: \""Indeed"," he has done it"," but he has been forgiven for his saying *Lā ilāha illā Allāh*.\"""""
"19886","(19880) And it is narrated from another route as a mursal report. Abū Manṣūr ʿAbd al-Qāhir ibn Ṭāhir al-Imām, Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥamdān al-Fārisī informed us, that Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us, that Abū Muslim narrated to us, that al-Anṣārī narrated to us, that Ashʿath narrated from al-Ḥasan, that a man lost a she-camel of his and claimed it against another man. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and the claimant said: \This man took my she-camel.\"" The other said: \""No"," by Allah"," there is no deity but He"," I did not take it.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""You have indeed taken it; return it to him.\"" So he returned it to him. The Prophet ﷺ then said to him: \""You have been forgiven for your sincerity.\"" This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\nIf the original is sound"," then the intended meaning is that a sin"," however grave"," does not necessitate the Fire when the creed is sound and the person is one for whom forgiveness has already been decreed. However"," this specification (of who is forgiven) cannot be made by anyone after the Prophet ﷺ."""
"19887","(19881) As for the athar which Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh informed us, they said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, that Khalaf ibn Hishām narrated to us, that ʿAbthar narrated from Layth, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \Oaths are four: two that are expiated and two that are not expiated. A man swears by Allah that he will not do such and such"," and then he does it; and a man says"," 'By Allah"," I will do it","' and then he does not do it. As for the two oaths that are not expiated: a man swears that he did not do such and such when he did do it; and a man swears that he did do such and such when he did not do it.\"" Thus did ʿAbthar ibn al-Qāsim narrate it from Layth ibn Abī Sulaym."""
"19888","(19882) Sufyān al-Thawrī contradicted him and narrated it from Layth, from Ziyād ibn Kulaib Abī Maʿshar, from Ibrāhīm, as his own statement, which is more likely.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, that Rūḥ narrated from al-Thawrī, from Layth, that Ziyād ibn Kulaib narrated to us from Ibrāhīm, who said: \Oaths are four: two that are expiated and two that are not expiated. A man's saying"," 'By Allah"," I did not do it","' and 'By Allah"," I did do it' — there is no expiation in either of these. If he deliberately did something"," then it is a lie; and if he thought it was as he said"," it is laghw (idle oath). And a man's saying"," 'By Allah"," I will not do it","' and 'By Allah"," I will surely do it' — these two carry expiation.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Layth and Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān are not used as authoritative proofs. And Allah knows best."""
"19889","(19883) And it is narrated from another route from Ibn Masʿūd. Abū al-Fatḥ al-Faqīh informed us, that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Sharīḥ narrated to us, that Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us, that ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, that Shuʿbah narrated from Abī al-Tayyāḥ, who said: I heard Abū al-ʿĀliyah say: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, said: \We used to count among the sins for which there is no expiation the ghamūs oath.\"" It was asked: \""What is the ghamūs oath?\"" He said: \""A man's usurping the wealth of his brother through a false oath.\"""""
"19890","(19884) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us, that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Abū Hurayrah used to narrate that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \I saw in the night a canopy dripping with ghee and honey"," and I saw the people scooping it up with their hands — some taking much and some little. And I saw a rope stretching from the sky to the earth"," and I saw you"," O Messenger of Allah"," take hold of it and ascend. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and it broke"," but then it was reconnected for him and he ascended.\"" Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""By my father"," O Messenger of Allah"," let me interpret it.\"" He said: \""Interpret it.\"" He said: \""As for the canopy"," it is the canopy of Islam. As for the dripping of ghee and honey"," it is the Qur'an"," its softness and its sweetness. As for those who take much and those who take little"," it is the one who learns much of the Qur'an and the one who learns little of it. As for the rope stretching from the sky to the earth"," it is the truth upon which you are. You take hold of it and Allah raises you. Then another man takes hold of it after you and is raised by it. Then another takes hold of it after him and is raised by it. Then another man takes hold of it and it is cut off for him"," but then it is reconnected and he is raised by it.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," tell me"," did I get it right or did I err?\"" He said: \""You got some of it right and some of it wrong.\"" He said: \""By my father"," O Messenger of Allah"," you must tell me in what I erred.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Do not swear.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," except that he said: from ʿUbayd Allāh"," sometimes from Ibn ʿAbbās and sometimes from Abū Hurayrah. And as al-Ramādī narrated it"," Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī"," Fiyāḍ ibn Zuhayr"," and Aḥmad ibn Azhar narrated it. And Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated it and said: Maʿmar used to say once from Abū Hurayrah and once from Ibn ʿAbbās"," that Abū Hurayrah used to narrate. And Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated it from ʿAbd al-Razzāq and said: from Ibn ʿAbbās"," that a man came. And Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbayd Allāh"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: A man came. And he said in the ḥadīth: \""I swear.\"" And thus Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated it from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī"," except that he said in the ḥadīth: He said"," \""By Allah"," O Messenger of Allah"," you must tell me in what I erred.\"""""
"19891","(19885) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to me, that al-Layth narrated from Yūnus —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, that Ibn Wahb informed me, that Yūnus informed him, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtban ibn Masʿūd, that Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — used to narrate that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I saw in a dream a cloud dripping with ghee and honey"," and I saw people stretching out their hands towards it — some taking much and some taking little. And I saw a rope extending from the heaven to the earth"," and I saw you take hold of it and ascend. Then a man after you took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then yet another man took hold of it"," and it broke. Then it was reconnected for him"," and he ascended.\"" Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," by my father and my mother"," you must let me interpret it.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Interpret it.\"" Abū Bakr said: \""As for the cloud"," it is the cloud of Islam. As for what dripped from it of ghee and honey"," that is the Quran — its sweetness and its softness. As for what people stretched their hands towards"," that is the one who takes much from the Quran and the one who takes little. As for the rope extending from the heaven to the earth"," it is the truth upon which you are"," by which Allah elevates you. Then a man after you takes hold of it and is elevated by it. Then another man takes hold of it and is elevated by it. Then yet another man takes hold of it and is elevated by it"," and then it breaks. Then it is reconnected for him and he is elevated by it. So tell me"," O Messenger of Allah"," by my father and my mother"," did I speak correctly or did I err?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""You spoke correctly in some things and erred in some things.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," you must inform me of wherein I erred.\"" He said: \""Do not swear.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of al-Layth"," he said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I saw during the night in a dream","\"" and he mentioned: \""And there was a rope extending from the earth to the heaven"," and I saw you take hold of it and ascend","\"" and the remainder is like the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it from Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā from Ibn Wahb.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: Sulaymān ibn Kathīr"," the brother of al-Zuhrī's nephew"," and Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn followed him"," from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbayd Allāh"," from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\n\n(t) And al-Zubaydī narrated from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbayd Allāh"," from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — from the Prophet ﷺ. And al-Zubaydī said"," from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbayd Allāh"," that Ibn ʿAbbās — or Abū Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with them both"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And in the ḥadīth"," he said: \""By Allah"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"19892","(19886) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, that Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us, that Abū Muslim narrated to us, that Abū ʿĀṣim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \When he says 'I swear' (aqsamtu)"," it is nothing until he says 'I swear by Allah' (aqsamtu bi-Llāh).\"" And a musnad ḥadīth has been narrated on this"," except that it is very weak (ḍaʿīf bi-marrā). [Ḥasan]"""
"19893","(19887) Isḥāq al-Ḥanẓalī narrated from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus, from Rashdīn ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — regarding his statement \I swear\"" (uqsimu): \""It is not an oath until he says 'I swear by Allah' (uqsimu bi-Llāh).\"" And regarding his statement \""I bear witness\"" (ashhadu): \""It is not an oath until he says 'I bear witness by Allah' (ashhadu bi-Llāh).\"" And this was informed to me by Abū ʿAbd Allāh"," by way of ijāzah"," from Abī al-Walīd"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shirawayh"," who said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Muḥammad ibn Naṣr — narrated to us: Isḥāq narrated"," and he mentioned it. And that was narrated from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī as his own statement. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19894","(19888) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us, that Musaddad narrated to us, that Abū ʿAwānah narrated, from Ashʿath ibn Sulaym, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with seven things and forbade us from seven things. He commanded us to visit the sick, to follow funeral processions, to respond to the one who sneezes, to spread the salām, to help the oppressed, to fulfill the oath of the one who swears, and to accept the invitation of the one who invites. And he forbade us from wearing gold rings, from drinking from silver vessels, from silk, from brocade, from silk brocade (istabraq), from cushioned silk covers (māyathir), and from striped garments (qassī).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl, and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Rabīʿ — both of them from Abī ʿAwānah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"
"19895","(19889) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, that Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ṣafwān — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my father to pledge allegiance to him upon the Hijrah. He said: \Rather"," I shall pledge allegiance to him upon Jihād.\"" I went to al-ʿAbbās"," who was at the watering place"," and said: \""O Abū al-Faḍl"," I went with my father to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon the Hijrah"," but he did not do it.\"" So al-ʿAbbās stood with him"," wearing a shirt over which there was no upper garment"," and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you know what is between me and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ṣafwān"," and he has come with his father for you to pledge allegiance to him upon the Hijrah"," but you did not do it.\"" He said: \""There is no Hijrah.\"" He (al-ʿAbbās) said: \""I swear upon you that you must pledge allegiance to him.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ extended his hand and said: \""Here"," I fulfill the oath of my uncle"," but there is no Hijrah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ṣafwān — or Ṣafwān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — from the Prophet ﷺ. Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād said"," from Mujāhid: it is not correct (lā yaṣiḥḥ). [Ḍaʿīf — 19890 has only an empty chain]"""
"19896","(19890) Abū Bakr al-Fārisī informed us of that, that Ibrāhīm al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, that Abū Aḥmad ibn Fārīs narrated, from al-Bukhārī. [Also ḍaʿīf]"
"19897","(19891) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Hārūn ibn Rustam narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Daqīqī narrated to us, that Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, that Baqiyyah narrated to us, that Isḥāq ibn Mālik al-Ḥaḍramī narrated, from ʿIkrimah, from Abī Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with him — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever swears an oath regarding someone"," thinking that he will fulfill it"," but he does not do so"," then his sin is upon the one who did not fulfill it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated by al-Bukhārī]"""
"19898","(19892) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, that al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ṭayyib narrated to us, that Ibn Wahb narrated to me, that Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated, from Abī al-Zāhiriyyah and Rāshid ibn Saʿd, from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — who said: A woman gave her a plate containing dates, and ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — ate from it and left some dates. The woman said: \I swear upon you that you must eat all of it.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Fulfill her oath"," for the sin is upon the one who breaks it (al-muḥnith).\""\n\nThe ḥadīth of Abī Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with him — in its isnād contains unknown narrators among the shaykhs of Baqiyyah. The ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah is better (amthal)"," though it is mursal. Abū Dāwūd included it in al-Marāsīl from the ḥadīth of Layth ibn Saʿd from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ"," and it has a corroborating witness (shāhid) from the ḥadīth of ʿAlī ibn Yazīd from al-Qāsim from Abī Ummāmah. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad"," and Makḥūl"," and al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah"," that the expiation (kaffārah) is upon the one who swears (al-muqsim). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19899","(19893) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us, that al-Layth narrated, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, ʿAlqamah ibn Waqqāṣ, and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtban narrated to me the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when the people of the Slander (Ahl al-Ifk) said what they said, and Allah declared her innocent of what they said. He mentioned the ḥadīth at length. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, while upon the minbar: \O company of Muslims"," who will excuse me regarding a man whose harm has reached my household? By Allah"," I know nothing regarding my household except good. And they mentioned a man about whom I know nothing except good"," and he would not enter upon my household except with me.\"" So Saʿd ibn Muʿādh al-Anṣārī — may Allah be pleased with him — stood and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws"," I will strike his neck. And if he is from our brothers of the Khazraj"," command us and we will carry out your command.\"" She said: Then Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah stood — he was the chief of the Khazraj"," and before that he had been a righteous man"," but tribal zeal (ḥamiyyah) overcame him — and said to Saʿd ibn Muʿādh: \""You have lied"," by the Lord of Allah! You will not kill him"," nor are you capable of killing him.\"" Then Uṣayd ibn Ḥuḍayr stood — and he was the paternal uncle of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh — may Allah be pleased with him — and said to Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah: \""You have lied"," by the Lord of Allah! We shall indeed kill him"," for you are a hypocrite"," arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.\"" And he mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it from another direction from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"19900","(19894) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, that Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us, that ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, that Abū al-Yamān informed me, that Shuʿayb narrated, from al-Zuhrī, who informed me: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and ʬāṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī informed me that Abū Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with him — informed them both that the people said: \O Messenger of Allah"," shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do you dispute about the moon on the night of the full moon"," when there is no cloud before it?\"" They said: \""No"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Do you dispute about the sun when there is no cloud before it?\"" They said: \""No"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Then you shall see Him thus.\"" And he mentioned the ḥadīth. He said: \""And a man will remain between the Garden and the Fire — the last of the people of the Garden to enter it — with his face turned towards the Fire"," saying: 'O Lord"," turn my face away from the Fire"," for its wind has scorched me and its flame has burned me.' Allah — Mighty and Majestic — will say: 'Then perhaps"," if I do that for you"," you will ask for something else?' He will say: 'No"," by Your Might.' His Lord will give him whatever He wishes of a covenant and pledge"," and Allah will turn his face away from the Fire. When he turns his face towards the Garden and sees its splendor"," he will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to be silent. Then he will say: 'O Lord"," bring me to the gate of the Garden.' Allah will say: 'Did you not give the covenants and pledges that you would not ask for other than what you were asking?' He will say: 'O Lord"," let me not be the most wretched of Your creation.' He will say: 'Then perhaps"," if I give you that"," you will ask for other than it?' He will say: 'No"," by Your Might"," I will not ask You for other than that.' And he mentioned the ḥadīth until he said: 'Then He will give him permission to enter the Garden"," and will say to him: \""Wish.\"" And he will wish until his wishes are exhausted"," and Allah — Blessed and Exalted — will say: \""From such-and-such and such-and-such","\"" reminding him"," until his wishes are exhausted. Allah will say to him: \""You shall have that and the like of it with it.\"" Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī said to Abū Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""You shall have that and ten times the like of it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū al-Yamān.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said"," and Ayyūb said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \""By Your Might"," I have no need of Your blessing.\"" And in the ḥadīth of Qatādah from Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet ﷺ"," in the story of Jahannam"," it will say: \""Enough"," enough"," by Your Might.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And in the ḥadīth of Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet ﷺ"," regarding the one who is dipped into the Garden"," it will be said to him: \""Have you ever seen misery at all?\"" He will say: \""No"," by Your Might and Your Majesty.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"19901","(19895) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, Maʿbad ibn Hilāl al-ʿAnazī narrated to us — and he spoke well of him — he said: I came to Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, among a group of the people of Baṣrah, and he named them for us. We asked him about the hadith of intercession, so he mentioned the hadith in its entirety — regarding his question and its answer, and their departure from him and their going to al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī. Al-Ḥasan said: He narrated to me just as he narrated to you. Then he said, meaning the Prophet ﷺ: \I shall come on the fourth occasion and praise Him with those praises"," then I shall fall down prostrate before Him. It will be said to me: 'O Muḥammad"," raise your head. Speak"," and you shall be heard. Ask"," and you shall be given. Intercede"," and your intercession shall be accepted.' I shall say: 'O my Lord"," grant permission for me regarding those who said: There is no deity but Allah.' He will say: 'That is not for you. But by My Might"," My Majesty"," and My Greatness"," I shall certainly bring out from it those who said: There is no deity but Allah.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb from Ḥammād ibn Zayd"," who added therein \""and My Majesty.\"" And it was narrated by Muslim from Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr and others from Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"19902","(19896) The two Sharīfs — Abū al-Fatḥ Nāṣir ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿUmarī and Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Ashʿath al-Qurashī — informed us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us that Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Shaybān narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, who said: A freed slave of Abū Masʿūd narrated to me, saying: Abū Masʿūd came to Ḥudhayfah and said: \Make a covenant with me.\"" He said to him: \""Has certainty not come to you?\"" He said: \""Yes"," by the Might of my Lord!\"" He said: \""Then know that the true misguidance — the real misguidance — is that you recognize what you used to reject and reject what you used to recognize. And beware of changing colours (inconsistency)"," for the religion of Allah is one.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19903","(19897) The two Sharīfs — Abū al-Fatḥ and Abū ʿAlī — informed us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us that ʿAbdullāh informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, Sharīk narrated from Ziyād ibn Fayyāḍ from Abū ʿIyāḍ, who said: I asked Ibn ʿUmar — or Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, was asked — while I was listening, about wine (khamr). He said: \No"," by the hearing of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," its sale and its purchase are not permissible.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19904","(19898) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Shawdhb al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us, Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated from Sufyān from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever swears an oath by a sūrah from the Qurʾān"," then for every verse therein there is an expiation (kaffārah). If he wishes"," he may fulfil it (by doing good)"," and if he wishes"," he may break it (and pay the expiation).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19905","(19899) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever swears an oath by a sūrah from the Qurʾān"," then for every verse therein there is a binding oath. Whoever wishes may fulfil it"," and whoever wishes may break it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19906","(19900) He said: And Sufyān narrated from Layth from Mujāhid from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it. This hadith has been narrated from two routes, both as mursal. It has also been narrated from Thābiṭ ibn al-Ḥaḥḥāk as marfūʿ and muttaṣil, but its chain is weak. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"19907","(19901) It has also been narrated regarding this from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd. Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Dabbī narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Zakariyyā narrated from al-Aʿmash from ʿAbdullāh ibn Murrah from Abū Kanaf, who said: While I was walking with Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, in the flour market, he heard a man swearing by Sūrat al-Baqarah. Ibn Masʿūd said: \Indeed"," for every verse therein there is an oath (upon him).\"" Al-Aʿmash said: I mentioned that to Ibrāhīm"," and he said: ʿAbdullāh (ibn Masʿūd) said: \""Whoever swears by the Qurʾān"," then for every verse therein there is an oath"," and whoever disbelieves in a verse of the Qurʾān has disbelieved in all of it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Jarḥ wa al-Taʿdīl 1722]"""
"19908","(19902) Abū Naṣr informed us that Abū Manṣūr narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Khālid ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated from Abū Sinān from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Hudhayl from Ḥanẓalah ibn Khuwaylid al-ʿAnbarī, who said: I went out with Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, until he reached a passageway — an elevated place in the market. He faced it and said: \I ask You for its good and the good of its people"," and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people.\"" Then he walked until he reached the steps of the mosque"," and he heard a man swearing by a sūrah from the Qurʾān. He said: \""O Ḥanẓalah"," do you see this one expiating his oath? Indeed"," for every verse there is an expiation\"" — or he said: \""an oath.\""\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by Misʿar from Abū Sinān. And Shuʿbah said: it is Suwayd ibn Ḥanẓalah. And Sufyān said: it is ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥanẓalah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously mentioned]"""
"19909","(19903) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Abū Sinān al-Shaybānī from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Hudhayl from ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥanẓalah, who said: I was with ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, and he heard a man swearing by Sūrat al-Baqarah. He said: \Do you see him expiating it? For every verse therein there is an oath upon him.\"" The statement of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd"," may Allah be pleased with him"," alongside the mursal hadith in this matter"," is evidence that swearing by the Qurʾān constitutes an oath in general terms"," while the severity in expiation is abandoned by consensus. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously mentioned]"""
"19910","(19904) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-ʿAnazī informed us, saying: I heard Abū Saʿīd ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī say: I heard Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī say: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, who said: \I have encountered the people for seventy years"," and they have been saying: Allah is the Creator"," and everything besides Him is created"," and the Qurʾān is the Word of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19911","(19905) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, he said: I heard Ibrāhīm ibn Maḥmūd say: I heard al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān say: Abū Shuʿayb informed me that Ḥafṣ al-Fard, the associate of al-Shāfiʿī, said: \The Qurʾān is created.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said to him: \""You have disbelieved in Allāh"," the Almighty.\"""""
"19912","(19906) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Shaybān ibn Farūkh narrated to us that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us that al-Zubayr ibn Saʿīd al-Hāshimī narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn Rukānah, from his father, from his grandfather, that he divorced his wife with an irrevocable divorce (al-batta) during the time of the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \What did you intend by that?\"" He said: \""One (divorce).\"" He said: \""By Allāh?\"" He said: \""By Allāh.\"" He said: \""Then it is according to what you intended.\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than him]"""
"19913","(19907) Abū al-Ḥasan informed us that al-Ḥasan informed us that Yūsuf narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Saʿīd, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly to that. Thus narrated Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim. And we have narrated it in the Book of Divorce from the ḥadīth of Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjeyr ibn ʿAbd Yazīd ibn Rukānah, from the Prophet ﷺ, in this story: \By Allāh"," I did not intend except one.\""\n\nRukānah said: \""By Allāh"," I did not intend except one.\"""""
"19914","(19908) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām al-Warrāq and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, that he heard Ibn ʿUmar, may Allāh be pleased with both of them, say: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ dispatched an expedition and appointed Usāmah ibn Zayd as its commander. The people criticized his command, so the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ stood up and said: \If you criticize his command"," you previously criticized the command of his father. By Allāh"," he is indeed worthy of command"," and he is among the most beloved of people to me"," and this one (meaning Usāmah) is among the most beloved of people to me after him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," from Ismāʿīl"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"19915","(19909) Al-Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī, may Allāh have mercy on him, narrated to us by dictation, that Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated to us that Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us, from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, who said: Abū al-Zinād informed me, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allāh be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd"," peace be upon them both"," said: 'I shall go around tonight with seventy women"," each one of whom shall bear a horseman who fights in the cause of Allāh.' His companion said to him: 'Say: In shāʾ Allāh (if Allāh wills).' But he did not say In shāʾ Allāh. He went around with all of them"," but none of them became pregnant except one woman"," who came with half a man. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad"," had he said In shāʾ Allāh"," they would all have striven in the cause of Allāh.\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah"," and al-Bukhārī extracted it from another route from Abū al-Zinād. And we have narrated in the ḥadīth of Abū Qatādah"," in the story of the spoils"," the statement of Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq"," may Allāh be pleased with him"," to the Prophet ﷺ: \""Lā hā Allāh idhan\"" — the meaning of which is \""By Allāh"," then.\"""""
"19916","(19910) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, that is Ibn al-Munādī, narrated to us that Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbd Allāh, may Allāh be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ, that he said: \Whoever swears a false oath by which he seizes the property of a Muslim\"" — or he said: \""the property of his brother\"" — \""he shall meet Allāh while He is angry with him.\"" He said: Then Allāh"," Mighty and Majestic"," revealed the confirmation of that in the Qurʾān: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allāh and their oaths for a small price…} [Āl ʿImrān:77] to the end of the verse.\n\nHe said: Then al-Ashʿath passed by and said: \""It was revealed concerning me and a man with whom we disputed over a well.\"" Al-Bukhārī extracted it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Shuʿbah"," and Muslim extracted it from other routes from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"19917","(19911) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Abū ʿAlī Hishām ibn ʿAlī ibn Hishām al-Sīrāfī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us that Shaybān Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ: \Who among people are the best?\"" He said: \""My generation"," then those who follow them"," then those who follow them"," then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose testimony will precede their oath and their oath will precede their testimony.\"" Ibrāhīm said: Our companions used to forbid us"," when we were boys"," from swearing by testimony and by covenant. The wording of both their ḥadīths is the same"," except that his saying \""then those who follow them\"" appears twice in the narration of al-Qaṭṭān.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿd ibn Ḥafṣ"," from Shaybān"," and both extracted it from another route from Manṣūr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"19918","(19912) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sālim narrate from Ismāʿīl ibn Rāfiʿ, from Khālid ibn Saʿd, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, that he said: \I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ say: 'Whoever makes a vow without naming it"," its expiation is the expiation of an oath.'\"" Thus said Khālid ibn Saʿīd"," and I think he is Khālid ibn Zayd"," who narrates from ʿUqbah the ḥadīth of archery. The authentic narration is from Abū al-Khayr"," from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir"," from the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ: \""The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath.\"" And that is understood by the scholars to refer to the vow of lajāj (compulsive vow) which takes the form of an oath. And Allāh knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19919","(19913) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Ḥamzah ibn al-Qāsim al-Imām narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿImrān al-Bayāḍī narrated to us that Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Musāfir narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Fudayk, who said: Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā al-Anṣārī narrated to me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allāh be pleased with both of them, that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \Whoever makes a vow without naming it"," its expiation is the expiation of an oath. And whoever makes a vow that he cannot fulfill"," its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\"" Ibn Musāfir did not mention al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān in his isnād.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Wakīʿ narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind and stopped it at Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allāh be pleased with both of them.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allāh have mercy on him"," said: And it has been narrated from others from ʿAbd Allāh"," likewise as a marfūʿ narration"," and it has been narrated from another route"," which is not strong"," from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj"," likewise as a marfūʿ narration.\n\nAnd if it is authentic"," it is understood by those who do not take its apparent meaning to refer to the vow of lajāj (quarrelsome vow) and anger. And Allāh knows best."""
"19920","(19914) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, may Allāh have mercy on him, narrated to us that Sufyān narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allāh be pleased with both of them, reaching the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever swears an oath and then says In shāʾ Allāh (if Allāh wills)"," he has indeed made an exception.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19921","(19915) Al-Qāḍī Abū ʿUmar Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Sinān al-Ḥīrī, Abū ʿAmr, informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Mūsā — and he was ʿAbdān al-Ahwāzī — narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes an oath and says 'In shā' Allāh","' he has the right of exception.\"" Thus I found it"," and it is in the first section of the Fawā'id of Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān — Ayyūb ibn Mūsā. And likewise it was narrated from Ibn Wahb"," from Sufyān"," from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā. However"," this hadith is known as marfūʿ (elevated to the Prophet) only from the hadith of Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"19922","(19916) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Wuhaib ibn Khālid, ʿAbd al-Wārith, and Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes an oath and then says 'In shā' Allāh","' he has the choice: if he wishes"," he may proceed"," and if he wishes"," he may leave it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"19923","(19917) The Shaykh al-Imām Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Ḥanafī (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us by dictation: The Imām, my father, informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Bishr ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAqadī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes an oath and makes an exception (istithnā')"," he has the choice: if he wishes to proceed with his oath"," he may do so"," and if he wishes to retract"," he may do so without any sin.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"19924","(19918) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: ʿAbdān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated it with a similar chain, except that he said: \I do not know except that it is from the Prophet (ﷺ)\"" — the doubt being from Ayyūb — and he said at its end: \""He retracts without having committed a violation (ḥanath).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"19925","(19919) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us: ʿAbdān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Khallād narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd said: Ayyūb used to raise this hadith (as marfūʿ), then he abandoned it. The Shaykh said: Perhaps he abandoned it due to a doubt that overcame him regarding its being raised (to the Prophet), and he is Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah al-Sakhtiyānī.\n\nAnd that has also been narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, Ḥassān ibn ʿAṭiyyah, and Kathīr ibn Farqad, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (ﷺ). However, its being raised (marfūʿ) is scarcely established except from the narration of Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, and Ayyūb also expressed doubt regarding it. And the narration of the group (al-jamāʿah) from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), is from his own statement (mawqūf), not raised (marfūʿ), and Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"19926","(19920) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, Mālik ibn Anas, and Usāmah ibn Zayd all informed me that Nāfiʿ narrated to them that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \Whoever says 'By Allah' and then says 'In shā' Allāh","' and then does not do that for which he took the oath"," he does not commit a violation (ḥanath).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19927","(19921) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Misʿar narrated from al-Qāsim — meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — who said: ʿAbdullāh — meaning Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) — said: \Whoever takes an oath and says 'In shā' Allāh","' he has indeed made an exception (istithnā').\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19928","(19922) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Bishr narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: al-Masʿūdī narrated from al-Qāsim, who said: Ibn Masʿūd said: \The exception (istithnā') is permissible in every oath.\"" And it has been narrated from ʿAṭā'"," Ṭāwūs"," and Mujāhid that the exception is permissible in divorce"," in manumission"," and in all matters. And that which has been narrated as marfūʿ (elevated) from Muʿādh regarding this is mentioned in the book of divorce. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19929","(19923) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb ibn Jibrīl al-Adīb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Shabīb al-Maʿmarī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Zurārah al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Mālik al-Lakhmī, from Makḥūl, from Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Muʿādh ibn Jabal"," when a man says to his wife"," 'You are divorced"," in shā' Allāh","' she is not divorced; and when he says to his slave"," 'You are free"," in shā' Allāh","' then he is free.\"" This hadith is narrated uniquely by Ḥumayd ibn Mālik"," and he is unknown (majhūl). There is disagreement regarding its chain of narration: it is said thus"," and it is said from him"," from Makḥūl"," from Mālik"," from Yukhāmir"," from Muʿādh; and it is said from him"," from Makḥūl"," from Muʿādh"," and it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). [Ḍaʿīf. See what the author said.]"""
"19930","(19924) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān al-Adamī narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Anṣārī narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Abī al-Ruṭayl narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aṭṭār narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \When a man takes an oath and makes an exception"," saying 'In shā' Allāh","' and then connects his speech with the exception"," and then does that for which he took the oath"," he does not commit a violation (ḥanath).\"" This is mawqūf (stopped at the Companion). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited as mawqūf"," no. 19920.]"""
"19931","(19925) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal informed us; Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl Abū Bakr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth narrated to me; my father narrated to me on the authority of my grandfather; al-Hiql ibn Ziyād narrated to me from al-Awzāʿī from Dāwūd ibn ʿAṭāʾ, a man from the people of al-Madīnah, who said: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated to me; Nāfiʿ narrated to me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: \Whoever swears an oath and then says immediately after his oath"," 'In shāʾ Allāh' (if Allah wills)"," and then breaks that oath"," the expiation for his oath is 'In shāʾ Allāh.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated before it]"""
"19932","(19926) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatāḍah al-Naḍrawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to me from his father from Sālim from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \Every exception (istithnāʾ) that is connected (to the oath) entails no breaking of oath for its maker"," but if it is not connected"," then he is a breaker of oath.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19933","(19927) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; al-Asfāṭī, meaning al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl, narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us; Sharīk narrated to us from Simāk from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \By Allah"," I shall certainly wage war against Quraysh! By Allah"," I shall certainly wage war against Quraysh!\"" Then he remained silent for a while"," then he said: \""In shāʾ Allāh.\"" [Munkar]"""
"19934","(19928) Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated it from Sharīk in the same manner, as a connected (mawṣūl) narration, and he said: \Then he remained silent for a moment"," then he said: 'In shāʾ Allāh.'\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad narrated to us; Sharīk narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Munkar]"""
"19935","(19929) Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated it from Sharīk, but he sent it as a mursal narration and did not mention the silence (sukūt).\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Sharīk narrated to us from Simāk from ʿIkrimah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \By Allah"," I shall certainly wage war against Quraysh! By Allah"," I shall certainly wage war against Quraysh! By Allah"," I shall certainly wage war against Quraysh!\"" Then he said: \""In shāʾ Allāh.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19936","(19930) Likewise, Misʿar narrated it from Simāk as a mursal narration, and he mentioned the silence at the end.\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ informed us; Ibn Bishr narrated to us from Misʿar from Simāk from ʿIkrimah, who raised it (to the Prophet), saying: \By Allah"," I shall certainly wage war against Quraysh!\"" Then he said: \""In shāʾ Allāh.\"" Then he said: \""By Allah"," I shall certainly wage war against Quraysh"," In shāʾ Allāh.\"" Then he said: \""By Allah"," I shall certainly wage war against Quraysh.\"" Then he remained silent"," then he said: \""In shāʾ Allāh.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It is possible—if this is authentic—that he (ﷺ) did not intend to attach the exception to the oath; rather"," he said that because of the words of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {And never say of anything"," 'Indeed"," I will do that tomorrow","'} [al-Kahf: 23]. [Ḍaʿīf; narrated before it]"""
"19937","(19931) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatāḍah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from al-AʿMash from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to consider the exception (istithnāʾ) valid even after a year. Then he recited: {And never say of anything, 'Indeed, I will do that tomorrow,' except [when adding], 'if Allah wills.' And remember your Lord when you forget.} [al-Kahf: 23–24] He said: \When you remember (the exception).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: He said this"," and we hold the view of Ibn ʿUmar regarding oaths. And the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) may carry the meaning that he was applying the verse"," and that he mentioned the exception after a period of time in a context similar to that in which the verse was revealed"," not in the context of an oath. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19938","(19932) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us; Ibn Muṣʿab narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated to us from his grandfather, Abū Saʿīd, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A man swears an oath and then makes an exception (istithnāʾ) in his heart.\"" He said: \""That is nothing"," until he makes the exception openly"," just as he makes the oath openly.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"19939","(19933) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr—this is the wording of the latter—both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us. He said: I said to al-Shāfiʿī: \What is the laghw (casual/inadvertent) oath?\"" He said: \""Allah knows best. As for what we hold as our position"," it is what ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said.\"" Mālik informed us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: \""The laghw of the oath is a person's saying: 'No"," by Allah","' and 'Yes"," by Allah.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated by Mālik]"""
"19940","(19934) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā al-Ḥīrī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated to us; Hishām narrated to me; my father narrated to me from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding this verse: {Allah will not impose blame upon you for what is meaningless (laghw) in your oaths} [al-Baqarah: 225]. She said: \It is a man's saying: 'No"," by Allah","' and 'Yes"," by Allah.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān. [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 6663]"""
"19941","(19935) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quq narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Ruh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us; Malik narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, used to say: \The oath of laghw (vain/inadvertent oath) is that which occurs in argumentation"," jesting"," and casual speech in which the heart is not firmly resolved. The expiation (kaffarah) is only for every oath sworn deliberately upon a matter of seriousness — whether in anger or otherwise — such as 'I shall certainly do' or 'I shall certainly abandon.' That is the binding oath for which Allah has prescribed expiation.\"" [Sahih]"""
"19942","(19936) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us; Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Maymun al-Sa'igh, one of the people of Marw, narrated from 'Ata': \The laghw in the oath\"" — he said: 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'It is the speech of a man in his household: \""No"," by Allah\"" and \""Yes"," by Allah.\""'\""\n\nAbu Dawud said: This hadith was also narrated by Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat from Ibrahim al-Sa'igh from 'Ata' from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," as a mawquf (stopped) narration. And it was narrated by al-Zuhri"," 'Abd al-Malik"," and ibn Mughwal — all of them from 'Ata' from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," also as a mawquf narration.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Likewise"," it was narrated by 'Amr ibn Dinar"," Ibn Jurayj"," and Hassan from 'Ata' from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," as a mawquf narration. [Munkar]"""
"19943","(19937) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; 'Amr and Ibn Jurayj narrated from 'Ata' who said: \I and 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr went to 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," while she was in i'tikaf at Thabir. We asked her about the words of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {Allah will not take you to task for laghw (vain oaths) in your oaths} [Al-Baqarah 225]. She said: 'No"," by Allah"," and yes"," by Allah.'\"" [Sahih; narrated previously by two narrators before it]"""
"19944","(19938) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Ruh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us; Hisham narrated from 'Ata' who said: \We came to 'A'ishah — I and 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr — while she was at Bi'r Maymun"," and we could hear the sound of the siwak from behind the screen as she was using it. She tossed a cushion toward us. He said: We asked her about several matters"," and we asked her about this verse: {Allah will not take you to task for laghw (vain oaths) in your oaths} [Al-Baqarah 225]. We said to her: 'What is laghw?' She said: 'It is the speech of people — \""We did such-and-such"," by Allah\"" and \""We made such-and-such"," by Allah.\""'\"" [Sahih; narrated previously by two narrators before it]"""
"19945","(19939) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu Mansur al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Nadrawi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; Khalid narrated from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib from Wasim from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: \The laghw oath is that you swear while you are angry.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19946","(19940) He said: And Sa'id narrated to us; 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated from Khusayf from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: \It is 'No"," by Allah' and 'Yes"," by Allah.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"19947","(19941) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzzi said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Qays informed me from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah who said: \I and 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr al-Laythi were with 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," the wife of the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him. 'Ubayd asked her about the words of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {Allah will not take you to task for laghw (vain oaths) in your oaths}. She said: 'It is when a man swears an oath based upon what he knows"," and then he does not find it to be so — there is no expiation in it.'\"" This is how 'Umar ibn Qays narrated it"," and it is not strong. The narration of the group from 'Ata' is upon the manner that has preceded in the chapter of laghw. It was also narrated from another chain from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. [Da'if]"""
"19948","(19942) Abu Bakr and Abu Zakariyya informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; the trustworthy one informed me from Ibn Shihab from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that she used to interpret this verse and say: \It is something upon which one of you swears"," intending nothing but truthfulness"," and then it turns out to be other than what he swore upon.\"" It was likewise narrated with this chain.\n\nAnd we received it from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," upon the manner that has preceded. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""
"19949","(19943) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr al-Qadi said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Ruh narrated to us; Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid regarding this verse. He said: \It is when a man swears upon something"," believing it to be so — he says: 'So-and-so is such-and-such","' when it is not so.\"" [Sahih]"""
"19950","(19944) He said: And Ruh narrated from 'Awf from al-Hasan regarding His words, the Mighty and Majestic: {Allah will not take you to task for laghw (vain oaths) in your oaths} [Al-Baqarah 225]. He said: \The laghw in oaths is that you swear upon something"," believing it to be so — there is no accountability and no expiation in it. Rather"," accountability is for that which you swear upon with knowledge.\"" [Sahih]"""
"19951","(19945) He said: And Rawḥ narrated to us, Hishām narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan, that he said: \By Allah"," I shall not do it\"" — then he does it out of forgetfulness — that is nothing. It is a lie for which he seeks Allah's forgiveness"," and there is no expiation upon him."""
"19952","(19946) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Qilābah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us, Ibn ʿAwn narrated from al-Ḥasan.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū ʿAmr al-Mustamlī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Manṣūr ibn Zādhān, Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, and Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah"," when you swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better"," then do that which is better and expiate for your oath.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Ibn ʿAwn"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19953","(19947) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Shabīb al-Maʿmarī narrated to us, Abū Kāmil al-Jaḥdarī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Simāk ibn ʿAṭiyyah, Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd, and Hushaym, among others, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," do not ask for authority"," for if you are given it as a result of asking"," you will be left to manage it"," and if you are given it without asking"," you will be helped in it. And when you swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better"," then do that which is better and expiate for your oath.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Kāmil"," and al-Bukhārī cited their narration as a supporting witness.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above.]"""
"19954","(19948) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl al-Khuzāʿī informed us, Abū Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us, Ayyūb narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Mu'addib narrated to us, ʿAffān narrated to us, Wuhibb narrated to us, Ayyūb narrated, from Abī Qilābah, and from al-Qāsim al-Tamīmī, from Zahdam al-Jarmī, who said: There was brotherhood between us and the Ashʿarīs. He said: We were with Abū Mūsā, and he brought us food containing chicken meat. Among the people was a ruddy man resembling the freedmen from Taymullāh. Abū Mūsā said: \Come forward and eat","\"" meaning him. He said: \""I saw him eating something foul"," so I swore that I would never eat it.\"" He said: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating from it.\"" Then he related that he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group of the Ashʿarīs to ask him for mounts. He came while he was distributing a herd of camels from the ṣadaqah. I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," give us mounts","\"" while he was angry. He said: \""By Allah"," I will not give you mounts"," and I do not have anything to mount you on.\"" Then a herd of camels with white humps was brought"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us five camels with white humps. I said: \""We have taken advantage of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; we shall never prosper.\"" So we came to him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you swore that you would not give us mounts.\"" He said: \""It was not I who mounted you"," but Allah mounted you. By Allah"," I do not swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better except that I do that which is better and expiate for my oath.\"" This is the wording of Wuhibb's ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿUmar"," both from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb. And Muslim narrated it from Abī Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī from ʿAffān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19955","(19949) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us, Ḥāmid ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us, Sharīḥ narrated to us, Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Kaysān, from Abī Ḥāzim, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever swears an oath and then sees something other than it that is better"," let him do it and expiate for his oath.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Marwān. And likewise ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Muṭṭalib narrated it from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ"," from his father"," from Abī Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and that has preceded in the Book of Siyar.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1650.]"""
"19956","(19950) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hishām and Abū al-Rabīʿ — who separated them — both said: Ḥammād narrated to us, from Ghaylān ibn Jarīr, from Abī Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group of the Ashʿarīs to ask him for mounts. He said: \By Allah"," I will not give you mounts"," and I do not have anything to mount you on.\"" He said: We stayed as long as Allah willed. Then camels were brought"," and he ordered for us three camels with white humps. When we departed"," we said — or some of us said to others — \""May Allah not bless us. We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him for mounts"," and he swore that he would not give us mounts"," then he gave us mounts. So we went to him and informed him.\"" He said: \""It was not I who mounted you"," but Allah mounted you. By Allah"," if Allah wills"," I do not swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better except that I expiate my oath and do that which is better.\"" This is the wording of Khalaf's ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," and Muslim narrated it from Khalaf ibn Hishām"," Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabīb"," and Qutaybah"," all from Ḥammād ibn Zayd. And likewise ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā"," Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī"," and others narrated it from Ḥammād ibn Zayd.\n\nAnd a group narrated it from Ḥammād with doubt: \""except that I expiate my oath and do that which is better","\"" or he said: \""except that I do that which is better and expiate my oath.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19957","(19951) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed him, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn informed us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated. They mentioned it with its chain and its meaning with doubt. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Nuʿmān from Ḥammād with doubt.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above.]"
"19958","(19952) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqri' informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abī Qilābah, from Zahdam al-Jarmī, who said: And al-Qāsim al-Kulīnī narrated to me, from Zahdam al-Jarmī — and I preserve al-Qāsim's ḥadīth better — who said: We were with Abū Mūsā, and he called for a table spread upon which was chicken meat. A ruddy man from Banī Taymullāh, resembling the freedmen, entered. Abū Mūsā, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: \Come forward","\"" but he hesitated. He said: \""Come forward"," for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating it","\"" or he said: \""eating from it.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I saw him eating something"," and I found it repulsive"," so I swore that I would not eat from it.\"" He said: \""Come forward"," I will inform you about that: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By Allah"," I do not swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better except that I expiate my oath and dissolve it. Go"," for it is Allah who has mounted you.'\"" This is how Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated it"," and he is among the firm and precise memorizers"," from Ḥammād ibn Zayd. And others narrated it from him and said in this ḥadīth: \""except that I do that which is better and dissolve it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 5517.]"""
"19959","(19953) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wāqid, from Busr ibn ʿUbaydillāh, from Ibn ʿĀ'idh, from Abī al-Dardā', may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Allah gave His Messenger camels as spoils"," and he distributed them. Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī said: 'Give me some.' He said: 'No.' He said this three times"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'By Allah"," I will not do it.' He said: Four camels with white humps remained"," and he said to him: 'O Abā Mūsā"," take them.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I asked you and you refused"," and you swore"," and I feared that some worry had befallen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'When I swear an oath and then see that something other than it is more excellent"," I expiate for my oath and do that which is more excellent.'\""\n\nThis corroborates the narration of those who did not express doubt in the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Zayd.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"19960","(19954) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Harawī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm and Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl both said: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām narrated to us, Shaybān ibn Farrūkh narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Julūdī narrated to me, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Māsarjasī narrated to us, Shaybān ibn Farrūkh narrated to us, Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us, al-Ḥasan narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah"," do not ask for authority"," for if you are given it as a result of asking"," you will be left to manage it"," and if you are given it without asking"," you will be helped in it. And when you swear an oath and then see something other than it that is better"," expiate for your oath and do that which is better.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Shaybān"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Abī al-Nuʿmān and Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl from Jarīr.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"19961","(19955) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azdī narrated to us, al-Sahmī — meaning ʿAbdullāh ibn Bakr — narrated to us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ, the same hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"
"19962","(19956) Abū Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khālid narrated from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and he mentioned it with the same meaning, and he said: \So expiate for your oath and do that which is better.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"19963","(19957) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkār narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah, and he mentioned it with the same meaning, and he said: \So expiate for your oath and come to that which is better.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"19964","(19958) And Abū Bakr ibn Rajāʾ al-Adīb informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Baghawī narrated to us, Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl al-Anmāṭī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Yūnus, Ḥumayd, Thābit, and Ḥabīb, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah — may Allah be pleased with him — that the Prophet ﷺ said, and he mentioned it with the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"
"19965","(19959) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr al-Tājir narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Ḥinnāʾī narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh — meaning Ibn Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAnbarī — narrated to us, al-Muʿtamir — meaning Ibn Sulaymān — narrated from his father, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah — may Allah be pleased with him — from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \When one of you swears an oath and then sees other than it to be better than it"," let him expiate for his oath and let him look to that which is better and do it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"19966","(19960) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Khalaf narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us, Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah — may Allah be pleased with him — that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to him: \O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān","\"" and he mentioned its meaning"," except that he said: \""So if you see other than it to be better than it"," expiate for your oath"," then come to that which is better.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," except that he referred the narrations to the narration of Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim from al-Ḥasan. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"19967","(19961) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Mālik ibn Anas informed me, from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with him — from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \Whoever swears an oath and then sees better than it"," let him expiate for his oath and let him act (upon the better).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1650.]"""
"19968","(19962) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Mu'adhdhin informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb informed us, Abū Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī narrated to us, Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with him — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you swears an oath and then sees better than that upon which he swore"," let him expiate his oath and let him do that which is better than it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"19969","(19963) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Abū Jaʿfar ibn Ḥurayḥ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ṭarīf Abū Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, from Tamīm al-Ṭāʾī, from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you swears an oath and then sees other than it to be better than it"," let him expiate it and let him come to that which is better.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ṭarīf. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1651.]"""
"19970","(19964) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: The hadiths of Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim, and Abū Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with them.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah — the hadith of each one of them was narrated, some of which indicate the breach (of the oath) before the expiation, and some of which indicate the expiation after the breach, and most of them said: \Let him expiate his oath and let him come to that which is better.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Sijistānī.]"""
"19971","(19965) The Shaykh, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: The evidence of al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy upon him, in this matter is what Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, and Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: If one gives expiation before the oath is broken by means of feeding, I hope that it will suffice him. This is because we maintain that Allah, the Most High, has a right over His servants in their persons and their wealth. The right that pertains to their wealth, if they bring it forward before its due time, is sufficient. The basis for this is that the Prophet ﷺ collected from al-ʿAbbās the charity of a year before it became due, and that the Muslims brought forward the Ṣadaqat al-Fiṭr before the day of Fiṭr occurred. Thus, we have made the rights pertaining to wealth analogous to this.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This ḥadīth has already been mentioned in the Book of Zakāh. [Ṣaḥīh — for al-Shāfiʿī]"
"19972","(19966) ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī al-Mu'adhdhin informed us that Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Simsār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd al-ʿAbdī narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Zakarīyā narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Dīnār from al-Ḥakam ibn ʤtaybah from Ḥujayyah ibn ʿAdī from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, that al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, may Allah be pleased with him, asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about paying his charity before it became due, and he granted him permission to do so. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"19973","(19967) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that he would sometimes give expiation for his oath before breaking it, and sometimes he would give it after breaking it. [Ḥasan]"
"19974","(19968) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that Abū ʿUmar ʿĪsā ibn Abī ʿImrān al-Bazzār in al-Ramlah narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us that al-Awzāʿī narrated to me that al-Zuhrī narrated from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am ruined!\"" He said: \""Woe to you"," what is the matter?\"" He said: \""I had intercourse with my wife on a day in Ramadan.\"" He said: \""Free a slave.\"" He said: \""I cannot find one.\"" He said: \""Fast two consecutive months.\"" He said: \""I am unable.\"" He said: \""Feed sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""I cannot find (the means).\"" Then the Prophet ﷺ was brought a basket (ʿaraq) containing fifteen ṣāʿ of dates. He said: \""Take it and give it in charity.\"" He said: \""To those poorer than my family? By Allah"," there is no one between the two lava tracts of Madīnah more in need than my family.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled until his teeth became visible"," then he said: \""Take it"," seek forgiveness from Allah"," and feed it to your family.\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: This isnād is ṣaḥīḥ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Hishāq ibn Ziyād also narrated it from al-Awzāʿī"," and its mention has already passed in the Book of Ḥajj. Ibn al-Mubārak also narrated it from al-Awzāʿī"," and he made the estimation of the ʿaraq in the narration of al-Zuhrī from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb.\n\nIt was also narrated from the ḥadīth of Manṣūr from al-Zuhrī"," and it has already passed in the Book of Fasting. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19975","(19969) As for the ḥadīth that Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that Mālik informed us from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned the ḥadīth of the one who had intercourse with his wife in Ramadan. ʿAṭāʾ said: I asked Saʿīd: \How much was in that basket (ʿaraq)?\"" He said: \""Between fifteen and twenty ṣāʿ.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: The most that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab said was a mudd and a quarter"," or a mudd and a third. This is merely a doubt introduced by Ibn al-Musayyab. The ʿaraq"," as I have described"," was estimated at fifteen ṣāʿ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The ḥadīth of Ibn al-Musayyab is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī is not more reliable than others. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19976","(19970) It has also been narrated from Ibn al-Musayyab through another route, with certainty, as fifteen ṣāʿ, without doubt. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adamī in Baghdād informed us that Muḥammad ibn Maslamah al-Wāsiṭī informed us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿĀmir from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, and from al-Zuhrī from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ…\"" and he mentioned the ḥadīth of the one who had intercourse (al-wāqiʿ). In it"," he said: \""Feed sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""I cannot find (the means).\"" So the Prophet ﷺ was brought a basket (ʿaraq) containing fifteen ṣāʿ of dates. He said: \""Take it and feed sixty poor persons with it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — mentioned one entry before]"""
"19977","(19971) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Aḥmad informed me that Abū Bakr ibn Dallūyah narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to me that my father narrated to me that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from ʿUmar ibn Saʿīd from Ṭalq ibn Ḥabīb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, who said: \A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ…\"" and he mentioned the ḥadīth of the one who had intercourse (al-wāqiʿ). In it"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a large basket (miktal) containing fifteen ṣāʿ of food"," which amounted to sixty quarters (rubʿ). He said: \""Go and give this in charity.\""\n\nThis has already passed from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash from Ṭalq in the Book of Ẓihār. [Ṣaḥīḥ — mentioned before it]"""
"19978","(19972) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us that Hishām narrated from Yaḥyā from Abū Salamah from Zayd ibn Thābit, who used to say: \The feeding of the poor in the expiation of an oath is a mudd of wheat for each poor person.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — mentioned before it]"""
"19979","(19973) Abū Zakarīyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Mālik ibn Anas informed us from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, used to expiate his oath by feeding ten poor persons, giving each of them a mudd of wheat, and he would free a slave when he made the oath emphatic. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"19980","(19974) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāʾinī informed us that Zāhir ibn Aḥmad narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: \For each poor person"," a mudd of wheat"," and a quarter of that is as a condiment (idām).\""\n\nAnd it is narrated from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with both of them"," who said: \""For each poor person"," a mudd"," a mudd.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"19981","(19975) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani informed us, saying: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi informed us: Yusuf ibn Sa'id ibn Muslim informed me: Hajjaj narrated to us from Ibn Lahi'ah from Sulayman ibn Musa from 'Ata', who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say in this mosque: \There are three matters in which the measure is a mudd"," a mudd: in the expiation of an oath (kaffarat al-yamin)"," in the expiation of zihar (kaffarat al-zihar)"," and in the ransom of feeding a poor person.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19982","(19976) Abu Ahmad al-Mihranjani informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanjī informed us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: \I did not find the people except that when they gave the expiation of an oath"," they gave a mudd of wheat by the smaller mudd"," and they considered that sufficient for them.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Malik]"""
"19983","(19977) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah al-Khusrujirdi informed us: Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ghitrif informed us: Abu Khalifah informed us: al-Hawdi narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who both said regarding the expiation (of an oath): \A mudd of wheat or a mudd of barley.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19984","(19978) As for what al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad, saying: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us from al-A'mash from Shaqiyq ibn Salamah from Yasar ibn Numayr, who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I swear an oath that I will not give certain people anything"," then it seems to me that I should give it to them. When you see me having done that"," then feed on my behalf ten poor persons"," between every two poor persons a sa' of wheat or a sa' of dates.\""\n\nThis was something that 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," held as his view. Perhaps he considered it recommended to give more"," and that less than that would also be sufficient"," based on what we have mentioned. [Sahih]"""
"19985","(19979) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: 'Ali ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil al-Khuza'i informed us: Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani informed us: 'Ali ibn al-Madini informed us: Hisham Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Hilal al-Wazzan informed me, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Layla say: A man came to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," provide me with a mount.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I will not provide you with a mount.\"" The man said: \""By Allah"," you must provide me with a mount.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I will not provide you with a mount.\"" The man said: \""By Allah"," you must provide me with a mount; I am a traveler (ibn al-sabil) and my mount has worn out.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I will not provide you with a mount","\"" until he had sworn approximately twenty oaths. A man from the Ansar said to him: \""What is your matter with the Commander of the Faithful?\"" The man said: \""By Allah"," he must provide me with a mount; I am a traveler and my mount has worn out.\"" 'Umar then said: \""By Allah"," I will provide you with a mount","\"" then: \""By Allah"," I will provide you with a mount.\"" Then he provided him with a mount and said: \""Whoever swears an oath then sees other than it to be better than it"," let him do that which is better and expiate for his oath.\"" 'Ali ibn al-Madini said: \""This is a hadith with a strange chain; the expiation is one (single expiation).\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""That is not clearly established in the hadith. It is narrated from Mujahid from Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," that he swore multiple times and made a single expiation. It is also narrated from Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," regarding the emphasis of an oath — which is its repetition concerning a single matter — that there is another view.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19986","(19980) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Malik informed us.\n\n(And) Abu Ahmad al-Mihranjani informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanjī informed us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from Nafi' from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who used to say: \Whoever swears an oath and emphasizes it"," then breaks it"," upon him is the freeing of a slave or clothing ten poor persons. And whoever swears an oath and does not emphasize it"," upon him is the feeding of ten poor persons"," for each poor person a mudd of wheat. Whoever cannot find (the means)"," then fasting for three days.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Bukayr"," and the narration of al-Shafi'i is abbreviated: \""Whoever swears an oath and emphasizes it"," upon him is the freeing of a slave.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""The apparent meaning of the Book"," then the apparent meaning of the Sunnah"," then what we have narrated in this chapter from 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him — even if it is mursal — none of that distinguishes between the emphasis of an oath and the absence of its emphasis. And Allah knows best.\"" [Sahih]"""
"19987","(19981) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us: Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us: Salamah ibn 'Alqamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Sirin that Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, swore an oath and made expiation. He ordered the poor persons to be brought into the bayt al-mal (public treasury). He ordered a bowl of tharid to be brought and it was presented to them, and they ate. Then he clothed each one of them with a garment — either a mu'qad or a zahrani garment.\n\nThe Sheikh said: \It is as though he did not consider the expiation by what he gave them of the tharid to be sufficient"," so he gave each one of them a garment.\""\n\nIt is narrated from Zahdam al-Jarmi from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he swore an oath and gave ten poor persons ten garments"," for each poor person a garment of mu'qad cloth from Hajar. [Da'if]"""
"19988","(19982) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us: Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us: 'Attab ibn Bashir informed us: Khasayf narrated to us from 'Ata', Mujahid, and 'Ikrimah, who said: \For each poor person (there should be) a garment — a shirt (qamis)"," or an izār"," or a ridā' (cloak).\"" I said to Khasayf: \""What if he is well-off?\"" He said: \""Whatever he does"," it is good. Whoever cannot find these means"," then fasting for three days.\"" He mentioned that in the recitation of Ubayy they are to be consecutive. And in the narration of Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata'"," he said regarding the expiation of an oath: \""A mudd"," a mudd"," and the clothing is a garment"," a garment.\"" [Da'if]"""
"19989","(19983) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali narrated to us from his father that a man narrated to him, saying: He asked 'Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, about a man who swore that he would not pray in the mosque of his people. 'Imran, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," say: 'There is no vow (nadhr) in disobedience to Allah"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.'\"" I said: \""O Abu Nujayd"," our companion is not well-off; with what should he expiate?\"" He said: \""If a group of people were to come to one of the commanders and he clothed each one of them with a qalansuwah (cap)"," the people would say: 'He has clothed them.'\""\n\nIt is narrated from Salman"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he said: \""An excellent garment is the tubban (short loincloth).\"" [Da'if]"""
"19990","(19984) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Malik ibn Anas informed me from Hilal ibn Usamah from 'Ata' ibn Yasar from 'Umar ibn al-Hakam, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I had a slave-girl who used to tend my sheep. She lost one of the sheep"," and I asked her about it. She said: \""A wolf ate it.\"" I became upset — and I am from the children of Adam — so I struck her face. I have a slave (to free); should I free her?' The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said to her: 'Where is Allah?' She said: 'He is in the heaven.' He said: 'Who am I?' She said: 'You are the Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Free her.'\""\n\nThis is how Malik ibn Anas narrated it. And it was narrated by Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Hilab ibn Abi Maymunah from 'Ata' ibn Yasar from Mu'awiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami. [Sahih. Narrated by Malik"," 1311]"""
"19991","(19985) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu 'Abd Allah Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Susi and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us: my father narrated to me: al-Awza'i narrated to me: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me: from Hilal ibn Abi Maymuna: 'Ata' ibn Yasar narrated to me: Mu'awiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith concerning omens and sneezing during Salah. He said: Then I looked at a flock of sheep of mine that a slave-girl of mine was tending towards Uhud and al-Jawwaniyyah, and I found that a wolf had taken one of them. I am a son of Adam; I became angry as they become angry, so I struck her a blow. Then I went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and informed him, and he considered it grave on my account. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not set her free? He said: Rather, bring her to me. He said: I brought her to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he said to her: Where is Allah? She said: In the heaven. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: She is a believer; so set her free.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of al-Awza'i, without the story of the slave-girl. [Sahih. It was mentioned before it.]"
"19992","(19986) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me: from Ibn Shihab: from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah: that a man from the Ansar came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with a black slave-girl and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am obligated to free a believing slave. If you consider this one a believer, I shall set her free. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you believe in the resurrection after death? She said: Yes. He said: Set her free.\n\nThis is a mursal narration. It has also been said: from 'Awn ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him). And it has been said: from 'Awn, from his father, from his grandfather. It has already been mentioned in the book of al-Zihar.\n\n[Sahih. Ibn Kathir 2/374]"
"19993","(19987) Abu Tahir al-Faqih narrated to us: Hajib ibn Ahmad al-Tusi narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Munib narrated to us: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to me: from his father: from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: The child of adultery is the worst of the three. [Sahih]"
"19994","(19988) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih in Bukhari narrated to us: Salih ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani and 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Jarir narrated to us: from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, and he mentioned it with the same wording, adding: Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: That I benefit from a whip in the cause of Allah is more beloved to me than that I should set free a child of fornication. [Sahih]"
"19995","(19989) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-'Anazi narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us: from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah: from his father: from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: The child of adultery is the worst of the three. [Sahih]"
"19996","(19990) Abu Tahir al-Faqih narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Qattan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: al-Thawri narrated to us: from Mansur: from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd: from Jabir: from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: The child of fornication shall not enter Paradise.\n\nThat was also narrated from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), as a marfu' narration. [Da'if. Ibn Khuzaymah: 57]"
"19997","(19991) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: from al-Zuhri: from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: It reached 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: That I benefit from a whip in the cause of Allah is more beloved to me than that I should set free a child of adultery. And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: The child of adultery is the worst of the three. And the deceased is punished by the weeping of the living. 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Hurayrah; he heard incorrectly and responded incorrectly. As for his statement that benefiting from a whip in the cause of Allah is more beloved to him than setting free a child of adultery, it was only that when the verse was revealed: {But he did not assault the steep ascent. And what will make you know what the steep ascent is? It is the freeing of a slave} [al-Balad 11-13], it was said: O Messenger of Allah, we have nothing to set free, except that one of us has a black slave-girl who serves him and attends to him. If we were to command them to commit fornication and they bore children, we could set them free. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: That I benefit from a whip in the cause of Allah is more beloved to me than that I should command fornication and then set free the child. As for his statement: The child of adultery is the worst of the three, the hadith was not like that. Rather, there was a man among the hypocrites who used to harm the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he said: Who will relieve me of so-and-so? It was said: O Messenger of Allah, despite what he is afflicted with, he is a child of adultery. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: He is the worst of the three. And Allah, the Most High, says: {And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another} [al-An'am 164]. As for his statement that the deceased is punished by the weeping of the living, the hadith was not like that. Rather, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by the house of a Jew who had died, and his family was weeping over him, and he said: They are weeping over him, and he is being punished. And Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: {Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity} [al-Baqarah 286].\n\nSalamah ibn al-Fadl al-Abrash narrates objectionable narrations. It has also been narrated from Abu Sulaymani al-Shami, who is Burd ibn Sinan, from al-Zuhri, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), as a mursal narration, regarding the freeing of a child of adultery. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"
"19998","(19992) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Lakhmi narrated to us: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Hisham: from his father: from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said regarding the child of adultery: There is upon him nothing of the sin of his parents. {And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another} [Fatir 18]. Some of the weak narrators raised it to the Prophet, but the correct version is that it is mawquf (stopped at the Companion). [Sahih]"
"19999","(19993) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us: from Ibrahim: from Muhammad ibn Qays: from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: The child of adultery is the worst of the three, when he does the deed of his parents. [Da'if]"
"20000","(19994) Abu Sa'd al-Malini narrated to us: Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Abu Umayyah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us: Habban ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us: from Dawud ibn 'Ali: from his father: from his grandfather Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: The child of adultery is the worst of the three, when he does the deed of his parents.\n\nThis chain of narration is weak, and what precedes it is not strong. [Da'if]"
"20001","(19995) This narration is reported as a statement from Sufyān al-Thawrī. It was relayed to us by ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān, who was informed by Abū al-Qāsim al-Ṭabarānī, who narrated to us from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, who narrated to us from Abū Ḥudhayfah, who narrated to us from Sufyān, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about the child of zinā (illegitimate child), so he said: \He is the worst of the three.\"" Sufyān said: \""That is"," if he commits the same sin as his parents.\"" [Weak]"""
"20002","(19996) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Farrāʾ informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Muslim al-Mulāʾī narrated from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \The child of zinā is the worst of the three"," because his parents have repented.\"" [Weak]"""
"20003","(19997) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated, saying: Sufyān mentioned, from a man, from al-Ḥasan, who said: \The child of the adulteress was called the worst of the three because his mother said to him: 'You are not the son of the father to whom you are attributed.' So he killed her"," and thus he was named the worst of the three.\"" [Weak]"""
"20004","(19998) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated, that it reached him from al-Maqburī, that Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a man upon whom the obligation of manumission (freeing a slave) rests: \May he free a child of zinā?\"" So Abū Hurayrah said: \""Yes.\"" [Weak]"""
"20005","(19999) He said: And Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar freed a child of zinā and his mother. [Weak]"
"20006","(20000) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAmr narrated to me; al-Zubayr ibn Mūsā narrated from Umm Ḥakīm bint Ṭāriq, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said regarding the children of zinā: \Free them and treat them well.\"" [Weak]"""
"20007","(20001) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Thawr ibn Yazīd, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Qurashī, that Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked about the child of zinā and the child of a legitimate union in the matter of manumission (as an act of expiation). He said: \Look at which of the two has the greater value.\"" So they found that the child of zinā had the greater value by one dīnār"," and so he commanded them to free him. [Good]"""
"20008","(20002) He said: And Sufyān narrated from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, that he considered the child of zinā and others to be equal in the matter of manumission.\n\nAnd from Firās, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \Look at which of the two has the greater value.\"" [Good]"""
"20009","(20003) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar freed a slave boy of his who was a child of zinā.\"" [Authentic. Previously referenced under number 1999.]"""
"20010","(20004) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Haytham al-Baṣrī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated from Shuʿbah, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he freed a child of zinā and said: \Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) have commanded us to show kindness to those who are worse than him.\"" Allah"," Blessed and Exalted"," said: {Either [freedom as] a grace afterward"," or ransom} [Muḥammad: 4]. And it is narrated from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he disliked it. [Authentic]"""
"20011","(20005) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, he said: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, he said: Abū Ṣāliḥ and Ibn Bukayr both said: Al-Layth narrated to us, he said: ʿUqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihāb, he said: Abū Ḥasan, the freedman of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith, informed me — and he was among the early freedmen of Quraysh and among their people of knowledge and righteousness — that he heard a woman saying to ʿAbdullāh ibn Nawfal, seeking his legal opinion regarding an illegitimate child (ibn zinā) in her neck (i.e., a slave she owned): ʿAbdullāh ibn Nawfal said to her: \I do not think that the emancipation of an illegitimate child fulfills the neck (manumission) that is incumbent upon you.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn Nawfal said: I heard ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \""That I carry two sandals in the cause of Allah is more beloved to me than that I emancipate an illegitimate child.\"" [Weak]"""
"20012","(20006) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, he said: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us, he said: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the verse of the expiation of oaths, he said: \He has the choice among these three initial options. If he does not find anything from that"," then fasting three consecutive days.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Layth ibn Abī Sulaym"," from Mujāhid"," from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," that he said: \""Everything in the Qurʾān where 'or' (aw) appears"," it indicates a choice. But when it says 'if he does not find' (fa-in lam yajid)"," then it reverts to the first"," the first.\"" [Weak]"""
"20013","(20007) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed me by way of ijāzah from Abū al-Walīd, he said: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, he said: Aḥmad narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yūnus narrated from al-Ḥasan: that he saw no harm in separating the three days in the expiation of an oath.\n\nAbū al-Walīd and others besides Hushaym said: \They used to see no harm in that.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20014","(20008) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, he said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, he said: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, he said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, he said: Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated from al-Rabīʿ, from Abū al-ʿĀliyah, from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to recite: \fasting three consecutive days\"" (fa-ṣiyām thalāthat ayyām mutatābiʿāt). [Good]"""
"20015","(20009) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, he said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, he said: Muḥammad, meaning Ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam, informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Mālik informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, he said: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, he said: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, he said: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Mālik narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Qays al-Makkī, that he said: I was performing ṭawāf with Mujāhid when a man came and asked him about the fast of expiation — \Is it to be consecutive?\"" Ḥumayd said: I said"," \""No.\"" So Mujāhid struck me on my chest and said: \""In the recitation of Ubayy it is mutatābiʿāt (consecutive).\"" [Good]"""
"20016","(20010) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, he said: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us, he said: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, he said: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from ʬāʾ or Ṭāwūs, he said: \If he wishes"," he may separate them.\"" Mujāhid said to him: \""In the recitation of ʿAbdullāh it is mutatābiʿah (consecutive).\"" He said: \""Then it is consecutive.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20017","(20011) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ḥajjāj informed me, he said: I asked ʿAṭāʾ about the fast in the expiation of an oath. He said: \If he wishes"," he may separate them.\"" I said: \""But in the recitation of ʿAbdullāh it is mutatābiʿah.\"" He said: \""Then we submit to the Book of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20018","(20012) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us, he said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ibn ʿAwn, from Ibrāhīm, he said: \In our recitation regarding the expiation of an oath: 'three consecutive days' (thalāthat ayyām mutatābiʿāt).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The narration of Ibn Abī Najīḥ in my book is from ʿAṭāʾ"," while in all other narrations it is from Ṭāwūs.\n\n(t) And it is narrated from al-Aʿmash that Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) used to recite: \""fasting three consecutive days\"" (fa-ṣiyām thalāthat ayyām mutatābiʿāt). All of that is mursal narrations from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and Allah knows best. [Authentic]"""
"20019","(20013) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, he said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, he said: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān al-Murādī narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated from al-Awzāʿī.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in another place, he said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, he said: Baḥr ibn Naṣr ibn Sābiq al-Khawlānī narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated from al-Awzāʿī, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah has pardoned my ummah for their mistakes"," their forgetfulness"," and that which they are coerced into.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Rabīʿ: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," Allah has pardoned me.\""\n\nThus he said in one of the two places from Abū al-ʿAbbās from Baḥr. And that has already passed from Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Sūsī and others from Abū al-ʿAbbās from al-Rabīʿ"," and it is the more well-known. A group among the Egyptians and others narrated it from al-Rabīʿ"," and by it he is known. Al-Buwayṭī and al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī Muʿāwiyah followed him in that. And al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Awzāʿī but did not mention ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr in his chain. [Good for other than it]"""
"20020","(20014) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, he said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, he said: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, he said: Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," Allah has pardoned my ummah for what occurs within their souls and for that which they are coerced into"," unless they speak of it or act upon it.\"" Thus he said"," from Abū Hurayrah. And it is apparent that ʿAṭāʾ heard it from both perspectives together"," and they are two ḥadīths"," each of which conveys what is intended from its meaning"," and in both of them together is the removal of the effect of coercion.\n\nAnd Ibn Abī Awfā narrated it from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," raising it"," in the ḥadīth of the soul (ḥadīth al-nafs) and whisperings"," with its meaning.\n\nAnd his statement \""unless they speak of it or act upon it\"" refers back to the ḥadīth of the soul"," not to coercion"," and Allah knows best.\n\n[Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"20021","(20015) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us, that Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Isbahani informed us, that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Karim narrated to us, that 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, that my paternal uncle narrated to me, that my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from Thawr ibn Yazid al-Himsi, from Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Abi Salih, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \There is no divorce and no manumission in a state of coercion (ighlaq).\""\n\nAbu Dawud narrated it in the Sunan from 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd. [Weak. Previously referenced under number 7/15097]"""
"20022","(20016) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisi informed us, that Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah al-Isbahani narrated to us, that Abu Ahmad ibn Faris narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to me, that Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ma'n, who heard Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrate from his father, from his grandfather, who heard 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Al-Hin (the appointed period) is six months.\""\n\n[Weak. Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Tarikh al-Kabir 4/1]"""
"20023","(20017) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us, that Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us, that Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us, that Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Zabyan, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \Al-Hin (the appointed period) may be a morning or an evening.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20024","(20018) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, that Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, that Muslim narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Mayssarah, that a man asked Ibn al-Musayyib, saying: \I have sworn that I will not speak to a man for a hin (period).\"" He said: \""[Allah says:] 'It gives its fruit every hin (season) by the permission of its Lord' [Ibrahim: 25].\"" He said: \""It is the date palm"," whose fruit may appear for one month or two months. Thus we consider al-hin to be two months.\"" [Hasan]"""
"20025","(20019) And Abu 'Abdullah narrated to us, that Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, that Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, that Zaidah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Minhal, from 'Ikrimah, who said: \Al-Hin (the appointed period) is six months.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20026","(20020) And Abu 'Abdullah narrated to us, that Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us, that Muhammad narrated to us, that Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, that Ibn al-Ghasil narrated to me, that 'Ikrimah informed me, saying: \'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz sent for me and said: 'I have sworn that I will not do such-and-such for a hin (period). What is the hin that cannot be attained?' So he recited: 'Has there come upon man a hin (period) of time?' [al-Insan: 1] — no one knows how long has passed since Allah created him. As for the hin that is attained"," it is the saying of Allah"," the Most High: 'It gives its fruit every hin (season)' [Ibrahim: 25] — that is"," from the time of the harvesting of the dates to the time of its fruit.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20027","(20021) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, that Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, that 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us, that Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: \And you will surely know his news after a hin (period)\"" [Sad: 88] — he said: \""After death.\"" And His words: \""And in Thamud"," when it was said to them: 'Enjoy yourselves until a hin (period)'\"" [al-Dhariyat: 43] — he said: \""Three days.\"" And regarding His words: \""It gives its fruit every hin (season)\"" [Ibrahim: 25] — he said: \""Every seven months.\"" And it is narrated from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman that he said: \""Al-Hin (the appointed period) is one year.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20028","(20022) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, that Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, that Abu Hafs Yazid ibn Kaisan narrated to us: Tawus was asked — and I was with him — about a man who swore that he would not speak to a man for a zaman (period). He said: \Al-Zaman (the period) is two months or three"," so long as he has not fixed a specific term.\"" Their differing regarding al-hin and the differing meanings of al-hin in its various contexts is evidence that al-hin has no fixed endpoint when used in an absolute sense. The same applies to al-zaman. And Allah knows best. [Hasan]"""
"20029","(20023) Abu al-Fath Hilal ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far in Baghdad informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, that Ibrahim ibn Mushajjar narrated to us, that Salamah ibn Salih al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Khalid, from 'Abd al-Karim Abi Umayyah, from Ibn Buraidah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \I will not leave the mosque until I inform you of a verse or a surah that was not revealed to any prophet after Sulayman other than myself.\"" He said: \""So he walked"," and I followed him until he reached the door of the mosque. He placed one of his feet outside the threshold of the mosque while the other remained inside. I said to myself: 'He has forgotten.' Then he turned to me with his face and said: 'With what do you begin the Qur'an when you open the prayer?' I said: 'With Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim [al-Fatihah: 1].' He said: 'It is it.' Then he went out.\"" Its chain of narration is weak. [Weak]"""
"20030","(20024) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me, that Abu 'Amr al-Hayri narrated to us, that 'Abdullah ibn Shirawayh narrated to us, that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi narrated to us, that Yahya ibn Hasssan narrated to us, that Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \What an excellent condiment is vinegar!\"" Muslim narrated it in the Sahih from al-Darimi. [Sahih. Muslim 2051]"""
"20031","(20025) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Abū Bishr from Abū Sufyān from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) asked his family for condiments (udum). They said, \We have nothing but vinegar.\"" So he called for it and began eating from it"," saying: \""What an excellent condiment vinegar is! What an excellent condiment vinegar is!\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2052]\n\n---"""
"20032","(20026) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal informed us: Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: ʤmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaḥyā al-Aslamī narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Umayyah al-Aʿwar from Yūsuf ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām, who said: I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) take a piece of barley bread, place a date upon it, and say: \This is the condiment (idām) of this.\"" Then he ate it.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]\n\n---"""
"20033","(20027) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated it (marfūʿan): \It is not permissible for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days. They meet"," and each turns away from the other. The best of the two is the one who initiates the salām.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]\n\n---"""
"20034","(20028) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Hilāl narrated from his father, who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is not permissible for a believer to forsake a believer for more than three days. When three days have passed"," he should meet him and offer salām. If he responds"," then they share in the reward. If he does not respond"," then the Muslim is freed from the sin of forsaking"," and the burden falls upon the one who refused.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\n---"""
"20035","(20029) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us. They both said: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us: Abū Naʿāmah al-ʿAdawī narrated from Muslim ibn Budayl from Iyās ibn Zuhayr from Suwayd ibn Hubayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The best wealth of a person is a productive mare (muhratun maʾmūrah) or a fruitful palm row (sikkatun maʾbūrah).\""\n\nIn the narration of al-Dūrī"," he said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say.\n\n(Ġ) Abū ʿUbayd said: \""Sikkah\"" means the selected palm trees"," and \""maʾbūrah\"" means those that have been pollinated. As for \""muhratun maʾmūrah","\"" it means one that produces abundant offspring.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]\n\n---"""
"20036","(20030) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Hamdānī narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, who informed me: Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf informed me that one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from the Anṣār told him that a man among them fell ill until his skin clung to his bones. A slave-girl of some of them entered upon him, and he became cheerful at her presence, so he had intercourse with her. Then he mentioned his story. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded that a hundred palm branches be gathered for him and that he be struck with them in a single blow.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Sijistānī 4472]\n\n---"
"20037","(20031) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: A man came to him while I was with him and said: \I have sworn that I will not clothe my family until I stand at ʿArafah"," and that was not during the days of Ḥajj.\"" ʿAṭāʾ said: \""Go"," stand at ʿArafah"," and clothe your family.\"" It was said to ʿAṭāʾ: \""He intended Ḥajj.\"" ʿAṭāʾ said: \""What about Ayyūb (peace be upon him) when he swore that he would strike his wife—he swore to strike her with a bundle of twigs? The Qurʾān consists of parables and lessons.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]\n\n---"""
"20038","(20032) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us: Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Mālik ibn Anas narrated from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \No one dies having lost three of his children except that the Fire will touch him—only as a fulfilment of the oath (taḥillat al-qasam).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: We understand his statement \""taḥillat al-qasam\"" to refer to the words of Allah"," the Blessed and Most High: {And there is none among you but will pass over it; this is"," with your Lord"," a decree that must be accomplished} [Maryam 71]. He means that one will only pass over it to the extent that Allah fulfils His oath regarding it. It is also the case that a man may swear to do such-and-such"," then does part of it and not all of it"," thereby fulfilling his oath.\n\nThe Shaykh said: He does that upon which the name applies.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]\n\n---"""
"20039","(20033) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Hāshimī informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us—I think he said: Isrāʾīl narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us: Isrāʾīl narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā from his grandmother from her father, Suwayd ibn Ḥanẓalah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and with us was Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr. A people who were his enemies met him. The people refused to take an oath, so I stepped forward and swore that he was my brother. When we came to the Prophet (ﷺ), I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," the people refused to take an oath"," so I stepped forward and swore that he was my brother.\"" He said: \""You have spoken the truth. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar"," and the ḥadīth of al-Zubayrī is its meaning in abbreviated form.\n\n---"""
"20040","(20034) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed me—and the wording is his: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī and Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, saying: Musaddad narrated to us: Hushaym informed me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, the brother of Suhayl, informed me from his father from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Your oath is according to what your companion believes you to mean by it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and ʿAmr al-Nāqid.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20041","(20035) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu'n-Nadr al-Faqih informed me that 'Uthman ibn Sa'id ad-Darimi and Hasan ibn Sufyan said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us that Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us from Hushaym from 'Abbad ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The oath is according to the intention of the one who administers it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. [Weak; see earlier]"""
"20042","(20036) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us that Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'quq ash-Shaybani narrated to us that Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us that Yazid ibn Harun informed us that Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, informed us from Mansur ibn 'Abdur-Rahman, a man from Banu 'Abdud-Dar, from his mother Safiyyah, that she heard 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) when a person asked her about one who says, \All my wealth is in the cause of Allah\"" or \""All my wealth is for the door of the Ka'bah\"" — what expiation is required for that? 'A'ishah said: \""Its expiation is the same as the expiation for an oath.\"" [Hasan]"""
"20043","(20037) Sufyan ath-Thawri narrated it from Mansur ibn 'Abdur-Rahman from his mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that a man or a woman asked her about a matter between her and a relative of hers, and she swore that if she spoke to him, her wealth would be for the door of the Ka'bah. 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \Its expiation is the same as the expiation for an oath.\""\n\nAbu Bakr al-Ardasistani informed us that Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us that Sufyan ibn Muhammad narrated to us that 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us that 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us that Sufyan narrated it. [Hasan; see earlier]"""
"20044","(20038) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abdil-'Aziz ibn Qatadah informed us that Abu'l-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Hasan as-Sarraj narrated to us that Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubaidillah al-Basri al-'Anbari narrated to us that Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us that Habib al-Mu'allim narrated to us from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: Two brothers from the Ansar had an inheritance between them, and one of them asked his brother for the division. He said: \If you ever ask me for the division again"," I shall never speak to you"," and all my wealth is for the door of the Ka'bah.\"" 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""The Ka'bah has no need of your wealth. Expiate your oath and speak to your brother"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'There is no oath or vow in disobedience to the Lord"," nor in severing ties of kinship"," nor concerning that which you do not possess.'\"" [Hasan]"""
"20045","(20039) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisi informed us that Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah al-Isbahani narrated to us that Abu Ahmad ibn Faris narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us that Musa ibn Isma'il informed us that Iyas ibn Abi Tamimah, Abu Makhlad, the Basri, narrated to me that 'Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to me from his father: He was a slave of the daughter of the paternal uncle of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), and she swore that her wealth was charity for the poor. Ibn 'Umar said: \Expiate your oath.\"" [Hasan]"""
"20046","(20040) He said: And Muhammad narrated to me that Mahmud narrated from an-Nadr that Ash'ath narrated from Bakr ibn 'Abdillah from Abi Rafi' from Ibn 'Umar, 'A'ishah, and Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \She should expiate her oath.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20047","(20041) He said: And Muhammad narrated to us that Hajjaj narrated from Hammad from 'Ali ibn Zayd from Abi Rafi' from Zaynab, a woman of the Muhajirun, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar and Hafsah bint 'Umar, something similar to it. And from Hammad from Thabit from Abi Rafi' something similar to it, and from Hammad from Humayd from Bakr ibn 'Abdillah from Abi Rafi' something similar to it. [Sahih]"
"20048","(20042) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us that Abu Tahir al-Muhammadabadi narrated to us that Abu Qilabah narrated to us that Ruh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us that al-Ash'ath narrated from Bakr ibn 'Abdillah al-Muzani from Abi Rafi': There was something between him and a woman of his, and his freedwoman swore an oath.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman as-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us that 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us that Abu Bakr an-Naysaburi narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us that Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us that al-Ash'ath narrated to us that Bakr ibn 'Abdillah al-Muzani narrated from Abi Rafi' that his freedwoman wanted to separate him from his wife. She said: \She is one day a Jewess and one day a Christian"," and every slave of hers is free"," and all her wealth is in the cause of Allah"," and upon her is walking to the House of Allah"," if she does not separate between them.\"" So he asked 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," Ibn 'Umar"," Ibn 'Abbas"," Hafsah"," and Umm Salamah"," and all of them said to her: \""Do you wish to be like Harut and Marut?\"" And they commanded her to expiate her oath and to leave them alone.\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of al-Ansari"," and the hadith of Ruh is abbreviated and does not mention Hafsah. [Sahih]"""
"20049","(20043) Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani informed us that 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us that Abu Bakr an-Naysaburi narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us that al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us that Abu Hilal narrated to us that Ghalib narrated from Bakr ibn 'Abdillah al-Muzani from Abi Rafi', who said: My freedwoman said: \I shall surely separate you from your wife"," and all her wealth is for the door of the Ka'bah"," and she is one day a Jewess"," one day a Christian"," and one day a Magian"," if you do not separate from your wife.\"" He said: So I went to Umm al-Mu'minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: \""My freedwoman wishes to separate me from my wife.\"" She said: \""Go to your freedwoman and say to her: 'This is not lawful for you.'\"" So I returned to her. He said: Then I went to Ibn 'Umar and informed him"," and he came until he reached the door and said: \""Are Harut and Marut here?\"" She said: \""I have made all my wealth for the door of the Ka'bah.\"" He said: \""What will you eat?\"" She said: \""And I am one day a Jewess"," one day a Christian"," and one day a Magian.\"" He said: \""If you become Jewish"," you will be killed; if you become Christian"," you will be killed; if you become Magian"," you will be killed.\"" She said: \""Then what do you command me?\"" He said: \""Expiate your oath and gather your slave-boys and slave-girls together.\"" [Sahih; see earlier]"""
"20050","(20044) Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Isfara'ini informed us that Zahir ibn Ahmad as-Sarakhsi narrated to us that Abu Bakr ibn Ziyad an-Naysaburi narrated to us that 'Abdur-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us that Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us that Sulayman at-Taymi narrated to us that Bakr ibn 'Abdillah narrated from Abi Rafi': Layla bint al-'Ajma', his freedwoman, said: \She is a Jewess and she is a Christian"," and every slave of hers is freed"," and all her wealth is a sacrificial offering"," if he does not divorce his wife"," if she does not separate between them.\"" So he went to Zaynab"," and she went with him"," and she said: \""Are Harut and Marut here?\"" She said: \""Allah knows what I said. All my wealth is a sacrificial offering"," and every slave of mine is freed"," and she is a Jewess and she is a Christian.\"" She said: \""Leave the man and his wife alone.\"" He said: So I went to Hafsah"," and I sent to her as Zaynab had said. She said: \""Leave the man and his wife alone.\"" So I went to Ibn 'Umar"," and he came with me and stood at the door. When he greeted"," she said: \""May my father be your ransom and my mother's.\"" He said: \""Are you made of stone or iron? Has Zaynab come to you and has Hafsah sent to you?\"" She said: \""I have sworn such-and-such.\"" He said: \""Expiate your oath and leave the man and his wife alone.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: This is other than manumission. It has been narrated from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) through another chain that the manumission takes effect"," and similarly from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). It is as though the narrator fell short in his transmission in the narration of Bakr ibn 'Abdillah"," or she had no slaves at the time"," so they did not address that issue. And Allah knows best. [Sahih; see earlier]"""
"20051","(20045) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Khushkananah al-Balkhi narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Musa al-Khatti narrated to us that Qutaybah narrated to us that Habib narrated from al-'Awwam from Mujahid, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with them both, said regarding a man who takes an oath to walk [for Hajj] or that his wealth is for the poor or for the restoration of the Ka'bah: it is an oath whose expiation is the feeding of ten poor persons. [Da'if]"
"20052","(20046) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that al-Rabi' said: I heard al-Shafi'i being asked by a man about walking [to the Ka'bah], and he broke his oath regarding walking to the Ka'bah, so he gave him the ruling of the expiation of an oath. The man said: \Do you say this"," O Abu 'Abd Allah?\"" He replied: \""This is the statement of one who is better than me.\"" He asked: \""Who is he?\"" He said: \""Ata' ibn Abi Rabah.\"""""
"20053","(20047) Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Ali al-Isfarayini informed us that Zahir ibn Ahmad narrated to us that Abu Bakr ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi narrated to us that Yusuf, meaning ibn Sa'id, narrated to us that Haytham, meaning ibn Kharijah, narrated to us that Hushaym informed us that Mansur narrated from al-Hasan and Hajjaj from Ata', who both said regarding the one who said: \I shall be in ihram for Hajj","\"" and then broke his obligation: the expiation is that of an oath."""
"20054","(20048) The Shaykh said: And the one who holds this opinion may cite as evidence what Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb —\n\n(And) Abu Nasr 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us that Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Sarraj narrated to us that Musa ibn Harun al-Bazzaz narrated to us that Abu Hamam al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid and Ahmad ibn 'Isa and Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed us that 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed us from Ka'b ibn 'Alqamah from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Shumasah from Abi al-Khayr from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \The expiation of a vow (nadhr) is the expiation of an oath (yamin).\""\n\nAbi al-Khayr was omitted from the narration of Ibn 'Abd al-Hakam; he did not mention him in his isnad. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Harun ibn Sa'id and Ahmad ibn 'Isa and Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la. [Sahih]"""
"20055","(20049) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri informed us that al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us that Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us that Ahmad ibn 'Isa narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yahya ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salim informed me from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \A vow (nadhr) is only that by which the Countenance of Allah is sought.\"" [Da'if. Musnad Ahmad 6714"," 6975]"""
"20056","(20050) And some who hold this opinion cited as evidence what Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yunus informed me from Ibn Shihab, who said: One of the sons of al-Sa'ib ibn Abi Lubabah informed me that Abi Lubabah, when he had bound himself [to a pillar] and Allah accepted his repentance, said: \O Messenger of Allah"," part of my repentance is that I abandon the house of my people in which I committed the sin"," and that I be your neighbour"," and that I give in charity from my wealth to Allah and His Messenger.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""A third of your wealth shall suffice you.\""\n\nMalik narrated it in al-Muwatta' from 'Uthman ibn Hafs from Ibn Shihab that it reached him that Abi Lubabah — and Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi narrated it from al-Zuhri from al-Husayn ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Abi Lubabah that his grandfather narrated to him that Abi Lubabah"," when Allah accepted his repentance"," mentioned it"," and it has already been discussed in the Book of Zakah.\n\nAnd Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated it from al-Zuhri from al-Husayn ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Abi Lubabah from his father"," and it is also said from him from al-Zuhri from al-Husayn ibn al-Sa'ib or someone else"," similarly. [Da'if]"""
"20057","(20051) And Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us that Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from al-Zuhri from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik from his father, who said to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him — or Abi Lubabah, or whomever Allah wills —: \Part of my repentance is that I abandon the house of my people in which I committed the sin and that I give in charity from all of my wealth.\"" He said: \""A third shall suffice you.\"" [Da'if. Previously mentioned]"""
"20058","(20052) And Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Abu Bakr informed us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us that 'Abd al-Razaq informed us that Ma'mar narrated from al-Zuhri, who informed me that Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik said: \He was Abi Lubabah\"" — and he mentioned its meaning. Abu Dawud said: And the story is about Abi Lubabah.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: It is with this wording in the story of Abi Lubabah. As for what was said to Ka'b ibn Malik"," it is not limited to a third. [Da'if. Previously mentioned]"""
"20059","(20053) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yunus ibn Yazid informed me from Ibn Shihab, who said: 'Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed me from his father, who said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, when repentance was accepted for him: \O Messenger of Allah"," I wish to give in charity from my wealth to Allah and His Messenger.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said to him: \""Retain some of your wealth"," for that is better for you.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Salih from Ibn Wahb.\n\nAnd it is also said from Ibn Wahb from Yunus from Ibn Shihab from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik from 'Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik from his father.\n\nThis hadith is sahih"," but the first narration differs in its isnad"," and it is not established as connected (mawsul)"," and it is not correct to use it as evidence in this matter. Abi Lubabah only intended to give his wealth in charity as gratitude to Allah"," Exalted is He"," when Allah accepted his repentance. So the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," ordered him to retain some of his wealth"," just as he said to Ka'b ibn Malik. And it has not reached us that he made a vow or swore an oath regarding anything. And Allah knows best. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"20060","(20054) As for the third opinion, it is in what Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Ali al-Isfarayini informed us with, that Zahir ibn Ahmad narrated to us that Abu Bakr ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi narrated to us that Abu al-Azhar and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir narrated to us, who said: 'Abd al-Razaq informed us that Ma'mar narrated from Isma'il ibn Umayyah from 'Uthman ibn Abi Hadir, who said: A woman from the family of Dhu Asbah took an oath, saying: \My wealth is in the way of Allah"," and my slave-girl is free"," if I do not do such and such\"" — something her husband detested. So her husband swore that he would not do it. Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with them"," were asked about that"," and they said: \""As for the slave-girl"," she is to be freed. And as for her statement 'My wealth is in the way of Allah","' she is to give in charity the zakah of her wealth\"" — this is what is in this narration. And we have narrated from Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with them"," what indicates the permissibility of expiation (takfir). And Allah knows best. And another opinion has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," regarding its meaning. [Sahih]"""
"20061","Abu al-Juwayriyyah reported that he heard Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrate regarding a man upon whom a hundred camels were obligatory: if he spoke to his brother, he said, \He should sacrifice thirty camels and speak to his brother.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20062","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Malik narrated to us.\n\n(Additionally) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan narrated to us in Baghdad: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah and Ibn Bukayr narrated from Malik, from Talhah ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Ayli, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever vows to obey Allah"," let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Allah"," let him not disobey Him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu 'Asim and Abu Nu'aym from Malik. [Sahih. Bukhari 6686]"""
"20063","Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Ibn 'Uyaynah and 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from 'Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \There is no vow in disobedience"," and there is no vow regarding that which the son of Adam does not possess.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: And in the hadith of 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi with this isnad"," it is narrated that a woman from among the Ansar made a vow and fled upon a she-camel of the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," saying: \""If Allah saves me upon it"," I shall sacrifice it.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said these words and took back his she-camel.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: He did not command her to sacrifice a similar one"," nor to expiate.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: Thus we say: whoever makes a vow of devotion to sacrifice the property of another"," the vow falls from him; and whoever vows that which he is unable to fulfil in any circumstance"," the vow falls from him"," because he does not possess the ability to fulfil it"," just as he does not possess anything else besides it.\n\n[Sahih. Muslim 1641]"""
"20064","Ayyub ibn 'A'idh al-Ta'i said: I said to al-Sha'bi, \A man vowed to sacrifice his son.\"" He said"," \""Perhaps you are among the practitioners of qiyas (analogical reasoning). I do not know anyone among the people more eager to seek knowledge across the horizons than Masruq.\"" He said: \""There is no vow in disobedience.\"" [Sahih. From al-Sha'bi]"""
"20065","Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Ayyub ibn 'A'idh al-Ta'i narrated to us — and this hadith was not heard by al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah. [Sahih]\n\nAbu Salamah narrated from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \There is no vow in disobedience"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\"""""
"20066","Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman in the original book of Yunus narrated to us: 'Abdullah narrated to us: Yunus narrated from al-Zuhri, who said: And it reached me from Abu Salamah that 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \There is no vow in disobedience"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20067","Ya'qub said: And Abu Muhammad al-Umayyi narrated to me from 'Anbasah ibn Khalid, who narrated to us: Yunus narrated from Ibn Shihab, who said: Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \There is no vow in disobedience"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\"" This indicates that al-Zuhri did not hear it directly from Abu Salamah; rather"," he heard it from Sulayman ibn Arqam from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah. [Sahih. Previously mentioned]"""
"20068","Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani narrated to us orally: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Faris al-Maliki narrated to us in Makkah.\n\n(Additionally) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us, both saying: al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: My brother narrated to me from Sulayman, that is Ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi 'Atiq and Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who used to reside in al-Yamamah, who narrated to him that he heard Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrate from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \There is no vow in disobedience to Allah"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\"" [Sahih. Previously mentioned]"""
"20069","'Abd al-Khaliq ibn 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Khanb narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Tirmidhi narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to me: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, and he mentioned it.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: And this is an error on the part of Sulayman ibn Arqam regarding Yahya ibn Abi Kathir; for Yahya only narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali from his father from 'Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace be upon him).\n\nSimilarly, 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated it from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir. [Sahih. Previously mentioned]"
"20070","Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi said: Ibn al-Mubarak said regarding this hadith: \Abu Salamah narrated it","\"" and that indicates that al-Zuhri did not hear it from Abu Salamah. Ahmad ibn Muhammad said: The confirmation of that is the hadith of Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal. Ahmad said: And the hadith is truly the hadith of 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr from his father from 'Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace be upon him).\n\nAbu Dawud said: He intended that Sulayman ibn Arqam erred in it"," and al-Zuhri carried it from him and attributed it to Abu Salamah.\n\nAbu Dawud said: Baqiyyah narrated it from al-Awza'i from Yahya from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr with the isnad of 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak"," similar to it.\n\n[Sahih. From Ibn al-Mubarak]"""
"20071","(20065) Abū ʿAbdullāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd — he being Ibn Mazīd — informed me that my father narrated to us that al-Awzāʿī narrated to me that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to me, from a man of Banī Ḥanẓalah, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no vow (nadhr) in a state of anger"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath (yamīn).\"" [Weak]"""
"20072","(20066) It was also narrated by Hiql ibn Ziyād, from al-Awzāʿī, from Yaḥyā, who said: A man of Banī Ḥanẓalah narrated to me, from his father, from ʿImrān, a similar narration. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated it to us, saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣr ibn Ṭuwayṭ narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather al-Layth, who said: Hiql narrated to me, and he mentioned it.\n\nThis hadith is well-known through Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥanẓalī, and there is disagreement regarding both its chain of narration (isnād) and its text (matn). [Weak]"
"20073","(20067) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdad, saying: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Rūḥ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥanẓalī, from his father, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no vow in disobedience to Allah"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\""\n\n[Weak. Preceded by one narration.]"""
"20074","(20068) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Abū Jaʿfar al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Karābīsī narrated to us, saying: Khalaf ibn Hishām narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no vow in a state of anger"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\""\n\nThis narration is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous). Al-Zubayr al-Ḥanẓalī did not hear (directly) from ʿImrān. [Weak. Preceded by one narration.]"""
"20075","(20069) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn said: It was said to Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥanẓalī, \Did your father hear from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn?\"" He said: \""No.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And that which indicates this is… [Sound"," according to Ibn Maʿīn.]"""
"20076","(20070) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥanẓalī narrated to us, from his father, that a man narrated to him that he asked ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him) about a man who swore that he would not pray in the mosque of his people. ʿImrān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \There is no vow in disobedience to Allah"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\""\n\nAnd it was also narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥanẓalī"," from a man who accompanied him"," from ʿImrān. [Sound"," without the story.]"""
"20077","(20071) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿArūbah narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Isḥāq, from Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr, from a man who accompanied him, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \A vow is of two types: whatever vow is made in obedience to Allah"," then it is for you and must be fulfilled; and whatever vow is made in disobedience to Allah"," then it is for Satan and there is no fulfillment of it — rather"," its expiation is that which expiates an oath.\""\n\nAnd it was also narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr"," from al-Ḥasan"," from ʿImrān. [Weak]"""
"20078","(20072) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated it to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj narrated to us, saying: Muṭayyin narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us, saying: Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no vow in disobedience"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\""\n\nAnd ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd al-ʿAdanī narrated it from Sufyān"," with his chain of narration: \""There is no vow in disobedience or in anger"," and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\""\n\nThis narration is also munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous). There is no sound"," established audition from al-Ḥasan from ʿImrān by any reliable means. [Sound]"""
"20079","(20073) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Barāʾ informed us, saying: I heard ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī say: There is no sound, established audition from al-Ḥasan from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him) by any reliable means.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥanẓalī is not strong (in hadith). [Sound, according to Ibn al-Madīnī.]"
"20080","(20074) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us, saying: I heard Ibn Ḥammād say: Al-Bukhārī said: \Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥanẓalī is munkar al-ḥadīth (one who narrates objectionable hadiths)"," and there is scrutiny regarding him.\"" [Sound"," according to al-Bukhārī.]"""
"20081","(20075) The Sheikh said: And others narrated it from al-Hasan, as Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Mahrūyah al-Rāzī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Layth narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Bakr ibn Dāwūd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Layth narrated to us: Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs narrated to me: the son of my brother Ibn Wahb narrated to me: my uncle narrated to me: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sālim narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Mubārak ibn Faḍālah from al-Hasan that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The expiation of a vow (nadhr) is the expiation of an oath (yamīn).\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Dāwūd added in his narration: Abū Ḥātim — and he is Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Rāzī — said: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated this single ḥadīth from Mubārak ibn Faḍālah"," although Mubārak narrated other aḥādīth from ʿUbayd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20082","(20076) The Sheikh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: The most authentic narration from al-Hasan on this matter is what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Abī ʿUthmān al-Ṭayālisī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-ʿAwfi informed us: Hammām narrated from Qatādah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAffān informed us: Hammām informed us: Qatādah narrated from al-Hasan from Hayyān ibn ʿImrān al-Barjamī: that a slave belonging to his father ran away, and his father made a vow to Allah that if he gained power over him, he would certainly cut off his hand. When he gained power over him, he sent me to ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), so I asked him. He said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) exhorting in his sermon about charity and forbidding mutilation (muthlah).\"" He said: \""Tell your father to expiate his oath and to pardon his slave.\"" He said: \""And he sent me to Samurah"," and he said: 'I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) exhorting in his sermon about charity and forbidding mutilation. Tell your father to expiate his oath and to pardon his slave.'\""\n\nThis is a connected (mawṣūl) chain of narration"," except that the command to expiate the oath is stopped (mawqūf) in it upon ʿImrān and Samurah. As for al-Hayyān ibn ʿImrān"," there is disagreement regarding his name; it is said thus"," and it is also said Ḥayyān ibn ʿImrān al-Barjamī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20083","(20077) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān informed us: Hāshim ibn Muḥammad al-Rabaʿī informed us: ʿAnbasah ibn Khālid al-Aylī narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Hind from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ashadd from Kurayb from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever makes a vow without specifying it"," its expiation is the expiation of an oath. Whoever makes a vow in disobedience to Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," its expiation is the expiation of an oath. Whoever makes a vow that he cannot fulfill"," its expiation is the expiation of an oath. And whoever makes a vow that he can fulfill"," let him fulfill it.\""\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā on one occasion from him from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind from Bukayr"," and on another occasion from him from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind. And Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd as a stopped (mawqūf) narration upon Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both). And it was narrated through another weak chain from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Munkar]"""
"20084","(20078) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Dalaj ibn Aḥmad informed us: Ibn al-Jārūd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn Aʿyan informed us: Khaṭṭāb informed us: ʿAbd al-Karīm narrated from ʬAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \A vow is of two types: whatever is for Allah"," its expiation is fulfilling it; and whatever is for Satan"," there is no fulfillment for it"," and upon its maker is the expiation of an oath.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20085","(20079) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from al-Qāsim.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd. He said: I heard al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad say: \A woman came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: 'I have vowed to sacrifice my son.' Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: 'Do not sacrifice your son"," and expiate your oath.' An old man sitting near Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'How can there be an expiation in this?' Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: 'Allah says: {And those who pronounce ẓihār from their wives} [Al-Mujādilah 3]"," and then He has prescribed an expiation therein"," as you have seen.'\""\n\nIn the narration of Jaʿfar"," he said: An old man said to him: \""How can there be an expiation in obedience to Satan?\"" He said: \""Yes"," indeed! Does not Allah say…\"" and he mentioned its meaning. This is a sound (ṣaḥīḥ) chain of narration.\n\nAnd al-Thawrī narrated it similarly from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī. However"," ʿIkrimah contradicted him from Ibn ʿAbbās"," saying: \""He should slaughter a ram.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20086","(20080) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadbādhī informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī informed us: Wahb ibn Jarīr informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah and Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said regarding a man who vowed to sacrifice his son: \He should slaughter a ram.\""\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from ʬAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) in one of the two narrations from him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20087","(20081) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us: Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʬAṭāʾ that a man said to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both): \I have vowed to sacrifice my son.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) commanded him with (the sacrifice of) a ram and said: \""{There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern} [Al-Aḥzāb 21].\"" Thus I found it in this narration.\n\nAnd Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it in al-Jāmiʿ from Ibn Jurayj from ʬAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man came to him and said: \""I have vowed to sacrifice myself.\"" He said: \""{There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern} [Al-Aḥzāb 21].\"" So he commanded him with (the sacrifice of) a ram. ʬAṭāʾ was asked: \""Where should he slaughter the ram?\"" He said: \""In Makkah.\""\n\nAbū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us: Sufyān narrated it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20088","(20082) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us: Ibn Abī Maryam informed us: al-Firyābī informed us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʬAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding a man who vowed to sacrifice himself. He said: \{There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern} [Al-Aḥzāb 21].\"" So he gave him a fatwa of (sacrificing) a ram.\n\nThis indicates that the narration of ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar is an error. And similarly others besides Sufyān narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20089","(20083) Manṣūr ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Sayyār informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Fawāris al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris, the brother of the Sheikh Abī al-Fatḥ al-Ḥāfiẓ, in Baghdād informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muẓaffar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Usāmah ibn ʿAlī ibn Saʿīd in Miṣr informed us: Abū ʿUbayd Allāh Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the nephew of Ibn Wahb, said: My uncle narrated to me: My uncle narrated to me: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to me. He said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said, and Ibn Jurayj claimed that ʬAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ narrated to him: \A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: 'I have vowed to sacrifice myself.' Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: '{There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern} [Al-Aḥzāb 21].' Then Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) recited: '{And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice} [Al-Ṣāffāt 107].'\"" This indicates that by \""the Messenger of Allah\"" he meant Ibrāhīm"," the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and upon our Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAnd another fatwa has been narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding one who vowed to sacrifice himself. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before.]"""
"20090","(20084) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Kurayb from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \A man came to him and said: 'I have vowed to sacrifice myself.' And at that time there was a man with Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) who wished to go out for jihād"," and his parents were with him. Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) was occupied"," saying to him: 'Stay with your parents.' The man kept saying: 'I have vowed to sacrifice myself.' Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to him: 'What should I do with you? Go and sacrifice yourself!' When Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) finished with the man and his parents"," he said: 'Bring me the man.' They went and found him kneeling down"," about to sacrifice himself. They brought him to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," who said: 'Woe to you! You intended to make permissible three things: to violate the sanctity of a ḥarām land"," to sever a forbidden tie of kinship — for your own self is the closest of kinship ties to you — and to shed forbidden blood. Do you find a hundred camels?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Go and sacrifice a third of them each year"," without letting the meat spoil.'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Muʿāwiyah"," and the narration of Ibn Numayr is in its meaning. And he added: Kurayb said: \""I witnessed him for two years. As for the third year"," I do not know what he did.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20091","(20085) Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from al-Aʿmash with the same meaning, and al-Aʿmash added: \It reached me that Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: 'If someone were to take an oath against me"," I would order him to sacrifice a ram.'\""\n\nAbū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī informed us"," Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us"," Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us"," ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us"," ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us"," Sufyān narrated it.\n\nIt has also been narrated from another chain from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he ordered in a similar case the sacrifice of a ram.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The difference in his legal opinions on this matter"," and regarding the one who vowed to slaughter his son"," indicates that he would say it based on independent reasoning and deduction"," not that he knew a specific transmitted ruling on it. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20092","(20086) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Ibn ʿAwn narrated to us — a man narrated to me that a man asked Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) about a man who vowed that he would not speak to his brother, and that if he did speak to him, he would slaughter himself between the Maqām and the Rukn during the days of Tashrīq. He said: \O son of my brother"," convey to those behind you: there is no vow in disobedience to Allah. If he had vowed not to fast Ramaḍān and then fasted it"," that would have been better for him. If he had vowed not to pray and then prayed"," that would have been better for him. Tell your companion to expiate his oath and speak to his brother.\""\n\nThis narration from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20093","(20087) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated to us — from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Murrah, from Masrūq, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said. And in the narration of Sufyān from the Prophet (ﷺ), he said: \There are four qualities: whoever possesses them is a pure hypocrite"," and whoever possesses one of them possesses a quality of hypocrisy until he abandons it: when he speaks"," he lies; when he makes a covenant"," he betrays it; when he makes a promise"," he breaks it; and when he disputes"," he resorts to falsehood and obscenity.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr from ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim extracted it from the ḥadīth of Sufyān al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20094","(20088) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us, Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to me — Abū Jamrah informed me and said: \Zahdam came to me and informed me that he heard ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'The best of you are my generation"," then those who follow them"," then those who follow them. Then there will come after them a people who betray and are not entrusted"," who testify but are not asked to testify"," who make vows but do not fulfill them"," and among whom obesity will become prevalent.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr"," and he extracted it from other chains from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20095","(20089) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us orally, Abū Muslim informed us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Mālik, from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, from al-Qāsim, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever vows to obey Allah"," let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Him"," let him not disobey Him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿĀṣim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 6696"," 6700]"""
"20096","(20090) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Walīd informed me, Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed me — and the wording is his — Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Zurārah ibn Wāqid al-Kilābī narrated to us. Both said: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ayyūb narrated from Abū Qilābah, from Abū al-Muhallab, from ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The tribe of Thaqīf were allies of Banī ʿUqayl"," and Thaqīf captured two companions of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) captured a man and seized his she-camel al-ʿAḍbāʾ along with him.\"" He mentioned the hadith as it has passed"," and in it he said: \""A woman from the Anṣār was captured"," and al-ʿAḍbāʾ was taken. The woman was in bonds"," and the people would rest their camels in front of their houses. She escaped one night from her bonds and came to the camels. Whenever she approached a camel"," it would bellow"," so she would leave it"," until she reached al-ʿAḍbāʾ"," and it did not bellow.\"" He said: \""It was a well-trained she-camel.\"" She sat on its hindquarters"," then urged it on"," and it set off. They vowed to search for her and pursued her"," but she outpaced them. She had vowed that if Allah saved her upon it"," she would sacrifice it. When she arrived in Madīnah"," the people saw her and said: \""Al-ʿAḍbāʾ is the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)!\"" She said: \""I have vowed that if Allah saves me upon it"," I will sacrifice it.\"" They came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Subḥān Allāh! How poorly she has requited it! If Allah saves her upon it"," she will sacrifice it! There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah"," nor in that over which the servant has no authority.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1641]"""
"20097","(20091) ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Khamb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī informed us, Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥārith, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the wife of Abū Dharr came upon al-Qaṣwāʾ, the mount of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and made it kneel by the mosque. She said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I vowed that if Allah saves me upon it"," I will eat from its liver and its hump.\"" He said: \""How poorly you have requited it! This is not a vow. A vow is only that by which the Face of Allah is sought.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20098","(20092) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ informed us, al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah informed us. Both said: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Wuhayb informed us, Ayyūb narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \While the Prophet (ﷺ) was delivering a sermon"," he noticed a man standing in the sun. He asked about him"," and they said: 'This is Abū Isrāʾīl. He vowed to stand and not sit"," not seek shade"," not speak"," and to fast and not break his fast.' He said: 'Tell him to speak"," to seek shade"," to sit"," and to complete his fast.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 6704]"""
"20099","(20093) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, from al-Shāfiʿī, who informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr, from Ṭāwūs, that the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by Abū Isrāʾīl while he was standing in the sun and said: \What is the matter with him?\"" They said: \""He vowed not to seek shade"," not to sit"," not to speak to anyone"," and to fast.\"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded him to seek shade"," to sit"," to speak to people"," and to complete his fast"," and he did not command him to offer expiation.\n\nThis is a good mursal narration. In it and in what precedes it there is evidence that he did not command expiation.\n\nAl-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah narrated it from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," with a similar narration"," and at the end of it: \""and he did not command him with expiation.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20100","(20094) It has been narrated from Muḥammad ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), and in it there is the command of expiation. However, Muḥammad ibn Kurayb is weak (ḍaʿīf).\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Naṣr al-Sabīʾī al-Shahīd informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maghrāʾ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Kurayb narrated from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Abū Isrāʾīl ibn Qushayr said: \He had vowed to fast"," not to sit"," not to seek shade"," and not to speak.\"" He was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \""Sit"," seek shade"," speak"," and offer expiation.\""\n\nThus I found it: \""and offer expiation\"" (wa kaffir). However"," in my view this is a scribal error (taṣḥīf); rather it is: \""and fast\"" (wa ṣum)"," as it is in all other narrations. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20101","(20095) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad and Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — they separated them — both saying: Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Iyād ibn Laqīṭ narrated to us from his father Iyād ibn Laqīṭ, who said: Laylā, the wife of Bashīr ibn al-Khaṣāṣiyyah, informed me — and his name before that was Zaḥm, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Bashīr — she said: Bashīr informed me that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about fasting on the condition that he would not speak to anyone that day. He ﷺ said to him: \Do not fast on Jumuʿah except on days you would normally fast"," or within a month. And do not refrain from speaking to anyone — for"," by my life"," that you speak and enjoin good and forbid evil is better than remaining silent.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Musnad Aḥmad 21447]"""
"20102","(20096) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb informed us from his original, both saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Mihrān narrated to us: ʿAffān ibn Muslim al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us: Bayān ibn Bishr narrated to us from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, who said: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) visited a woman from Aḥmas whose name was Zaynab. He saw that she was not speaking. He said: \Why does she not speak?\"" They said: \""She performed Ḥajj in silence (muṣmitah).\"" He said: \""Speak"," for this is not permissible. This is from the practice of the Jāhiliyyah.\"" So she spoke and said: \""Who are you?\"" He said: \""I am from the Muhājirūn.\"" She said: \""Which of the Muhājirūn?\"" He said: \""From Quraysh.\"" She said: \""Which of Quraysh?\"" He said: \""You are indeed inquisitive! I am Abū Bakr.\"" She said: \""How long shall we remain upon this righteous affair that Allah has brought after the Jāhiliyyah"," after the Prophet ﷺ?\"" He said: \""Your remaining upon it depends upon the steadfastness of your leaders (a'immah).\"" She said: \""What are the leaders?\"" He said: \""Did your people not have chiefs and nobles who would command them and they would obey them?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then they are the likes of those who are over the people.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Nuʿmān from Abī ʿAwanah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3834]"""
"20103","(20097) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Abū Khaythamah narrated to us: Jarīr narrated to us from Yazīd from Zayd ibn Wahb from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) that he came to a woman's tent and greeted her, but she did not speak to him. He did not leave her until she spoke. She said: \O servant of Allah"," who are you?\"" He said: \""From the Muhājirūn.\"" She said: \""The Muhājirūn are many; which of them are you?\"" He said: \""From Quraysh.\"" She said: \""Quraysh are many; which of them are you?\"" He said: \""I am Abū Bakr.\"" She said: \""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you! There was something between us and a people during the Jāhiliyyah"," and I vowed that if Allah granted us safety"," I would not speak to anyone until I performed Ḥajj.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," Islam has demolished that"," so speak.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20104","(20098) The faqīh Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abī Isḥāq from Ḥārithah ibn Muḍarrib, who said: I was sitting with ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) when two men came. One of them gave salām, but the other did not. We said — or he said: \What is the matter with your companion that he did not give salām?\"" He said: \""He has vowed a fast in which he will not speak to any human being today.\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""Evil is what you have said. Rather"," that was a woman who said that as an excuse"," and they used to deny that a child could be from other than a husband or except through zinā. So give salām"," and enjoin good and forbid evil — that is better for you.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20105","(20099) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us by dictation: Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar ibn Manīʿ informed us from his original: Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥakīm narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to me from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \I vowed to perform iʿtikāf in al-Masjid al-Ḥarām. When I embraced Islam"," I asked the Prophet of Allah ﷺ about that.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Fulfil your vow.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20106","(20100) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh. Nāfiʿ informed me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the Prophet ﷺ: \Indeed"," I vowed during the Jāhiliyyah to perform iʿtikāf in al-Masjid al-Ḥarām.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Fulfil your vow.\""\n\nThe wording is that of Muḥammad's ḥadīth. In the narration of Musaddad: \""Indeed"," I vowed to perform iʿtikāf for one night during the Jāhiliyyah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr and others. [Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20107","(20101) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah narrated to us from his father that the Prophet ﷺ returned from one of his military expeditions, and a dark-skinned slave girl came to him and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I vowed that if Allah returned you safely"," I would play the duff before you.\"" He ﷺ said: \""If you have vowed"," then play.\"" She began to play. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) entered while she was playing. Then ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) entered"," and she threw the duff beneath her and sat upon it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"," Shayṭān fears you"," O ʿUmar.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20108","(20102) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUbayd, Abū Qudāmah, narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Akhnas from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I vowed to play the duff over your head.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Fulfil your vow.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is as though he ﷺ only permitted her to play the duff because it is a permissible matter and involves expressing joy at the appearance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his safe return — not that it becomes obligatory by way of a vow. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"20109","(20103) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī narrated to us: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrrah narrated to us: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Fawāris al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris in Baghdād informed us: Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us. Both said: Sufyān narrated to us from Manṣūr from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Murrah from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade from making vows and said: \Indeed"," it does not repel anything. Rather"," it is only a means by which is extracted from the miserly.\""\n\nIn the narration of Khallād: \""Rather"," it is a means by which is extracted from the miserly.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym and Khallād ibn Yaḥyā"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20110","(20104) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, the mawlā of al-Muṭṭalib, narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Indeed"," a vow does not bring the son of Ādam anything that Allah has not decreed for him. However"," a vow coincides with the decree"," and thereby is extracted from the miserly one that which the miserly one did not intend to give.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb and others"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Abī al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20111","(20105) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-'Adl informed us in Baghdad, that Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Ja'far al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us, that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, that Sulaymān narrated from Abū 'Uthmān, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: There was a man — I know no one among the people of Madinah who prayed facing the qibla more distant from the mosque than he was — and he would attend the prayers with the Prophet ﷺ. It was said to him: \Would you not buy a donkey and ride it through the scorching heat and the darkness?\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I would not love for my dwelling to be adjacent to the mosque.\"" This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," so he asked him. He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," that my footsteps and my tracks"," my return to my family"," and my coming and going be recorded [in my favour].\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Allah has granted you"," all together"," what you sought reward for.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from Sulaymān al-Taymī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 663]"""
"20112","(20106) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, that Abū al-Bakhtarī 'Abdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us, that Abū Usāma Ḥamād ibn Usāma narrated to us, that Burayd ibn 'Abdullāh ibn Abī Burda narrated from his grandfather, from Abī Mūsā al-Ash'arī, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The greatest of people in reward for prayer is the one who is farthest in walking to it. And the one who awaits the prayer until he performs it with the imam in congregation has a greater reward than the one who prays it and then sleeps.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Abī Usāma. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq 'alayh]"""
"20113","(20107) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū 'Alī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ al-Khath'amī narrated to us, that 'Alī ibn Sa'īd ibn Masrūq al-Kindī narrated to us, that 'Īsā ibn Sawāda narrated, that Ismā'īl ibn Abī Khālid narrated, that Zādhān said: Ibn 'Abbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — fell ill, so he called his children and gathered them, and said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever performs ḥajj from Makkah on foot until he returns to Makkah"," Allah will record for him seven hundred good deeds for every step"," each good deed being equal to the good deeds of the Ḥaram.'\"" It was asked: \""And what are the good deeds of the Ḥaram?\"" He said: \""Each good deed is equal to one hundred thousand good deeds.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated in the Book of Ḥajj the virtue of walking to the Sacred House of Allah. [Ḍa'īf]"""
"20114","(20108) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us, that Muḥammad ibn 'Abdullāh ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam informed us, that Ibn Wahb informed us, that Ya'qūb ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Zuhrī and Ḥafṣ ibn Maysara narrated, that Mūsā ibn 'Uqba narrated, that Nāfi' narrated, that 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with them both — said: \When a person vows to walk to the Ka'ba"," this is a vow"," so let him walk to the Ka'ba.\""\n\nIbn Wahb said: Al-Layth said the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20115","(20109) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, that 'Ubdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr informed us — (ḥ) and Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Mahrūyah ibn 'Abbās ibn Sinān al-Rāzī informed us — both saying: Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn 'Abdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated to me, that Ḥumayd narrated, that Thābit narrated, that Anas said: \An elderly man was being supported between his two sons"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with this man?' They said: 'He has vowed to walk"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Indeed"," Allah"," exalted is He"," is in no need of this man tormenting himself.' And he commanded him to ride"," so he rode.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq 'alayh]"""
"20116","(20110) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū 'Amr 'Uthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, that Ḥamād ibn Mas'ada narrated to us, that Ḥumayd narrated, that Thābit narrated, that Anas said: \The Prophet ﷺ saw a man being supported between two men and said: 'What is the matter with him?' They said: 'He has vowed to walk to the House.' He said: 'Then indeed"," Allah"," exalted is He"," is in no need of this man tormenting himself. Command him"," so let him ride.'\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in their Ṣaḥīths from the ḥadīth of Marwān al-Fazārī and others from Ḥumayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously cited]"""
"20117","(20111) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqri' informed us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Yūsuf ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, that Abū al-Rabī' narrated to us — (ḥ) and Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, that Abū Bakr ibn 'Abdillāh informed us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, that Qutayba ibn Sa'īd informed us — both saying: Ismā'īl ibn Ja'far narrated to us, that 'Amr ibn Abī 'Amr narrated, that 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-A'raj narrated, that Abū Hurayra — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon an elderly man walking between his two sons"," leaning upon them"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with this elderly man?' His two sons said: 'He had a vow [to fulfil].' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Ride"," O elderly man"," for indeed"," Allah"," exalted is He"," is in no need of you and of your vow.'\""\n\nThe wording of both is the same. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutayba ibn Sa'īd and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1643]"""
"20118","(20112) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — (ḥ) and Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismā'īl al-Bazzāz in Ṭabarān informed us, that 'Abdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭūsī narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Ismā'īl al-Ṣā'igh narrated to us — both saying: Rūḥ ibn 'Ubāda narrated to us, that Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, that Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed me, that Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb informed him, that Abū al-Khayr informed him, that 'Uqba ibn 'Āmir — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah"," and she commanded me to seek a fatwa for her from the Prophet ﷺ. So I sought the fatwa from the Prophet ﷺ"," and he said: 'Let her walk and let her ride.'\"" He said: \""And Abū al-Khayr would never part from 'Uqba.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī 'Āṣim from Ibn Jurayj"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim and others from Rūḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq 'alayh]"""
"20119","(20113) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, that al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Faḍāla narrated to us, that 'Abdullāh ibn 'Ayāsh narrated, that Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated, that Abū al-Khayr narrated, that 'Uqba ibn 'Āmir — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah barefoot"," and she commanded me to seek a fatwa for her from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So I sought the fatwa from him"," and he said: 'Let her walk and let her ride.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Miṣrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq 'alayh]"""
"20120","(20114) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-'Alawī informed us verbally, that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn 'Abdillāh narrated to me, that my father narrated to me, that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated, that Maṭar al-Warrāq narrated, that 'Ikrima narrated, that Ibn 'Abbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — said: \The sister of 'Uqba vowed to perform ḥajj on foot"," and she was not able to do that"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed"," Allah has no need of your sister walking. Let her ride and let her offer a badana (a camel or cow as sacrifice).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20121","(20115) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Hudbah narrated to us, Hammām narrated from Qatādah, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the Prophet (ﷺ): \Indeed"," her sister has vowed to walk to the House (the Kaʿbah).\"" He (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," Allah is free from need of your sister's vow. Let her perform Ḥajj riding and offer a badanah (a sacrificial camel or cow).\"" He said: \""And offer a badanah.\""\n\nAnd Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated it from Hammām and said in the hadith: \""And offer a hady (sacrifice).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20122","(20116) Hishām al-Dastawāʾī contradicted him and narrated it from Qatādah without mentioning the hady (sacrifice) in it. ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated to us, Qatādah narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both): \That it reached the Prophet (ﷺ) that the sister of ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir had vowed to perform Ḥajj on foot. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: 'Indeed"," Allah is free from need of her vow. Command her"," so she may ride.'\""\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from ʿIkrimah without mentioning the hady (sacrifice) in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated before it]"""
"20123","(20117) Ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated it from Qatādah, sending it as a mursal narration and not mentioning the hady (sacrifice) in it. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʾAṭāʾ informed us, Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from ʿIkrimah: \That the sister of ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir vowed to perform Ḥajj on foot. So ʿUqbah asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'Command her to ride"," for indeed Allah"," the Most High"," is free from need of your sister's vow or your sister's walking.'\"" Saʿīd expressed doubt."""
"20124","(20118) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from ʿIkrimah: \That the sister of ʿUqbah…\"" with the same meaning as Hishām's narration"," and he did not mention the hady (sacrifice) in it. And he said in it: \""Command your sister to ride.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: And Khālid narrated it from ʿIkrimah with its meaning. And it was said: from ʿIkrimah"," from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir"," without mentioning the hady (sacrifice) in it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated before it]"""
"20125","(20119) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed him, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated from Sufyān, from his father, from ʿIkrimah, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī, that he said to the Prophet (ﷺ): \Indeed"," my sister has vowed to walk to the House (the Kaʿbah).\"" He (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," Allah does not benefit in anything from your sister's walking to the House (the Kaʿbah).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated before it]"""
"20126","(20120) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Sharīk narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the mawlā of the family of Ṭalḥah, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," my sister has vowed to perform Ḥajj on foot.' He (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed"," Allah does not benefit in anything from your sister's hardship. Let her perform Ḥajj riding"," and then let her expiate her oath.'\"" Sharīk al-Qāḍī was alone in narrating it.\n\n[Ḥasan due to other chains]"""
"20127","(20121) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī narrated to us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ẓahr, from Abī Saʿīd al-Ruʿaynī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mālik, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \My sister vowed to perform Ḥajj for Allah on foot"," without covering herself (ghayra mukhtamirah).\"" He said: \""So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'Command your sister to cover herself (fa-ltakhtamir)"," to ride"," and to fast three days.'\""\n\nAnd similarly"," Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī. And similarly"," Ibn Jurayj narrated it; he said: \""Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd wrote to me and mentioned it.\""\n\nAnd al-Thawrī narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"," and there was disagreement regarding its isnād. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20128","(20122) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris narrated; he said: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: \The hady (sacrifice) is not authentic in it","\"" meaning in the hadith of ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī]"""
"20129","(20123) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd informed me, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was traveling with a caravan in the middle of the night"," he caught sight of a figure from which their camels had bolted. He sent a man to look"," and behold"," it was a woman"," naked"," with her hair undone. He said: 'What is the matter with you?' She said: 'I vowed to perform Ḥajj to the House (the Kaʿbah) on foot"," naked"," with my hair undone. I conceal myself during the day and take to the path by night.' So he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and informed him. He (ﷺ) said: 'Go back to her and command her to wear her garments and to shed blood (offer a sacrifice).'\""\n\nThis isnād is weak. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20130","(20124) It was narrated through another disconnected chain without mentioning the hady (sacrifice) in it. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — al-Aṣamm — narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʾAṭāʾ informed us, Saʿīd narrated from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah: \That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) glanced and behold"," there was a woman with her hair spread out. He (ﷺ) said: 'What is this?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," she vowed to perform Ḥajj on foot with her hair spread out.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Command her to cover her head and to ride.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20131","(20125) Abu Bakr ibn Furak narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Abu 'Amir Salih ibn Rustam narrated from Kathir ibn Shindhir from al-Hasan from 'Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Rasul Allah ﷺ seldom addressed us without exhorting us to give charity and forbidding us from mutilation (muthlah)"," saying: 'Among the forms of mutilation is that a person vow to pierce his own nose"," and among the forms of mutilation is that a person vow to perform Hajj on foot. If any of you vows to perform Hajj on foot"," let him offer a sacrificial animal (hadya) and ride.'\""\n\nMuhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Ansari also narrated it from Salih"," and in his version of the hadith he said: \""Let him offer a she-camel (badanah) and ride.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20132","(20126) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Baghawi in Baghdad informed us — Abu Qalabah 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us — Salih ibn Rustam narrated it with its meaning, saying: \Let him offer a she-camel (badanah) and ride.\""\n\nHowever"," the hearing (sama') of al-Hasan from 'Imran is not established; hence there is an irsal (broken link) in it. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""
"20133","(20127) And it has been narrated regarding this from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asam informed us — al-Rabi' said: al-Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, said — from Ibn 'Ulayyah from Sa'id from Qatadah from al-Hasan from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning a man who took an oath to walk (to the Ka'bah): \He should walk"," and if he is unable"," he should ride and offer a she-camel (badanah) as sacrifice.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"20134","(20128) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Malik ibn Anas and 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated from 'Urwah ibn Udhaynah, who said: \I went out with my grandmother"," upon whom was an obligation of walking (to the Ka'bah). When we had covered part of the way"," she became unable (to continue). She sent her freed slave to 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with both of them"," to ask him. I went with him and he asked Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with both of them. He said: 'Let her ride"," then let her walk from the point at which she became unable.'\"" [Sahih]"""
"20135","(20129) Abu Zakariyya and Abu Bakr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas informed us — Muhammad informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from al-Sha'bi from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with both of them, with the same ruling as that of Ibn 'Umar. Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with both of them, added: \And let him offer a she-camel (badanah) as sacrifice.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20136","(20130) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Razzaz in Baghdad informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Shafi'i narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Jahm al-Samari narrated to us — Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd and Yazid ibn Harun narrated from Isma'il from 'Amir, meaning al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who vowed to walk to the Ka'bah: he walked half the road and then rode. Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with both of them, said: \Let him ride in the coming year the distance he walked"," and walk the distance he rode"," and let him offer a she-camel (badanah) as sacrifice.\"" [Hasan]"""
"20137","(20131) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas, he is al-Asam, informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Malik narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id, who said: \I had an obligation of walking (to the Ka'bah)"," but I was afflicted with a pain in my flank"," so I rode until I reached Makkah. I asked 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah and others"," and they said: 'A sacrificial offering (hadya) is incumbent upon you.' When I arrived in Madinah"," I asked (the scholars there) and they instructed me to walk from the point at which I had become unable"," so I walked once again.\""\n\nThe position that al-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," validated in the Kit al-Nudur regarding the obligation of walking to the extent of one's ability and its falling away in the event of inability is the strongest of the opinions"," by the hadith of Abu Hurayrah and Anas ibn Malik"," may Allah be pleased with both of them"," and Abu al-Khayr from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir"," may Allah be pleased with him"," from the Prophet ﷺ. And this is the most deserving position. And with Allah lies all success. [Sahih. Reported by al-Shafi'i]"""
"20138","(20132) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Isfahani informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us — al-Walid ibn Muslim said: \I asked Abu 'Amr"," meaning al-Awza'i"," about one upon whom walking to the House of Allah is obligatory — from where should he walk?\"" He said: \""If he intended a specific place"," then from where he intended; and if he did not intend a specific place"," then from his miqat (designated station).\""\n\n'Ata' also informed me from Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with both of them"," to that effect. [Da'if]"""
"20139","(20133) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us — Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us — Musaddad and 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from al-Zuhri from Sa'id from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Mounts shall not be saddled (for travel) except to three mosques: al-Masjid al-Haram"," Masjid Rasul Allah ﷺ"," and al-Masjid al-Aqsa.\""\n\nIbn al-Madini said: \""Thus Sufyan narrated it to us this time with this wording"," though the more common wording of his is: 'Mounts are saddled to three mosques.'\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Ali ibn al-Madini"," and Muslim narrated it from 'Amr al-Naqid from Sufyan. [Sahih]"""
"20140","(20134) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Ibn Abi Qumash narrated to us — Abu al-Walid narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr from Qaza'ah, the freed slave of Ziyad, who said: \I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri"," may Allah be pleased with him"," narrate from the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: 'Four things have amazed me and captivated me: A woman should not travel more than three days except with a mahram; there should be no fasting on two days — the day of Fitr and the day of Adha; there should be no prayer (i.e."," supererogatory prayer) after two prayers — after the morning prayer until the sun rises"," and after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets; and mounts shall not be saddled except to three mosques — my mosque"," al-Masjid al-Haram"," and al-Masjid al-Aqsa' — or he said"," 'Bayt al-Maqdis.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Walid"," and Muslim reported it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Sahih. Muttafagun 'alayh]"""
"20141","(20135) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar narrated to us, Quraysh ibn Anas narrated from Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd; and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us, Bakkār ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated to us, Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I made a vow at the time of the Conquest that if Allah granted you victory"," I would pray in Bayt al-Maqdis.\"" He said: \""Pray here.\"" He repeated it to him two or three times"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Then it is your affair.\""\n\nḤammād ibn Salamah narrated it from Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim from ʿAṭāʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20142","(20136) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿbad, who said: A woman complained of an ailment and said: \If Allah heals me"," I shall certainly go out and pray in Bayt al-Maqdis.\"" She recovered and prepared to set out. Maymūnah"," the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," came to greet her and she delayed her departure for that reason. She said: \""Sit down"," and partake of what I have prepared"," and pray in the mosque of the Messenger (ﷺ)"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'One prayer in it is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque"," except the Masjid al-Ḥarām.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1396]"""
"20143","(20137) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, Rūḥ ibn al-Faraj narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr, from Mālik ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Rabbāḥ and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Salmān—both of them—from Abī ʿAbd Allāh al-Agharr, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \One prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other"," except the Masjid al-Ḥarām.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20144","(20138) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr both narrated to us, saying: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have sacrificed here"," and all of Minā is a place of sacrifice.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ from his father. And the ḥadīth of ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ) has already been mentioned in the Book of Ḥajj: \""All of Minā is a place of sacrifice"," and all the open pathways of Makkah are a road and a place of sacrifice.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20145","(20139) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq narrated from al-Awzāʿī, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abī Qilābah; Thābit ibn al-Ḥaḥḥāk narrated to me, saying: A man made a vow during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he would sacrifice at Buwānah. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Was there any idol from among the idols of the Jāhiliyyah that was worshipped there?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Was there any festival from among their festivals?\"" They said: \""No.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Then fulfil your vow"," for there is no fulfilment of a vow in disobedience to Allah"," nor in that over which the son of Ādam has no power.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20146","(20140) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, Mālik ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd ibn Miqsam—and he is the son of Ḍabbah—narrated to me; my paternal aunt Sārah ibnat Miqsam narrated to me from Maymūnah ibnat Kardam, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Makkah upon his she-camel, and I was with my father. She mentioned the hadith. She said: My father said to him in that place: \I have vowed to slaughter a number of sheep.\"" He said—I do not know except that he said: \""Fifty sheep at the head of Buwānah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Is there anything of these idols upon it?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then fulfil for Allah what you have vowed to Him.\"" He said: My father gathered them and began to slaughter them"," but one sheep escaped from him. He searched for it"," saying: \""O Allah"," fulfil my vow for me","\"" until he caught it and slaughtered it.\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī from Yazīd"," and he said: \""I vowed that if a male child were born to me"," I would sacrifice at the head of Buwānah"," at a pass among the mountain passes"," a number of sheep.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20147","(20141) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in Gharāʾib al-Shuyūkh, Aḥmad ibn Sulmān al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sallām al-Sawwāq narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ al-Ghudānī narrated to us, al-Masʿūdī narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \I have vowed to slaughter at Buwānah.\"" He said: \""Is there anything of the Jāhiliyyah in your heart?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then fulfil your vow.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20148","(20142) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad al-Hilālī—and he is Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah—narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), narrating it as reaching the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \On the day of Jumuʿah"," there are angels at every door of the mosque who record the people"," the first first. The one who hastens to the prayer is like one who offers a camel in sacrifice"," then the one who follows him is like one who offers a cow"," then the one who follows him is like one who offers a ram"," until he mentioned the hen and the egg. When the imām sits"," the scrolls are folded and they gather for the khutbah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Sufyān. And both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from another route from al-Zuhrī from al-Agharr from Abū Hurayrah: \""Then like the one who offers a hen"," then like the one who offers an egg.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated in the Book of Ḥajj from ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them) that they both said: \""The sacrificial animals from among the pairs are eight.\"" And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20149","(20143) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī narrated to us, Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah; Ḥakīm ibn Abī Ḥurrah al-Aslamī narrated to me: I heard a man asking ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) about a man who vowed that no day would pass by him—which he named—except that he would be fasting on it, and that coincided with the day of Aḍḥā or the day of Fiṭr. Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \Indeed"," in the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) you have a good example\"" [al-Aḥzāb 21]. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not fast on the day of Aḍḥā nor on the day of Fiṭr"," nor did he command fasting on them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī.\n\nAnd in this narration"," along with what we have narrated from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ)—\""There is no fulfilment of a vow in disobedience to Allah"," nor in that over which the son of Ādam has no power\""—there is an indication that its fulfilment is not obligatory. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20150","(20144) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zuraʿī narrated to us, Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd narrated from Ziyād ibn Jubayr, who said: I was with Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) when a man came to him and said: \I have vowed to fast every Tuesday or Thursday for as long as I live"," even if this day happens to be the day of sacrifice.\"" Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \""Allah has commanded the fulfilment of vows"," and we have been forbidden to fast on this day.\"" He said: It seemed to the man that he had not understood"," so he repeated the words a second time. Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \""Allah has commanded the fulfilment of vows"," and we have been forbidden to fast on this day.\"" Yūnus said: I mentioned that to al-Ḥasan"," and he said: \""Let him fast another day in its place.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī from Yazīd ibn Zuraʿī"," without the statement of al-Ḥasan. And Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAwn from Ziyād ibn Jubayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20151","(20145) Abu al-Zubayr reported that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah being asked about a woman who had performed an 'Umrah in a specified month, then only one night passed before she experienced her menses. He said: She should set out, then enter into ihram for an 'Umrah, then wait until she becomes pure, then perform tawaf around the Ka'bah, then pray. [Sahih]"
"20152","(20146) Abu Ghalib narrated in a hadith he mentioned from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding the funeral prayer, saying: 'Ala' ibn Ziyad said, \O Abu Hamzah"," did you participate in a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him?\"" He said: \""Yes"," I participated in the Battle of Hunayn with him. The polytheists came out and attacked us until we saw our horses behind our backs. Among the people was a man who was attacking us"," striking and crushing us. Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," routed them all and caused them to come to him"," pledging allegiance to Islam.\"" A man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," said: \""I have taken a vow that if Allah brings me the man who was crushing us since this day"," I will surely strike his neck.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," remained silent. The man was then brought before him. When he saw the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," he said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I repent to Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," did not accept his allegiance so that the man might fulfill his vow. The man then kept presenting himself before the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," seeking his command to kill him"," while he feared that the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," would have him killed. When the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," saw that he would do nothing"," he accepted his allegiance. The man said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," my vow!\"" He said: \""I did not hold back concerning him since this day except that you might fulfill your vow.\"" He said: \""O Messenger Allah"," why did you not give me a signal?\"" The Prophet"," peace be upon him"," said: \""It is not befitting for a prophet to give a signal.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20153","(20147) 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utban ibn Mas'ud informed me that Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubada al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, consulted the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, regarding a vow that had been incumbent upon his mother, but she had passed away before fulfilling it. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, commanded him to fulfill it on her behalf. This subsequently became an established Sunnah thereafter. Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu al-Yaman. [Sahih — agreed upon]"
"20154","(20148) Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a woman embarked upon a sea voyage and vowed that if Allah saved her, she would fast for one month. Allah saved her, but she did not fast before she died. Her daughter or her sister came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and he commanded her to fast on her behalf. All other narrations on this subject have been previously cited in the Book of Fasting and the Book of Hajj. And with Allah lies all success. [Sahih — agreed upon]"
"20155","(20149) Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Prophet, peace be upon him, sent a man over Najran, and they complained about him. He said: \I shall send over you a man of true trustworthiness"," a man truly deserving of trust.\"" The Companions of the Prophet"," peace be upon him"," looked up eagerly for this"," and he sent Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muslim ibn Ibrahim"," and Muslim also recorded it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"20156","(20150) Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, sent him and Mu'adh to Yemen, saying: \Make things easy and do not make them difficult; give glad tidings and do not repel people; be in harmony with one another and do not differ.\"" He said: \""Each of them had a tent (fusṭāṭ) in which each would visit the other.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah"," and al-Bukhari cited it as evidence through the narration of Yazid ibn Harun and Waki'. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"20157","(20151) Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated: When the Prophet, peace be upon him, sent him to Yemen, the Prophet, peace be upon him, set out with him, giving him counsel and instruction, while Mu'adh was riding and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was walking beneath his mount. When he had finished, he said: \O Mu'adh"," it may be that you will not meet me after this year of mine"," and it may be that you will pass by my mosque and my grave.\"" The Sheikh said: \""This refers to his second mission.\"" [Hasan]"""
"20158","(20152) Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, sent 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, to collect the alms (ṣadaqah). Muslim recorded it in his Sahih as stated. [Sahih — Muslim 983]"
"20159","(20153) 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, sent me as a judge to Yemen. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am a young man"," and you are sending me to a people of mature age.\"" He then supplicated with several prayers for me and said: \""When two disputants come to you and you hear the words of one of them"," do not render judgment until you hear the words of the other"," for that is more fitting for you.\"" He said: \""After that"," no judicial ruling ever troubled me.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20160","(20154) 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, sent me to Yemen. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you send me while I am young and have no knowledge of judging.\"" He said: \""Go"," for Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," will guide your heart and make your tongue firm.\"" He said: \""After that"," I never felt doubt in any judgment between two men.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20161","(20155) Ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who heard Abū al-Bakhtarī say: One who heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to Yemen, I said, \O Messenger of Allah"," you are sending me while I am a young man and I have no knowledge of much of the matter of judging.\"" He (ﷺ) then placed his hand on my chest and said"," \""Indeed"," Allah will make your tongue firm and guide your heart.\"" After that"," no judgment between two people was difficult for me.\n\n[Weak]"""
"20162","(20156) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr informed us: Miṣʿar ibn Kidām narrated from Muḥārib ibn Dithār, who said: When Abū Bakr became caliph, he appointed ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) as judge and appointed Abū ʿUbaydah (may Allah be pleased with him) over the treasury, and said, \Assist me.\"" So ʿUmar remained for a year without two people coming to him"," or without him passing judgment between two people.\n\n[Weak]"""
"20163","(20157) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī informed us: Sufyān informed us: ʿĀmir ibn Shaqīq informed us that he heard Abū Wāʾil say: Indeed, ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) appointed ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) over the judiciary and the treasury.\n\n[Sound]"
"20164","(20158) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Nuʿaym informed us: Zakariyyā narrated from ʿĀmir: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) appointed Ibn Masʿūd over the judiciary of Baṣrah and appointed Shurayḥ over the judiciary of Kūfah.\n\n[Weak]"
"20165","(20159) Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb informed me: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Khālid ibn Yazīd, from his father: that when death approached Abū al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with him), and he was the judge of Damascus, Muʿāwiyah said to him, \Whom do you see for this matter?\"" He said"," \""Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"20166","(20160) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read to Mālik, from Khubayb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿĀṣim, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī or Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Seven will be shaded by Allah in His shade on the day when there shall be no shade except His shade: a just leader; a youth who grew up in the worship of Allah; a man whose heart is attached to the mosque when he leaves it until he returns to it; two men who love each other for the sake of Allah"," meeting upon that and parting upon it; a man who remembers Allah in solitude and his eyes overflow with tears; a woman of beauty and status invites him"," but he says"," 'I fear Allah'; and a man who gives charity in secret so that his left hand does not know what his right hand spends.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar"," from Khubayb"," from Ḥafṣ"," from Abū Hurayrah"," without doubt.\n\n[Sound — Agreed Upon]"""
"20167","(20161) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Hishām narrated from Qatādah, from Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr, from ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār al-Mujāshiʿī, that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said one day in his sermon — and he mentioned the ḥadīth — and said: \The people of Paradise are three: a just and rightly guided ruler who gives charity; a man who is merciful and tender-hearted towards every relative and every Muslim; and a poor"," chaste man who gives charity. And the people of the Fire are five: the weak one who has no sense — those who are among you as followers"," seeking neither family nor wealth; the traitor whose greed is not hidden"," however small it may be"," without him betraying it; and a man who does not pass morning or evening except that he deceives you regarding your family and your wealth.\"" And he mentioned miserliness and lying"," and \""the obscene"," foul-mouthed one.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hishām and others from Qatādah"," and he said: \""a just ruler\"" (dhū sulṭānin muqsiṭ).\n\n[Sound — Muslim 2865]"""
"20168","(20162) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl informed us: Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī informed us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿAmr ibn Aws, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The just ones"," on the Day of Resurrection"," will be upon pulpits of light"," at the right hand of the Most Merciful — and both His hands are right — those who are just in their judgments"," their families"," and those under their authority.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān.\n\n[Sound — Muslim 1827]"""
"20169","(20163) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Zuhayr narrated from Saʿd al-Ṭāʾī: Abū al-Mudallah narrated to me — he heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Three supplications are not rejected: the supplication of a just leader"," the supplication of one who is fasting until he breaks his fast"," and the supplication of the oppressed. It is carried upon the clouds"," and the gates of heaven are opened for it"," and the Lord says"," 'By My glory"," I will surely help you"," even if it is after a while.'\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"20170","(20164) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān said: Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī said:\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us: al-Ḥumaydī informed us: Sufyān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated this ḥadīth, not as al-Zuhrī narrated it to us. He said: I heard Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim say: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and empowered him to spend it in the truth"," and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom"," by which he judges and teaches it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," and Muslim narrated it from another chain from Ismāʿīl.\n\n[Sound — Agreed Upon]"""
"20171","(20165) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that ʿAbbās al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Yūnus narrated to us that Mulāzim ibn ʿAmr narrated to me that Mūsā ibn Najdah narrated from his grandfather Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who was Abū Kathīr, who narrated to me that Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: \Whoever seeks the judiciary of the Muslims and attains it"," and his justice prevails over his wrongdoing"," he shall have Paradise; and whoever's wrongdoing prevails over his justice"," he shall have the Fire.\"" [Weak]"""
"20172","(20166) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Sulaymān al-Burlusī narrated to us that al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yazīd al-Ashʿarī narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When the judge sits in his place"," two angels descend upon him"," guiding him"," directing him rightly"," and showing him the correct path"," so long as he does not commit injustice. When he commits injustice"," they ascend and leave him.\"" [Weak]"""
"20173","(20167) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Abū Aḥmad Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us that Abū Qalābah ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn ʢĀṣim al-Kilābī narrated to us that ʿImrān al-Qaṭṭān narrated from al-Shaybānī from Ibn Abī Awfā, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," is with the judge so long as he does not commit injustice. When he commits injustice"," Allah disassociates Himself from him"," and Satan clings to him.\"" [Weak]"""
"20174","(20168) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy informed us that Ibn Ṣāʿid informed us that Aḥmad ibn Sinān al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Bilāl narrated from ʿImrān al-Qaṭṭān from Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī from Ibn Abī Awfā, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," is with the judge so long as he does not commit injustice. When he commits injustice"," He leaves him to himself.\""\n\nIbn Ṣāʿid said: ʿAmr ibn ʿĀṣim narrated it from ʿImrān al-Qaṭṭān but did not mention Ḥusayn in his chain of narration. [Weak]"""
"20175","(20169) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hāniʾ narrated to us that Abū Saʿīd al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad al-Quhunduzī narrated to us that ʿAbdān ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us that al-Fuḍayl ibn Marzūq narrated to us that ʿAṭiyyah al-ʿAwfī narrated from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The most beloved of people to Allah on the Day of Resurrection and the closest of them to Him in station is a just leader"," and the most hated of people to Allah on the Day of Resurrection and the most severely punished of them is an unjust leader.\"" [Weak]"""
"20176","(20170) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAliyy ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq narrated to us that Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, who said: I heard Kurz ibn Qays, who was the general judge of Kūfah, say: A man from the Companions of Badr informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \That I sit in a gathering such as this is more beloved to me than that I free four slaves.\"" Shuʿbah said: I asked"," \""What type of gathering did he mean?\"" He said: \""A judicial gathering.\"" [Weak]"""
"20177","(20171) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Maʿmar ibn Sulaymān al-Raqqī narrated from al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh that Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: \That I judge for one day and therein attain truth and justice is more beloved to me than fighting for a year\"" — or he said"," \""a hundred days.\"" Al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh raised it to Ibn Masʿūd with a broken chain"," whereas it is narrated from Masrūq. [Weak]"""
"20178","(20172) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us that ʿAliyy ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Ḥāmid Muḥammad ibn Hārūn al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Mujālid ibn Saʿīd narrated to me that ʿĀmir narrated from Masrūq from ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \There is no ruler who judges between people…\"" — and he mentioned the hadith. And Masrūq said: \""That I judge for one day with truth is more beloved to me than that I fight for a year in the cause of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\"" [Weak]"""
"20179","(20173) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated from Rabiʿah ibn ʿUthmān from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah than the weak believer"," though there is good in both. Strive for that which benefits you"," seek help from Allah"," and do not feel helpless. If something befalls you"," do not say"," 'If only I had done such and such.' Rather say"," 'Allah has decreed"," and what He wills He does.' For indeed 'if only' opens the door to the work of Satan.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others. [Authentic. Muslim 2664]"""
"20180","(20174) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated from Shuʿbah from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that ʿAmmār ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated from Shuʿbah, who said: al-Aʿmash narrated to me from Yaḥyā ibn Waththāb from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \The believer who mixes with people and is patient with their harm is better than the believer who does not mix with people and is not patient with their harm.\""\n\nThe wording is from the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh. [Authentic. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī 1988]"""
"20181","(20175) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us — al-'Abbas narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us — al-A'mash narrated from Yahya ibn Waththab and Abu Salih, from a shaykh among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The believer who mingles with people and endures their harm is greater in reward than the believer who does not mingle with people and does not endure their harm.\"" [Sahih. Previously referenced.]"""
"20182","(20176) Abu Bakr ibn Fawak informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from 'As'as ibn Salamah, that the Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and missed one of his Companions. The man was brought before him and said: \I wish to seclude myself to worship my Lord and withdraw from people.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do not do that"," and let none of you do that\"" — he said it three times — \""For an hour of patience in the gatherings of Muslims is better than forty years of worship in seclusion.\"" [Da'if.]"""
"20183","(20177) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, both saying — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Jahm narrated to us — Yazid ibn Harun narrated from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Help your brother"," whether he is an oppressor or is oppressed.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," we can help him if he is oppressed"," but how can we help him if he is an oppressor?\"" He said: \""By preventing him from oppressing.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in al-Sahih from two other routes from Humayd.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with seven things\"" — and he mentioned them"," among them being \""helping the oppressed.\"" [Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"20184","(20178) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Tamtam narrated to us — Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Harith, meaning ibn Fudayl al-Khatmi, from Ja'far ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar, from Abu Rafi', from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no prophet whom Allah sent to a community before me except that he had from his community disciples (hawariyyun) and companions who followed his ways and adhered to his Sunnah. Then after them came successors who said what they did not do and did what they were not commanded. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer; whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer; and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer. And beyond that"," there is not even a grain of mustard seed of faith.\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in al-Sahih from another route from Ibrahim"," and the hadith of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri to the same effect has already been fully presented in the Book of the Two Eid Prayers. [Sahih. Muslim 50.]"""
"20185","(20179) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl al-Fahham narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yahyadh-Dhuhli narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us — al-A'mash narrated from Isma'il ibn Raja' from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Whoever among you sees an evil"," let him change it with his hand if he is able; if he cannot"," then with his tongue; and if he cannot"," then with his heart — and that is the weakest of faith.\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in al-Sahih. [Sahih. Muslim 49.]"""
"20186","(20180) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed us by dictation — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Baghdadi narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from Qatadah, who said: I heard Abu Nadrah narrating from —\n\nAnd Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr al-Fahham narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us — Wahb ibn Jarir and 'Abd al-Samad both narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let not the fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he knows it.\"" Abu Sa'id said: \""Calamity continued to befall us until we fell short"," and we would only convey it in secret.\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20187","(20181) 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us — Abu Bakr al-Qattan narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from Abu Maslamah, who said: I heard Abu Nadrah narrating from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and he mentioned it. Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: \That is what compelled me to set out for Mu'awiyah"," to fill his ears with it"," and then return.\"" [Sahih. Previously referenced.]"""
"20188","(20182) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr al-Fahham narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Sufyan narrated from Zubayd, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Juhayfah, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Jihad is of three kinds: the first over which the hand prevails"," then the tongue"," then the heart. When the heart neither recognizes truth nor rejects evil"," it is inverted — its upper part is made its lower part.\""\n\nThis is mawquf. [Sahih.]"""
"20189","(20183) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us — Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us — al-Humaydi narrated to us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us — Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated from Abu Tawalah, from Nahhari al-'Abdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Indeed"," Allah will ask the servant on the Day of Resurrection about everything"," until He will ask: 'What prevented you"," when you saw an evil"," from rejecting it?' When Allah confronts the servant with His proof"," the servant will say: 'O Lord"," I hoped in You and feared the people.'\"" [Hasan.]"""
"20190","(20184) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr al-Fahham narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us by ijazah — Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us — al-A'mash narrated from 'Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let none of you belittle himself regarding a matter of Allah's command about which he has something to say but does not act upon it"," so that he meets Allah and Allah says: 'What prevented you from saying such-and-such on such-and-such a day?' He will say: 'O Lord"," I feared the people.' Allah will say: 'I am more deserving of being feared.'\""\n\nZubayd and Shu'bah followed him regarding this from 'Amr ibn Murrah. [Da'if.]"""
"20191","(20185) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Faḥḥām narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Muṭahhar narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān narrated from al-Muʿallā ibn Ziyād from Abū Ghālib from Abū Umāmah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked when he stoned the jamrah: \O Messenger of Allah"," which jihād is most beloved to Allah?\"" He said: \""A word of truth spoken before an unjust ruler.\""\n\nAl-Muʿallā said: And al-Ḥasan used to say \""before an oppressive ruler.\"" [Weak]"""
"20192","(20186) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Faḥḥām narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us that Salām ibn Sulaymān, the Qurʾān reciter of the people of Baṣrah, narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir informed us, saying: Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us that Yazīd ibn ʿUmar ibn Janzah al-Madāʾinī narrated to us that Salām Abū al-Mundhir al-Muqriʾ al-Baṣrī narrated from Muḥammad ibn Wāsiʿ from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ṣāmit from Abū Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: My intimate friend, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, enjoined upon me seven things: He commanded me to look to those below me and not to look to those above me; he commanded me to love the poor and to be close to them; he commanded me not to ask anyone for anything; he commanded me to maintain ties of kinship even if they turn away; he commanded me to speak the truth even if it is bitter; he commanded me not to let the blame of any blamer deter me in the matter of Allah; and he commanded me to frequently say \Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh","\"" for it is from the treasures of Paradise.\n\nThe wording of his hadith is from al-Muḥammadābādhī. [Authentic]"""
"20193","(20187) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī narrated to us that Ismāʿīl Muḥammad al-Fasawī narrated to us that Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Hishāb ibn Ḥassān and al-Ḥasan ibn Dīnār narrated from Muḥammad ibn Wāsiʿ, and he mentioned it with its chain, similar to it, in the ninth dictation."
"20194","(20188) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us that al-Aʿmash narrated from al-Shaʿbī from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The example of those who transgress the limits of Allah and those who are complacent therein is like a people who drew lots for their places on a ship: some of them got the lower deck and some got the upper deck. When those on the lower deck wanted water"," they had to pass by those above them"," causing them harm. So those on the upper deck said: 'You are harming us by pouring water upon us.' Then those on the lower deck took an axe — meaning they began to bore holes in the ship. Those on the upper deck said: 'What are you doing? If you leave them and what they intend"," you will all perish; but if you restrain their hands"," you will all be saved.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of al-Aʿmash. [Authentic. Previously cited]"""
"20195","(20189) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Faḥḥām narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, who said: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \O people"," you recite this verse: {O you who believe"," upon you is your own selves; those who go astray will not harm you when you are guided} [al-Māʾidah 105]. And indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When the people see an unjust oppressor and do not restrain his hand"," it is near that Allah will encompass them all with punishment.'\"" [Authentic]"""
"20196","(20190) Khālid ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Wāsiṭī narrated it from Ismāʿīl with the same meaning, adding: \You recite this verse and place it in other than its proper context.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated from Khālid"," and he mentioned it.\n\n[Authentic. Previously cited]"""
"20197","(20191) Hushaym narrated from Ismāʿīl with his addition, except that he said: \And indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no people among whom sins are committed while they have the power to change it and do not change it"," except that it is near that Allah will encompass them all with punishment.'\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Mahrūyah ibn ʿAbbās ibn Sinān al-Rāzī narrated to us that Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn al-Wāsiṭī informed us that Hushaym narrated from Ismāʿīl"," and he mentioned it.\n\n[Authentic. Previously cited]"""
"20198","(20192) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Faḥḥām narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ʿAbdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Simsār narrated to us that Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us, both saying: Shuʿbah informed us from Abī Isḥāq from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Jarīr from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no people among whom sins are committed while they are more numerous and more powerful than those who commit them"," and they do not change it"," except that it is near that Allah will encompass them all with punishment.\"" And in the hadith of Wahb: \""except that He will encompass them.\"" [Good]"""
"20199","(20193) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd informed us that Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb informed us that ʿUtbah ibn Abī Ḥakīm al-Hamdānī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAtakī narrated to us that Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from ʿUtbah ibn Abī Ḥakīm. ʿAmr ibn Jāriyah al-Lakhmī narrated to me that Abū Umayyah al-Shaʿbānī narrated to me. And in the narration of Ibn Shuʿayb: from Abū Umayyah al-Shaʿbānī, who said: I came to Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī and said: \How do you understand this verse?\"" He said: \""Which verse?\"" I said: \""His statement"," the Most High: {O you who believe"," upon you is your own selves; those who go astray will not harm you when you are guided} [al-Māʾidah 105].\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I asked about it one who is knowledgeable — I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it"," and he said: 'Rather"," enjoin one another to good and forbid one another from evil"," until when you see obeyed greed"," followed desires"," preferred worldliness"," and every person of opinion admiring his own opinion"," and you see a matter over which you have no power"," then concern yourself with your own soul and leave the affairs of the common people. For ahead of you are days of patience — patience in them is like holding onto burning coals — and the one who acts in them shall have the reward of fifty men who perform the like of his deeds.'\"" The wording is from the hadith of Ibn Shuʿayb. Ibn al-Mubārak added in his narration: \""And someone else added to me: They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," the reward of fifty of them?' He said: 'The reward of fifty of you.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20200","(20194) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī in Kūfah informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah informed us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated from al-Rabīʿ ibn Anas from Abū al-ʿĀliyah, who said: We were with ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd when a dispute arose between two men, as occurs among people, and each of them leapt toward his companion. Some of them said: \Shall I not stand and enjoin them to good and forbid them from evil?\"" Some of them said: \""Upon you is your own self; indeed Allah"," the Most High"," said: {O you who believe"," upon you is your own selves; those who go astray will not harm you when you are guided} [al-Māʾidah 105].\"" Ibn Masʿūd heard this and said: \""The interpretation of this verse has not yet come. The Qurʾān was revealed as it was revealed: among its verses are those whose interpretation passed before they were revealed"," among them are those whose interpretation came after this day"," among them are those whose interpretation will come at the Hour"," and among them are those whose interpretation will come after the Day of Reckoning"," Paradise"," and the Fire. So long as your hearts are united"," your desires are one"," you have not been divided into sects"," and some of you have not tasted the harm of others"," then enjoin and forbid. But when hearts and desires differ"," you are divided into sects"," and some of you taste the harm of others"," then let a man concern himself with his own soul. At that time"," its interpretation will come.\"" [Weak]"""
"20201","(20195) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿIkrimah, who said: I entered upon Ibn ʿAbbās while he was reciting from the Muṣḥaf, before his sight had been taken, and he was weeping. I said, \What makes you weep"," O Ibn ʿAbbās? May Allah make me your ransom.\"" He said to me"," \""Do you know Aylah?\"" I said"," \""And what is Aylah?\"" He said"," \""It was a village in which there were people of the Jews. Allah forbade them from catching fish on the Sabbath. Their fish would come to them on their Sabbath"," appearing openly"," white and fat"," like she-camels"," in their courtyards and their dwellings. But when it was not the day of the Sabbath"," they would not find them"," nor could they obtain them except through great hardship and severe difficulty. Some of them said to one another — or those among them who said it — 'Perhaps if we catch them on the Sabbath and eat them on a day other than the Sabbath.' So one household among them did that. They caught some fish and roasted them. Their neighbors smelled the aroma of the roast and said"," 'By Allah"," we do not see that the so-and-so family has suffered any harm.' Then others also took some"," until that became widespread among them and became frequent. They split into three groups: one group ate"," one group forbade them"," and one group said"," 'Why do you admonish a people whom Allah will destroy or punish with a severe punishment?' [al-Aʿrāf 164] The group that forbade them said"," 'We warn you of the wrath of Allah and His punishment"," that Allah may afflict you with an earthquake"," or a pelting of stones"," or with some of the punishment that is with Him. By Allah"," we will not spend the night in any place where you are.' They went out from behind the wall. The next morning they went to it and knocked on the gate of the wall"," but no one answered them. They brought a ladder and leaned it against the wall. Then one of them climbed up onto the wall and said"," 'O servants of Allah"," by Allah"," they are monkeys"," they have tails!' He said this three times. Then he came down from the wall and opened the gate. The people entered upon them. The monkeys recognized their kin among the humans"," but the humans did not recognize their kin among the monkeys. The monkey would come to his relative and kinsman among the humans and cling to him and press close to him"," and the human would say"," 'Are you so-and-so?' And he would nod with his head"," meaning 'yes","' and he would weep. The she-monkey would come to her relative and kinsman among the humans"," and the human would say to her"," 'Are you so-and-so?' And she would nod with her head"," meaning 'yes","' and she would weep. The humans said to them"," 'We warned you of the wrath of Allah and His punishment"," that He might afflict you with an earthquake"," or a transformation of form"," or with some of the punishment that is with Him.'\"" Ibn ʿAbbāh"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," said: \""And I heard Allah"," the Most High"," say: 'And We saved those who forbade evil"," and We seized those who did wrong with a terrible punishment because of what they used to do of transgression.' [al-Aʿrāf 165] I do not know what happened to the third group.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," said: \""How many an evil have we seen and not forbidden it!\"" ʿIkrimah said: I said"," \""Do you not consider — may Allah make me your ransom — that they did reject and disapprove when they said"," 'Why do you admonish a people whom Allah will destroy or punish with a severe punishment?' [al-Aʿrāf 164]\"" My statement pleased him"," and he ordered for me two thick cloaks"," which he gave me. [Weak]"""
"20202","(20196) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Nufaylī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Rāshid narrated from ʿAlī ibn Badhīmah from Abū ʿUbaydah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The first deficiency that entered the Children of Israel was that a man would meet a man and say"," 'O so-and-so"," fear Allah and leave what you are doing"," for it is not lawful for you.' Then he would meet him the following day"," and that would not prevent him from being his eating companion"," his drinking companion"," and his sitting companion. When they did that"," Allah struck the hearts of some of them against others.\"" Then he said: \""Cursed were those who disbelieved among the Children of Israel by the tongue of Dāwūd and ʿĪsā"," son of Maryam. That was because they disobeyed and were transgressing. They did not forbid one another from the evil they committed. Evil indeed was what they used to do.\"" [al-Māʾidah 78–79] Then he said: \""Nay"," by Allah"," you will certainly enjoin what is good"," and you will certainly forbid what is evil"," and you will certainly take hold of the hand of the oppressor"," and you will certainly compel him to the truth by constraint"," and you will certainly restrict him to the truth by restriction.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20203","(20197) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us orally that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah that Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Ghālib narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from four women, some of whom were lower in chain than others. It was said, \O Abū Muḥammad"," whom did you mention?\"" He said: \""Al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from four women"," some of whom were lower in chain than others.\"" It was said"," \""O Abū Muḥammad"," what are their names?\"" Al-Zuhrī narrated from ʿUrwah from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah from Ḥabībah from her mother Umm Ḥabībah from Zaynab bint Jaḥsh"," who said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) awoke from sleep"," his face flushed red"," and he said: 'There is no god but Allah. Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today"," a hole has been opened in the barrier of Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj.' And he made a circle of ninety with his fingers. I said"," 'O Messenger of Allah"," shall we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?' He said"," 'Yes"," when wickedness becomes prevalent.'\"" [Authentic]"""
"20204","(20198) ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us that Abū Saʿīd narrated to us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah from Ḥabībah from her mother Umm Ḥabībah from Zaynab, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), and he mentioned something similar to it, except that he said: \He was saying"," 'There is no god but Allah","' three times"," and he said: 'And he made a circle with his finger.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl from Sufyān"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān. [Authentic. Preceded before it]"""
"20205","(20199) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ashhalī from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \You will certainly enjoin what is good and forbid what is evil"," or Allah will soon send upon you a punishment from Him"," and then you will supplicate to Him"," but He will not respond to you.\"" [Weak]"""
"20206","(20200) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm Abū Bakr al-Faḥḥām narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Abū Hammām al-Dallāl narrated to us that Hishām, meaning Ibn Saʿd, narrated from ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān ibn Hānīʿ from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿUthmān from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me one day"," and I recognized in his face that something had come over him. He performed wuḍūʾ and went out"," and he did not speak to anyone. I pressed close to the chambers to hear what he said. He sat upon the minbar and then said: 'O people"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," says: \""Enjoin what is good and forbid what is evil"," before you call upon Me and I do not answer you"," and you ask Me and I do not give you"," and you seek My help and I do not help you.\""'\"" [Weak]"""
"20207","(20201) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us in Marw that Aḥmad ibn Sayyār narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Jabalah narrated to me that my father narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Simāk, who said: \We were with Muddarik ibn al-Muhallab in Sijistān"," in his tent"," and I heard an old man narrating from Abū Sufyān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," who said: 'Allah does not sanctify a nation in which the weak does not take his right from the strong without being hindered.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20208","(20202) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that Abū Mūsā and Bundār both said: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Sufyān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, who said: \A man owed the Prophet (ﷺ) some dates. He came to him demanding repayment"," so the Prophet (ﷺ) borrowed dates from Khawlah bint Ḥakīm and gave them to him. He said: 'Indeed"," I had dates with me"," but they were old and spoiled.' Then he said: 'Thus do the believing servants of Allah act. Allah does not have mercy upon a nation in which the weak among them does not take his right without being hindered.'\""\n\nThis is a mursal narration"," and it is correct. [Weak]"""
"20209","(20203) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated from Manṣūr, meaning Ibn Abī al-Aswad, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Muḥārib ibn Dithār from Ibn Buraydah from his father, who said: \When Jaʿfar returned from Abyssinia"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him"," 'What is the most remarkable thing you saw?' He said"," 'I saw a woman with a basket of food on her head. A horseman passed by"," galloping"," and he scattered it. She began gathering her food and said"," \""Woe to you"," on the day when the King sets up His throne and takes for the oppressed from the oppressor.\""' The Prophet (ﷺ)"," confirming her words"," said: 'A nation is not sanctified' — or he said"," 'How can it be sanctified — when the weak among them does not take their right from the strong without being hindered.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20210","(20204) ʿAlī informed us, Aḥmad narrated to us, al-Asfāṭī — that is, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl — narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān Saʿdawayh narrated to us that Manṣūr ibn Abī al-Aswad narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Muḥārib ibn Dithār from Ibn Buraydah from his father, with that.\n\n(T) And it has preceded in the Book of Usurpation from ʿAmr ibn Abī Qays from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib with something similar, and it has been narrated from another chain from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh. [Weak. Preceded before it]"
"20211","(20205) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us that Abū Qilābah narrated to us that Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us that Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Faḥḥām narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Masʿūd narrated to us that Zuhayr — and he is Ibn Muḥammad — from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Beware of sitting on the roadways.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," we have no choice but to sit and converse in our gatherings.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""If you insist upon sitting"," then give the road its right.\"" They asked: \""What is the right of the road?\"" He said: \""Lowering the gaze"," refraining from harm"," returning the greeting of peace"," enjoining what is good"," and forbidding what is evil.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad from Abū ʿĀmir"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ḥafṣ ibn Mayṣarah from Zayd ibn Aslam. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20212","(20206) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to me that Simāk ibn Ḥarb said: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrate from his father that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \You will be tested"," you will be granted victory"," and conquest will be opened for you. So whoever among you witnesses that"," let him fear Allah"," enjoin what is good"," and forbid what is evil.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20213","(20207) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʔbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah, from his father, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Upon every Muslim there is a charity (ṣadaqah) every day.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what if he does not find anything?\"" He said: \""Let him work with his hands"," benefit himself"," and give charity.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what if he cannot do that?\"" He said: \""Let him assist the one in desperate need.\"" They said: \""What if he is unable?\"" He said: \""Let him enjoin what is good and forbid what is evil.\"" They said: \""What if he is unable?\"" He said: \""Let him refrain from evil"," for that is a charity for him.\"" The wording is that of Abū Dāwūd's ḥadīth"," and in the narration of Sulaymān there is no mention of \""every day\"" nor his statement \""and forbid what is evil.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ as mentioned above. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20214","(20208) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrīʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us that Mahdī ibn Maymūn narrated to us that Wāṣil, the freedman of Abū ʿUyaynah, narrated from Yaḥyā ibn ʿUqayl, from Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar, from Abū al-Aswad al-Duʾilī, from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Upon every one of you Muslims there is a charity. Every utterance of 'Subḥān Allāh' (Glory be to Allah) is a charity; every utterance of 'Alḥamdulillāh' (Praise be to Allah) is a charity; every utterance of 'Lā ilāha illallāh' (There is no god but Allah) is a charity; every utterance of 'Allāhu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) is a charity; enjoining what is good is a charity; and forbidding what is evil is a charity. And two rakʿahs of prayer performed at forenoon (al-Ḍuḥā) will suffice for all of that.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad. And in this statement there is an indication that both [enjoining good and forbidding evil] are among the collective obligations (furūḍ al-kifāyāt). And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 720]"""
"20215","(20209) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal informed us that Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us that Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated from Shaqīq, from Usāmah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \By Allah"," I will never say to a man"," 'You are the best of people","' even if he is a commander over me"," after having heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say.\"" They asked: \""What did you hear him say?\"" He said: \""I heard him say: 'A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and thrown into the Fire"," and his intestines will spill out"," and he will go around with them in the Fire just as a donkey goes around its millstone. The people of the Fire will gather around him and say: \""O so-and-so"," what has happened to you? Did you not used to enjoin us to do good and forbid us from evil?\"" He will say: \""I used to enjoin you upon good but not do it myself"," and I used to forbid you from evil but commit it myself.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20216","(20210) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar al-Khaṭmī narrated that his grandfather ʿUmayr ibn Ḥabīb — who had pledged allegiance to the Prophet (ﷺ) — left a will for his sons. He said to them: \O my sons"," beware of keeping company with the foolish"," for sitting with them is a disease. Whoever shows forbearance toward a fool will be gladdened by his own forbearance. Whoever responds to him will regret it. And whoever does not accept the little that a fool brings him will be made to accept much. When one of you intends to enjoin what is good and forbid what is evil"," let him prepare himself for hardship beforehand"," and let him be certain of reward from Allah. For whoever is certain of reward from Allah will not feel the touch of hardship.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20217","(20211) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Naẓīf al-Miṣrī narrated to us in Makkah that Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Rāzī narrated to us by dictation in Egypt that Hārūn ibn ʿĪsā ibn Mallūl narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqrīʾ narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī informed us that Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Abī Hāshim al-Zāhid al-Naḥwī narrated to us that Bishr ibn Mūsā al-Asadī narrated to us that Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqrīʾ narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar al-Qurashī, from Sālim ibn Abī Sālim al-Jayshānī, from his father, from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \O Abū Dharr"," I love for you what I love for myself. I see you are weak"," so do not take command over two people"," and do not assume guardianship over the property of an orphan.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others from al-Muqrīʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1826]"""
"20218","(20212) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Walīd Ḥassān ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us. He said: I read to Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl, saying: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb narrated to you, from his father, from al-Layth, who narrated to me that Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated from Bakr ibn ʿAmr, from al-Ḥārith ibn Yazīd al-Ḥaḍramī, from Ibn Ḥujayrah al-Akbar, from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," appoint me as a governor.\"" He struck his hand upon my shoulder and then said: \""O Abū Dharr"," you are weak"," and it is a trust. On the Day of Resurrection"," it will be a source of disgrace and regret — except for the one who takes it up with its due right and fulfills what is incumbent upon him regarding it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1825]"""
"20219","(20213) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Sayyār al-Bazzāz informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah ibn al-ʿUryān al-Qurashī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \You will covet leadership"," and it will be a source of regret and remorse on the Day of Resurrection. How excellent is the nursing mother"," and how terrible is the weaning mother!\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 7148]"""
"20220","(20214) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us that Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najīd al-Sulamī informed us that Abū Muslim al-Baṣrī narrated to us that Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no commander of ten people but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand shackled to his neck.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20221","(20215) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Muhammad 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dabbas narrated to us in Makkah: Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Zayd al-Makki narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan narrated from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no leader of ten people but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bound in chains"," until justice frees him or injustice destroys him.\"" [Munkar]"""
"20222","(20216) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: al-'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \O Messenger of Allah"," appoint me over some of that which Allah has entrusted you with.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""O 'Abbas"," O uncle of the Messenger of Allah"," saving a soul is better than an authority you cannot account for.\"" This is the preserved version"," and it is mursal.\n\nAnd it was also narrated from him"," from Ibn al-Munkadir"," from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah"," who said: 'Abd al-Muttalib said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," will you not appoint me?\"" And he mentioned it.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Ahmad ibn Qani' al-Qadi narrated to us in Baghdad: Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Walid al-Sulami al-Basri narrated to us: Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated from Sufyan ibn Sa'id"," and he mentioned it as a connected narration. However"," the first version is more authentic"," and this al-Sulami al-Basri is the only one who narrated it in this form. [Da'if]"""
"20223","(20217) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Tayyibi narrated to us: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Nu'aym al-Hadrami narrated to us: I heard Ziyad ibn al-Harith al-Sudai', a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), narrating. He said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam.\"" He mentioned the hadith at length"," and in it he said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) encamped at a place"," and the people of that place came to him complaining about their governor"," saying: 'He has taken from us things that were between us and his people during the Jahiliyyah.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Did he do that?' They said: 'Yes.' The Prophet (ﷺ) turned to his Companions"," and I was among them"," and said: 'There is no good in leadership for a believing man.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"20224","(20218) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-'Anbari informed us: My grandfather, Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Amr Kashmard informed us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us.\n\n(Additionally), Abu al-Qasim 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Tahmani informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Fadlawayh narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated from 'Uthman al-Akhnasi from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is appointed to the position of judge"," it is as though he has slaughtered himself without a knife.\""\n\nAnd Ibn Ayyub said in his narration from 'Uthman ibn al-Akhnasi. [Sahih]"""
"20225","(20219) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi narrated to us orally: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Qalanisi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us: al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated from 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Akhnasi, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, and from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sits as a judge among the Muslims has been slaughtered without a knife.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20226","(20220) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us: Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr narrated from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is appointed to the position of judge has been slaughtered without a knife.\""\n\n[Sahih. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"20227","(20221) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Isbahani narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: 'Umar ibn al-'Ala' al-Yashkuri narrated to us: Salih ibn Sarj ibn 'Abd al-Qays narrated from 'Imran ibn Hittan, who said: I heard 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) — and the judgeship was mentioned in her presence — say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \The just judge will be brought on the Day of Resurrection"," and he will encounter such severity of reckoning that he will wish he had never judged between two people"," even in the matter of a single date.\"" Thus it is in my book from 'Umar ibn al-'Ala'. [Da'if]"""
"20228","(20222) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Hijjah narrated to us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: 'Amr ibn al-'Ala' al-Yashkuri narrated from Salih ibn Sarj, from 'Imran ibn Hittan, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The just judge will be brought...\"" And he mentioned it with its like. [Da'if. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"20229","(20223) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'Abd Allah — perhaps he mentioned the Prophet (ﷺ) — who said: \There is no judge who judges between people but that an angel is appointed to him"," holding him by the back of his neck"," until he stands him on the brink of Hellfire. Then he raises his head to Allah"," and if He commands him to cast him"," he casts him into a chasm of forty autumns (years).\"" [Da'if]"""
"20230","(20224) The Shaykh, the Imam, Abu al-Tayyib Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman (may Allah have mercy on him), narrated to us orally: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us: Hisham narrated from 'Abbad ibn Abi 'Ali, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \Woe to the commanders"," woe to the chiefs"," and woe to the trustees! On the Day of Resurrection"," a people will wish that their forelocks are tied to the Pleiades"," dangling between the heavens and the earth"," and that they were never put in charge of any matter.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20231","Abu Bakr ibn Furak, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Hisham narrated it with its chain, similarly, except that he said: \Their forelocks were suspended from al-Thurayya"," swaying back and forth.\"" [Weak. Previously cited.]"""
"20232","And Abu Bakr informed us: Abdullah narrated to us; Yunus narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Hisham narrated to us; 'Abbad ibn Abi 'Ali narrated from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The marketplace — its beginning is blame"," its end is regret"," and punishment on the Day of Resurrection.\"" He said: I said: \""O Abu Hurayrah"," except the one among them who feared Allah.\"" He said: \""I am only narrating to you as I heard it.\"" [Weak. Previously cited.]"""
"20233","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Abu 'Awanah narrated from Husayn, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, in the story of the murder of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: \We entered upon him while the people were praising him. A young man came and said: 'Give glad tidings"," O Commander of the Faithful"," of the glad tings Allah has given you — companionship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and early standing in Islam"," as you know. Then you were appointed and you were just"," then martyrdom.' He said: 'O my nephew"," I wish that this were sufficient — neither against me nor for me.' When he turned to leave"," his lower garment was touching the ground. He said: 'Bring the young man back to me.' He said: 'O my nephew"," raise your garment"," for it is purer for your garment and more God-fearing for your Lord.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il. [Sahih. Bukhari 3700.]"""
"20234","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qubb narrated to us; al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid informed us; 'Uqbah, i.e., ibn 'Alqamah, narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us; Simak narrated to me: I heard Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, say: \When 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was stabbed"," I entered upon him and said: 'Give glad tidings"," O Commander of the Faithful"," for Allah"," the Most High"," has established cities through you"," repelled hypocrisy through you"," and spread provision through you.' 'Umar said: 'Are you praising me for my governorship"," O Ibn 'Abbas?' I said: 'Yes"," O Commander of the Faithful"," and for other things as well.' He said: 'By the One in whose Hand is my soul"," I wish I had emerged from it as I entered it — neither reward nor sin.'\"" [Hasan in the context of other narrations.]"""
"20235","Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Zakariyya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Malik said: \Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib was a man who fasted. A man came to him while he was eating bread and greens. He said to him: 'Come and eat.' The man asked him about something. He said: 'What is it with you? I thought it was a matter of judicial ruling.' Sa'id said to him: 'You are foolish! Go to the judge who has been appointed for this. Do you think I should occupy myself with this — or with you?'\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20236","And Abu al-Husayn informed us: 'Abd Allah narrated to us; Ya'qub narrated to us; Abu 'Amr al-Namari narrated to us; Hammad said: Ayyub said: \I found the most knowledgeable people of judicial ruling to be the most severe in fleeing from it"," and the most fearful of it.\"" Then he said: \""And I did not know anyone more knowledgeable of judicial ruling than Abu Qilabah — I do not know what Muhammad ibn Sirin was — who"," when he was sought for the judiciary"," would flee to Syria once and to al-Yamamah once. And when he came to al-Basrah"," he would remain in hiding until he departed.\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20237","And Abu al-Husayn informed us: 'Abd Allah narrated to us; Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad informed us; al-Harith ibn 'Umayr narrated from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said: \The likeness of a judge is only like the likeness of a man swimming in the sea — how long can he swim before he drowns?\"" He said: \""And Abu Qilabah was sought for the judiciary"," so he fled.\"" [Hasan.]"""
"20238","And Abu al-Husayn informed us: 'Abd Allah narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to me; Ahmad ibn al-Khalil narrated to us; al-Akhnasiyy Ahmad ibn 'Imran narrated to me; al-Hasan ibn 'Amr narrated from Abu al-Sahba' al-Taymi, who said: \I came and found Harith ibn Dithar standing in prayer. When he saw me"," he shortened the prayer. Then he came and sat in the seat of the judiciary. Then he sent to me: 'Is it a disputant"," a greeter"," or a need?' I said: 'No"," rather a greeter.' The messenger went and informed him. Then he came to me and said: 'Stand.' I stood and greeted him. He praised Allah and extolled Him"," then said: 'O Allah"," You know that I did not sit in this seat with which You have tested me and decreed for me except that I detest it and abhor it. So protect me from the evil of its consequences.' Then he took out a clean cloth and placed it on his face"," and he did not cease weeping until I stood. He remained as long as Allah willed. Then after him"," Ibn Shubrumah was appointed. I came and found him standing in prayer. When he saw me"," he shortened the prayer. Then he sent to me: 'Is it a disputant"," a greeter"," or a need?' I said: 'No"," rather a greeter.' The messenger went and informed him. Then he came to me and said: 'Stand.' I stood"," greeted him"," and sat beside him. He said: 'Narrate to me the hadith of my brother Harith ibn Dithar.' I narrated the hadith to him. He said: 'O Allah"," You know that I did not sit in this seat with which You have tested me except that I love it and desire it. So suffice me against the evil of its consequences.' Then he took out a clean cloth and placed it on his face"," and he did not cease weeping until I stood.\"" [Weak.]"""
"20239","Abu al-'Abbas Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Bazzaz al-Kisai' al-Misri in Makkah informed us: Abu 'Isa 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Isma'il al-'Arudi narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Tahawi said: I heard Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas say: \When Harith ibn Dithar was appointed to the judiciary"," it was said to al-Hakam ibn 'Utbah: 'Will you not come to him?' He said: 'By Allah"," he has not obtained any bounty with me that I should congratulate him for it"," nor has any affliction befallen him with me that I should console him for it. And I was not a visitor of his before today that I should visit him today.'\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20240","Abu al-Husayn ibn Bushran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn al-Sammak narrated to us; Hanbal ibn Ishaq narrated to us. He said: Abu Nu'aym said: \Shurayh came out from Ziyad's presence. A man met him and said: 'Your age has advanced"," your bones have weakened"," and your son has been bribed.' He returned to Ziyad and informed him. He said: 'Who said this to you?' He said: 'I do not know him. Excuse me.' He said: 'I will not excuse you until you point me to a man.' He pointed to Abu Burdah"," and he appointed him to the judiciary.\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20241","(20235) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Sufyān said: Qaʿnab al-Tamīmī was summoned by a governor who appointed him to the judiciary, but he refused. The governor persisted until he finally accepted. When he departed from the governor's presence with the appointment letter, he cast it aside and went into hiding. The governor sent men to search for him. While they were seeking him, the house in which he was hiding collapsed upon him. They only became aware of it when his funeral bier was brought out before them. [Ḥasan]"
"20242","(20236) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bukayr say: Al-Layth said: Abū Jaʿfar said to me, \Serve as a judge on my behalf in Egypt.\"" I said"," \""O Commander of the Faithful"," I am too weak for that"," and I am a man of the mawālī (freedmen).\"" He said"," \""There is no weakness in you with me; rather"," your resolve is weak in working for me in this matter. Do you seek a power stronger than me and my authority?\"" Then he said"," \""If you refuse"," then direct me to a man whom I may entrust with the affairs of Egypt.\"" I said"," \""ʿUthmān ibn al-Ḥakam al-Judhāmī — he is a righteous man and he has a tribe (supporting him).\"" When this reached him"," he vowed to Allah that he would never speak to al-Layth ibn Saʿd. [Ḥasan]"""
"20243","(20237) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Khalaf ibn Muḥammad al-Bukhārī informed me, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Aḥmad, the Ḥāfiẓ al-Bukhārī, said: I heard Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Ṭawāwisī say: Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar said: It was reported to me from Abū Yūsuf that he said: When Sawwār, the judge of the people of Baṣrah, died, Abū Jaʿfar — that is, al-Manṣūr — summoned Abū Ḥanīfah and said to him, \Sawwār has died"," and this province is in need of a judge. Accept the judiciary"," for I have appointed you as judge of Baṣrah.\"" Abū Ḥanīfah said"," \""By Allah"," besides Whom there is no deity"," I am not fit for the judiciary. And by Allah"," O Commander of the Faithful"," if I am speaking the truth"," it is not permissible for you to appoint a man who is unfit for the judiciary. And if I am lying"," it is not permissible for you to appoint a liar. This post is only suitable for a man of the Arabs"," and I have now become opposed to you.\"" Abū Jaʿfar said to him"," \""You have spoken truly. You said that this post is only fit for the likes of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar — that is a nation that has passed away"," for it has what it earned\"" [Sūrah al-Baqarah"," 134]. \""As for your statement that this post is only suitable for a man of the Arabs"," if we were to follow what Allah"," the Most High"," says in His Book"," 'Indeed"," the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most righteous among you' [Sūrah al-Ḥujurāt"," 13]. We are only obligated to strive among the people of our time. And as for your statement that you have become opposed to me"," one opinion may differ from another. So accept this matter.\"" Abū Ḥanīfah said"," \""O Commander of the Faithful"," either leave me alone"," or I shall begin saying the talbiyah from this very spot"," and you cannot detain one who is saying the talbiyah.\"" So he let him go after that. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20244","(20238) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, ʿUbayd ibn Yaʿīsh narrated to us, and a man who was praising Sufyān said:\n\n\Sufyān took precaution and fled with his religion"," and Shurayk lay in wait for his dirhams.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20245","(20239) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, ʿUbayd ibn Yaʿīsh said: A man was praising Sufyān (al-Thawrī), reciting:\n\n\Sufyān took precaution and fled with his religion"," while Shurayk became a partner lying in wait for the dirhams.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20246","(20240) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī said: I heard my father say —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Mufassir informed us from the original of his book, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Musayyab al-Arghiyānī said: I heard Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā say: The Caliph wrote to ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb regarding the judiciary of Egypt. So he feigned madness, confined himself to his house, and intended to perform wuḍūʾ in the middle of the house. Rashīd ibn Saʿd spotted him from the rooftop and said, \O Abū Muḥammad"," will you not come out to the people and judge between them by what Allah and His Messenger have commanded? You have feigned madness and confined yourself to your house.\"" He raised his head toward him and said"," \""This is as far as your knowledge extends! Do you not know that judges will be resurrected on the Day of Judgment alongside the sultans"," while the scholars will be resurrected alongside the prophets and messengers?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20247","(20241) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā al-Ḥīrī narrated to us, Abū Yaḥyā Zakariyyā ibn Dāwūd said: I heard Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā rebuking al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr for entering into the judiciary (al-ʿadālah). Then he said to him, \Have you not yourself narrated from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah — 'Do not sit with a judge"," nor with anyone known to be a judge'?\"" Then Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: \""The judiciary is a trust (ṭabaq) that is delegated to one of them.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20248","(20242) And Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr informed me, my father narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb said: I heard al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr say: I entered upon Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and greeted him, but he did not turn toward me. I sat to one side until the people dispersed. Then I drew near and kissed his head and said, \O my master"," what crime have I committed?\"" He said"," \""Indeed"," you have committed a crime and perpetrated a grave sin.\"" I said"," \""What is it?\"" He said"," \""Tell me — when the caller calls out on the Day of Judgment"," 'Where are the companions of ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṭāhir?' — are you not among those who were taken into the judiciary?\"" I said"," \""I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him.\"" He drew close to me"," embraced me"," and said"," \""Now you are my brother.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20249","(20243) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: I heard Abū Ṣāliḥ Khalaf ibn Muḥammad al-Bukhārī say: I heard Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn Naṣr, the chief of Naysābūr in Bukhārā, say: Al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr al-Naysābūrī was offered the judgeship of Naysābūr. He went into hiding for three days and supplicated to Allah, and he died on the third day. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20250","(20244) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: I heard Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ say: I heard Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib say: I heard Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Ribāṭī say: I came to Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, and he would not raise his head toward me. I said, \O Abū ʿAbdullāh"," narrations are written from me in Khurāsān"," and if you treat me this way"," they will discard my ḥadīth.\"" He said to me"," \""O Aḥmad"," is there no escape on the Day of Judgment from it being said"," 'Where are ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṭāhir and his followers?' See where you will be in relation to him.\"" I said"," \""O Abū ʿAbdullāh"," he only appointed me over the affairs of the ribāṭ; that is why I entered into it.\"" He kept repeating to me"," \""O Aḥmad"," is there no escape on the Day of Judgment from it being said"," 'Where are ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṭāhir and his followers?' See where you will be in relation to him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20251","(20245) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dārim, the ḥāfiẓ, narrated to us. He said: I heard ʿAlī ibn al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd al-Bajalī say: We were with Naṣr ibn ʿAlī al-Jahḍamī one evening when a letter from the Sulṭān arrived appointing him as judge of al-Baṣrah. He said: \I shall consult myself tonight and inform you tomorrow.\"" So we went to him the following morning"," and behold"," there was a bier at his door. We said: \""What is this?\"" They said: \""Naṣr has died.\"" We asked his family about him"," and they said: \""He spent the night in prayer. When it was the time of saḥr"," he went into prostration and prolonged it. So we moved him and found him dead.\"" May Allah be pleased with him. [Weak]"""
"20252","(20246) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh, the ḥāfiẓ, informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil ibn Khalaf, the judge in Baghdād, narrated to us: Abū Qilābah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī and Ashhal ibn Ḥātim narrated to us. They both said: Ibn ʿAwn narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \O Abā ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," do not ask for authority (al-imārah)"," for if you are given it as a result of asking for it"," you will be left to manage it on your own; and if you are given it without asking for it"," you will be helped in it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it"," then do that which is better and expiate for your oath.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Ibn ʿAwn"," and then he said: Ashhal ibn Ḥātim followed him in narrating it"," and they both narrated it from another route from al-Ḥasan. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"20253","(20247) Abū ʿAbd Allāh, the ḥāfiẓ, narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr al-Mustamlī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Manṣūr ibn Zādhān, and Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, and Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me:\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq, the jurist, informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," do not ask for authority"," for if you are given it as a result of asking for it"," you will be left to manage it on your own; and if you are given it without asking for it"," you will be helped in it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it"," then do that which is better and expiate for your oath.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"20254","(20248) Abū ʿAbd Allāh, the ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī — by recitation — and Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Muzāḥim al-Ṣaffār, the man of letters — verbatim — all of them said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated to me: Burayd narrated to me, from his grandfather, from Abū Mūsā, who said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) along with two men from my paternal uncles. One of the two men said: \O Messenger of Allah"," appoint us as rulers over some of that which Allah has placed under your authority.\"" The other said the same. He said: \""By Allah"," we do not appoint over this matter anyone who asks for it or anyone who is eager for it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," both of them from Abū Usāmah. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"20255","(20249) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān, the trustworthy narrator, in Baghdād, informed us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Sammāk narrated to us, dictating: Aḥmad ibn Mulāʿib narrated to us: Abū Ghassān narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Bilāl ibn Abī Burdah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever seeks the position of judge (al-qaḍāʾ) and seeks help against it will be left to manage it on his own; and whoever does not seek it and does not seek help against it"," Allah will send down to him an angel to guide him aright.\""\n\nWakīʿ and others also narrated it from Isrāʾīl"," from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿĀmir al-Thaʿlabī"," from Bilāl ibn Abī Burdah ibn Abī Mūsā al-Ashʿarī"," from Anas. [Weak]"""
"20256","(20250) It was also narrated from Abū ʿAwānah, from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, as Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū al-Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf, the jurist, narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥammād al-Ḥannāṭ narrated to us: Abū ʿAwānah narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Thaʿlabī, from Bilāl ibn Mirdās al-Fazārī, from Khaythamah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever seeks the position of judge and enlists intercessors for it will be left to himself; and whoever is compelled to it"," Allah — Mighty and Majestic — will send down to him an angel to guide him aright.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said"," as it reached me: \""This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith"," and it is more authentic than the hadith of Isrāʾīl from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā.\"" [Weak]"""
"20257","(20251) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: Qabīṣah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Rajāʾ, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: Two men came to the mosque and said: \Who will judge between us?\"" A young man said: \""I will.\"" Abū Masʿūd said: \""Do not rush to arbitration.\"" [Weak]"""
"20258","(20252) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us. They both said: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Rajāʾ al-Anṣārī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr al-Azraq, who said: Two men entered through the gates of Kindah while Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī was sitting in a circle. He said: \Is there not a man who will arbitrate between us?\"" A man from the circle said: \""I will.\"" So Abū Masʿūd took a handful of pebbles and threw them at him and said: \""Stop! Indeed"," rushing to arbitration is disliked.\"" [Weak — as previously mentioned]"""
"20259","(20253) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Ṭabarānī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from Abū Mūsā — meaning al-Yamānī — from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who raised it (as a marfūʿ hadith) and said: \Whoever settles in the desert becomes harsh; whoever pursues hunting becomes heedless; and whoever comes to the ruler is put to trial.\"" [Weak]"""
"20260","(20254) He said: And Abū al-Qāsim informed us: Ibn Kaysān narrated to us: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated it, mentioning it with its chain of narration, and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said the like of it. [Weak]"
"20261","(20255) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn Mihrān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Zakariyyā narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥakam al-Nakhaʿī from ʿAdī ibn Thābit from Abī Ḥāzim from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever dwells in the desert becomes harsh; whoever pursues game becomes heedless; whoever comes to the doors of the ruler is put to trial. And no servant draws near to a ruler except that he increases in distance from Allah.\"" Others narrated it from al-Nakhaʿī from ʿAdī from a shaykh of the Anṣār from Abī Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," with the same meaning. [Weak]"""
"20262","(20256) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Thābit, who said: I heard Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, saying to some of his family: \Do you know so-and-so woman? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by her while she was at a grave"," weeping. He said to her: 'Fear Allah and be patient.' She said: 'Leave me alone"," for you have not been afflicted by my affliction.' It was said to her: 'He is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' She was seized by something like death. She went to his door and found no gatekeepers"," so she entered upon him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I did not recognize you.' He said to her: 'Patience is at the first blow.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from various chains from Shuʿbah. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20263","(20257) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from a man from al-Ḥasan that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Doors were not closed before him, no chamberlain stood before him, and food was not brought to him in large trays morning or evening. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was accessible; whoever wished to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would find him. He sat on the ground, his food was placed on the ground, he wore coarse clothing, rode a donkey, had someone ride behind him, and, by Allah, he would lick his hand. [Weak]"
"20264","(20258) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Mubārak narrated to us that Ṣadaqah and Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Maryam, who said: Al-Qāsim ibn Makhīmarah narrated to us from a man of the people of Palestine, known as Abū Maryam, from the tribe of Asad, who came to Muʿāwiyah. Muʿāwiyah said to him: \What has brought you?\"" He said: \""A hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I saw your station"," I came to inform you.\"" I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Whomsoever Allah places in charge of any affair of the people and he conceals himself from their needs"," their requests"," and their destitution"," Allah will conceal Himself on the Day of Resurrection from his need"," his request"," and his destitution.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20265","(20259) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Abū Yaḥyā ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us that Abū al-Yamān informed us that Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī, who informed me that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Thawr and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding the story of the two women who had mutually invoked ẓihār. He said: I came to the upper chamber in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was, and I said to a black slave boy of his: \Seek permission for ʿUmar.\"" The boy entered and spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," then returned to me and said: \""I spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned you to him"," but he remained silent.\"" I went back and sat with the group who were near the pulpit. Then what I felt overcame me"," so I went to the boy and said: \""Seek permission for ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.\"" He entered and then returned to me and said: \""I have mentioned you to him"," but he remained silent.\"" When I turned to leave"," the boy called me and said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has granted you permission.\"" So I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him lying on the woven mat of palm leaves"," with no bedding between him and it. The marks of the mat had imprinted on his side. He was leaning on a leather cushion stuffed with palm fibre.\n\nAnd he mentioned the hadith. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20266","(20260) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Abū Khaythamah narrated to us that Jarīr narrated from Mughīrah that Shurayḥ used to enter a house on Friday in which he would be secluded, and the people did not know what he did in it. [Authentic]"
"20267","(20261) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Abū Khaythamah narrated to us that Jarīr narrated from Mughīrah, who said: Shurayḥ used to enter a house on Friday in which he would be secluded, and the people did not know what he did in it. [Authentic]"
"20268","(20262) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī and Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Anas al-Qurashī both said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us that Ḥaywah narrated, who said: I heard Abū al-Aswad inform me that Abū ʿAbd Allāh, the mawlā of Shaddād, informed him that he heard Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Whoever hears a person announcing a lost animal in the mosque"," let him say: 'May Allah not return it to you","' for mosques were not built for this.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from al-Muqriʾ. [Authentic — Muslim 568]"""
"20269","(20263) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Jarīr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Shaybah from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad from Ibn Buraydah from his father that the Prophet ﷺ heard a Bedouin — or a man — saying: \Whoever calls for the red camel!\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""You shall not find it! These mosques were only built for what they were built for.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Authentic — Muslim 569]"""
"20270","(20264) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Tamtām narrated to us that Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us that ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār ibn Isḥāq narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque. The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: \Stop! Stop!\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Do not interrupt him.\"" When he had finished"," the Prophet ﷺ called him and said: \""These mosques are not meant for filth"," urine"," and impurities. Rather"," they are only for the recitation of the Qurʾān and the remembrance of Allah.\"" Then he ordered one of his Companions to bring a bucket of water and pour it over it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from another chain from ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār"," and he said in the hadith: \""They are only for the remembrance of Allah"," the Ṣalāh"," and the recitation of the Qurʾān.\"" [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20271","(20265) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed him that Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed him that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar al-Jushamī informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from al-Jaʿd ibn Aws from Yazīd ibn Khuṣayfah from al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd, who said:\n\n\While I was lying down in the mosque"," suddenly a man began pelting me with pebbles. I raised my head and lo"," it was ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: 'Go to these two men and bring them to me.' So I went and brought them to him. ʿUmar said to them: 'Who are you"," or where are you from?' They said: 'From the people of al-Ṭāʾif.' He said: 'Had you been from the people of this city"," I would have given you a severe beating. You are raising your voices in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī from Yaḥyā. And al-Jaʿd ibn Aws — this is al-Jaʿd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Aws"," and he is also called Juʿayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 470]"""
"20272","(20266) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that Mālik informed me from Abū al-Naḍr from Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) built an open space adjacent to the mosque and named it al-Buṭayḥāʾ. He used to say: \Whoever wishes to speak loudly"," recite poetry"," or raise his voice"," let him go out to this open space.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20273","(20267) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb ibn Yaḥyā informed me that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī informed me that ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Muhājir from Zufar ibn Wathīmah ibn Aws ibn al-Ḥadathān from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that retaliation be carried out in the mosque"," or that poetry be recited therein"," or that the prescribed punishments (ḥudūd) be executed therein.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20274","(20268) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār informed us that Aḥmad ibn Mihrān al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Nuʿaym, meaning al-Nakhaʿī, informed us that al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Kathīr narrated from Makḥūl, from Abū al-Dardāʾ, from Wāthilah, and from Abū Umāmah (may Allah be pleased with them all), each of them saying:\n\n\We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," while he was upon the pulpit"," saying: 'Keep your mosques free of your children"," your madmen"," your disputes"," the raising of your voices"," the unsheathing of your swords"," the execution of your prescribed punishments"," and fumigate them on Fridays. And place vessels for purification at the doors of your mosques.'\""\n\nAl-ʿAlāʾ ibn Kathīr — this one is a Shāmi (Levantine) narrator"," and his hadith is rejected (munkar).\n\nAnd it is also narrated from Makḥūl from Yaḥyā ibn al-ʿAlāʾ from Muʿādh"," in a marfūʿ (elevated) chain"," but it is not authentic. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20275","(20269) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd informed us that Sufyān narrated from Jābir, who said:\n\n\ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz (may Allah have mercy on him) wrote to ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Zayd: 'Do not judge based on suspicion (bi-l-jawr).' And he wrote to him: 'Do not pass judgment in the mosque"," for the Jew"," the Christian"," and the menstruating woman will come to you.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20276","(20270) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Siqqāʾ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us that Abū al-Walīd informed us that al-Layth narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Saʿd ibn Sinān from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\Deliberation (al-taʾannī) is from Allah"," and haste (al-ʿajalah) is from Satan.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20277","(20271) The Ḥākim, Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ (may Allah have mercy on him), and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muʿādhī, and Abū Saʿd Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Shuʿaybī, and Abū al-Faḍl ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Harawī — they said: Abū Ḥafṣ ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Zayyāt al-Ṣayrafī al-Baghdādī in Baghdad informed us that Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Nājiyah ibn Najbah informed us that Muḥammad ibn Thaʿlabah ibn Suwāʾ informed us that my uncle Muḥammad ibn Suwāʾ —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Dharān ibn Sufyān informed us that ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Suwāʾ narrated from Saʿd ibn Simāk ibn Ḥarb from his father from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said:\n\n\The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'When you exercise deliberation (taʾannayta)…'\"" And in the narration of al-Muʿādhī"," al-Shuʿaybī"," and al-Harawī: \""When you exercise deliberation (tabayyanata)"," you will attain correctness or nearly attain it. And when you hasten (istaʿjalta)"," you will err or nearly err.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20278","(20272) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Anmāṭī informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal informed us that Qurrah narrated from Abū Jamrah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to al-Ashajj, the chief of ʿAbd al-Qays:\n\n\Indeed"," there are two qualities in you that Allah loves: forbearance (al-ḥilm) and deliberation (al-ānāh).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 17]"""
"20279","(20273) And Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār in Baghdad informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān informed us that Abū al-Ashʿath informed us that Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, who narrated from more than one person who had met the delegation — and he mentioned Abū Naḍrah — that he narrated from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) — and he mentioned the hadith — in it the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to al-Ashajj of ʿAbd al-Qays:\n\n\Indeed"," there are two qualities in you that Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," and His Messenger love: forbearance (al-ḥilm) and deliberation (al-ānāh).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20280","(20274) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said: Abū ʿUbayd said regarding the hadith of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) about a man who traveled with some companions of his and did not return when they returned. His family accused his companions (of his murder) and brought them before Sharīḥ. He asked them for proof of his killing, so they went up to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him of Sharīḥ's ruling. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said:\n\n\Saʿd brought them to the water"," and Saʿd is wrapped up (asleep). O Saʿd"," by this the camels will not be watered.\""\n\nThen he said: \""Indeed"," the easiest form of watering is al-tashrīʿ (allowing access to the watering place).\"" Then he separated them and questioned them"," and they gave conflicting accounts. Then they confessed to his killing. I think he said: \""So he had them executed for it.\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: A man whose name I do not recall narrated it to me from Hishām ibn Ḥassān from Ibn Sīrīn from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). Abū ʿUbayd said: His statement \""Saʿd brought them to the water"," and Saʿd is wrapped up\"" — this is a proverb. Its origin is that a man brought his camels to a watering place that could only be reached by drawing water with a bucket"," and then he wrapped himself up (in his garment) and slept"," leaving them. It is said: \""By this action the camels will not be watered.\"" And his statement \""Indeed"," the easiest form of watering is al-tashrīʿ\"" is also a proverb. It means: the simplest thing that should be done for them is to give them access to the watering place (al-sharīʿah) or the pool. He is saying: the easiest thing that Sharīḥ should have done was to investigate the matter thoroughly"," examine it"," and uncover the truth about the man until he had exhausted all avenues of inquiry"," rather than limiting himself solely to demanding proof (bayyinah)."""
"20281","(20275) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed me — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us — Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us — Adam ibn Abi Iyyas narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated to us — 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr said: I heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah saying: Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to his son while he was in Sijistan: \Do not judge between two persons while you are angry"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: 'No judge shall render judgment between two persons while he is angry.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Adam"," and Muslim recorded it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh).]"""
"20282","(20276) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki informed us — Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Abu 'Awanah narrated to us — 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, who said: My father wrote — and I wrote it with my own hand — to his son 'Ubayd Allah while he was in Sijistan: \Let me not come to know that you have judged between two persons while you are angry"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: 'No judge shall judge between two persons while he is angry.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Qutaybah"," from Abu 'Awanah. [Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh).]"""
"20283","(20277) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us — my grandfather, Abu 'Amr ibn Nujayd, informed us — Abu Muslim al-Kajji narrated to us — Abu 'asim al-Nabil informed us — Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, (narrated):\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami — all of them said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Sufyan, meaning Ibn 'Uyaynah, (narrated):\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us — Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya informed us — Hushaym narrated — all of them from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The judge shall not render judgment between two persons while he is angry.\""\n\nTheir meaning is one and the same. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and he also recorded it through another chain from Sufyan al-Thawri. [Sahih.]"""
"20284","(20278) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar narrated — from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: A man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," advise me.\"" He said: \""Do not become angry.\"" The man said: \""I reflected upon what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had said"," and lo — anger gathers all evil together.\"" [Sahih"," up to his words \""Do not become angry.\""]"""
"20285","(20279) And Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Tamtam narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yusuf narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us — Abu Hasin narrated — from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \Advise me.\"" He said: \""Do not become angry.\"" The man returned to him several times"," and he did not add anything beyond saying: \""Do not become angry.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yusuf"," and 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad also narrated it from al-A'mash"," from Abu Salih"," from Abu Sa'id. [Sahih. Bukhari 6116.]"""
"20286","(20280) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us — al-A'mash narrated — from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," teach me a deed by which I may enter Paradise"," and make it brief so that I may understand.\"" He said: \""Do not become angry.\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20287","(20281) And Abu Mu'awiyah and Shayban narrated from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah or from Abu Sa'id — with doubt — who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," teach me something by which Allah may benefit me"," and make it brief so that I may retain what you say.\"" He said to him: \""Do not become angry.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," teach me something by which I may benefit myself.\"" He repeated it to him several times"," saying to him: \""Do not become angry.\"" Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and al-Sayrafi both said: Abu al-'Abbas"," that is"," al-Asamm"," narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us — Abu Mu'awiyah narrated.\n\nAnd it was also reported through another chain from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). [Sahih. Previously mentioned.]"""
"20288","(20282) Abu al-Fath Hilal ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Haffar in Baghdad informed us — al-Husayn ibn 'Ayyash al-Qattan narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us — Musa ibn Dawud narrated — from al-Qasim ibn 'Abd Allah:\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Hisham ibn 'Ali narrated to us — Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us — al-Qasim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar al-'Umari narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Tuwalah narrated — from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The judge shall not render judgment except while he is satiated and well-nourished.\""\n\nAl-Qasim al-'Umari is the sole narrator of this version"," and he is weak (da'if). The authentic hadith on this topic that precedes it conveys the same meaning. [Da'if (weak).]"""
"20289","(20283) Abu Tahir al-Faqih dictated to us as dictation and recitation — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us — Yahya ibn al-Rabi' al-Makki narrated to us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated — from Idris al-Awdi, who said: Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah brought out to us a document and said: \This is the letter of 'Umar to Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with both of them).\"" And he mentioned the hadith"," and in it he said: \""Beware of irritation (al-dajar)"," anxiety (al-qalaq)"," harming people (al-ta'adh-dhi bi al-nas)"," and being harsh with litigants (al-tanakkur bi al-khusum) in matters of truth for which Allah"," the Most High"," obligates reward and through which He grants provision. For whosoever purifies his inner self in that which is between him and his Lord"," Allah shall set right that which is between him and the people. And whosoever adorns for the people that which Allah knows to be the contrary thereof"," Allah shall disgrace him. So what do you suppose the reward to be other than with Allah"," in the immediate worldly life and in the treasures of His mercy? And peace.\""\n\n[Sahih.]"""
"20290","(20284) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us — Abu 'Amr ibn al-Sammak informed us — Hanbal ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Musaddad informed us — Hushaym narrated — from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Hariz, from Shurayh: that when he became angry or hungry, he would stand and not render judgment between anyone. [Da'if (weak).]"
"20291","(20285) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿUmārah ibn Shubrumah said: Ibn Abī Laylā would not sit for the purpose of rendering judgment unless a bowl was brought to him, which he would eat from, and then a covered vessel would be brought to him, which he would open. And when it was the day of the women [i.e., the day designated for hearing women's cases], he would seat a man alongside him."
"20292","(20286) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl and ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Ḍabbī narrated to us — the narrator separated them — they both said: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, that Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us, that Yaḥyā — he is ibn Bukayr — narrated to us, that al-Layth narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, that he narrated to him that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him: that a man from the Anṣār disputed with al-Zubayr before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the irrigation channels of al-Ḥarrah, by which they watered the date palms. The Anṣārī said: \Release the water"," let it flow","\"" but he refused. So they brought the dispute before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-Zubayr: \""Irrigate"," O Zubayr"," then release the water to your neighbor.\"" The Anṣārī became angry and said: \""Is he your cousin?\"" And the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed. Then he said: \""O Zubayr"," irrigate"," then hold back the water until it returns to the wall [i.e."," the raised bank of the irrigation channel].\"" Al-Zubayr said: \""By Allah"," I reckon that this verse was revealed concerning that matter: {But no"," by your Lord"," they will not truly believe until they make you judge in all disputes between them} [al-Nisāʾ 65].\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah and others"," all from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20293","(20287) And Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Ḥibbān informed us that ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: A man from the Anṣār disputed with al-Zubayr — may Allah be pleased with him — over a channel of al-Ḥarrah. The Prophet ﷺ said: \Irrigate"," O Zubayr"," then release the water to your neighbor.\"" The Anṣārī said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," is he your cousin?\"" And the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed. Then he said: \""Irrigate"," O Zubayr"," then hold back the water until it returns to the wall"," then release it to your neighbor.\"" He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established for al-Zubayr his full right through the explicit judgment when the Anṣārī objected"," although previously he had indicated to them both a matter that would have allowed ample room for both of them.\n\nAl-Zubayr said: \""I do not think this verse was revealed except concerning that matter: {But no"," by your Lord"," they will not truly believe until they make you judge in all disputes between them} [al-Nisāʾ 65].\"" He said: \""I heard other than al-Zuhrī saying: 'We examined the statement of the Prophet ﷺ: Then hold back the water until it returns to the wall — and that was up to the ankles.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak"," in abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20294","(20288) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us, that Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from his father, from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \When Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — was appointed as khalīfah"," he said: 'My people know that my trade was never insufficient for the maintenance of my family. But now I have been occupied with the affairs of the Muslims. So the family of Abū Bakr shall eat from this wealth [i.e."," the bayt al-māl]"," and I shall work for the Muslims through it.'\""\n\nHe said: And ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: \""When ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — was appointed as khalīfah"," he and his family ate from the wealth"," and he traded with his own wealth.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Yūnus from al-Zuhrī"," as was previously mentioned in the Book of Division. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 2070]\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥasan that Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — addressed the people when he was appointed as khalīfah and mentioned the ḥadīth. He said: \""When morning came"," he went to the market"," and ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — said to him: 'Where are you headed?' He said: 'To the market.' He said: 'You have a responsibility that should keep you from the market.' He said: 'Glory to Allah! Will it distract me from my family?' He said: 'Then assign a known stipend.' Then he mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it he mentioned his bequest to return what he had taken from the bayt al-māl.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20295","(20289) ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — the wife of the Prophet ﺻﻠﻰ اﷲ ﻋﻠﻴﻪ وسلم, who said: \When ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — was appointed as khalīfah"," he and his family ate from the wealth"," and he traded with his own wealth.\""\n\nAl-Ḥasan said: \""Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — addressed the people when he was appointed as khalīfah…\"" When morning came"," he went to the market"," and ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — said to him: \""Where are you headed?\"" He said: \""To the market.\"" He said: \""You have a responsibility that should keep you from the market.\"" He said: \""Glory to Allah! Will it distract me from my family?\"" He said: \""Then assign a known stipend.\"" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it he mentioned his bequest to return what he had taken from the bayt al-māl."""
"20296","(20290) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī narrated to us, that Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥafṣ informed us, that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Ḥafṣ ibn Ghaylān, from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — wrote: \The trading of an amīr during his governorship is a loss.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20297","(20291) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me, that Ḥarmalah informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to me, that al-Layth narrated from some of his brethren, from Juzayy ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, that Zabbān ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz: \O Amīr al-Muʾminīn"," if you were to ride and take rest…\"" ʿUmar said: \""Then who will fulfill the work of that day?\"" He said: \""You can make up for it the next day.\"" He said: \""The work of a single day has exhausted me — so how can I manage the work of two days in a single day?\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20298","(20292) And Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us that ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, that Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, that Sufyān said: I heard Ibn Shubrumah say: When Ibn Hubayrah appointed al-Shaʿbī as qāḍī and required him to spend the night in conversation with him, al-Shaʿbī said to him: \I cannot do this. Leave me with one of the two matters — I cannot combine being a qāḍī with spending the night in conversation.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20299","(20293) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, that al-Mukhtār — he is ibn Nāfiʿ — narrated from Ibn Maṭar, who said: I went out from the mosque, and lo, a man was calling out from behind me: \Raise your izār"," for it is purer for your garment and more pious for you. And cut your hair"," if you are a Muslim.\"" I walked behind him and said: \""Who is this?\"" A man said to me: \""This is ʿAlī"," Amīr al-Muʾminīn.\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth. He said: Then he came to the Dār al-Furāt"," which is the market of the cloth merchants"," and said: \""O shaykh"," sell me a shirt for three dirhams.\"" When he recognized him"," he would not buy anything from him. Then he came to another man"," and when he recognized him"," he would not buy anything from him either. Then he came to a young slave boy and bought a shirt from him for three dirhams"," and he wore it"," reaching from the wrists to the ankles. He said: Then the father of the slave boy"," the owner of the garment"," came"," and it was said: \""O so-and-so"," your son has sold a shirt to Amīr al-Muʾminīn today for three dirhams.\"" He said: \""Why did you not take two dirhams?\"" So his father took one dirhams and brought it to Amīr al-Muʾminīn and said: \""O Amīr al-Muʾminīn"," keep this dirham.\"" He said: \""What is this dirham about?\"" He said: \""The shirt was worth two dirhams.\"" He said: \""He sold it with my consent"," and he took payment with his consent.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20300","(20294) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, that Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī, from al-Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with seven things: he commanded us to follow the funeral processions, to visit the sick, to respond to the one who sneezes, to help the oppressed, to spread the salām, to accept the invitation of the one who invites, and to fulfill the oath of the one who swears.\n\nBoth [al-Bukhārī and Muslim] extracted it in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections from the ḥadīth of Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"20301","(20295) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Muqri' informed me; Abu Ya'la narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated from al-'Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The rights of a Muslim over another Muslim are six.\"" It was asked: \""What are they"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""When you meet him"," greet him with salam; when he invites you"," accept his invitation; when he seeks your counsel"," counsel him; when he sneezes and praises Allah"," say 'Yarhamuk Allah' (may Allah have mercy on him); when he falls ill"," visit him; and when he dies"," follow his funeral procession.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Ayyub and others. [Sahih — Agreed Upon]"""
"20302","(20296) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih al-Isbahani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Hayyan informed us; Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Abu Hafs 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from al-Aswad, who said: \When delegations came to 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," he would ask them about their governor: 'Does he visit the sick? Does he accept the invitation of a slave? How is his conduct? Who stands at his gate?' If they said 'No' regarding any one of these qualities"," he would remove him.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20303","(20297) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us; Hajjaj and Abu 'Asim narrated from Ibn Jurayj; Ibn Abi Mulkaykah informed me from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The most hated of men to Allah is the most obstinate disputant (al-add al-khasim).\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu 'Asim"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Waki' from Ibn Jurayj. [Sahih — Agreed Upon]"""
"20304","(20298) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran narrated to us; Abu 'Amr ibn al-Sammak narrated to us; Hanbal ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Abu 'Abd Allah, meaning Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us; 'Affan narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated from Muhammad ibn Sirin that 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him: \Look into the judgment of Abu Maryam.\"" He said: \""I do not suspect Abu Maryam.\"" He said: \""I do not suspect him either"," but when you see injustice from a litigant"," then punish him.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20305","(20299) Abu al-Hasan 'Ala' ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sa'id al-Isfarayini narrated to us there; Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyub from Muhammad ibn Sirin that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I will certainly remove so-and-so from the judiciary"," and I will appoint over the judiciary a man at the sight of whom the evildoer will tremble in fear.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20306","(20300) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad Muhammad al-Baghdadi narrated to us in Naysabur; Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us in Egypt; Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And consult them in the matter} [Al 'Imran 159]: He said: \Abu Bakr and 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with them both.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20307","(20301) Abu 'Amr al-Adib narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to us; Abu Ahmad ibn Ziyad narrated to us; Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzak informed us; Ma'mar narrated from al-Zuhri from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan ibn al-Hakam, who both said in the story of al-Hudaybiyyah: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Advise me. Do you think we should turn toward the children of those who aided them and take them"," or do you think we should head toward the House"," and whoever prevents us from it"," we will fight him?\"" Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best. We have come only as pilgrims"," not to fight anyone. But whoever stands between us and the House"," we will fight him.\"" The Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""Then go forth.\""\n\nAl-Zuhri said: Abu Hurayrah said: \""I have not seen anyone who consulted his companions more than the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of 'Abd al-Razzak. [Sahih — Bukhari 1695"," 1811]"""
"20308","(20302) Abu Tahir al-Faqih narrated to us; 'Abdus ibn al-Husayn ibn Mansur narrated to us; Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us; al-Ansari narrated to me; Humayd narrated from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, set out for Badr, he consulted the Muslims. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, gave his counsel. Then he consulted them again, and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, gave his counsel. Then he consulted them again, and the Ansar said: \O company of the Ansar! The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," means you.\"" They said: \""Then we will not say what the Children of Israel said to Musa: {Go forth"," you and your Lord"," and fight; indeed"," we are remaining here} [Al-Ma'idah 24]. By the One who sent you with the truth"," if you were to strike the saddles of camels as far as Bark al-Ghumad"," we would follow you.\"" [Sahih — Muslim 1779]"""
"20309","(20303) Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Harfi narrated to us in Baghdad; Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us; Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us; 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated from Abu Zumayl from Ibn 'Abbas from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \On the day of Badr"," he said: 'What do you think about these captives?' Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'O Prophet of Allah"," they are your paternal uncles"," your kinsmen"," and your brothers. We should take ransom from them so that it may be a strength for us against the polytheists"," and perhaps Allah will guide them to Islam"," and they will be a support for us.' He said: 'What do you think"," O Ibn al-Khattab?' I said: 'O Prophet of Allah"," I do not see what Abu Bakr sees. Rather"," these are the leaders of disbelief and their notables. Bring them close and strike their necks.' The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," inclined toward what Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said"," and did not incline toward what I said. He took ransom from them. When morning came"," I went to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and there he and Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," were sitting and weeping. I said: 'O Prophet of Allah"," tell me what you and your companion are weeping for. If I find cause for weeping"," I will weep; otherwise"," I will weep in sympathy for your weeping.' He said: 'What your companions suggested to me — your punishment was shown to me closer than this tree.' — A tree was nearby at that time. So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: {It is not for a prophet to take captives until he has thoroughly subdued the land. You desire the fleeting gains of this world"," but Allah desires the Hereafter"," and Allah is Almighty"," All-Wise} [Al-Anfal 67].\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar. [Sahih — Muslim 1736]"""
"20310","(20304) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah narrated to us; Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Ibn Shubrumah from al-Hasan regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And consult them in the matter} [Al 'Imran 159]: He said: \Allah"," glorified is He"," taught him that he had no need of them"," but He intended that those after him would follow this practice.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20311","(20305) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Qabīṣah narrated to us, that Sufyān narrated from Ṣāliḥ, meaning Ibn Ḥayy, who said: al-Shaʿbī said: \Whoever is pleased to take a firm hold of the office of judgment"," let him take the judgment of ʿUmar"," for he used to seek counsel.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20312","(20306) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān informed us in Baghdād, that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zibriqān narrated to us, that Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us, that Ashʿath informed us, that ʿAlī ibn Zayd narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The foundation of intellect after faith in Allah is showing affection to people. And no man is independent of seeking counsel. And indeed"," the people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter"," and indeed"," the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20313","(20307) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, that Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf ibn al-Bukhārī narrated to us, that Yaḥyā, meaning Abī Ṭālib, informed us, that Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us, that Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \Men are three: a complete man"," half a man"," and nothing at all. As for the complete man"," he has his own opinion and seeks counsel. As for half a man"," he has no opinion of his own but seeks counsel. And as for the one who is nothing"," he has no opinion and does not seek counsel.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20314","(20308) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf said: Sufyān mentioned from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who said: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz asked about the judge of Kūfah, and the judge said: \It is not befitting for a judge to be appointed until he possesses five qualities: he must be ch forbearing"," knowledgeable of what has preceded him"," he must consult the people of understanding"," and he must not care about the blame of people.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20315","(20309) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān informed us, that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us, that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Abū ʿAbdullāh, meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, narrated to us, that Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated from Mughīrah, who said: \ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz had companions with whom he would consult regarding the matters of people that were brought before him. And the sign between him and them"," when he wished for them to leave"," was that he would say: 'When you wish.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20316","(20310) Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Lāsakī in al-Rayy informed us, that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar informed us, that Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥātim narrated to us, that Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from al-Awzāʿī, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, who said: Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd, peace be upon him, said to his son: \O my son"," do not decide any matter until you consult a guiding advisor"," for if you do that"," you will not regret it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20317","(20311) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, that Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām ibn Sufyān narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl, who said: \Salmān ibn Rabīʿah used to pass judgment in the mosque. He was asked about an inheritance share and erred in it. ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl said to him: 'The judgment in it is such and such.' It seemed as though he felt something within himself"," so he referred the matter to Abū Mūsā"," who said: 'As for you"," O Salmān"," it is not for you to become angry. And as for you"," ʿAmr"," it was for you to consult him in his ear [i.e."," privately].'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20318","(20312) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah al-Anṣārī and Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ both said: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, that Hushaym narrated to us, that Sayyār narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \When ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," appointed Sharīḥ as judge over Kūfah"," he said: 'Look at what is clear to you from the Book of Allah"," and do not ask anyone about it. And whatever is not clear to you in the Book of Allah"," then follow the Sunnah in it. And whatever is not clear to you in the Sunnah"," then exert your own judgment (ijtihād) in it.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20319","(20313) And Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, that Sufyān narrated from Abī Isḥāq al-Shaybānī, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," wrote to Sharīḥ: 'When a matter comes to you that is in the Book of Allah"," the Most High"," judge by it"," and do not let men divert you from it. And if it is not in the Book of Allah"," and it is in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," then judge by it. And if it is not in the Book of Allah"," nor in the Sunnah of His Messenger"," then judge by what the guided imams have judged by. And if it is not in the Book of Allah"," nor in the Sunnah of His Messenger ﷺ"," nor in what the guided imams have judged by"," then you have the choice: if you wish"," you may exert your own judgment"," and if you wish"," you may consult me. I do not see your consulting me except that it would be safer for you.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," informed about the place of consultation (al-mu'āmarah)"," which is consultation (al-mushāwarah). For sometimes he might have principles that did not reach Sharīḥ"," and he would inform him of them. And by Allah"," success is from Him alone.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20320","(20314) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Mu'adhdhin informed us, that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khunb informed us — and Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Razzāz both said: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Shāfiʿī informed us — both said: Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, that Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān narrated to me, that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, who said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd told me that Ibn Shihāb informed him, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Allah has never sent any prophet"," nor has He ever appointed any successor"," except that he had two groups of close advisors (biṭānatān): one group commanding him to do good and urging him toward it"," and another group commanding him to do evil and urging him toward it. And the one protected is the one whom Allah protects.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 6611"," 7198]"""
"20321","(20315) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed me, Ḥibbān informed us, ʿAbdullāh — that is, Ibn al-Mubārak — informed us, Yūnus narrated on the authority of al-Zuhrī, Abū Salamah narrated to me on the authority of Abū Saʿīd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \No khalīfah is appointed except that he has two retinues.\"" Then he mentioned it. [Authentic. Preceded before it.]"""
"20322","(20316) And Abū ʿAmr informed us, Abū Bakr informed us, al-Ḥasan informed me, Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me, Yūnus informed me on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, on the authority of Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, on the authority of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \No prophet is sent and no khalīfah is appointed except that he has two retinues.\"" Then he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of ʿAbdān"," on the authority of Ibn al-Mubārak"," and on the authority of Aṣbagh ibn al-Faraj"," on the authority of Ibn Wahb"," and he cited the narration of Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd as a supporting witness. [Authentic. Preceded before it.]"""
"20323","(20317) Al-Bukhārī said: And al-Awzāʿī said on the authority of al-Zuhrī, on the authority of Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah — then he mentioned what Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us. They said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — that is, al-Aṣamm — narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, al-Awzāʿī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd informed me, my father narrated to me, al-Awzāʿī narrated to me, Ibn Shihāb narrated to me, Abū Salamah narrated to me on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no prophet nor any ruler except that he has two retinues: a retinue that commands him to what is good and forbids him from what is evil"," and a retinue that does not spare him from corruption. So whoever is protected from the evil of the two has indeed been protected — and it is the one of the two that overcomes him.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Sūsī. [Authentic.]"""
"20324","(20318) And al-Bukhārī mentioned what Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Shādyākhī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us. They said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, my father and Shuʿayb narrated on the authority of al-Layth, on the authority of ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar, who said: Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym narrated to me on the authority of Abū Salamah, on the authority of Abū Ayyūb, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah ﷺ say: \Allah does not send any prophet nor appoint any khalīfah after him except that he has two retinues: a retinue that commands him to what is good and forbids him from what is evil"," and a retinue that does not spare him from corruption. So whoever is protected from the evil retinue has indeed been protected.\"" [Authentic.]"""
"20325","(20319) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Mihrānī and Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī from his original copy and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Aṭṭār informed us. They said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū ʿUtbah Aḥmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubārak narrated on the authority of Ibn Abī Ḥusayn, on the authority of al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, who said: I heard my aunt ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever among you is given charge of some work"," and Allah intends good for him"," He appoints for him a righteous minister: if he forgets"," he reminds him"," and if he remembers"," he assists him.\"" [Weak.]"""
"20326","(20320) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Ayyūb al-Naṣībī narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated on the authority of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When Allah intends good for a ruler"," He appoints for him a truthful minister: if he forgets"," he reminds him"," and if he remembers"," he assists him. And when He intends otherwise"," He appoints for him an evil minister: if he forgets"," he does not remind him"," and if he remembers"," he does not assist him.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan on the authority of Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir"," on the authority of al-Walīd. [Weak.]"""
"20327","(20321) And Abū Dāwūd narrated in the Marāsīl on the authority of Mūsā ibn Marwān al-Raqqī, on the authority of al-Muʿāfā ibn ʿImrān, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khālid ibn Maʿdān, who said: A man said, \O Messenger of Allah"," what is al-ḥazm (prudence)?\"" He said: \""That you consult a person of sound judgment and then obey him.\""\n\nAnd on the authority of Muḥammad ibn al-Wazīr"," on the authority of Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah"," on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazīd"," on the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥusayn: that a man said"," \""O Messenger of Allah","\"" and he mentioned something similar"," except that he said: \""dhā lubb (a person of understanding).\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us with both of them"," Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us"," Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us"," Abū Dāwūd narrated to us"," and he mentioned them both. [Weak.]"""
"20328","(20322) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, Shaybān narrated on the authority of ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, on the authority of Abū Salamah, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The one whose counsel is sought is a trustee (amīn).\""\n\nAbū ʿAwanah narrated it on the authority of ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr"," on the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr. And ʿAbd al-Ḥakīm ibn Manṣūr narrated it on the authority of ʿAbd al-Malik"," on the authority of Abū Salamah"," on the authority of Abū al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihān. [Authentic.]"""
"20329","(20323) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar narrated to us. They said: al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us, Sharīk narrated on the authority of al-Aʿmash, on the authority of Abū ʿAmr al-Shaybānī, on the authority of Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The one whose counsel is sought is a trustee (amīn).\""\n\nAnd in the narration of al-ʿAbbās"," he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. [Denounced (Munkar).]"""
"20330","(20324) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Faqīh in Ṭabarān — may Allah have mercy on him — narrated to us, Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥaṣan al-Ṣawwāf narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ narrated to me, Saʿīd narrated to me, Bakr ibn ʿAmr narrated on the authority of Abū ʿUthmān Muslim ibn Yasār.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Saʿīd ibn Ayyūb narrated to me, Bakr ibn ʿAmr narrated on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Abī Nuʿaym, on the authority of Abū ʿUthmān Muslim ibn Yasār, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever attributes to me what I have not said"," let him take his seat in the Fire. And when a brother seeks his counsel and he directs him other than to what is right"," he has betrayed him. And whoever gives a fatwā without firm proof"," its sin falls upon the one who issued the fatwā.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb. [Authentic.]"""
"20331","(20325) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, that Ibn Wahb informed me, that Yūnus informed on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, who said: It reached us that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Do not speak of that which does not concern you"," and keep away from your enemy. Be cautious of your close friend"," except the trustworthy one"," for nothing among people equals the trustworthy one. Do not accompany the wicked person"," lest he teach you of his wickedness"," and do not disclose your secrets to him. And consult in your affairs those who fear Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\"" [Weak]"""
"20332","(20326) Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qirmīsīnī informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Kuhaylī informed us that al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us, that al-Layth ibn Hārūn Abū ʿUtbah al-ʿUkklī narrated to us, that Zayd ibn Ḥubāb narrated on the authority of ʿUmar ibn ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Saʿīd — whose name was al-Ṣurm, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Saʿīd — who said: My grandfather narrated to me, saying: \When ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," sat upon the seats (for judgment)"," the two disputing parties would come to him. He would say to one of them: 'Go and summon ʿAlī","' and to the other: 'Go and summon Ṭalḥah"," al-Zubayr"," and a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.' Then he would say to them both: 'Speak.' Then he would turn to the people and say: 'What do you say?' If they said something in accordance with his own opinion"," he would implement it; otherwise"," he would consider the matter further. Then the two parties would depart"," having made peace with each other.\"" [Weak]"""
"20333","(20327) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd informed me that Ibn Shuʿayb informed me that ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad informed on the authority of his father Muḥammad ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, recited this verse: {He has not placed upon you in the religion any hardship} [al-Ḥajj: 78], and then he said: \Bring me a man from Banī Mudlij"," for they are (true) Arabs.\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," then asked: \""What does al-ḥaraj mean among you?\"" He said: \""Constriction (al-ḍayq).\"" [Weak]"""
"20334","(20328) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Sufyān narrated on the authority of ʿUbaydillāh ibn Abī Yazīd, who said: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, being asked about al-ḥaraj. He said: \Is there anyone from Hudhayl here?\"" A man said: \""I am.\"" He said: \""What do you consider al-ḥaraj to be?\"" He said: \""A narrow or constricted thing.\"" He said: \""That is it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20335","(20329) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us that Sufyān narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik said: ʿUmar wrote to Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, may Allah be pleased with him: \Consult Ṭalḥah and ʿAmr ibn Maʿdīkarib in the matter of your warfare"," but do not entrust them with any command"," for every craftsman is most knowledgeable of his own craft.\"" [Weak]"""
"20336","(20330) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to me that Abū ʿAbdillāh, meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us that Abū Bakr narrated on the authority of ʀāṣim, who said: Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh was among the most Bedouin of people. ʿAbdillāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, would ask him about the Arabic language. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20337","(20331) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū ʿAlī al-Fasawī in Baṣrah narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Yūsuf al-Mājishūn narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us that Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾīnī informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn al-Mājishūn narrated, saying: Ibn Shihāb said to us — myself, my nephew, and a paternal cousin of mine, while we were young boys asking him about ḥadīth: \Do not belittle yourselves on account of your youth"," for ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," when a difficult matter befell him"," would call the young men and consult them"," seeking the sharpness of their intellects.\"" This is the wording of ʿAlī's ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20338","(20332) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī narrated to us that Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥafṣ al-Kūfī informed us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated on the authority of Hishām, on the authority of Ibn Sīrīn, who said: \Indeed"," ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," would consult in matters — to the extent that he would even consult a woman. At times he would see something good in her statement or something he deemed commendable"," and he would adopt it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — from Ibn Sīrīn]"""
"20339","(20333) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that ʿAbdillāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us that Saʿīd ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭāʾī narrated on the authority of ʿAlī ibn Rabīʿah, who said: \I came to ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and said: 'I am more capable than my uncle and more courageous. If you see fit"," appoint me in his place.' He said: 'O nephew"," the opinion of an elder is better than the presence of a youth.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20340","(20334) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Qabīṣah narrated to us that Sufyān narrated on the authority of Saʿīd ibn ʿUbayd, on the authority of ʿAlī ibn Rabīʿah, that a man came to ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, offering his son as a substitute. ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The opinion of an elder is dearer to me than the presence of a young man.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20341","(20335) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Zuhrī informed us that Jaʿfar, meaning Ibn ʿAwn, and Yaʿlā, meaning Ibn ʿUbayd, narrated from Abū Ḥayyān al-Taymī from Yazīd ibn Ḥayyān, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) say: One day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among us and delivered a sermon. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \To proceed"," O people"," I am merely a human being. Soon the messenger of my Lord will come"," and I shall respond to him. I am leaving among you the two weighty things (al-thaqalayn): the first of them is the Book of Allah"," in which there is guidance and light. Hold fast to the Book of Allah and adhere to it.\"" He exhorted us regarding the Book of Allah and encouraged us in it"," then he said: \""And my Ahl al-Bayt — I remind you of Allah"," the Most High"," concerning my Ahl al-Bayt.\"" He repeated this three times.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Abū Ḥayyān al-Taymī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2408]"""
"20342","(20336) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Shaʿrānī informed us that my grandfather informed us that Ibn Abī Uways informed us that my father narrated from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dilī from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: \O people"," I have left among you that which"," if you hold fast to it"," you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20343","(20337) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Abū Aḥmad Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us that ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Haytham informed us that Ṣāliḥ ibn Mūsā al-Ṭalḥī narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \I have left among you that after which you will never go astray"," so long as you adhere to them or act upon them: the Book of Allah and my Sunnah. They will never separate until they come to me at the Pool (al-Ḥawḍ).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20344","(20338) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn al-Ḥammāmī al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad informed us that Abū ʀāṣim informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī informed us that Abū ʀāṣim informed us that Thawr ibn Yazīd narrated from Khālid ibn Maʿdān from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Sulamī from al-ʿIrāḍ ibn Sāriyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the morning prayer, then turned to us and admonished us with an admonishment that caused hearts to tremble and eyes to shed tears. We said: \O Messenger of Allah"," it is as though this is the admonishment of one bidding farewell — so advise us.\"" He said: \""I enjoin you to have taqwā of Allah"," and to hear and obey"," even if a slave is appointed over you. Whoever among you lives shall see much disagreement"," so adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the Rightly Guided Caliphs. Hold fast to it with your molar teeth. Beware of newly introduced matters"," for every innovation (bidʿah) is misguidance.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Dawrī. [Ḥasan]"""
"20345","(20339) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us that Shuʿbah informed me that Abū ʿAwn al-Thaqafī said: I heard al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAmr narrate from the companions of Muʿādh from the people of Ḥimṣ — and he once said from Muʿādh — that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Muʿādh to Yemen, he said to him: \How will you judge when a matter of judgment is presented to you?\"" He said: \""I will judge by the Book of Allah.\"" He said: \""And if you do not find it in the Book of Allah?\"" He said: \""I will judge by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" He said: \""And if you do not find it in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""I will exert my own opinion (ajtahidu bi-raʾyī) and not fall short.\"" He (Muʿādh) said: \""He struck his hand upon my chest and said: 'All praise is due to Allah"," Who has guided the messenger of the Messenger of Allah to that which pleases the Messenger of Allah.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20346","(20340) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us that Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī informed us that Musaddad informed us that Yaḥyā narrated from Shuʿbah, who informed me that Abū ʀāwn narrated from al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAmr from some of the companions of Muʿādh from Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent him to Yemen, with the same meaning. [Ḍaʿīf. Preceded above]"
"20347","(20341) The noble Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us that Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us that Dāwūd ibn Rushayd informed us that ʿUmar ibn Ayyūb informed us that Jaʿfar ibn Burqān narrated from Maymūn ibn Mihrān, who said: Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) — when a disputant came to him — would look into the Book of Allah. If he found in it something by which to judge, he would judge between them by it. If he did not find it in the Book, he would look to see whether there was a Sunnah of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) concerning it. If he knew it, he would judge by it. If he did not know, he would go out and ask the Muslims, saying: \Such-and-such came to me"," and I looked in the Book of Allah and in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) but found nothing concerning it. Do you know whether the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged in such-and-such a matter?\"" Sometimes a group would come to him and say: \""Yes"," he judged in it by such-and-such","\"" and he would take the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\nJaʿfar said: Someone other than Maymūn informed me that Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say at that time: \""All praise is due to Allah"," Who has placed among us those who preserve the knowledge of our Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nAnd if that exhausted him"," he would summon the leaders of the Muslims and their scholars and consult them. When their opinion converged upon a matter"," he would judge by it.\n\nJaʿfar said: Maymūn informed me that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to do likewise. If he could not find the matter in the Qurʾān and the Sunnah"," he would look to see whether Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) had a judgment concerning it. If he found that Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) had judged in it by a certain judgment"," he would judge by it. Otherwise"," he would summon the leaders of the Muslims and their scholars and consult them. When they agreed upon a matter"," he would judge between them by it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20348","(20342) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī al-Ḥimṣī informed us that Muʿāwyah ibn Ḥafṣ al-Kūfī informed us that ʿAlī ibn Mushir and Ibn Fuḍayl and Asbāṭ and others narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī from al-Shaʿbī from Sharīḥ that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to him: \When a matter comes to you that is in the Book of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," judge by it"," and let not men turn you away from it. If a matter comes to you that is not in the Book of Allah"," look to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and judge by it. If a matter comes to you that is not in the Book of Allah and there is no Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) concerning it"," look to that upon which the people have agreed"," and take it. If a matter comes to you that is not in the Book of Allah"," and there is no Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) concerning it"," and no one before you has spoken about it"," then choose whichever of the two options you wish: if you wish"," you may exert your own judgment and proceed"," and if you wish"," you may delay. And I do not see delay except as better for you.\""\n\nSufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20349","(20343) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us that Abū Khalīfah informed us that Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us that Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd — and sometimes he said from Ḥurayth ibn Ẓuhayr — who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \O people"," a time has come upon us when we did not used to judge and we were not present there. Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," has conveyed to us what you see. So if any of you is presented with a judgment after this day"," let him judge by what is in the Book of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," let him judge by that by which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not judge in it"," let him judge by that by which the righteous ones judged. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not judge in it"," and the righteous ones did not judge in it"," let him exert his own opinion"," and let none of you say: 'I fear' or 'I think.' For the ḥalāl is clear and the ḥarām is clear"," and between them are doubtful matters. So leave that which makes you doubt for that which does not make you doubt.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Nasāʾī 5397]"""
"20350","(20344) Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr from Ḥurayth ibn Ẓuhayr from ʿAbd Allāh with the same meaning.\n\nAbū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Quhustānī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us that Abū ʿUmar informed us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash, and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"
"20351","(20345) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us that Ibn Wahb narrated to me that ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed him from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Maslamah ibn Makhlad: that he stood before Zayd ibn Thābit and said, \O son of my uncle"," we are being compelled to pass judgments.\"" Zayd said"," \""Judge by the Book of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic. If it is not in the Book of Allah"," then by the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ. If it is not in the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ"," then summon the people of opinion"," then exert your independent reasoning (ijtihād) and choose for yourself"," and there is no blame upon you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20352","(20346) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb said: I heard Sufyān narrating from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd who said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbāh (may Allah be pleased with them both) — when he was asked about something that was in the Book of Allah, he would rule by it; and if it was not in the Book of Allah but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said it, he would rule by it; and if it was not in the Book of Allah and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not said it, but Abū Bakr and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) had said it, he would rule by it; otherwise he would exert his own opinion (ijtihād). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20353","(20347) Abū Ṭāhir the Faqīh narrated to us by dictation and recitation that Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Idrīs al-Awdī who said: Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah brought out a document to us and said, \This is the letter of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) to Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" He then mentioned the hadith"," in which it contained: \""Understanding"," understanding! Regarding that which troubles your chest and which has not reached you from the Qur'an and the Sunnah"," then recognize the examples and the resemblances"," and measure the matters accordingly. Then aim for that which is most beloved to Allah and most resembling in your view.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited under no. 20283]"""
"20354","(20348) Abū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from al-Shaybānī from Abī al-Ḍuḥā from Masrūq who said: A scribe of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote: \This is what Allah showed the Commander of the Faithful"," ʿUmar.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) rebuked him and said"," \""No! Rather write: 'This is what ʿUmar thinks.' If it is correct"," then it is from Allah"," and if it is an error"," then it is from ʿUmar.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20355","(20349) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Qanṭarī narrated to us that Abū al-Aḥwaṣ al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-Miṣṣīṣī narrated to us that al-Awzāʿī narrated to me that ʿAbdah ibn Abī Lubābah informed me that Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Beware! Let no man blindly follow another man in his religion. If he believes"," he believes"," and if he disbelieves"," he disbelieves. If one must blindly follow someone"," then let him follow the dead and leave the living"," for the living is not safe from fitnah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20356","(20350) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated from ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb al-Mulāʾī from Ghuṭayf al-Jazarī from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was wearing a gold cross around my neck. He said: \They have taken their rabbis and their monks as lords besides Allah\"" [al-Tawbah: 31]. I said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," they did not worship them.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," but they used to declare lawful for them what Allah had made unlawful"," so they deemed it lawful"," and they used to declare unlawful for them what Allah had made lawful"," so they deemed it unlawful. That was their worship of them.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20357","(20351) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated from al-Aʿmash. (Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir the Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us that Ṭalq ibn Ghannām narrated to us that Zāʾidah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Ḥabīb from Abī al-Bakhtarī who said: Ḥudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about this verse: \They have taken their rabbis and their monks as lords besides Allah\"" [al-Tawbah: 31]. \""Did they pray to them?\"" He said: \""No"," but they used to declare lawful for them what Allah had made unlawful for them"," so they deemed it lawful"," and they used to declare unlawful for them what Allah had made lawful for them"," so they deemed it unlawful. Thus they became lords by that.\"" The wording is that of Zāʾidah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20358","(20352) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated in Makkah. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us. Both said: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us that Abū Usāmah narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father who said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from the people"," but He takes it away by taking the scholars"," until when no scholar remains"," the people take ignorant ones as their leaders. They are asked for fatwas and they give rulings without knowledge"," so they go astray and lead others astray.\"" The wording is that of Abū al-ʿAbbās. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb from Abū Usāmah"," and al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it through other chains from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"20359","(20353) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baghdādī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Sahmī narrated to me that my father narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from Bakr ibn ʿAmr from ʿAmr ibn Abī Naʿīmah, the foster-brother of ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān — and he was a truthful man — from Muslim ibn Yasār who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever attributes to me what I have not said"," let him take his seat in Hellfire. Whoever gives a ruling without knowledge"," its sin falls upon the one who gave the ruling. Whoever advises his brother regarding a matter while knowing that guidance lies in something other than it"," has betrayed him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20360","(20354) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah both informed us that Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah al-Qurashī narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Khalaf ibn Khalīfah narrated to us that Abū Hāshim said: Were it not for a hadith that Ibn Buraydah narrated to me from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. A man who knows the truth and judges by it — he is in Paradise. A man who judges between the people out of ignorance — he is in the Fire. A man who knows the truth but deviates from it — he is in the Fire\"" — we would have said that if a judge exerts independent reasoning (ijtihād)"," there is nothing upon him. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: His exertion of independent reasoning without knowledge does not guide him to the truth except by coincidence"," and he is not permitted to do so. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20361","(20355) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhabārī informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us that Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Bishr al-Bajalī narrated to us that Sharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from al-Aʿmash from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah from Ibn Buraydah from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Judges are three: two judges in the Fire and one judge in Paradise. A judge who ruled unjustly while knowing the truth — he is in the Fire. A judge who ruled while ignorant"," thereby destroying the rights of people — he is in the Fire. And a judge who ruled with the truth — he is in Paradise.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"20362","(20356) And Abū Saʿid al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ḥarmalah narrated to us that Ibn Wahb narrated to us that Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Sharīk, and he mentioned it similarly. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"
"20363","(20357) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us that Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us that Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah from Abū al-ʿĀliyah from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. As for the two in the Fire: a man who deviated from the truth deliberately"," and a man who exercised his personal opinion and erred. As for the one in Paradise: a man who exercised his personal opinion in pursuit of the truth and arrived at it.\"" He (the narrator) said: I said to Abū al-ʿĀliyah"," \""What of the one who exercised his personal opinion in pursuit of the truth but erred?\"" He said: \""Had he willed"," he would not have sat to judge when he was not competent to judge.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The explanation of Abū al-ʿĀliyah regarding one who is not competent to judge is evidence that the hadith refers to one who exercises personal opinion while not being among the people of ijtihād. As for one who is among the people of ijtihād and errs in a matter wherein ijtihād is permissible"," his error is lifted from him"," if Allah wills"," by the ruling of the Prophet (ﷺ) in the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ and Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with them both). And this is what is meant"," and with Allah lies success. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20364","(20358) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me from Ibn Shihāb that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said while upon the minbar: \O people"," the opinion (of the Prophet) from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was correct because Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," used to guide him. As for us"," it is merely conjecture and striving.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: What he meant by this"," and Allah knows best"," is an opinion that is not grounded in a foundational principle. It is in this sense that reports of censure of personal opinion have been narrated from him and from others. Yet we have narrated from most of them the practice of exercising ijtihād in matters where no explicit text exists. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20365","(20359) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿid ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd informed us that ʿUqbah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to me that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Woe to the judge of the earth from the Judge of the heavens on the Day they meet Him — except one who upheld justice and ruled with the truth"," and did not rule based on desire"," nor on the basis of kinship"," nor on the basis of greed"," nor on the basis of fear"," and he made the Book of Allah a mirror between his eyes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20366","(20360) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī al-Khusrawjirdī (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us that Abū Aḥmad al-Ghiṭrīfī informed us that Abū Khalīfah informed us that Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated from Shuʿbah that Abū Ḥuṣayn narrated from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) came to a judge and said to him: \Do you know the abrogating from the abrogated?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""You have perished and caused others to perish.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20367","(20361) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: \It is not befitting for a man to be a judge until he possesses five qualities. If he falls short in one"," there is a blemish in him; if he falls short in two"," there are two blemishes in him — until he is knowledgeable of what came before him"," one who seeks counsel from people of sound judgment"," free from greed"," forbearing toward the litigant"," and one who bears reproach.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20368","(20362) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī and Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated — and they differed in wording — they said: ʿUthmān ibn al-Haytham narrated to us that ʿAwf narrated from al-Ḥasan from Abū Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Allah benefited me with a word I heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) after I nearly joined the Companions of the Camel and fought alongside them. It reached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that the people of Persia had made the daughter of Kisrā their ruler"," so he said: 'A people will never prosper who entrust their affairs to a woman.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Ḥarbī. And in the narration of Hishām: \""They entrusted their affairs to a woman.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn al-Haytham. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 4425"," 7099]"""
"20369","(20363) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz narrated to us that Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to us that Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān narrated from Hilāl ibn ʿAlī from ʬāʾib ibn Yasār from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \While the Prophet (ﷺ) was sitting in his gathering narrating to the people"," a Bedouin came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," when is the Hour?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) continued narrating. Some of the people said: 'He heard what he said and disliked what he said","' and some said: 'He did not hear.' When he finished his narration"," he said: 'Where is the one who asked about the Hour?' He said: 'Here I am"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'When trust is lost"," then await the Hour.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," how is it lost?' He said: 'When authority is entrusted to those who are not worthy of it"," then await the Hour.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Sinān from Fulayḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 591"," 6496]"""
"20370","(20364) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baghdādī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us that my father narrated to us that Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \Whoever appoints a worker from among the Muslims while knowing that among them there is one more deserving of that position and more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of his Prophet"," he has betrayed Allah"," His Messenger"," and all the Muslims.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20371","(20365) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī bin ʪsá narrated to us: Abū Yaḥyā bin Zakariyyā bin Dāwūd narrated to us: Yaḥyā bin Yaḥyā informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān bin Muḥammad al-Muḥāribī narrated from Ashʿath, from Abū Isḥāq, from Murrah, from Ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the words of the Almighty, \And Dāwūd and Sulaymān"," when they judged concerning the field"," when the sheep of the people had strayed into it\"" [al-Anbiyāʾ 78–79]: its clusters of grapes had sprouted and they ruined it. He said: So Dāwūd (peace be upon him) judged that the sheep be given to the owner of the vineyard. Sulaymān said"," \""Other than this"," O Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)!\"" He said"," \""And what is that?\"" He said"," \""Hand over the vineyard to the owner of the sheep so that he tends it until it returns to its [original] state"," and hand over the sheep to the owner of the vineyard so that he benefits from them. Then"," when the vineyard is as it was"," return the vineyard to its owner and return the sheep to their owner.\"" Allah"," the Almighty"," said"," \""And We gave Sulaymān the understanding thereof. And to each We gave judgment and knowledge\"" [al-Anbiyāʾ 78–79]. And it has been narrated to us from Masrūq and Mujāhid with the same meaning. And Allah"," the Most High"," has referred judgment in this incident and its likes to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged regarding the she-camel of al-Barāʾ bin ʿĀzib when it entered the garden of a group of the Anṣār and ruined it. He judged that the guarding of properties rests upon their owners during the day"," and upon the owners of livestock for whatever the livestock destroy at night.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: Al-Ḥasan bin Abī al-Ḥasan said: Were it not for this verse"," I would have thought that the judges were doomed. But Allah praised this one for his correctness and commended this one for his ijtihād. [Weak]"""
"20372","(20366) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad bin Ṣāliḥ bin Hānīʾ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad bin ʿAbd Allāh bin Dīnār both said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad bin Aḥmad bin Anas al-Qurashī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh bin Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Ḥaywah narrated to us: Yazīd bin ʿAbd Allāh bin Usāmah bin al-Hād narrated to me: Muḥammad bin Ibrāhīm bin al-Ḥārith narrated from Busr bin Saʿīd, from Abū Qays, the freedman of ʿAmr bin al-ʿĀṣ, from ʿAmr bin al-ʿĀṣ (may Allah be pleased with him), that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \When a judge rules and exercises ijtihād and is correct"," he has two rewards. And when a judge rules and exercises ijtihād and errs"," he has one reward.\""\n\nHe"," meaning Ibn al-Hād"," said: I narrated this hadith to Abū Bakr bin Muḥammad bin ʿAmr bin Ḥazm"," and he said: Thus Abū Salamah bin ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh bin Yazīd al-Muqriʾ. [Sound — Agreed upon]"""
"20373","(20367) ʿAlī bin Aḥmad bin ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad bin ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad bin Ibrāhīm bin Milḥān narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād, and he mentioned with its chain something similar.\n\nHe said: I narrated this hadith to Abū Bakr bin Muḥammad bin ʿAmr bin Ḥazm, and he said: Thus Abū Salamah bin ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me from Abū Hurayrah. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh bin ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Marwān bin Muḥammad from al-Layth, and he also narrated it from the hadith of al-Dārawardī from Ibn al-Hād. [Sound — preceded before it]"
"20374","(20368) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī bin Aḥmad bin ʿAbdān informed us: Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān bin Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us: Ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: My father narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Thawrī, from Yaḥyā bin Saʿīd, from Abū Bakr bin Muḥammad bin ʿAmr bin Ḥazm, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \When a judge rules and exercises ijtihād and is correct"," he has two rewards. And when he rules and exercises ijtihād and errs"," he has one reward.\""\n\nNone narrated it from Sufyān except Maʿmar"," and ʿAbd al-Razzāq was alone in narrating it from him. [Denounced]"""
"20375","(20369) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad bin al-Ḥusayn bin Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad bin Aḥmad bin Dallawayh al-Daqqāq narrated to us: Abū al-Azhar al-Salīṭī narrated to us: Marwān bin Muḥammad narrated to us: Yazīd bin Rabīʿah narrated to us: Rabīʿah bin Yazīd narrated to me: I heard Wāthilah bin al-Asqaʿ say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever seeks knowledge and attains it shall have two portions of reward. And if he does not attain it"," he shall have one portion of reward.\"" [Good]"""
"20376","(20370) Abū Naṣr bin Qatādah informed us: ʿAlī bin al-Faḍl bin Muḥammad bin ʿUqayl al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm bin Hāshim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh bin Muḥammad bin Asmāʾ narrated to us: My uncle Juwayriyah bin Asmāʾ narrated from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called out to us on the day he departed from [the battle of] al-Aḥzāb: \Let no one pray Ẓuhr except in Banū Qurayẓah.\"" He said: So some people feared missing the time [of prayer]"," so they prayed before reaching Banū Qurayẓah. Others said: \""We shall not pray except where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us"," even if the time elapses.\"" He said: He did not rebuke either of the two groups.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh bin Muḥammad bin Asmāʾ. [Sound — Agreed upon]"""
"20377","(20371) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid bin Bilāl narrated to us: Yaḥyā bin al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Idrīs al-Awdī, who said: Saʿīd bin Abī Burdah brought out a letter to us and said: \This is the letter of ʿUmar to Abū Mūsá (may Allah be pleased with both of them): 'To proceed: Let not a judgment you rendered yesterday prevent you from returning to the truth"," for the truth is ancient"," and nothing invalidates the truth. And returning to the truth is better than persisting in falsehood.'\"" Aḥmad bin Ḥanbal and others narrated it from Sufyān"," and they said in the hadith: \""Let not a judgment you rendered yesterday prevent you from reconsidering it and being guided therein to your rectitude"," for the truth is ancient"," and nothing invalidates the truth. And returning to the truth is better than persisting in falsehood.\"" [Sound — preceded under no. 20283]"""
"20378","(20372) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid bin Bilāl narrated to us: Yaḥyā bin al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Idrīs al-Awdī, who said: Saʿīd bin Abī Burdah brought out a letter to us and said: \This is the letter of ʿUmar to Abū Mūsá (may Allah be pleased with both of them): 'To proceed: Let not a judgment you rendered yesterday prevent you from returning to the truth"," for the truth is ancient"," and nothing invalidates the truth. And returning to the truth is better than persisting in falsehood.'\"" Aḥmad bin Ḥanbal and others narrated it from Sufyān"," and they said in the hadith: \""Let not a judgment you rendered yesterday prevent you from reconsidering it and being guided therein to your rectitude"," for the truth is ancient"," and nothing invalidates the truth. And returning to the truth is better than persisting in falsehood.\"" [Sound — preceded under no. 20283]"""
"20379","(20373) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Aḥmad bin Sahl narrated to us: Ibrāhīm bin Maʿqil narrated to me: Ḥarmalah narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā bin Saʿīd and Rabīʿah bin Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who both said: ʿUmar bin ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz used to say: \No lump of clay is easier for me to break apart"," and no judgment is easier for me to overturn"," than a judgment I rendered and then saw that the truth lay elsewhere"," so I annulled it.\"" [Sound]\n\nChapter: Whoever among the judges exercises ijtihād and then his ijtihād changes"," or the ijtihād of another changes"," in a matter wherein ijtihād is permissible — that which he previously judged is not reversed.\n\nBy analogy with what has preceded regarding the error in the direction of prayer (qiblah) in the Book of Prayer."""
"20380","(20374) And with what Abū Saʿīd bin Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad bin Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī narrated to us: Muḥammad bin Naṣr al-Marwazī narrated to us: Al-Ḥasan bin ʪsá informed us: Ibn al-Mubārak informed us: Maʿmar said: I heard Simāk bin al-Faḍl al-Khawlānī narrating from Wahb bin Munabbih, from al-Ḥakam bin Masʿūd al-Thaqafī, who said: I witnessed ʿUmar bin al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) include the full siblings with the maternal siblings in the third [of the estate]. A man said to him: \You ruled last year differently than this.\"" He said: \""How did I rule?\"" He said: \""You gave it to the full siblings and gave nothing to the maternal siblings.\""\n\nHe said: \""That was what we judged then"," and this is what we judge now.\"" [Weak]"""
"20381","(20375) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us — Ibn Numayr narrated from al-A'mash — from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, who said: Had 'Ali ever spoken critically of 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with them both — at any time, he would have done so on the day when the people of Najran came to him. And 'Ali — may Allah be pleased with him — used to write correspondence between the people of Najran and the Prophet ﷺ. Their numbers increased during the era of 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with him — until he feared for the people on their account, and discord arose among them. They came to 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with him — and requested an exchange, and he granted them the exchange. Then they regretted it, or something was placed before them, and they came to him seeking to annul it, but he refused to rescind it. When 'Ali — may Allah be pleased with him — assumed the caliphate, they came to him and said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," your intercession with your own tongue and your written attestation with your right hand.\"" 'Ali — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \""Woe upon you! Indeed"," 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with him — was one of sound judgment in affairs.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20382","(20376) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Salam al-Naysaburi narrated to us — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — 'Ata' ibn Muslim narrated, saying: I heard Salih al-Muradi say — 'Abd Khayr said: I was near 'Ali — may Allah be pleased with him — when the people of Najran came to him. I said: \If he were to reject anything of 'Umar's position"," today would be the day.\"" He said: \""They offered their greetings and sat before him.\"" Then he placed his hand inside his sleeve and produced a document"," which was placed in the hand of 'Ali — may Allah be pleased with him. They said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," your written attestation with your right hand"," and the dictation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon you.\"" I saw 'Ali — may Allah be pleased with him — with tears flowing down his cheeks. Then he raised his head toward them and said: \""O people of Najran"," this is the last document I ever wrote in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" They said: \""Then grant us what is in it.\"" He said: \""I shall inform you of that. Whatever 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with him — took from you"," he did not take it for himself; rather"," he took it for a body of Muslims. And what he took from you was better than what he gave you. By Allah"," I shall not reverse anything that 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with him — enacted"," for 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with him — was one of sound judgment in affairs.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20383","(20377) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us — Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us — 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' narrated — from Sa'id — from Qatadah — from Abu Hassan, that al-'Abbas ibn Kharashah al-Kalabi said to him: The sons of his paternal uncle and the sons of his wife's paternal uncle said to him: \Your wife does not love you. If you wish to know this"," then give her the choice.\"" He said: \""O Barzah bint al-Hur"," choose!\"" She said: \""Woe to you! I have exercised my choice"," and you are not given a choice.\"" She said this three times. They said: \""She is forbidden to you.\"" He said: \""You have lied.\"" Then he came to 'Ali — may Allah be pleased with him — and mentioned that to him. He said: \""If you approach her until she marries another man"," I shall surely pelt you with stones\"" — or he said"," \""I shall crush you with stones.\"" When Mu'awiyah — may Allah be pleased with him — assumed the caliphate"," he came to him and said: \""Abu Turab separated me from my wife on such-and-such grounds.\"" He said: \""We have affirmed his judgment upon you\"" — or he said"," \""We would not reverse a judgment he rendered upon you.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20384","(20378) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us — 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us — Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Bazzaz narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us — Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated — from Ibn 'Awn — from 'Isa ibn al-Harith, who said: The umm walad of my brother, Shurayh ibn al-Harith, had borne him a young girl. She was married and bore a son. Then the umm walad died. Shurayh ibn al-Harith and the son of his daughter's daughter came to dispute over her inheritance before Shurayh (the qadi). Shurayh ibn al-Harith kept saying to Shurayh: \He has no share of inheritance in the Book of Allah; he is merely the son of her daughter.\"" Shurayh (the qadi) judged that her inheritance go to the son of her daughter"," and he said: {And those of kinship are closer to one another in the Book of Allah} [al-Anfal 75]. Then Masayrah ibn Yazid set out to Ibn al-Zubayr and informed him of what Shurayh had done. Ibn al-Zubayr wrote to Shurayh: \""Masayrah ibn Yazid has mentioned to me such-and-such"," and that you recited at that time: {And those of kinship are closer to one another in the Book of Allah} [al-Anfal 75]. That verse was only concerning the matter of mutual inheritance (al-'asabah)"," whereby a man would enter into a pact with another man"," saying: 'You inherit from me and I inherit from you.' When it was revealed"," that practice was abandoned.\"" Masayrah ibn Yazid then came to Shurayh with the letter. When he read it"," he refused to reverse his judgment and said: \""I only freed her while she was in my womb.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20385","(20379) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Ma'qil narrated to us — Harmalah narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Malik narrated: That when Aban ibn 'Uthman was appointed governor of Madinah during the caliphate of 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, he wished to overturn what 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr had previously judged. Aban ibn 'Uthman wrote to 'Abd al-Malik regarding this matter. 'Abd al-Malik wrote back to him: \We do not take issue with Ibn al-Zubayr for the judgments he used to render; rather"," we take issue with him for what he sought in the way of authority. When this letter of mine reaches you"," carry out what Ibn al-Zubayr judged and do not reverse it"," for the reversal of judgments is a burdensome affliction.\"" [Hasan]"""
"20386","(20380) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Yusuf al-Hafiz narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us — Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us — al-Jariri narrated.\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Ali al-Khusrajirdi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to us — Abu 'Abd Allah Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi narrated to us — Abu Khaythamah narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, that is Ibn 'Ulayyah, narrated — from al-Jariri.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us — al-Jariri narrated — from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah — from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins?\"" — three times. They said: \""Indeed"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Associating partners with Allah (shirk)"," and disobedience to one's parents.\"" He said: \""And he sat up"," having been reclining: 'Beware — and false speech.'\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept repeating it until we said: \""Would that he were silent.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Bishr. And in the narration of Ibn 'Ulayyah"," he said: \""We were sitting in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'Shall I not inform you?' — and he said: 'False testimony' — three times.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musaddad"," and both he and Muslim transmitted it from the hadith of Ibn 'Ulayyah from al-Jariri. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"20387","(20381) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Darabadijardi narrated to us — 'Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated — from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas ibn Malik — from Anas ibn Malik — may Allah be pleased with him: That the major sins were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \Associating partners with Allah"," taking a life unjustly"," disobedience to one's parents"," and false testimony — or false speech.\"" [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"20388","(20382) And Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki informed us — Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl al-Muzakki narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us — 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated, mentioning it with its chain of narration similarly, except that he said: \The greatest of major sins is associating partners with Allah.\"" Then he mentioned the rest.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Munir from 'Abd al-Malik al-Juddi"," and he said — and 'Amr ibn Marzuq also narrated it. And Muslim transmitted it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Sahih]"""
"20389","(20383) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Garazah informed us — Muhammad and Ya'la, the two sons of 'Ubayd, both narrated — from Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-'Asfuri — from his father — from Habib ibn al-Nu'man al-Asadi — from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi — may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer. When he had finished, he stood up and said: \False testimony has been made equal to associating partners with Allah\"" — three times. Then he recited this verse: {So avoid the abomination of idols"," and avoid false speech"," being upright toward Allah"," not associating anything with Him} [al-Hajj 30–31]. [Da'if]"""
"20390","(20384) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us — 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Furat al-Tamimi said: I heard Harib ibn Dithar say — I heard Ibn 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with them both — say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The false witness's feet will not move from their place until the Fire becomes obligatory for him.\""\n\nAnd the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Birds on the Day of Resurrection shall raise their beaks"," strike with their tails"," and cast out what is in their bellies"," and there will be none to demand anything from them — so beware of it.\""\n\nMuhammad ibn al-Furat al-Kufi is da'if.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Abu al-Walid narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Hashim narrated from his father — from Muhriz ibn Salih: That 'Ali — may Allah be pleased with him — separated between the witnesses. [Very Da'if]"""
"20391","(20385) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd al-Ḥafarī narrated to us, from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us, saying: my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, saying: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ḥudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me two ḥadīths. I have seen one of them [fulfilled], and I am awaiting the other. He narrated to us: \Trustworthiness (al-amānah) descends into the roots of the hearts of men. Then the Qurʾān was revealed"," and they learned from the Qurʾān and they learned from the Sunnah.\"" Then he narrated to us about its removal"," saying: \""A man sleeps"," and the trustworthiness is withdrawn from his heart"," leaving a trace like the trace of a prick. Then the man sleeps"," and the trustworthiness is withdrawn from his heart"," leaving a trace like a blister — like a coal you have rolled across your foot"," causing it to swell; you see it raised up"," yet there is nothing inside it. People will rise in the morning and trade with one another"," and scarcely anyone will fulfill his trust"," until it is said: 'In the tribe of so-and-so there is a trustworthy man.' And until it is said of a man: 'How resolute he is"," how refined"," how intelligent!' — while there is not in his heart so much as a mustard seed of good.\""\n\nḤudhayfah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""There was a time when I did not care with whom I traded. If he was a believer"," his religion would compel him to return my due; and if he was a Jew or a Christian"," his deputy would return it to me. But as for today"," I do not trade except with so-and-so and so-and-so.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Ṣāliḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," from Sufyān; and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20392","(20386) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūṣuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥassān al-Qaṭṭān informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us, from Bayān, from Qays — that is, ibn Abī Ḥāzim — from Mirdās al-Aslamī, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The righteous will depart one after another"," and there will remain the dregs of people like the dregs of barley or dates. Allah will not care about them at all.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 4156"," 6434]"""
"20393","(20387) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, saying: Muḥāḍir narrated to us, saying: al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUbaydah, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The best of people are my generation"," then those who follow them"," then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths will outpace their testimony and whose testimony will outpace their oaths.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20394","(20388) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us, saying: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us, saying: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us, saying: Abū Jamrah narrated to us, saying: I heard Zuhdham ibn Muḍarrib say: I heard ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The best of you are my generation"," then those who follow them"," then those who follow them"," then those who follow them.\"" ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn said: \""I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned two generations after his own or three.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"," after you there will come a people who betray and are not entrusted"," who testify and are not asked to testify"," who make vows and do not fulfill them"," and among whom obesity will appear.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20395","(20389) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Rabīʿ and Musaddad narrated to us — and the wording is that of Musaddad — saying: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thābit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and the deceased was praised with good. He said: \It has become obligatory.\"" Then another funeral procession passed by him"," and the deceased was praised with evil. He said: \""It has become obligatory.\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you said 'It has become obligatory' for this one and 'It has become obligatory' for this one.\"" He said: \""The testimony of the people. The believers are the witnesses of Allah upon the earth.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," from Ḥammād; and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20396","(20390) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, saying: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn al-ʿAzīz informed us, saying: Dāwūd ibn ʿAmr al-Ḍabbī narrated to us. They both said: Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmār al-Jumaḥī narrated to us, saying: Umayyah ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us, from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Zuhayr al-Thaqafī, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ, at al-Nabāt — or he said, at al-Nabāwah — say: \You will soon come to know the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire\"" — or he said"," \""the best of you from the worst of you.\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," by what?\"" He said: \""By good praise and bad praise. You are witnesses"," some of you"," over others.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20397","(20391) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: Dāwūd ibn Abī al-Furāt narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us — and the wording is theirs — saying: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, saying: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, saying: Dāwūd ibn Abī al-Furāt al-Kindī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from Abū al-Aswad al-Dīlī, who said: I came to Madīnah when a plague had struck it and people were dying a rapid death. I sat with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him. A funeral procession passed by him, and the deceased was praised with good. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \It has become obligatory.\"" Then another passed by"," and the deceased was praised with good. ʿUmar said: \""It has become obligatory.\"" Then a third passed by"," and the deceased was praised with evil. ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""It has become obligatory.\"" Abū al-Aswad said: I said: \""What has become obligatory"," O Commander of the Faithful?\"" He said: \""I said as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Any Muslim for whom four people testify to his goodness"," Allah will admit him into Paradise.'\"" He said: We said: \""And three?\"" He said: \""And three.\"" We said: \""And two?\"" He said: \""And two.\"" Then we did not ask him about one.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 1368"," 2643]"""
"20398","(20392) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to us, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Anṣārī informed me that ʿItbān ibn Mālik — who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who witnessed Badr — informed him: He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," my sight has become impaired"," and I lead my people in prayer. When the rains come"," the valley between me and them floods"," and I am unable to come to their mosque to lead them in prayer. I wish"," O Messenger of Allah"," that you would come and pray in my house so that I could take it as a place of prayer.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \""I shall do so"," Allah willing.\"" ʿItbān said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abū Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," came the following morning when the day had risen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought permission"," and I gave him permission. He did not sit until he entered the house"," and said to me: \""Where in your house would you like me to pray?\"" I said: I pointed to a corner of the house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and pronounced the takbīr"," and we stood and formed rows behind him. He prayed two rakʿahs and then gave the salām. He said: We detained him for a dish of khazīrah that we had prepared for him. He said: Men of the household"," a large number of them"," gathered and assembled. One of them said: \""Where is Mālik ibn al-Dukhshun?\"" Some of them said: \""That one is a hypocrite; he does not love Allah and His Messenger.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do not say that about him. Do you not see that he has said 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh","' seeking thereby the Countenance of Allah?\"" He said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," we see his face and his counsel directed toward the hypocrites.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"," Allah has forbidden the Fire upon anyone who says 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh","' seeking thereby the Countenance of Allah.\"" Ibn Shihāb said: I then asked al-Ḥuṣayn ibn Muḥammad al-Anṣārī — who was one of Banū Sālim and among their notables — about the ḥadīth of Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ"," and he confirmed it.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from al-Zuhrī. The Prophet ﷺ did not accept the statement of the one who called Mālik ibn al-Dukhshun a hypocrite until it became clear to him from what basis he said that. Then"," when he explained that he did not consider him a hypocrite"," the Prophet ﷺ rejected his statement. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20399","(20393) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad ibn Sufyān narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb narrated to us, saying: al-Fuḍayl ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, who said: \A person among the Muslims was considered just (ʿadl) so long as no suspicion (rībah) was apparent from him.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""This is our position regarding one whose uprightness (ʿadālah) has been established — he remains upon his original uprightness so long as no suspicion becomes apparent from him. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20400","(20394) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from ʿUrwah, that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," granted me such-and-such land. al-Zubayr went to the family of ʿUmar and purchased their share from them. Then he came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and said: 'ʿAbd al-Raḥmān claims that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him such-and-such land.' He said: 'His testimony is accepted"," both for him and against him.'\"" And it has already been mentioned in the ḥadīth of the lapse in prayer that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," may Allah be pleased with him: \""You are"," in our eyes"," the upright and accepted one (al-ʿadl al-riḍā). What did you hear?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20401","(20395) And in what Abū Dāwūd narrated in al-Marāsil, from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, from Abū Usāmah and Yazīd, from al-Ṣaʿq ibn Ḥazn, from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a man is asked about his brother"," he has the choice; if he wishes"," he may remain silent"," and if he wishes"," he may speak—and thus he speaks the truth.\""\n\nAbū Bakr al-Sulaymānī informed us"," Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us"," Abū ʿAlī al-Lu'lu'ī narrated to us"," Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," and he mentioned it. He said: And one of them said: \""about the man.\"" [Weak]"""
"20402","(20396) As evidence, from what Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated, from Manṣūr, from Abū Wā'il, from Ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man said to the Prophet (ﷺ): \O Messenger of Allah"," how do I know when I have done good and when I have done evil?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""When you hear your neighbours saying"," 'You have done well","' then you have indeed done well. And when you hear them saying"," 'You have done evil","' then you have indeed done evil.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Maʿmar narrated it in his Jāmiʿ"," 19749]"""
"20403","(20397) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from Jāmiʿ ibn Shaddād, from Kulthūm al-Khuzāʿī, who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," how can I know when I have done well that I have indeed done well"," and when I have done evil that I have indeed done evil?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""When your neighbours say to you"," 'You have done well","' then you have indeed done well. And when your neighbours say to you"," 'You have done evil","' then you have indeed done evil.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ by other than this chain]"""
"20404","(20398) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated, from Abū ʿAbbād narrated to me, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when a man passed by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asking him. He said: \O ʿAbd Allāh"," do you know him?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""What is his name?\"" I said: \""I do not know.\"" He said: \""Where is his dwelling?\"" I said: \""I do not know.\"" He said: \""This is not (true) knowledge (of a person).\"" Thus he said. [Weak]"""
"20405","(20399) And Abū Dāwūd narrated it in al-Marāsil, from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, from Ibn ʿUyaynah, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, who said: A man passed by the Prophet (ﷺ), and he said: \Who knows him?\"" A man said: \""I know him by his face"," but I do not know him by his name.\"" He said: \""That is not (true) knowledge (of a person).\""\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us"," Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us"," Abū ʿAlī al-Lu'lu'ī narrated to us"," Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," and he mentioned it as a mursal narration"," and it is the correct one. [Weak]"""
"20406","(20400) Al-Sharīf Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayh al-Harawī informed us, Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Ziyād narrated to us, Shaybān narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from Sulaymān ibn Musāhir, from Kharashah ibn al-Ḥurr, who said: A man testified before ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) with a testimony. He said to him: \I do not know you"," and it does not harm you that I do not know you. Bring someone who knows you.\"" A man from the people said: \""I know him.\"" He said: \""By what do you know him?\"" He said: \""By his justice and his virtue.\"" He said: \""Is he your nearest neighbour"," whose night and day you know"," and whose comings and goings you know?\"" He said: \""No.\""\n\nHe said: \""Is he your business partner in dinars and dirhams"," by which piety is inferred?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Is he your companion in travel"," by which noble character is inferred?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""You do not know him.\"" Then he said to the man: \""Bring someone who knows you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20407","(20401) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Raffāʾ narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Yaḥyya ibn ʿAmr ibn Mālik al-Nukarī narrated, from his father, from Abū al-Jawzā', from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the words of the Most High: {The day We shall fold up the heavens like the folding up of the scroll for the books} [al-Anbiyā' 104]. He said: The Prophet (ﷺ) had a scribe who was called al-Sijill. [Munkar]"
"20408","(20402) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Nūḥ ibn Qays narrated, from Yazīd ibn Kaʿb, from ʿAmr ibn Mālik, from Abū al-Jawzā', from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \Al-Sijill was a scribe of the Prophet (ﷺ).\"" [Munkar. It was narrated before it]"""
"20409","(20403) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hāni' narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah al-Mājishūn narrated, from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Abī ʿAwn, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: A letter from a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ). He said to ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Arqam: \Reply on my behalf.\"" So he wrote the reply and then read it back to him. He said: \""You have done well and excelled. O Allah"," grant him success.\"" When ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) became caliph"," he used to consult him. [Weak]"""
"20410","(20404) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Ghassān al-Ghulābī narrated to us, Yaʿlā narrated, and al-Aʿmash narrated. He said: I said to Shaqīq: \Who was the scribe of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Arqam. And a letter from Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us at al-Qādisiyyah"," and at the bottom of it was written: 'ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Arqam.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20411","(20405) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn al-Faḍl narrated to me — Muḥammad ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us — Salamah narrated from Ibn Isḥāq — from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr — from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ appointed ʿAbdullāh ibn Arqam as a scribe. ʿAbdullāh ibn Arqam used to write, and he used to compose replies on his behalf to the kings. His trustworthiness reached such a degree that he [the Prophet ﷺ] would instruct him to write to certain kings, and he would write, and then he would instruct him to seal it and not to read it, on account of his trustworthiness before him. Then he ﷺ also appointed Zayd ibn Thābit as a scribe, and he used to write the waḥy and also write to the kings. And when ʿAbdullāh ibn Arqam and Zayd ibn Thābit were both absent, and there was a need to write to certain commanders of the armies or to the kings, or to write a letter to someone to be dispatched, he would order Jaʿfar to write. ʿUmar and ʿUthmān had written for him, and Zayd, al-Mughīrah, Muʿāwiyah, Khālid ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ, and others besides them from among the Arabs who have been named, [also wrote for him]. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20412","(20406) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — al-Ḥasan, meaning al-Ashyaʿ, narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd al-Zuhrī narrated to us — from Ibn Shihāb — from ʿUbayd ibn al-Sabbāq — from Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \You are a young"," intelligent man"," and we do not suspect you. You used to write the waḥy for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So seek out the Qurʾān and compile it.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Thābit and others"," from Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2807"," 3506]"""
"20413","(20407) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father — from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: Zayd ibn Thābit said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me"," so I learned the script of the Jews for him"," and he said: 'By Allah"," I do not trust the Jews regarding my correspondence.' So I learned it"," and half a month did not pass before me.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: \""Except half a month — until I became proficient in it.\"" He said: \""My father said: 'So I would write for him when he wrote"," and I would read to him when something was written to him.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Also numbered 6/12195]"""
"20414","(20408) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Hushaym narrated — from al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥawshab — from al-Azhar ibn Rāshid, who said: Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, used to narrate to his companions. When he narrated to them a hadith they did not understand, they would go to al-Ḥasan, and he would explain it to them. One day he narrated and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not seek light from the fire of the polytheists"," and do not engrave Arabic on your signet rings.\"" So they went to al-Ḥasan and said: \""Anas has narrated to us today a hadith we do not understand.\"" He said: \""What did you narrate?\"" They mentioned it. He said: \""Yes. As for his statement"," 'Do not engrave Arabic on your signet rings' — he means: Do not engrave 'Muḥammad' on your signet rings. And as for his statement"," 'Do not seek light from the fire of the polytheists' — he means: Do not consult the polytheists in any of your affairs.\"" And the confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic: {O you who have believed"," do not take as intimates those other than yourselves; they will not spare you any ruin} [Āl ʿImrān 118]. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20415","(20409) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Saʿīd Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī informed us by dictation — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad — Abū ʿAlī al-Washshāʾ narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us — Shuʿbah narrated — from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, who said: I heard ʿIyāḍ al-Ashʿarī say that Abū Mūsā, may Allah be pleased with him, came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with both of them, as part of a delegation, and with him was a Christian scribe. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, was impressed by what he saw of his [the scribe's] memorization, so he said: \Tell your scribe to read a letter to us.\"" He said: \""He is a Christian; he does not enter the mosque.\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," rebuked him and was about to seize him"," and said: \""Do not honor them when Allah has humiliated them"," do not bring them near when Allah has distanced them"," and do not trust them when Allah has declared them treacherous"," the Almighty and Majestic.\""\n\nAnd Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī and Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Najjār al-Muqriʾ in al-Kūfah informed us — Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us — ʿAmr ibn Ḥammād narrated — from Asbāṭ — from Simāk — from ʿIyāḍ al-Ashʿarī — from Abū Mūsā"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," ordered him to bring to him what he had taken and what he had given in a single hide. Abū Mūsā had a Christian scribe who would bring that to him"," and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was amazed and said: \""Indeed"," this one has a good memory.\"" He said: \""We have a letter in the mosque.\"" He had come from al-Shām. He said: \""Call him so he may read it.\"" Abū Mūsā said: \""He is not able to enter the mosque.\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Is he in a state of janābah?\"" He said: \""No"," rather he is a Christian.\"" He said: \""He rebuked me and struck my thigh and said: 'Remove him","' and he recited: {O you who have believed"," do not take the Jews and the Christians as allies; they are allies of one another. And whoever is an ally to them among you — then indeed"," he is of them. Indeed"," Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people} [al-Māʾidah 51].\"" Abū Mūsā said: \""By Allah"," I have not taken him as an ally; he only writes.\"" He said: \""Did you not find among the people of Islam someone to write for you? Do not bring them near when Allah has distanced them"," do not trust them when Allah has declared them treacherous"," and do not honor them after Allah has humiliated them.\"" So he removed him. [Ḥasan]"""
"20416","(20410) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Nujayd narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik narrated to me — Abū Laylā ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl — from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah, who informed him that men from the elders of his people informed him, and he mentioned the hadith of al-qasāmah, in which it is stated: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to them regarding that"," and they wrote: 'By Allah"," we did not kill him.'\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ as previously mentioned. (t) And it has been narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUkaym that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the land of Juhaynah. And it has been narrated in the hadith of ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm that the Prophet ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen a letter containing the farāʾiḍ"," the sunan"," and the diyāt"," and he sent it with ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm"," and it was read to the people of Yemen. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20417","(20411) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhb al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us — Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated to me — my father ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to me — Thumāmah ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Anas narrated to me that Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote this book when he sent it to al-Baḥrayn: \In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful. These are the obligatory ṣadaqah that Allah has imposed upon the Muslims"," which Allah has commanded His Messenger ﷺ [to collect]. Whoever among the Muslims is asked for it in its proper form"," let him give it"," and whoever is asked for more than that"," let him not give it.\"" And he mentioned the hadith. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Anṣārī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20418","(20412) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī informed us — Abū Yaʿlā al-Mawṣilī narrated to us — Abū Khaythamah narrated to us — Jarīr narrated — from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal — from Abū ʿUthmān, who said: ʿUtbah ibn Farqad sent to ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, along with a slave boy of ʿUtbah's from Adharbayjān, a fine ḥabīṣ that he had made in al-Salālī upon which were al-lubūd. When he reached ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, ʿUmar uncovered the ḥabīṣ and said: \Will the Muslims be satisfied in their dwellings with this?\"" The messenger said: \""No.\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""I do not want it.\"" And he wrote to ʿUtbah: \""To proceed: It is not from your toil"," nor the toil of your father"," nor the toil of your mother. So satisfy the Muslims in your vicinity in their dwellings with what you would be satisfied with in your own dwelling.\"" Then he said: \""Tie your izārs"," wear your ridaʾs"," put on your sandals"," cast aside the sarāwīls and the khifāfs"," throw the targets"," abandon the saddles"," and dismount with a leap. Hold fast to the Maʿaddīyah and the ʿArabīyah"," abandon the luxuries and the adornments of the non-Arabs"," and beware of wearing silk"," for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from wearing silk","\"" — except thus — and he placed his index finger and middle finger [together]. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Khaythamah"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it in abridged form as previously mentioned."""
"20419","(20413) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us — Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated — from Qatādah — from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to write to the Romans, it was said to him: \They will not read your letter unless it is sealed.\"" So he ﷺ took a seal of silver"," and its engraving was \""Muḥammad"," Messenger of Allah.\"" Anas said: \""It is as if I am looking at its whiteness in his hand.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and he also extracted it from the hadith of Ghundar"," from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20420","(20414) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bulshān informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar narrated — from Thābit — from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ made a seal of silver and engraved upon it \Muḥammad"," Messenger of Allah ﷺ","\"" and he said: \""Do not engrave upon it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20421","(20415) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took a ring of silver and had inscribed upon it \Muḥammad Rasūl Allāh","\"" and he said: \""Indeed"," I have taken a ring of silver and inscribed upon it 'Muḥammad Rasūl Allāh","' so let no one engrave upon the like of its inscription.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20422","(20416) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Mahdī ibn Maymūn narrated to us; Ghaylān ibn Jarīr narrated to us, who said: Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbd Allāh said: \Guard yourselves against people through suspicion (sūʾ al-ẓann).\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: This has also been narrated from Anas ibn Mālik in a marfūʿ (elevated) chain. And caution against such matters is a followed Sunnah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20423","(20417) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Fāris narrated to us; Nūḥ ibn Yazīd ibn Sayyār al-Muʾaddib narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to me; Ibn Isḥāq narrated it to him, from ʿĪsā ibn Maʿmar, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Faghwāʾ al-Khuzāʿī, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called me when he intended to send me with some wealth to Abū Sufyān to distribute among the Quraysh in Makkah after the Conquest. He said: \Seek a companion.\"" So ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī came to me and said: \""It has reached me that you intend to travel and are seeking a companion.\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then I am your companion.\"" So I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \""I have found a companion.\"" He said to me: \""Who?\"" I said: \""ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī.\"" He said: \""When you descend upon the land of his people"," beware of him"," for the one who says has said: 'Your brother al-Bakrī — do not feel safe from him.'\"" He said: \""So we set out until we were at al-Abwāʾ"," and he said: 'I have a need to attend to among my people at Waddān — wait for me.' I said: 'Very well.' When he turned away"," I remembered the statement of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," so I urged on my camel until I departed swiftly. When I was at al-Aṣāfir"," suddenly he appeared before me with a group.\"" He said: \""And I hastened and outpaced him. When he saw that I had escaped him"," they departed"," and he came to me and said: 'I had a need among my people.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'Yes.' And we continued on until we arrived in Makkah"," and I delivered the wealth to Abū Sufyān.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20424","(20418) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me; Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Aḥmad ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth narrated, from ʿUqayl, from al-Zuhrī, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \A believer is not stung from the same hole twice.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20425","(20419) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Khālid narrated, from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, that he used to dislike a man's testimony regarding a will on a sealed document until he knew what was in it.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyūb, that Abū Qilābah used to dislike testifying regarding a sealed document. He said: \Perhaps there is injustice in it.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20426","(20420) And Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us; ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Saʿīd narrated to us; Jarīr narrated, from Mughīrah, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, regarding a man who seals upon his will and says: \Bear witness to what is in it.\"" He said: \""It is not valid until he reads it or it is read to him and he affirms what is in it.\""\n\nHe said: \""And Yaʿqūb narrated to me; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿImrān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated"," who said: 'Sufyān was asked about a man who wrote his will"," sealed it"," and said: \""Bear witness to what is in it.\"" He said: \""Ibn Abī Laylā used to invalidate it.\"" Sufyān said: \""And the judges do not permit it for him.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20427","(20421) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; Hushaym narrated, from Manṣūr, from Ibn Sīrīn. Aḥmad said: \He once said: 'From some of the children of al-ʿAlāʾ' — that al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Ḍaramī (may Allah be pleased with him) was the governor of the Prophet (ﷺ) over al-Baḥrayn"," and when he wrote to him"," he would begin with himself.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20428","(20422) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated, from Hishām ibn Ḥassān, from Ibn Sīrīn, that al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Ḍaramī wrote to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm — from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Ḍaramī to Muḥammad"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20429","(20423) And Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us; Abū ʿAmr informed us; Ḥanbal narrated to us; ʿAlī, meaning ibn al-Jaʿd, narrated to us; Abū Hilāl narrated to us; Qatādah informed us that Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ and Khālid ibn al-Walīd both wrote to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and began with themselves. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20430","(20424) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Khusrawjirdī informed us, both saying: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī informed us; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Qutaybah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn Muḥammad narrated, from Qays, from Abū Hāshim, from Zādān, from Salmān (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \No one was of greater sanctity than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when they wrote to him"," would write: 'From so-and-so to Muḥammad"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20431","(20425) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us, that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, that Abū Salamah al-Minqarī narrated to us, that Abū ʿAwānah narrated from ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with him — that he heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There was a man among the Children of Israel who would lend people money. When his agent would come to him…\"" He mentioned the hadith"," and in it he said: \""The debtor would take a piece of wood and carve it out when the appointed term arrived"," placing the money inside it and writing to him a document: 'From so-and-so to so-and-so — I have indeed delivered your money to the agent whom you appointed for me.'\"" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in numerous places.]"""
"20432","(20426) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us, that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us, that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, that my father narrated to me, that Yazīd — meaning Ibn Hārūn — informed us, that Ibn ʿAwn narrated from Nāfiʿ, that Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — once wrote a letter to Muʿāwiyah and intended to begin with his own name, but they kept at him until he wrote: \From ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar to Muʿāwiyah.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20433","(20427) And Ibn Bashrān informed us, that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us, that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to us, that Ḥammād narrated from Ḥumayd, that Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh wrote to an official interceding on behalf of a man: \In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful — to so-and-so son of so-and-so"," from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh.\"" I said to him: \""Will you begin with his name?\"" He said: \""What harm is there if Allah fulfils the need of my Muslim brother and I begin with his name?\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20434","(20428) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us, that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us, that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that my father Isḥāq ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us in Baghdad, that al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, that Abū al-Ashʿath narrated to us, that Sulaym ibn Akhḍar informed us, that Ibn ʿAwn narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, who said: \They mentioned in the presence of Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — that a man had written: 'In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful — to so-and-so.' So Ibn ʿUmar said: 'Stop! The names of Allah are for Him alone.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20435","(20429) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us, that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us, that Ḥanbal narrated, that Surayj narrated, that Ḥammād ibn Salamah said: Ḥumayd said, and Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh used to say: \Write: 'In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful — to so-and-so son of so-and-so","' and do not write: 'To so-and-so son of so-and-so.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20436","(20430) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bashrān informed us, that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtban, from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Hiraql, the great ruler of Rome: \Peace be upon whoever follows true guidance.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Razzāq said: \""And Ibn ʿAbbās did not go beyond this wording in this place.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"20437","(20431) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us, that my grandfather narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtban, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — that he informed him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Qayṣar, calling him to Islam, and dispatched his letter to him with Dihyah al-Kalbī. He mentioned the hadith, and in it he said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Abū Sufyān informed me","\"" and he mentioned the hadith regarding Hiraql being sent for"," his entering upon him"," and his questioning about him. Abū Sufyān said: \""Then he called for the letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ordered it to be read. And in it was: 'In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful — from Muḥammad"," the servant of Allah and His Messenger"," to Hiraql"," the great ruler of Rome. Peace be upon whoever follows true guidance. To proceed…'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah"," and Muslim likewise narrated it as previously mentioned.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"20438","(20432) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī informed us in al-Kūfah, that Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn narrated to us, that Abū Ghassān narrated to us, that Zuhayr narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, that Ibrāhīm ibn Sharīk narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, that Zuhayr narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who said: I heard Anas — may Allah be pleased with him — saying: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the Anṣār to write a document for them regarding al-Baḥrayn. They said: 'No"," by Allah — not until you write something similar for our brothers from Quraysh.' He said: 'That is for them — whatever Allah wills.' They kept saying that to him. So he said: 'You will see after me preferential treatment (atharah). Be patient until you meet me.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"20439","(20433) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshāẓ al-ʿAdl informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed them that Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī narrated to them, that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated, who said: \Anas ibn Mālik — may Allah be pleased with him — came to us in al-Madīnah and narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had granted the Anṣār al-Baḥrayn and intended to write a document for them regarding it. They said: 'No — not until you give our brothers from Quraysh the same.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You will see after me preferential treatment (atharah). Be patient until you meet me.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"20440","(20434) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us, that Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us, that ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, that al-Ḥārith ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, that Isrāʾīl narrated from ʿUthmān al-Shaḥḥām, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the story of the man who struck his wife dead for insulting the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \When it was the evening"," she mentioned you and insulted you"," and I could not restrain myself — I rose to the pickaxe"," placed it upon her belly and killed her.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Bear witness that her blood is of no consequence (hadar).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously referenced as no. 7/13375.]"""
"20441","(20435) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Khalīfah informed us; Musaddad narrated to us; Abū ʿAwwānah narrated from Saʿīd ibn Masrūq from ʿAbāyah ibn Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj from his grandfather Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah when the people were afflicted with hunger. We obtained camels and sheep. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was among the rear of the people. They hastened and slaughtered the animals and set up the cooking pots. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came to them and ordered that the cooking pots be overturned. He then divided the spoils and made a fair apportionment, equating ten sheep to one camel. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl and others from Abū ʿAwwānah, and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim transmitted it through other chains from Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"20442","(20436) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf informed us; my father narrated to us; Abū Kurayb and Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān both said: Abū Usāmah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Burdah ibn Abī Mūsā narrated to me from his grandfather Abī Burdah from Abū Mūsā, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"," the Ashʿarīs"," when they are in hardship during military expedition and the provisions of their families in Madīnah become scarce"," they gather whatever they have into a single cloth and then divide it equally among themselves from a single vessel. They are from me"," and I am from them.\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20443","(20437) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Bushayr ibn Yasār, the freedman of the Anṣār, from some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, conquered Khaybar, he divided it into thirty-six shares, each share comprising one hundred portions. Half of that was for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and the Muslims, and he set aside the remaining half for the delegations who came, for affairs, and for the needs of the people. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20444","(20438) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Bushayr ibn Yasār that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, divided Khaybar into thirty-six shares. Eighteen shares were for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, on account of the rights and affairs of the people that devolved upon him, and eighteen shares he distributed, gathering eighteen men, each man being counted as equivalent to one hundred men. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously mentioned]"
"20445","(20439) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Ḥazm narrated to me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Miknaf, the brother of Banū Ḥārithah, who said: When ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, expelled the Jews of Khaybar, he rode forth with the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār. With him went Jabbār ibn Ṣakhr ibn Khansāʾ, one of Banū Salamah, who was the estimator and assessor of the people of Madīnah, along with Zayd ibn Thābit. The two of them divided Khaybar among its people according to the original basis of the shares that had been established. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20446","(20440) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq al-Saylaḥīnī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Lahīʿah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar from ʿAmr ibn al-Aswad from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The Hand of Allah is with the judge when he judges"," and the Hand of Allah is with the one who divides when he divides.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20447","(20441) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy upon him, reported as a narration from Abī Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ from Mūsā ibn Ṭarīf al-Asadī, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, entered the public treasury and expressed displeasure with it, saying: \I shall not remain in the evening while there is a single dirham remaining in it.\"" He ordered a man from Banū Asad to distribute it throughout the night. The people said: \""If only you had compensated him.\"" He said: \""If he wishes"," but it is unlawful (suḥt).\"" Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""It is not permissible for anyone to give unlawful earnings"," just as it is not permissible for anyone to take them. And we do not consider ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," to have given anything that he deemed unlawful"," if Allah wills.\"" The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: Its chain of narration is weak. Mūsā ibn Ṭarīf is not used as a basis for proof. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20448","(20442) And it was narrated from him from his father from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, as Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ from Mūsā ibn Ṭarīf from his father that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, distributed something and called a man to calculate. It was said: \If only you had given him something.\"" He said: \""If he wishes"," though it is unlawful (suḥt).\"" [Ḍaʿīf — as previously mentioned]"""
"20449","(20443) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh; Isḥāq ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated to me from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Among the rulings of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, is that he decreed: \There shall be no harm nor reciprocal harm.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"20450","(20444) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Najīd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī from his father that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \There shall be no harm nor reciprocal harm.\"" This is a mursal narration"," and we have narrated it in the Book of Reconciliation (al-Ṣulḥ) in a connected (mawṣūl) form. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"20451","(20445) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us: al-Aḥwaṣ ibn Jawāb Abū al-Jawāb narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Juʿfī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, from a freedwoman of his, who heard Abū Ṣirmah narrate that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever causes harm"," Allah will cause him harm"," and whoever makes things difficult"," Allah will make things difficult for him.\"" [Weak]"""
"20452","(20446) Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said in the older recension: Ibn Jurayj narrated from Ṣudayq ibn Mūsā, and he mentioned the hadith that Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Riyāḥī narrated to us: Rūḥ narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Ṣudayq ibn Mūsā informed me, from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr, meaning Ibn Ḥazm, from his father, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \There shall be no dismemberment (ʿaḍīyah) regarding inheritance except that which the division can accommodate.\"" He said: \""That is"," do not break up the inheritance into fragments for the heirs.\"" [Weak]"""
"20453","(20447) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿUbayd said regarding the hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ): \There shall be no dismemberment (ʿaḍīyah) in inheritance except that which the division can accommodate.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: Ḥajjāj narrated to me from Ibn Jurayj"," from Ṣudayq ibn Mūsā"," from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm"," from his father"," who raised it (to the Prophet). Abū ʿUbayd said: His statement \""There shall be no dismemberment in inheritance\"" means that a person dies and leaves something which"," if divided among his heirs when some of them request division"," would result in harm to them or to some of them. He said: \""So it should not be divided.\"" Al-taʿḍīyah means fragmentation"," and it is derived from al-iʿḍāʾ. It is said: \""I ʿaḍaytu the meat\"" when I cut it into pieces. Al-Zaʿfarānī said: Al-Shāfiʿī said in the older recension: \""A hadith such as this cannot be used as a proof because it is weak.\"" This is the view of all the jurists we have met. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It is deemed weak only due to its discontinuity"," and this is the view of the majority.\"" [Weak]"""
"20454","(20448) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Kaʿb narrated to us: ʪsā narrated from Thawr, from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, from Nuṣayr, the freedman of Muʿāwiyah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the division that causes harm.\"" The Shaykh Aḥmad (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""This is a mursal hadith.\"" [Weak]"""
"20455","(20449) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Oppression (ẓulm) will be darknesses (ẓulumāt) on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus"," and he also reported it through another chain from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. [Authentic. Agreed upon.]"""
"20456","(20450) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us orally: Abū al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Sakan both said: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Miqsam, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Beware of oppression"," for oppression will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of miserliness (shuḥḥ)"," for miserliness destroyed those who came before you; it led them to shed their blood and make lawful their sacred prohibitions.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Authentic. Muslim 2578.]"""
"20457","(20451) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān al-Muqriʾ in Baghdad narrated to us: Abū Qilābah narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: ʿImrān al-Qaṭṭān narrated from al-Shaybānī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Awfā, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," Allah is with the judge as long as he does not commit injustice. But when he commits injustice"," Allah disassociates Himself from him and the Shayṭān attaches himself to him.\"" [Weak]"""
"20458","(20452) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Musaddad narrated — (ḥ) and ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: my father narrated to us — both said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I strongly urge you regarding the rights of the two weak ones: the orphan and the woman.\"" ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-ʿUmarī narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) in a mursal narration that when he appointed ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) over Yemen"," he said to him: \""Give precedence to the lowly over the noble"," and give precedence to the weak over the strong.\"" [Fair]"""
"20459","(20453) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us: Shuʿbah and Misʿar narrated from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm, from al-Ḥakam ibn Mināʾ, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said: I heard ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) — and one of my fingers was in this wound of his or that one — saying: \O company of Muslims"," I do not fear the people for you; rather"," I fear you for the people. I have left among you two things by which you will not cease to be in goodness so long as you adhere to them: justice in judgment and justice in distribution. And I have left you upon a path like the grazing ground of the flock"," except that a people may deviate and be led astray with them.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20460","(20454) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn al-Muhallab Abū Kudaynah narrated from Ibn ʿAwn, from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: Abū ʿUbaydah ibn Ḥudhayfah was a judge. A man of nobility came to him while he was lighting a fire, and he asked him for a need. Ibn Ḥudhayfah said to him: \Shall I ask you to put your finger in this fire?\"" He said: \""Subḥān Allāh!\"" He said: \""Are you miserly with me regarding one of your fingers in this fire"," yet you ask me to consign my body — or he said"," all of it — to the Fire of Jahannam?\"" [Weak]"""
"20461","(20455) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us in Baghdad, that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār related to us, that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr related to us, that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, that Maʿmar related from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The people are like a hundred camels — a man will not find among them a mount (rāḥilah) suitable for riding.\"" Muslim narrated this in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and al-Bukhārī also reported it through another chain from al-Zuhrī.\n\nThis hadith may be interpreted to mean that the people are equal in the rulings of the religion — there is no distinction therein of a noble over a non-noble"," nor of a person of high standing over one of low standing"," just as among a hundred camels there is no rāḥilah — that is"," the tractable camel that is saddled and ridden — the word jāʾat being used in the active form (fāʿilah) with the meaning of the passive (mafʿūlah).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20462","(20456) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Bakr related to us, that Abū Dāwūd related to us, that Aḥmad ibn Munīʿ related to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak related to us, that Muṣʿab ibn Thābit related from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed that the two disputing parties should sit before the judge (ḥākim).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20463","(20457) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār related to us, that Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Muʾaddib related to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Muqriʾ related to us, that Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah, Abū Khaythamah, related from ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr, that he related to me, that ʿAbd Allāh related from ʬāʾ ibn Yasār, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever is afflicted with the task of judging between the Muslims"," let them be just between them in their glance (laḥẓ)"," their gesture (ishārah)"," and their seating (maqʿad).\""\n\nZayd ibn Abī al-Zarqāʾ narrated it from ʿAbbād"," from Abī ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAnzī"," with his chain"," and said: \""in their gesture"," their glance"," and their speech (kalām).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20464","(20458) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ related to us, that Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Ismāʿīl al-Maḥāmilī related to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr related to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr related to us, that Zuhayr related from ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr, from Abī ʿAbd Allāh, from ʬāʾ ibn Yasār, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever is afflicted with the task of judging between the people"," let them be just between them in their glance"," their gesture"," and their seating.\"""""
"20465","(20459) And through it, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever is afflicted with the task of judging between the people"," let them not raise their voice upon one of the two disputing parties more than they raise it upon the other.\"" This chain contains weakness.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20466","(20460) And reliance is placed on what Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh related to us by dictation and recitation, that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Bazzāz related to us, that Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī related to us, that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah related from Idrīs al-Awdī, who said: Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah brought out a document to us and said: \This is the letter of ʿUmar to Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with them both): 'To proceed: Verily"," judging (qaḍāʾ) is a binding obligation (farīḍah) and a followed practice (sunnah). Understand"," when the case is presented to you"," for a word of truth is of no benefit if it is not implemented. Be equitable among the people in your countenance"," your assembly"," and your justice"," so that no noble person may hope for your partiality (ḥayf)"," and no weak person may fear your injustice (jawr).'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — previously cited under no. 20283]"""
"20467","(20461) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh related to us, that Aḥmad ibn Najdah related to us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr related to us, that my father related to us, that ʿUbayd Allāh related from Yazīd ibn Rūmān, who said: ʿUmar wrote to Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with them both): \The people will continue to fulfill their obligations toward the Imam as long as the Imam fulfills his obligations toward Allah. When the Imam grazes (i.e."," lives in ease)"," the flock will graze. And it is near that the people will develop resentment toward their rulers. I seek refuge in Allah that rancor carried (ḍaghāʾin maḥmūlah)"," followed desires (ahwāʾ muttabaʿah)"," and a preferred worldly life (dunyā muʾtharah) should overtake me and you. Establish the truth"," even if only for a single hour of the day.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20468","(20462) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah and Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ both informed us, that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Najdah related to us, that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr related to us, that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh related from Abī Rāwāḥah, Yazīd ibn Ayham, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to the people: \Make the people equal before you in the truth — their near one as their far one"," and their far one as their near one. Beware of bribery (rishā)"," judgment by desire (ḥukm bil-hawā)"," and taking people at the time of anger. Establish the truth"," even if only for a single hour of the day.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20469","(20463) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Najdah al-Qurashī related to us, that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr related to us, that Hushaym related to us, that Sayyār related to us, that al-Shaʿbī related, who said: There was a dispute between ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding something. Ubayy made a claim against ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and ʿUmar denied it. So they appointed Zayd ibn Thābit as arbiter between them. They came to him at his home, and when they entered upon him, ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \We have come to you so that you may judge between us"," and in the judge's own home"," the judge is to be given honor.\"" So Zayd made room for him at the head of his bed and said: \""Here"," O Commander of the Faithful.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""You have been bold in giving legal opinion (fatwā). Rather"," I shall sit alongside my adversary.\"" So they both sat before him. Ubayy made his claim"," and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) denied it. Zayd said to Ubayy: \""Relieve the Commander of the Faithful of the oath — I would not ask it of anyone other than him.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) took the oath. Then Zayd swore that Zayd ibn Thābit would not render judgment until ʿUmar and an ordinary man of the Muslims were equal before him.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20470","(20464) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī related to us, that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr related to us, that Abū Muʿāwiyah related from al-Aʿmash, from Tamīm ibn Salamah, who said: Ibn Abī ʿUṣayfīr came to Shurayḥ disputing with a man, and he sat with him on the cushion (ṭinfisah). Shurayḥ said to him: \Rise and sit with your adversary"," for your sitting here arouses suspicion.\"" Ibn Abī ʿUṣayfīr became angry"," so Shurayḥ said to him: \""Rise and sit with your adversary! I will not abandon victory (nuṣrah) while I am capable of it.\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"20471","(20465) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz narrated to us that Asīd ibn Zayd al-Jammāl narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Shamr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn al-Khurāsānī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Abī Hārūn narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Shamr narrated from Jābir from al-Shaʿbī, who said:\n\nʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, went out to the market and there he saw a Christian selling a coat of mail. ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, recognized the coat of mail and said: \This is my coat of mail; between you and me is the judge of the Muslims.\"" He said: The judge of the Muslims was Sharīḥ"," whom ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," had appointed as judge. When Sharīḥ saw the Commander of the Faithful"," he rose from his seat of judgment and seated ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in his own seat"," and Sharīḥ sat before him beside the Christian. ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to him: \""O Sharīḥ"," were my adversary a Muslim"," I would sit with him in the seat of the litigant"," but I heard the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," say: 'Do not shake hands with them"," do not initiate the greeting of peace with them"," do not visit their sick"," do not pray over their dead"," confine them to the narrow paths"," and belittle them as Allah has belittle them.' Judge between me and him"," O Sharīḥ.\"" Sharīḥ said: \""Speak"," O Commander of the Faithful.\"" ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""This is my coat of mail; it went missing from me some time ago.\"" Sharīḥ said: \""What do you say"," O Christian?\"" The Christian said: \""I do not call the Commander of the Faithful a liar"," but the coat of mail is my coat of mail.\"" Sharīḥ said: \""I do not see that it should be taken from his hand. Do you have any proof?\"" ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Sharīḥ has spoken the truth.\"" The Christian said: \""As for me"," I bear witness that these are the judgments of the prophets. The Commander of the Faithful comes to his judge"," and his judge rules against him. By Allah"," O Commander of the Faithful"," this is your coat of mail. I purchased it from the army. It had fallen from your grey camel and I took it. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah.\"" ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Now that you have embraced Islam"," it is yours.\"" And he mounted him on a noble horse. Al-Shaʿbī said: \""I later saw him fighting the polytheists.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Zakariyyā. In the narration of Ibn ʿAbdān"," he said: \""O Sharīḥ"," were my adversary not a Christian"," I would have sat before you on my knees.\"" And at the end of it he said: ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," gifted it to him"," assigned him a stipend of two thousand"," and he was martyred alongside him on the day of Ṣiffīn. The remainder is to the same meaning. It has also been narrated from another weak chain from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī.\n\n[Very weak]\n\n---"""
"20472","(20466) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ḥusayn ibn Ḥasan ibn Muhājir narrated to us that Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī narrated to us that Ibn Wahb narrated to us that Ḥarmalah al-Miṣrī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shumāsah said:\n\nI came to ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, to ask her about something. She said: \Where are you from?\"" I said: \""A man from the people of Egypt.\"" She said: \""I shall tell you what I heard the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings upon him"," say in this house of mine: 'O Allah"," whoever is given charge of any affair of my Ummah and makes it difficult for them"," then make it difficult for him. And whoever is given charge of any affair of my Ummah and is gentle with them"," then be gentle with him.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1828]\n\n---"""
"20473","(20467) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us that Zuhayr narrated to us that Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir, who said:\n\nTwo young men fought, one from the Muhājirūn and one from the Anṣār. The Muhājir called out: \O Muhājirūn!\"" and the Anṣārī called out: \""O Anṣār!\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings upon him"," came out and said: \""What is this"," the call of the Jāhiliyyah?\"" They said: \""No"," O Messenger of Allah"," except that two young men fought and one of them struck the other on the backside.\"" He said: \""No harm. Let a man support his brother whether he is wrongdoer or wronged. If he is a wrongdoer"," let him restrain him"," for that is support for him\"" — or words to that effect — \""and if he is wronged"," then let him support him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]\n\n---"""
"20474","(20468) Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh al-Fāmī in Baghdad, in the Mosque of al-Ruṣāfah, narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Abū ʿAwanah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil from his father Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nI was with the Prophet, peace and blessings upon him, when two men came to him disputing. One of them said: \This man seized my land during the Jāhiliyyah.\"" He was Imruʾ al-Qays ibn ʿĀbis al-Kindī"," and his opponent was Rabīʿah. The other said: \""It is my land; I cultivate it.\"" The Prophet"," peace and blessings upon him"," said: \""Do you have proof?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then you have his oath.\"" He said: \""He does not care what he swears to.\"" He said: \""You have nothing but that.\"" When he went to take the oath"," the Prophet"," peace and blessings upon him"," said: \""If he swears falsely regarding his wealth"," he will surely meet Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," while He is angry with him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Abū al-Walīd.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: And Rabīʿah is Ibn ʿAydān"," with a fatḥah on the ʿayn and a yāʾ with two dots beneath it. It is also said Ibn ʿAbdān"," with a kasrah on the ʿayn and a bāʾ with one dot beneath it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 139]\n\n---"""
"20475","(20469) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Shawdhab al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us there that Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī narrated from Zāʾidah from Simāk from Ḥanash from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings upon him, said: \When two men come to you disputing"," do not judge in favor of the first until you hear the words of the other. You will then see how to judge.\"" He said: \""After that I continued as a judge.\""\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"""
"20476","(20470) And a narration has been reported on this matter with a chain containing weakness. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Shawdhab al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us that Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishr narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim narrated from al-Ḥasan, who said:\n\nA man came as a guest to ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was in Kūfah. Then his opponent came. ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: \Are you the opponent?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then move away"," for the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings upon him"," forbade us from hosting a litigant unless his opponent is with him.\""\n\nAbū Muʿāwiyah and others corroborated it from Ismāʿīl with the same meaning"," thus.\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"""
"20477","(20471) And the Sharīf Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shurayḥī narrated to us that Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us that Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim from al-Ḥasan, who said:\n\nA man narrated to me who had been a guest of ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, in Kūfah. He stayed with him for some days, then he mentioned a dispute he had. ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: \Move away from my house"," for the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings upon him"," forbade that a litigant be hosted unless his opponent is with him.\""\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"""
"20478","(20472) And I read in the book of Ibn Khuzaymah from Mūsā ibn Sahl al-Ramlī from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Ramlī from al-Qāsim ibn Ghuṣn from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind from Abī Ḥarb ibn al-Aswad al-Dīlī from his father from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nThe Prophet, peace and blessings upon him, would not host a litigant unless his opponent was with him.\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"
"20479","(20473) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed me that ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us that Abū al-Yamān informed me that Shuʿayb informed me from al-Zuhrī, who informed me that ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me from Abū Ḥumayd al-Anṣārī, then al-Sāʿidī, who informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings upon him, appointed an agent over the charity. When the agent finished his work, he came and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," this is what is yours"," and this is what was given to me as a gift.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings upon him"," said: \""Why did you not sit in your father's and mother's house and see whether gifts would be given to you or not?\"" Then the Prophet"," peace and blessings upon him"," stood on the pulpit in the evening after the prayer"," praised and extolled Allah as He deserves"," and then said: \""To proceed: What is the matter with the agent whom we appoint? He comes to us and says: 'This is from your work"," and this is what was given to me as a gift.' Why did he not sit in his father's and mother's house and see whether gifts would be given to him or not? By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad"," none of you will take anything of it without bringing it on the Day of Resurrection"," carrying it on his neck. If it is a camel"," he will bring it with its grunting; if it is a cow"," he will bring it with its lowing; if it is a sheep"," he will bring it with its bleating. I have conveyed.\"" Abū Ḥumayd said: \""Then the Prophet"," peace and blessings upon him"," raised his hands until we could see the whiteness of his armpits.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]\n\nAbū Ḥumayd said: \""Zayd ibn Thābit also heard that from the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings upon him"," along with me"," so ask him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān.\n\n---"""
"20480","(20474) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Maʿmar and Dāwūd ibn Rushayd both said: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from ʿUrwah from Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings upon him, said: \The gifts given to rulers are ghulūl (embezzlement).\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"20481","(20475) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī narrated to us that ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Qays from ʿAdī ibn ʿUmayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \O people"," whoever is appointed by us to a task and conceals from us even a needle"," he shall come with it on the Day of Resurrection.\"" A man from the Anṣār stood up — as though I could see him — and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," accept my resignation from your service.\"" He said: \""What is the matter with you?\"" He said: \""I heard you say what you said.\"" He said: \""And I say it now: whomever we appoint to a task"," let him bring the little and the much of it; whatever is given to him"," he may take"," and whatever he is forbidden from"," he should abstain.\"" Muslim narrated this in his Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1833]"""
"20482","(20476) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū Umayyah al-Ṭarsūsī narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Abū Ziyād al-Fuqaymī narrated to me that Abū Ḥarīz narrated: A man used to send as a gift to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) every year a thigh of a camel. He came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) to litigate, and said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," judge between us with a decisive judgment"," just as the thigh is separated from the camel.\"" So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to his governors: \""Do not accept gifts"," for they are a form of bribery.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20483","(20477) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Aṣbugh ibn al-Faraj al-Miṣrī narrated to us that my father informed me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us that Mālik said: A man from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who was one of the governors of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), sent two cushions as a gift to the wife of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him). ʿUmar entered and saw them and said: \Where did you get these two? Tell me"," and do not lie to me.\"" She said: \""So-and-so sent them to me.\"" He said: \""May Allah destroy so-and-so! When he wants something and cannot obtain it through me"," he comes to me through my family.\"" He then pulled them out forcefully from beneath whoever was sitting on them"," and went out carrying them. His slave-girl followed him and said: \""Their wool belongs to us.\"" So he tore them apart"," threw the wool to her"," and went out with them. He gave one of them to a woman from the Muhājirāt and the other to a woman from the Anṣār. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20484","(20478) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to me that my uncle al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the one who offers a bribe and the one who accepts it. [Ḥasan]"
"20485","(20479) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us that ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us that ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Manṣūr from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Masrūq, who said: I asked ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, about suḥt (unlawful gain), and he said: \It is bribery (rishwah).\"" And I asked him about injustice (jawr) in judgment"," and he said: \""That is disbelief (kufr).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20486","(20480) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us that Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Fiṭr ibn Khalīfah narrated from Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Masrūq, who said: ʿAbd Allāh was asked about suḥt, and he said: \It is bribery in judgment.\"" He was asked about judgment"," and ʿAbd Allāh said: \""That is disbelief.\"" And he recited this verse: {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed — it is they who are the disbelievers} [al-Māʾidah: 44]. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20487","(20481) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from ʿAmmār al-Duhnī from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Masrūq, who said: I asked Ibn Masʿūd about suḥt — is it bribery in judgment? He said: \No. And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed — it is they who are the disbelievers"," the wrongdoers"," and the transgressors. Rather"," suḥt is that a man seeks your help against an injustice done to him"," and he gives you a gift"," and you accept it — that is suḥt.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20488","(20482) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Zayd ibn al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī — and he was among the righteous — narrated to us that Wakīʿ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿUmays narrated from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) that when he arrived in the land of Abyssinia, he took something and was held accountable for it. He gave two dīnārs until he was released. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20489","(20483) Ibn al-Faḍl informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Zayd narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd from his father from Wahb ibn Munabbih, who said: The bribery in which the one who offers it sins is not that one bribes to protect his wealth or his life — he is not sinful in that. Rather, the bribery in which one sins is that one bribes in order to be given what is not one's right. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20490","(20484) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ said: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Qurqūb al-Tammār in Hamadhān informed me that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us that Abū al-Yamān informed us that Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab informed me that Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \A group from my Ummah shall enter Paradise — they are seventy thousand"," their faces shining like the light of the moon.\"" Then ʿUkkāshah ibn Miḥsan al-Asadī stood up"," raising a cloak upon him"," and said: \""Supplicate for me"," O Messenger of Allah"," that He make me among them.\"" He said: \""O Allah"," make him among them.\"" Then a man from the Anṣār stood up and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," supplicate to Allah that He make me among them.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""ʿUkkāshah has preceded you in this.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and both he and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yūnus from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20491","(20485) And in what Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us, Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Dāwudī narrated to us, Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Ḥayyān narrated from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is called to one of the judges and does not respond"," he is an oppressor.\"" This is a mursal hadith. [Weak]"""
"20492","(20486) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhb al-Wāsiṭī informed us, Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated from Ḥātim ibn Abī Ṣaghīrah from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Ḥanash ibn al-Muʿtamir from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to Yemen, and I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you are sending me to a people to judge between them"," and I am young in age and have no knowledge of judging.\"" He said to me: \""O ʿAlī"," when one of the two disputants comes to you and you hear from him"," do not rule in his favor until you hear from the other as you heard from the first"," for then the judgment will become clear to you.\"" He said: \""So I continued to be a judge.\"" This is in the narration of Ḥātim ibn Abī Ṣaghīrah. [Weak]"""
"20493","(20487) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us in the Sunan of Abī Dāwūd, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn informed us, Sharīk narrated from Simāk from Ḥanash from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to Yemen as a judge, and I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you are sending me while I am young in age and have no knowledge of judging.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," Allah"," exalted be His praise"," will guide your heart and make your tongue firm. When the two disputants sit before you"," do not judge until you hear from the other as you heard from the first"," for that is more likely to make the judgment clear to you.\"" He said: \""So I continued to be a judge"," or I never doubted in any judgment thereafter.\""\n\nThis pertains to the situation where both disputants are present together"," and it is in this meaning that others narrated it besides Sharīk. [Weak]"""
"20494","(20488) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Sharīk, Zāʾidah, and Sulaymān ibn Muʿādh said: Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated to us from Ḥanash ibn al-Muʿtamir from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to Yemen, I said: \You are sending me while I am young in age and have no knowledge of much of judging.\"" He said to me: \""When the two disputants come to you"," do not rule for the first until you hear what the other says"," for when you hear what the other says"," you will know how to judge. Indeed"," Allah will make your tongue firm and guide your heart.\"" ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""So I continued to be a judge thereafter.\"" [Weak]"""
"20495","(20489) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, Sufyān narrated from Hishām.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm informed me, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Hind, the mother of Muʿāwiyah, came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \Abū Sufyān is a stingy man"," and he does not give me what suffices me and my children except what I take from him without his knowledge. Is there any sin upon me in that?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to her: \""Take what suffices you and your children in a reasonable manner.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"20496","(20490) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Dīnār from his father: That a man from Juhaynah used to buy riding camels, inflate their prices, and then travel swiftly, outpacing the pilgrims. He became bankrupt, and his matter was raised to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: \To proceed"," O people: Indeed"," al-Usayfiʿ"," the Usayfiʿ of Juhaynah"," was content with his religion and trustworthiness that it be said he outpaced the pilgrims"," except that he incurred debt openly and became overwhelmed. So whoever has a claim of debt against him"," let us come in the morning so that we may divide his wealth among his creditors.\"" [Weak]"""
"20497","(20491) The noble Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shuḥayb informed us, Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, Sharīk narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbaydullāh from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a false witness. He stood him before the people from day until night, saying: \This is so-and-so who testifies falsely"," so recognize him.\"" Then he imprisoned him.\n\nAnd Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated it from Sharīk from ʿĀṣim"," and added: \""Then he flogged him and stood him before the people.\"" [Weak]"""
"20498","(20492) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, ʿAṭāʾ ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Abī Naḍrah from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him): That he caught a false witness and struck him eleven lashes, then said: \Do not imprison the people on account of false witnesses"," for we do not accept from witnesses except those who are just.\"" [Weak]"""
"20499","(20493) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Abī Bakr from Makhūl and ʬīyah ibn Qays: That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) flogged a false witness forty lashes, blackened his face, and paraded him around Madinah. [Weak]"
"20500","(20494) He said: And Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū Shihāb narrated from Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh from Makhūl: That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to his governors in the districts of Shām regarding the false witness: that he should be flogged forty lashes, his head should be shaved, his face should be blackened, he should be paraded, and his imprisonment should be prolonged.\n\nThese two narrations are weak and disconnected. The first two narrations are connected (mawṣūlah), except that in each one of them there is someone who cannot be used as a proof. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd we have narrated in the book of Ḥudūd the authentic hadith from Abū Burdah ibn Niyār from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \He shall not be flogged more than ten lashes except in one of the prescribed punishments of Allah.\"" Adhering to this is more appropriate"," and with Allah lies success. [Weak]"""
"20501","(20495) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us — Abū al-Azhar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yāmīn, who said: I heard ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn saying: ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) would, when he apprehended a false witness, send him to his tribe and say: \This is a false witness"," so recognize him and make him known.\"" Then he would release him.\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I asked ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn"," \""Was there any beating involved?\"" He replied"," \""No.\"" And this narration is also discontinued (munqaṭiʿ). [Weak (ḍaʿīf)]"""
"20502","(20496) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us — Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Jaʿd ibn Dhakwān, who said: Shurayḥ was brought a false witness, so he removed his turban, struck him several blows, and made him known to the people of the mosque. (Ḥasan)"
"20503","(20497) And with his chain of narration, he said: Sufyān narrated from Abī Ḥaṣīn that Shurayḥ used to be brought a false witness, so he would parade him among the people of his mosque and his market, saying: \We have declared this man's testimony to be false.\"" (Ḥasan)"""
"20504","(20498) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī and Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Naṣr both said: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā), who said: Hind bint ʿUtbah, the wife of Abū Sufyān, came to the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," my husband Abū Sufyān is a stingy man who does not give me enough maintenance for myself and my children"," except what I take from his wealth without his knowledge. Is there any sin upon me for that?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \""Take what is reasonable (bil-maʿrūf)"," enough for you and your children.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr"," and al-Bukhārī reported it from another route from Hishām. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ) — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20505","(20499) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Tamtām narrated to us — ʿAffān narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to me — ʿAbd al-Malik Abū Jaʿfar narrated from Abū Naḍrah, from Saʿd ibn al-Aṭwal, who said: His brother died and left three hundred dirhems and dependents. He said: \I wanted to spend it on his dependents.\"" The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \""Your brother is detained by his debt"," so pay it on his behalf.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have paid it except for two dinars — a woman claims them"," but she has no proof.\"" He said: \""Give them to her"," for she is truthful (muḥiqqah).\""\n\nThe wording is that of ʿAffān's ḥadīth. In the narration of ʿAbd al-Wāḥid"," it reads: \""Give them to her"," for she is truthful (ṣādiqah).\"" [Weak (ḍaʿīf)]"""
"20506","(20500) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan narrated to us — Yūsuf narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Saʿīd al-Jurayrī, from Abū Naḍrah, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), with the same meaning, except that he did not specify how much the deceased had left. [Weak (ḍaʿīf)]"
"20507","(20501) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā), the wife of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), that she informed him: Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), sent a message to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) asking him about her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) — from what Allah had granted him in al-Madīnah, from Fadak, and from the remainder of the khums of Khaybar. Abū Bakr (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) said: \The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: 'We are not inherited from; whatever we leave is charity (ṣadaqah). The family of Muḥammad may only eat from this wealth.' By Allah"," I shall not change anything from the charity of the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) from the state it was in during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam)"," and I shall act in it as the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) acted.\"" And Abū Bakr refused to give anything from it to Fāṭimah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā)"," and he mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim reported it from another route from al-Layth. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ) — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20508","(20502) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Maslamah, narrated from Mālik, from Hishām, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah, from Umm Salamah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā), that the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \I am but a human being"," and you bring your disputes to me. Perhaps some of you may be more eloquent in his argument than others. I judge according to what I hear. So whomever I rule in favor of his brother's right — let him not take it"," for I am only cutting out for him a piece of the Fire.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah"," and Muslim reported it from another route from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. This applies to cases where no prior knowledge of the matter had reached him. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ) — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20509","(20503) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed me — both said: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us — Abū al-Yamān informed us — Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī — ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Abī Salamah and her mother, Umm Salamah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā), the wife of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), informed him that her mother, Umm Salamah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā), said: \The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) heard the clamor of a dispute at his door"," so he went out to them and said: 'I am but a human being. A disputant comes to me"," and perhaps some of you may be more articulate than others. I may rule in his favor based on what I hear"," thinking him to be truthful. So whomever I rule in favor of a Muslim's right — it is but a piece of the Fire. Let him take it or leave it.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim reported it from other routes from al-Zuhrī. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ) — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20510","(20504) The Faqīh Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Fāmī in Baghdād informed us — Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us — Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Simāk, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil, from his father, who said: A man from Ḥaḍramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam). The Ḥaḍramī said: \O Messenger of Allah"," this man has seized my land — it belonged to my father.\"" The Kindī said: \""It is my land; I cultivate it. He has no right to it.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said to the Ḥaḍramī: \""Do you have proof (bayyinah)?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then you have his oath.\"" He said: \""O Prophet of Allah"," he does not care what he swears upon; he does not abstain from anything.\"" He said: \""You have nothing but that.\"" So he went with him to have him swear the oath. The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said as he turned away: \""Beware — if he swears an oath to take wealth unjustly"," he shall meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He turns away from him.\""\n\nThus did I find it in my book"," and thus did I find it in the book of Muslim from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," from Abū al-Walīd"," from Abū ʿAwānah"," from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr"," from ʿAlqamah.\n\nAnd ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī"," Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn"," and Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Kajjī and others narrated from Abū al-Walīd"," and they said in the ḥadīth: \""You have nothing but that from it.\"" And likewise Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and others narrated from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ: \""You have nothing but that from it.\""\n\nThis does not negate ruling based on knowledge; rather"," it negates that the claimant has any recourse other than the oath. And Allah knows best. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ) — Muslim (139)]"""
"20511","(20505) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Ashbahani informed us — Abu Nasr al-Iraqi narrated to us — Sufyan ibn Muhammad narrated to us — Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us — Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from Ibn Abi Dhi'b — from al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Were I to find a man upon one of the prescribed punishments of Allah"," I would not carry it out upon him myself"," nor would I call upon anyone for assistance"," until there be with me other than myself.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20512","(20506) He said, and Sufyan narrated from Abd al-Karim — from Ikrimah: that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf: \What do you think — if you were to see a man who had committed murder"," or theft"," or adultery?\"" He replied: \""I consider your testimony to be like the testimony of any Muslim.\"" He said: \""You have spoken correctly.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20513","(20507) He said, and Sufyan narrated from Ja'far — from his father — from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I would not be the first of the four.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20514","(20508) He said, and Sufyan narrated to me — Ibn Shubrumah, who said: I asked al-Sha'bi about a man who had been a witness and was then appointed as a judge. He said: \Shurayh was brought regarding this matter"," and he said: 'Bring the governor"," and I will bear witness for you.'\"" And these narrations are interrupted (munqati')"," except for the narration of Shurayh. [Sahih]"""
"20515","(20509) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us — Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab informed us — Ja'far ibn Awn informed us — Mis'ar narrated from Abu Husayn, who said: Shurayh said: \Judgement is an ember — remove the ember from yourself with two sticks.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20516","(20510) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Mihran narrated to us — Ali ibn al-Ja'd informed us — Shu'bah narrated from Sayyar, who said: I heard al-Sha'bi say: There was a dispute between Umar and Ubayy, may Allah be pleased with both of them. Umar said: \Appoint a man to judge between us.\"" So they appointed Zayd ibn Thabit as arbiter between them. The narrator said: They came to him. Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""We have come to you that you may judge between us"," for in his house the judge is given authority.\"" So when they entered upon him"," he seated him with him upon the head of his bed. He said: \""This is the first injustice you have committed in your ruling — seat me and my adversary in a single sitting.\"" The narrator said: So they presented their case to him. Zayd said to Ubayy: \""The oath is upon the Commander of the Faithful; if you wish"," you may pardon him.\"" So Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," swore an oath upon that"," and then swore to him: \""You shall not reach the door of judgement so long as I possess any virtue over anyone in your estimation.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20517","(20511) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated — al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated from Yazid ibn al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh — from his father — from his grandfather Shurayh — from his father Hani': When he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he arrived in Madinah and heard them calling him \Abu al-Hakam.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: \""Allah is al-Hakam (the Judge)"," and to Him belongs judgement. Why are you called Abu al-Hakam?\"" He said: \""When my people disagreed on a matter"," they would come to me and I would judge between them"," and both parties would be pleased.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""How excellent is this! Do you have any children?\"" He said: \""I have Shurayh"," Muslim"," and Abd Allah.\"" He asked: \""Who is the eldest among them?\"" I said: \""Shurayh.\"" He said: \""Then you are Abu Shurayh.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20518","(20512) Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Razzaz in Baghdad informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafi'i narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Jahm al-Samari narrated to us — Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated from Isma'il — from Amir, who said: There was a dispute between Umar and Ubayy, may Allah be pleased with both of them, regarding a wall. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Let Zayd ibn Thabit be the arbiter between us.\"" So they set out"," and Umar knocked upon the door. Zayd recognized his voice and opened the door"," saying: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," would you not have sent for me so that I could come to you?\"" For in his house the judge is given authority. And he mentioned the hadith. [Da'if]"""
"20519","(20513) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn Adi al-Hafiz informed us — Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Shahriyar narrated to us — Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated — (and) Abu Amr al-Razjahi informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us — al-Sufi, who is Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar, narrated to us — Abu Hamam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated — Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Nadrah narrated from his father — from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: He recited {O you who have believed, when you contract a debt for a specified term} [al-Baqarah 282] until he reached {and if you entrust one another} [al-Baqarah 283]. He said: This abrogated what preceded it. [Hasan]"
"20520","(20514) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi Amr said: Al-Abbas ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us — Affan narrated — Wuhayb narrated — Dawud narrated — from Amir, regarding this verse: {And if you entrust one another} [al-Baqarah 283]. He said: If you call witnesses, it is binding; and if you trust one another, then it is permissible and ample.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Hasan al-Basri that he said: If he wishes, he may call witnesses, and if he wishes, he need not call witnesses. Do you not hear His statement: {And if you entrust one another} [al-Baqarah 283]? Al-Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: And it has been authentically reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he concluded a sale with a Bedouin regarding a horse. The Bedouin denied the matter due to the scheming of some hypocrites, and there was no proof between the two of them. [Sahih]"
"20521","(20515) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us; my father Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Qurqūb al-Tammār in Hamadhān narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUmārah ibn Khuzaymah that his paternal uncle — who was among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) — narrated to him.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī and al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād both said: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; my brother Abū Bakr narrated to me from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAtīq from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUmārah ibn Khuzaymah that his paternal uncle — who was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — informed him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) purchased a horse from a Bedouin man. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked him to accompany him so that he might pay the price of his horse. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) walked swiftly, while the Bedouin lagged behind. Some men began approaching the Bedouin, bargaining with him for the horse, unaware that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had already purchased it. Some of them raised the price against the Bedouin. When they increased the bidding, the Bedouin called out to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \If you wish to buy this horse"," buy it; otherwise"," I shall sell it!\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up upon hearing the Bedouin's call and came to him and said: \""Did I not already purchase it from you?\"" He said: \""No"," by Allah"," I did not sell it to you.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," I purchased it from you.\"" The people began taking refuge with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the Bedouin as the two were engaged in discussion. The Bedouin began saying: \""Bring me a witness that I sold it to you!\"" Khuzaymah said: \""I bear witness that you sold it.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned to Khuzaymah and said: \""On what basis do you testify?\"" He said: \""By your truthfulness.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made the testimony of Khuzaymah equal to the testimony of two men. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20522","(20516) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ustādh Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib and Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq both said: ʿAbdatullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to me; Muḥammad ibn Zurārah ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thābit narrated to me; ʿUmārah ibn Khuzaymah narrated to me from his father Khuzaymah ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) purchased a horse from Sāwīʾ ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muḥāribī, and the latter denied the sale. So Khuzaymah ibn Thābit testified on behalf of the Prophet (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \What compelled you to give testimony when you were not present?\"" He said: \""You have spoken the truth"," O Messenger of Allah"," but I believed you in what you said"," and I knew that you do not speak except the truth.\"" He said: \""Whoever Khuzaymah testifies for or against"," that shall suffice him.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \""Had it been an absolute obligation"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would not have transacted without evidence.\"""""
"20523","(20517) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us; Abū al-Muthannā Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā ibn Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us; my father narrated to me; my father narrated to me; Shuʿbah narrated from Firās from al-Shaʿbī from Abū Burdah from Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Three persons supplicate to Allah"," but their supplications are not answered: a man who has an ill-tempered wife and does not divorce her; a man to whom another man owes a debt and he does not call witnesses regarding it; and a man who gives his wealth to a foolish person"," while Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has said: *'And do not give the foolish your wealth'* [al-Nisāʾ: 5].\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20524","(20518) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAlī ibn Zayd from Yūsuf ibn Mihrān from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: *'When you contract a debt for a specified term, write it down'* [al-Baqarah: 282] — to the end of the verse: \Indeed"," the first person to deny a covenant was Adam (peace be upon him). Verily"," Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," showed him his progeny and he saw a man whose radiance was resplendent"," his light shining forth. He said: 'O my Lord"," who is this?' He said: 'This is your son Dāwūd.' He said: 'O my Lord"," what is his lifespan?' He said: 'Sixty years.' He said: 'O my Lord"," increase his lifespan.' He said: 'No"," unless you increase it from your own lifespan.' He said: 'And what is my lifespan?' He said: 'A thousand years.' Adam said: 'I have granted him forty years.' And Allah wrote a document for him and made His angels bear witness over it. When death came to him and the angels came to him"," he said: 'There remain forty years of my lifespan.' They said: 'You granted them to your son Dāwūd.' He said: 'I granted nothing to anyone.' So Allah brought forth the document"," and His angels bore witness against him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20525","(20519) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Baghawī narrated to us; Abū Salamah Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated, mentioning the meaning of this hadith, except that he said at its beginning: \When the verse of debt was revealed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said…\"" And he said at its end: \""So He completed for Adam a thousand years and for Dāwūd a hundred years.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20526","(20520) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Bakkār ibn Qutaybah al-Qāḍī in Egypt narrated to us; Ṣafwān ibn ʿĪsā al-Qāḍī narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Dhubāb narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When Allah created Adam and breathed into him the spirit"," he sneezed and said: 'Al-ḥamdu lillāh' (All praise is due to Allah). He praised Allah by Allah's permission. His Lord said to him: 'May your Lord have mercy upon you"," O Adam.' Then He said to him: 'O Adam"," go to those angels — to a group of them seated — and say: al-salāmu ʿalaykum (peace be upon you).' So he went and said it. They said: 'And upon you be peace"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.' Then he returned to his Lord. He said: 'This is your greeting and the greeting of your children and their children.' Then Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," said to him — and His two hands were closed — 'Choose whichever of them you wish.' He said: 'I choose the right hand of my Lord"," and both the hands of my Lord are right hands"," blessed.' Then He spread it open"," and in it were Adam and his progeny. He said: 'O my Lord"," who are these?' He said: 'These are your progeny.' And behold"," the lifespan of every human being was written between his eyes. And among them was the most radiant of them — or he said: among the most radiant of them — for whom only forty years were written. He said: 'O my Lord"," increase his lifespan.' He said: 'That is what was written for him.' He said: 'Then I have given him sixty years from my lifespan.' He said: 'That is between you and him.' Then he dwelt in Paradise as long as Allah willed"," then he descended from it. Adam kept count for himself. Then the angel of death came to him. Adam said to him: 'You have come too quickly! A thousand years were written for me.' He said: 'Yes"," but you gave sixty years from it to your son Dāwūd.' So he denied"," and his progeny denied. He forgot"," and his progeny forgot. On that day"," the command for writing and witnesses was decreed.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20527","(20521) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ from his father from Abū Hurayyah that Saʿd said: \O Messenger of Allah"," tell me: if I find a man with my wife"," should I delay him until I bring four witnesses?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Yes.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik as above. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1498]"""
"20528","(20522) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Anṣārī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us; Suhayl narrated from his father from Abū Hurayrah, who said: Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah said: \If I find a man with my wife"," I shall not touch him until I bring four witnesses.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""No"," by the One Who sent you with the truth"," I shall hasten to strike him with the sword!\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Listen to what your chief says. He is a man of jealousy (ghayrah)"," and I am more jealous than he"," and Allah is more jealous than me.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously cited]"""
"20529","(20523) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Abū Shihāb ʿAbd Rabbih ibn Nāfiʿ narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib that Muʿāwiyah wrote to Abū Mūsā: \Ask ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) about a man who enters his house and finds a man with his wife — should he kill her or kill him?\"" So Abū Mūsā asked him"," and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""What reminds you of this? This is a matter that does not occur in our land. I adjure you.\"" He said: \""Muʿāwiyah wrote to me to ask you about it.\"" He said: \""I am Abū al-Ḥasan: if he brings four witnesses"," [he shall have his right]; otherwise"," he shall be handed over [for punishment].\"" Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said: \""He shall be killed.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \""And there has preceded the ḥadīth of Mālik ibn Anas from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \""And three men testified against a man with ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding zinā"," but the fourth did not confirm it"," so he flogged the three.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20530","(20524) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr — that is, Ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated from Ibn ʿUlayyah from al-Taymī from Abū ʿUthmān, who said: When Abū Bakrah and his two companions testified against al-Mughīrah, Ziyād also came. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \A man who"," if he testifies"," will testify only for the truth"," Allah willing.\"" He said: \""I saw a commotion and a wicked gathering.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""Did you see the applicator entering the kohl container?\"" He said: \""No.\"" So he ordered that they be flogged. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20531","(20525) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Rāshid informed us that Hushaym informed us, from Abū Ḥayyān al-Taymī, that ʿAbāyah ibn Rifāʿah narrated to us, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, who said:\n\nA man from the Anṣār was found killed in Khaybar. His heirs went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: \Do you have two witnesses who can testify to the killing of your companion?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," there were no Muslims present there; they are Jews"," and they would dare to do even greater than this.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith. [Weak]"""
"20532","(20526) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Raffāʾ al-Harawī narrated to us that Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥammād al-Qūmisī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yūnus narrated to us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no marriage except with a guardian (walī) and two just witnesses. If they dispute"," then the ruler (sulṭān) is the guardian of the one who has no guardian. If she marries herself off"," her marriage is invalid.\""\n\n(T) And it has been narrated to us in the Book of Marriage from al-Ḥasan and Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābl (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses.\"" And it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and that which Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh narrated from ʿAṭāʾ"," from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābl (may Allah be pleased with him)"," that he permitted the testimony of a man along with women in marriage — and this is not valid.\n\n(J) The narration of ʿAṭāʾ from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ)"," and Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh is not used as a proof"," and the mursal narration of Ibn al-Musayyab from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) is more authentic. And with Allah lies success. [Authenticated; previously mentioned in the Book of Marriage]"""
"20533","(20527) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Hushaym informed us that Yūnus narrated from al-Ḥasan:\n\nThat he did not permit the testimony of women regarding divorce. [Authentic]"
"20534","He said, and Hushaym narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm:\n\nThat he did not permit the testimony of women regarding the prescribed punishments (ḥudūd) and divorce. He said: \And divorce is among the most severe of the prescribed punishments.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20535","(20529) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Ibn Milḥān narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:\n\n\O company of women"," give charity and increase in seeking forgiveness"," for I have seen you to be the majority of the inhabitants of the Fire.\"" A woman among them said: \""What is the matter with us"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands. I have not seen anyone more deficient in intellect and religion more overwhelming to the possessor of reason than you.\"" She said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is the deficiency in intellect and religion?\"" He said: \""As for the deficiency in intellect"," the testimony of two women is equal to the testimony of one man — this is the deficiency in intellect. And she spends nights without praying and breaks her fast in Ramadan — this is the deficiency in religion.\"" [Authentic; Muslim 807]"""
"20536","(20530) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm al-Nasawī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ al-Tujībī informed us that al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it with its chain of narration similarly, except that he said: \A woman among them"," a dignified one"," said: 'Why is it that we are the majority of the inhabitants of the Fire"," O Messenger of Allah?'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ. [Authentic; previously mentioned]"""
"20537","(20531) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik narrated, from Hishām, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\I am only a human being"," and you bring your disputes to me. Perhaps one of you may be more eloquent in presenting his argument than another"," so I judge in his favor based on what I hear from him. Whomever I adjudge something that belongs to his brother"," let him not take it"," for I am only cutting out for him a piece of the Fire.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī and others"," from Mālik. [Authentic; previously mentioned]"""
"20538","(20532) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-ʿAbdī informed us that Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from ʿUrwah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \I am only a human being"," and you bring your disputes to me. Perhaps one of you may be more eloquent in presenting his argument than another"," so I judge in his favor based on what I hear. Whomever I adjudge something that belongs to his brother"," let him not take anything from it"," for I am only cutting out for him a piece of the Fire.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr. [Authentic; previously mentioned]"""
"20539","(20533) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, who narrated it with its chain of narration and text, except that he said: \Whomever I cut off from the right of his brother"," let him not take it"," for I am only cutting out for him thereby a piece of the Fire.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Authentic]"""
"20540","(20534) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bisṭāmī informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Qāsim — meaning Ibn Zakariyyā — narrated to us that Ibn Ishkāb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. Both said: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us that my father narrated to me, from Ṣāliḥ, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Abī Salamah informed him that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), informed her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he heard a dispute at the door of his chamber, so he went out to them and said:\n\n\I am only a human being"," and a disputant comes to me. Perhaps one of them may be more eloquent than another"," so I consider him to be truthful and judge in his favor accordingly. Whomever I adjudge something belonging to a Muslim"," it is but a piece of the Fire — so let him take it or leave it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," from Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid"," from Yaʿqūb. [Authentic; agreed upon]"""
"20541","(20535) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Layth narrated from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Saʿd and ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah disputed over a boy. Saʿd said, \O Messenger of Allah"," this is my nephew"," the son of my brother ʿUtbah. He entrusted him to me"," saying he is his son. Look at his resemblance to him.\"" And ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah said"," \""This is my brother"," O Messenger of Allah; he was born on my father's bed from his slave woman.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked and saw a clear resemblance to ʿUtbah. He said"," \""He is yours"," O ʿAbd. The child belongs to the [owner of the] bed"," and the adulterer receives the stone [i.e."," nothing]. And veil yourself from him"," O Sawdah.\"" So she never saw Sawdah at all."""
"20542","(20536) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Sinān narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from his father from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever introduces into this affair of ours that which is not from it"," it is rejected.\"""""
"20543","(20537) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us that Ibn Kunāsah informed us that Jaʿfar ibn Burqān narrated from Maʿmar al-Baṣrī from Abū al-ʿAwwām al-Baṣrī, who said: ʿUmar wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with them both): \Judgment is an established obligation and a followed tradition. So understand when a case is presented to you"," for a right is of no benefit if it is not enforced. Treat people equally in your demeanor"," your gathering"," and your judgment"," so that the noble does not hope for your injustice and the weak does not despair of your fairness. The burden of proof lies upon the claimant"," and the oath is upon the one who denies. Reconciliation is permissible among Muslims"," except a reconciliation that makes lawful what is unlawful or makes unlawful what is lawful. Whoever claims a right that is absent or a proof"," set for him a deadline to which he may refer. If he brings a proof"," grant him his right. If he is unable to do so"," pass judgment against him"," for that is more thorough in excuse and clearer in removing blindness. Let not a judgment you have passed today prevent you from revisiting it upon reflection and being guided to what is correct"," so that you return to the truth. For the truth is ancient"," and nothing nullifies the truth. Returning to the truth is better than persisting in falsehood. Muslims are witnesses against one another in testimony"," except one who has been flogged in a ḥadd punishment"," or one upon whom false testimony has been tested"," or one suspected of partiality due to allegiance or kinship. For Allah"," the Mighty and Sublime"," has taken charge of the hidden matters of His servants and has veiled their ḥudūd except through clear evidence and oaths. Then understanding"," understanding"," in what is presented to you of that which is not in the Qurʾan or Sunnah. Then analogize matters in that regard"," and recognize the examples and similarities. Then direct yourself to that which is most beloved to Allah in your view and that which is closest to the truth. Beware of anger"," anxiety"," weariness"," and harming people during disputes"," and of harshness. For judgment in matters of truth obligates for it reward from Allah and improves one's provision. Whoever purifies his intention for the truth"," even if it be against himself"," Allah will suffice him between him and the people. And whoever adorns himself for them with what is not in his heart"," Allah will disgrace him. For Allah"," Blessed and Exalted"," accepts from His servants only what is sincere for Him. And what do you think of the reward other than from Allah in the immediacy of His provision and the treasures of His mercy?\"""""
"20544","(20538) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Hishām from Ibn Sīrīn from Sharīḥ that he used to say to a man: \I will judge in your favor"," and yet I consider you unjust. However"," I can only judge based on the evidence presented before me"," and my judgment does not make the unlawful lawful for you.\"""""
"20545","(20539) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Hushaym informed us that Mujāld narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: Sharīḥ used to accept the testimony of women regarding the newborn's first cry and that which men do not see."
"20546","(20540) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us that Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ al-Tujībī informed us that Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Ibn al-Hād from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that he said—and he mentioned the hadith, in which is: \I have not seen anyone deficient in intellect and religion more overwhelming to men of sound mind than you [women].\"" She said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is the deficiency in intellect and religion?\"" He said: \""As for the deficiency in intellect"," the testimony of two women is equal to the testimony of one man; that is the deficiency in intellect. And she spends nights without praying and breaks her fast in Ramadan; that is the deficiency in religion.\"""""
"20547","(20541) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj and ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, who said: \It is not valid except with four women regarding the newborn's first cry.\"""""
"20548","(20542) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Aḥmad ibn al-Qāsim ibn Musāfir informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Maʿmar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Mālik al-Wāsiṭī narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abū Wāʾil from Ḥudhayfah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) accepted the testimony of the midwife."
"20549","(20543) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿUmar ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn al-Faḍl and Muḥammad ibn Bishr ibn Maṭar both said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Mālik narrated from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Madāʾinī from al-Aʿmash, and he mentioned it similarly."
"20550","(20544) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Abū ʿAwanah and Hushaym narrated from Jābir from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to accept the testimony of the midwife. Abū ʿAwanah added: \alone.\"" This is not authentic. Jābir al-Juʿfī is abandoned (matrūk)"," and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy is subject to criticism. It was also narrated by Suwayd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz—and he is weak—from Ghaylān ibn Jāmiʿ from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Marwān from his father that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned it. Isḥāq al-Ḥanẓalī said: \""Had the testimony of the midwife been authentically established from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," we would have acted upon it"," but there is a defect in its chain of narration.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Had it been established from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," we would have followed it"," Allah willing. But it is not established according to you or to us from him.\"""""
"20551","(20545) He narrated the hadith which Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ narrated to us — al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Zuhrī saying: The people of Iraq claim that the testimony of one who has been subjected to a prescribed punishment (ḥadd) is not valid. I bear witness that someone informed me that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Abū Bakrah: \Repent"," and your testimony will be accepted","\"" or he said"," \""If you repent"," your testimony will be accepted.\""\n\nSufyān said: al-Zuhrī named the one who informed him"," and I memorized it"," but then I forgot it and became uncertain about it. When rose"," I asked those who were present"," and ʿUmar ibn Qays said to me: \""It is Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I said to him"," \""Did you have any doubt about what he told you?\"" He said: \""No"," it is Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," without any doubt.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""I often heard him narrate it and name Saʿīd"," and I often heard him say"," 'From Saʿīd"," if Allah wills.' Others among the people of precise memorization have narrated it from Saʿīd without any doubt"," and they added therein that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) called the three to repent. Two of them repented"," so he accepted their testimony"," but Abū Bakrah refused to repent"," so he rejected his testimony.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20552","(20546) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Shaybān narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Abū Bakrah: \If you repent"," your testimony will be accepted","\"" or he said"," \""Repent"," and your testimony will be accepted.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"20553","(20547) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us, who said: Someone from the people of Madīnah whom I trust informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that when ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) flogged the three, he called them to repent. Two of them repented, so he accepted their testimony, but Abū Bakrah refused to repent, so he rejected his testimony.\n\nSulaymān ibn Kathīr narrated it from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Abū Bakrah, Shibl, and Nāfiʿ: \Whoever among you repents"," his testimony will be accepted.\""\n\nAl-Awzāʿī narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," from Ibn al-Musayyib"," that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) called Abū Bakrah to repent.\n\nThe Shaykh said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Muḥammad ibn Muslim"," from Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah"," from Ibn al-Musayyib"," that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to those who testified against al-Mughīrah (may Allah be pleased with him): \""Repent"," and your testimony will be accepted.\"" He said: Two of them repented"," but Abū Bakrah refused to repent. He said: And ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) would not accept his testimony. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20554","(20548) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us — Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us — Abū al-Azhar narrated to us — ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad narrated from Qays, from Sālim al-Afṭas, from Saʿīd ibn ʿĀṣim, who said: When a man came to Abū Bakrah to bear witness, he would say: \Appoint someone other than me as a witness"," for the Muslims have declared me a transgressor (fāsiq).\""\n\nHe said: \""If this is authentic"," it is because he refused to repent from his false accusation (qadhf) and persisted in it. Had he repented from it"," they would not have imposed upon him the label of fisq. And Allah knows best.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It has reached me that Ibn ʿAbbās used to permit the testimony of the false accuser (qādhif) if he repented.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20555","(20549) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the words of the Most High: \And do not accept their testimony ever"," and it is they who are the transgressors\"" (al-Nūr"," 4)"," then He said"," \""Except those who repent\"" (al-Baqarah"," 160). He said: \""Whoever repents and reforms"," his testimony is accepted according to the Book of Allah.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20556","(20550) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ narrated to us — al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ regarding the false accuser (qādhif) who repents: he said, \His testimony is accepted.\"" He said: \""All of us say this — ʿAṭāʾ"," Ṭāwūs"," and Mujāhid.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20557","(20551) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated to us — Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, Ṭāwūs, and Mujāhid, that they said regarding the false accuser (qādhif): \If he repents"," his testimony is accepted.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"20558","(20552) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Malik narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \Allah accepts his repentance"," but I reject his testimony.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20559","(20553) He said: And Shuʿbah narrated to us — Sharīk narrated from Abī Ḥuṣayn, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \Allah accepts his repentance"," but you do not accept his testimony.\""\n\nHe said: And Saʿīd narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Muṭarrif narrated from al-Shaʿbī"," that he used to say regarding the false accuser (qādhif): \""When he has been flogged and then retracts his statement and repents from what he said"," his testimony is accepted.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20560","(20554) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Misʿar, from a man, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, who said: \If he repents"," his testimony is accepted.\""\n\nHe said: And Saʿīd narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Juwaybir narrated from al-Ḥakam"," that he used to say: \""If he repents"," his testimony is accepted.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20561","(20555) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Ḥuṣayn informed us, saying: I saw a man who was flogged a ḥadd punishment for false accusation (qadhf) based on suspicion of zinā. When the lashing was completed, he made repentance, saying: \I seek forgiveness from Allah and I repent to Him from falsely accusing chaste women.\"" I met Abū al-Zinād and informed him of that"," and he said to me: \""The matter"," according to us"," is that when he retracts his statement and seeks forgiveness from his Lord"," his testimony is accepted.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Abū Muʿāwiya and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Misʿar"," from ʿImrān ibn ʿUmayr"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtba"," his statement regarding the testimony of the one who makes a false accusation (qādhif). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20562","(20556) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik informed us that it reached him that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Sulaymān ibn Yasār were asked about a man who was flogged — is his testimony valid? They both said: \Yes"," if repentance becomes evident from him.\""\n\nAnd from Ibn Shihāb that he was asked about a man: if he is flogged the ḥadd"," is his testimony valid? He said: \""Yes"," if repentance becomes evident from him.\""\n\nMālik said: \""And that is the matter according to us.\"" Allah"," the Most High"," said: *\""Except those who repent after that and make amends; indeed"," Allah is Forgiving"," Merciful\""* [Āl ʿImrān 89]. So the one upon whom the ḥadd is carried out"," if he repents and makes amends"," his testimony is accepted. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20563","(20557) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us — Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Shahīd narrated to us — Abū al-Rabīʿ Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAtakī al-Zahrānī narrated to us — Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān al-Madanī narrated to us — from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwa ibn al-Zubayr, Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, ʿAlqama ibn Waqqāṣ al-Laythī, and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtba, from ʿĀʾisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when the people of the slander (Ilfk) said what they said about her, and Allah declared her innocent from it. He mentioned the hadith in its entirety, and in it she said: \He (i.e."," the Prophet ﷺ) gave testimony — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — then said: 'To proceed"," O ʿĀʾisha"," indeed such-and-such has reached me about you. If you are innocent"," then Allah will declare you innocent"," and if you have committed a sin"," then seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him"," for when a servant acknowledges his sin and then repents"," Allah accepts his repentance.'\""\n\nAnd he mentioned the hadith regarding the revelation of the verses declaring her innocence.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20564","(20558) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī, from Ziyād ibn Abī Maryam, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿqil, that his father asked Ibn Masʿʿūd: \Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Remorse (nadam) is repentance (tawba)'?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20565","(20559) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us — Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiya narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī, from Ziyād, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿqil, who said: \I was with my father beside ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," and my father said to him: 'Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes"," I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Remorse (nadam) is repentance (tawba).\""'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"20566","(20560) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us — Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī, from Ziyād ibn Abī Maryam, from ʿAbd Allāh, that he said: \Remorse (nadam) is repentance (tawba)"," and the one who repents is as one who has no sin.\"" This is how ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it from Maʿmar"," as a disconnected (muʿḍal) and stopped (mawqūf) narration"," with the additional wording. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20567","(20561) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatāda informed us — Abū ʿAlī al-Raffāʾ informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Raqāshī narrated to us — Wuhibb ibn Khālid narrated to us — Maʿmar narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī, from Abī ʿUbayda, from ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The one who repents from sin is as one who has no sin.\"" This is how he said it"," and it is an error (wahm). The hadith"," as narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm"," from Ziyād ibn Abī Maryam"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿqil"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," may Allah be pleased with him"," is as has preceded. And Allah knows best. It has been narrated through other weak chains with this wording"," and what we have mentioned is sufficient. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20568","(20562) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāmī narrated to us — Baqiyya ibn al-Walīd narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Alhānī narrated, saying: I heard Abū ʿUtba al-Khawlānī say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \The one who repents from sin is as one who has no sin.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20569","(20563) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī, the father of Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muzakkī, narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us — Abū Kurayb narrated to us — Salm ibn Sālim narrated from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār, from ʿĀṣim al-Ḥuddānī, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The one who repents from sin is as one who has no sin.\""\n\nThis chain contains weakness. And it has been narrated through another weak route from Abū Saʿda al-Anṣārī from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20570","(20564) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us — Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — Mūsā ibn ʿUqba narrated to us — ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Salmān, meaning al-Agharr, narrated to me from his father, from Abū al-Dardāʾ, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Everything that the son of Ādam speaks is recorded against him. So when he commits a sin and loves to repent to Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," let him come to an elevated spot"," let him extend his hands to Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," and then say: 'I repent to You from it; I shall never return to it.' Then he is forgiven"," so long as he does not return to that deed.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20571","(20565) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāy (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: \Turn to Allah in sincere repentance\"" [al-Taḥrīm 8]. He said: It is that a person commits a sin and then does not return to it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20572","(20566) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated from ʿAlī ibn Ṣāliḥ from Abī Isḥāq from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ from ʿAbdullāh regarding His words: \O you who believe"," turn to Allah in sincere repentance\"" [al-Taḥrīm 8]. He said: He repents from the sin and then does not return to it. Isrāʾīl corroborated it from Abī Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20573","(20567) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn Isḥāq ibn Aḥmad al-Kādī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: My father narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr from his father from ʿAwf ibn Mālik, who said: There is no sin except that I know its repentance. They said to him: O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, what is its repentance? He said: That he abandons it and then does not return to it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20574","(20568) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated from Ādam ibn Fāʾid from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The testimony of a treacherous man"," a treacherous woman"," one who has been subjected to a prescribed punishment (ḥadd) in Islam"," a woman who has been subjected to a ḥadd"," and one who harbours rancour against his brother shall not be accepted.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20575","(20569) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Muḥammad Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad ibn Daʿlaj al-Sijzī narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Qazaʿah ibn Suwayd narrated to us: al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The testimony of a treacherous man"," a treacherous woman"," one who has been subjected to a prescribed punishment"," one who harbours rancour against his brother shall not be accepted.\""\n\nĀdam ibn Fāʾid and al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ are not used as proofs. It has been narrated through weak chains from ʿAmr"," and those trustworthy narrators who narrated this hadith from ʿAmr did not mention the one who was lashed (al-majlūd). And Allah knows best. It has also been narrated through two other weak chains. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20576","(20570) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated in Ṣūr: Mūsā ibn Ayyūb al-Naṣībī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) He said, and Abū Aḥmad narrated to us: He said, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq narrated to us in Dimashq: Duḥaym narrated to us. They both said: Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād al-Dimashqī from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The testimony of a treacherous man"," a treacherous woman"," one who has been lashed for a prescribed punishment"," one who harbours rancour against his brother"," one against whom false testimony has been established"," and one who is under suspicion regarding lineage or kinship shall not be accepted.\""\n\nYazīd ibn Abī Ziyād"," also called ibn Ziyād al-Shāmī"," is weak in this narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20577","(20571) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: They said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Khalaf al-Dimashqī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Zuhrī narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon and said: \Beware! The testimony of a treacherous man"," a treacherous woman"," one who harbours rancour against his brother"," and one who has been brought forward for a prescribed punishment shall not be accepted.\""\n\nʿAlī said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd is al-Fārisī"," abandoned (matrūk)"," and ʿAbd al-Aʿlā is weak.\n\nThe Sheikh said: Nothing is authentically established in this regard from the Prophet (ﷺ) upon which one may rely. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20578","(20572) And it is narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated it to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Idrīs al-Awdī, who said: Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah brought out a document to us and said: This is the letter of ʿUmar to Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with them both). He mentioned it and said in it: \The Muslims are upright witnesses over one another"," except one who has been lashed for a prescribed punishment"," or one against whom false testimony has been established"," or one who is under suspicion regarding lineage or kinship.\""\n\nThis refers to the state before repentance. For it has been narrated from him that he said to Abū Bakrah (may Allah have mercy on him): \""Repent"," and your testimony will be accepted.\"" This is what is intended by those reports that may be authentic in this regard"," as is the intention regarding all those whose testimony is rejected alongside him. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited under no. 20283]"""
"20579","(20573) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: al-Shaybānī narrated from al-Shaʿbī from Sharīḥ, who used to say: \The testimony of the one who accuses of fornication (qādhif) shall never be accepted"," and his repentance is a matter between him and his Lord.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20580","(20574) Saʿīd narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Mughīrah narrated from Ibrāhīm. And Yūnus informed us from al-Ḥasan. They both said: \His testimony shall never be accepted"," and his repentance is a matter between him and Allah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20581","(20575) Sa'īd narrated to us: Sharīk narrated to us from Sālim from Sa'īd ibn Jubayr, who said: \His repentance is a matter between him and his Lord"," from the great torment"," and his testimony shall not be accepted.\"" [Weak]"""
"20582","(20576) He said: Sa'īd narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: 'Ubaydah informed us from Ibrāhīm regarding the one who accuses [another of fornication]: if he testifies before he is flogged, his testimony is valid.\ [Weak]"""
"20583","(20577) Abū Dāwūd narrated in al-Marāsīl from Muhammad ibn al-Muthannā from 'Affān from Ḥammād from Qatādah and Ḥumayd from al-Ḥasan that a man from Quraysh stole a she-camel, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cut off his hand, and he was one whose testimony was valid. Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Nasawī informed us: Abū 'Alī al-Lu'lu'ī narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated it. [Weak]"
"20584","(20578) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Ya'qūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Harawī narrated to us: Ismā'īl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah narrated to us from his father, who said: We were in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he said: \Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins?\"" He said: \""Associating partners with Allah (shirk)"," and disobedience to parents.\"" He said: \""And he was reclining"," so he sat up and said: 'And false testimony"," and false testimony"," and false testimony' — or 'false speech.'\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) kept repeating it until we said: \""Would that he remain silent.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qays ibn Ḥafṣ"," and Muslim narrated it from 'Amr al-Nāqid"," both from Ismā'īl. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20585","(20579) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Shaybānī informed us: Abū 'Abd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Mālik al-Baṣrī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Masmūl al-Makkī narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Salamah ibn Wahram al-Makkī narrated to us from his father from Ṭāwūs from Ibn 'Abbās, who said: A man who gives testimony was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so he said: \As for you"," O Ibn 'Abbās"," do not testify except upon a matter that shines for you like the brightness of this sun.\"" And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gestured with his hand toward the sun. Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Masmūl — al-Ḥumaydī spoke critically regarding him"," and it was not narrated from any reliable source. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"20586","(20580) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: 'Uthmān ibn 'Umar informed us: 'Imrān ibn Ḥudayr narrated to us from Abī Mijlaz, who said: I said to Ibn 'Umar, \People call upon me to bear witness"," and I dislike that.\"" He said: \""Bear witness to what you know.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20587","(20581) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-'Alawī — may Allah have mercy upon him — informed us by dictation: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn 'Abd Allāh informed us: My father informed me: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān informed me from Mūsā ibn 'Uqbah from Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym from 'Aṭā' ibn Yasār from Abū Hurayrah that he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Īsā ibn Maryam"," peace be upon them both"," saw a man stealing and said: 'Did you steal?' He said: 'No"," by the One in Whose Hand is my soul.' He said: 'By the One in Whose Hand is my soul.' So Īsā"," peace be upon him"," said: 'I believed in Allah and I denied my eyesight.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""And Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān said…\""\n\nal-Shāfi'ī said: Among these are reports that corroborate one another regarding matters that cannot"," for the most part"," be established by direct observation"," yet their knowledge is confirmed in the hearts"," and one testifies to them on this basis. [Agreed Upon]"""
"20588","(20582) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us: Isḥāq ibn Sa'īd informed us: My father informed me: I was in the presence of Ibn 'Abbās when a man came to him and asked him: \Who are you?\"" He traced for him a distant lineage. He then softened his speech and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Know your lineages and maintain your ties of kinship"," for there is no nearness of kinship when it is severed"," even if it is close"," and no distance when it is maintained"," even if it is far.\""\n\nHe commanded the knowledge of lineages"," and knowledge of their origins is only established through the corroboration of reports"," and direct observation of most of them is not possible. [Authentic — Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī"," 2880]"""
"20589","(20583) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū 'Amr 'Uthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Daqqāq in Baghdād informed us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: Abū Ghassān narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Yūsuf ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us from his father from Abī Isḥāq that he heard al-Aswad say: I heard Abū Mūsā al-Ash'arī say: \My brother and I arrived from Yemen and stayed for a time"," and we did not think that 'Abd Allāh ibn Mas'ūd was anything other than a member of the household of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," given the frequency of his and his mother's visits to the Prophet (ﷺ).\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm ibn Yūsuf. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20590","(20584) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū 'Abd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us: Ibn Abī Zā'idah narrated to us from his father from Abī Isḥāq from al-Aswad ibn Yazīd from Abū Mūsā, who said: \We arrived from Yemen and stayed for a time"," and we did not think that Ibn Mas'ūd and his mother were anything other than members of the household of the Prophet (ﷺ) due to the frequency of their visits and their close attachment to him.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Abd Allāh ibn Muḥammad and others from Yaḥyā ibn Ādam"," and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. In this is an indication that frequent entry into a house and activity within it may be used as evidence of ownership. And Allah knows best.\n\nal-Shāfi'ī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: Among these are matters that one hears and then testifies to what one has established through hearing regarding the one upon whom testimony is given"," along with the confirmation of sight. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20591","(20585) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us that Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us that Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us.\n\n(Chain variant) He said: And Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed us — and the wording is his — that Abu 'Ali Salih ibn Muhammad and Tamim ibn Muhammad both said: Muhammad ibn Rumh informed us, they both said: Al-Layth informed us from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man from Banu Layth said to him: \Indeed"," Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrates this from the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," that he prohibited the exchange of silver for silver except in equal measure"," and the exchange of gold for gold except in equal measure.\"" Abu Sa'id pointed with his two fingers to his eyes and his ears and said: \""My eyes saw and my ears heard the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," saying: 'Do not exchange gold for gold"," and do not exchange silver for silver"," except in equal measure. Do not increase one over the other. And do not sell any of it"," absent for present"," except hand to hand.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Qutaybah and Muhammad ibn Rumh. He thereby informed that knowledge of a statement is established by witnessing its speaker and hearing it from him. And regarding this"," there are many examples from the Companions"," may Allah be pleased with them.\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""And upon this I say: the testimony of a blind person is not valid"," except that he have firmly established something through direct observation"," or through observation and hearing"," and then became blind — in which case his testimony is valid. But if the statement or action occurred while he was blind"," it is not valid"," on account of the fact that one voice resembles another.\"" [Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"20592","(20586) Abu Hazim al-'Abadawi al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamirawayh informed us that Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us that Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us that Sufyan informed us that al-Aswad ibn Qays al-'Anazi heard his people saying: \Indeed"," 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," rejected the testimony of a blind person in a case of theft and did not accept it.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20593","(20587) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi informed us that Sufyan ibn Muhammad informed us that 'Ali ibn al-Hasan informed us that 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid informed us that Sufyan informed us from Yunus from al-Hasan that he disapproved of the testimony of a blind person.\n\n(Sh) Al-Shafi'i said: \And if this is so"," then writing is more appropriate"," and it is not permissible for anyone to testify thereby.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20594","(20588) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ma'ruf al-Faqih informed us that Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us that Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn al-Husayn al-Hadda' informed us that 'Ali ibn al-Madini informed us that Waki' ibn al-Jarrah informed me that Abu Mu'awiyah 'Amr ibn 'Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Nakha'i said: I said to al-Sha'bi — or I heard a man say to al-Sha'bi: \I recognize the inscription of my ring on the document"," but I do not know about testimony.\"" He said: \""Do not testify except upon that which you know"," for people do inscribe upon rings.\"" [Hasan]"""
"20595","(20589) He said: And 'Ali informed us that Azhar ibn Sa'd informed us that Ibn 'Awn said: I said to Ibrahim: \I see my name on the document"," but I do not recall the testimony.\"" He said: Allah"," the Most High"," said: **{Except he who bears witness to the truth"," and they know}** [Al-Zukhruf: 86]."""
"20596","(20590) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzzi informed us that Abu al-Hasan al-Tara'ifi informed us that 'Uthman ibn Sa'id informed us that 'Abdullah ibn Salih informed us from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn 'Abbas regarding His statement: **{Be persistently standing firm in justice, witnesses for Allah, even if it be against yourselves or parents and relatives}** [Al-Nisa': 135]. He said: \Or your fathers or your sons. And do not favor a wealthy person for his wealth"," and do not show mercy to a poor person for his poverty.\"" That is His statement: **{If the person is rich or poor"," Allah is more worthy of them both}** [Al-Nisa': 135]. And regarding His statement: **{And do not follow inclination"," lest you not be just}** [Al-Nisa': 135]: \""So you abandon the truth and thus commit injustice.\"" [Da'if]"""
"20597","(20591) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us that Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn informed us that Adam ibn Abi Iyas informed us that Warqa' informed us from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid regarding His statement: **{And if you distort your testimony or refuse to give it, indeed Allah is ever Acquainted with what you do}** [Al-Nisa': 135]: \You distort\"" — he says: \""You alter the testimony.\"" \""Or refuse to give it\"" — he says: \""You conceal it.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20598","(20592) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid informed us that al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati informed us that Ibrahim ibn Hamzah informed us that 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us from Yazid ibn 'Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Hadi, from 'Ubadah, meaning Ibn al-Walid ibn 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from his father, who said: My father informed me, saying: \We gave our pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," to hear and obey"," in hardship and ease"," in times of vigor and reluctance"," and even if others are given preference over us; and that we do not contest the authority of those to whom it belongs; and that we speak the truth wherever we may be"," fearing not"," for the sake of Allah"," the blame of any blamer.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ibn Abi 'Umar from 'Abd al-'Aziz"," and al-Bukhari narrated it through other chains from 'Ubadah ibn al-Walid. [Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"20599","(20593) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us that 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us that Yunus ibn Habib informed us that Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi informed us that Shu'bah informed us from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Kudayr al-Dabbi say — Abu Ishaq said: I heard it from him fifty years ago. Shu'bah said: And I heard it from Abu Ishaq forty years ago, or more. Abu Dawud said: And I heard it from Shu'bah forty-five or forty-six years ago. He said: \A man came to the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise.' He said: 'Speak justice and give the surplus.' He said: 'Then if I am unable to do that?' He said: 'Then feed the food and spread the greeting of peace.' He said: 'Then if I am unable to do that"," or if I lack the capacity for that?' He said: 'Do you have any camels?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then look after a camel of yours and its water-skin"," and look for a household who drink water only every other day"," and give them to drink. For perhaps your camel will not expire and your water-skin will not tear until Paradise becomes obligatory for you.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"20600","(20594) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us that Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam al-Warraq informed us that Yahya ibn Yahya informed us. He said: I read to Malik, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, from Ibn Abi 'Amrah al-Ansari, from Zayd ibn al-Khalid al-Juhani, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Shall I not inform you of the best of witnesses — those who bring their testimony before they are asked for it?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya.\n\nAnd this — and Allah knows best — pertains to the one who has testimony regarding a person but does not know that person"," so he informs of his testimony.\n\nAnd with this meaning Malik ibn Anas mentioned it"," and Ibn Wahb narrated it from Malik"," and he mentioned the hearing of each one of these narrators from the one above him. [Sahih. Muslim 1719]"""
"20601","(20595) And it was narrated by Ubayy ibn al-'Abbas ibn Sahl, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr — Kharijah ibn Zayd informed me, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi 'Amrah informed me, he said: Zayd ibn Khalid informed me, he heard the Prophet (ﷺ). And Kharijah ibn Zayd added in his chain of narration: Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us, Abu 'Amr ibn Matar informed us, al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Dawri informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak al-Mukharimi informed us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed me, Ubayy ibn 'Abbas informed me, and he mentioned it.\n\n[Sound. Preceded before it]"
"20602","(20596) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qattan informed us, Hashim ibn al-Junayd Abu Salih al-Badhashi al-Qumisi informed us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, Muslim ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi informed us, 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \Whoever has testimony"," let him not say"," 'I will not testify to it","' except before an imam. Rather"," let him testify"," perhaps he will return and desist.\""\n\nThis is a mawquf narration"," and it is the correct one. It has also been narrated as marfu'"," but its being raised (to the Prophet) is not sound. [Hasan]"""
"20603","(20597) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamirawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us, Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us, Hushaym informed us, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani informed us, from Muhammad ibn 'Ubaidullah al-Thaqafi, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote: \Whoever has testimony and does not testify to it when he sees it or when he knows of it"," then he is only summoned to testify out of resentment.\""\n\nThis is munqati' (disconnected) between al-Thaqafi and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). [Da'if]"""
"20604","(20598) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu 'Amr 'Uthman ibn Ahmad al-Daqqaq, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Amawi, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Tamim al-Qantari, and Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdan al-Sayrafi said: Abu Qalabah 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad informed us, Azhar ibn Sa'd al-Samman informed us, Ibn 'Awn informed us, from Ibrahim, from 'Ubaydah, who said: 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he said: \The best of people are my generation"," then those who follow them"," then those who follow them.\"" He said: \""And I do not know whether he said it after the third or after the fourth: 'Then there will come after them a people whose testimony will precede their oath and their oath will precede their testimony.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from al-Hasan ibn 'Ali"," from Azhar"," and al-Bukhari narrated it through another chain from Ibrahim. [Da'if]"""
"20605","(20599) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu 'Abdullah ibn Ya'qub and Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us, they said: Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar informed us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed me, from my father, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The best of people are my generation"," then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who make vows but do not fulfill them"," and they swear oaths but are not asked to swear"," and they betray and are not trusted"," and they testify but are not asked to testify"," and obesity will become widespread among them.\"" Abu al-Fadl said in his hadith: I heard Ahmad ibn Salamah say: \""They swear oaths\"" — it is only in the hadith of Hisham from the companions of Qatadah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Bashshar with this addition. This is a addition narrated uniquely by Mu'adh ibn Hisham from his father. [Sound. Agreed upon]"""
"20606","(20600) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib informed us, Abu Dawud informed us, Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best of my Ummah is the generation in which I was sent"," then those who follow them"," then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who make vows but do not fulfill them"," and they betray and are not trusted"," and they testify but are not asked to testify"," and obesity will become widespread among them.\"" Thus did all the companions of Hisham narrate it — there is no mention of swearing oaths in it. And the mention of swearing oaths in it"," if Mu'adh preserved it"," would correspond with the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud. And it may be understood that what is meant by that regarding testimony is that one testifies to that which he did not witness and does not know"," in which case he would be a false witness. And with Allah lies success and protection from error.\n\n[Sound. Preceded before it]"""
"20607","(20601) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us, Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi informed us, Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us, Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us, Hushaym, Khalid, and Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubaid, from al-Hasan, who said: \When he is called to testify and when he is called to establish it — both of them (are obligatory).\""\n\nOther than him added on the authority of al-Hasan: \""If all the people were to refuse to testify for one another"," that would not be permissible for them.\""\n\nA group of the exegetes have held that this verse pertains to the establishment of testimony"," and the verse is open to both meanings"," as al-Hasan held. And it (testimony) is a fard kifayah (communal obligation) in its assumption (tahammul). So when one who suffices undertakes it and the writing"," those who remain behind are freed from sin. And Allah knows best. [Sound]"""
"20608","(20602) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, Ibrahim ibn Marzuq informed us, Abu Hufayfah informed us, from Sufyan, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And no scribe or witness shall be harmed} [al-Baqarah: 282], he said: \That one should come and summon the scribe and the witness"," and they should say"," 'We are occupied","' and they should be harmed by that. He said: 'You have both been commanded to respond"," so do not harm them.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"20609","(20603) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, Abu al-Hasan al-Tara'ifi informed us, 'Uthman ibn Sa'id informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih informed us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His words: {And let not the witnesses refuse when they are called upon} [al-Baqarah: 282], he says: \When a Muslim is in need of him"," and he has testified to a testimony or he has testimony with him"," it is not lawful for him to refuse when he is called.\"" Then he said after that: {And no scribe or witness shall be harmed} [al-Baqarah: 282]. And harming is that a man should say to another"," while he has no need of him: \""Allah has commanded you not to refuse when you are called","\"" and he harms him by that"," while he is sufficiently served by someone else. So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," forbade him and said: {And if you do so"," it is sinfulness (fusuq) among you} [al-Baqarah: 282]. He means by fusuq: disobedience (ma'siyah)."""
"20610","(20604) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us, Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi informed us, Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us, Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us, Sufyan informed us.\n\n(And) The sharif Abu al-Fath al-'Umari informed us, Abu al-Hasan ibn Faras informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli informed us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ikrimah, who said: 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) recited: {And no scribe or witness shall be harmed} [al-Baqarah: 282]. Sufyan said: \It is that a man should come to another and say"," 'Write for me","' and he should say"," 'I am busy"," look for someone else","' and he should not harm him by saying"," 'I do not want anyone but you — look for someone else.' And (regarding) the witness: that a man should come to have him witness something"," and he should say"," 'I am busy"," look for someone else","' and he should not harm him by saying"," 'I do not want anyone but you — let someone else witness.'\""\n\nThe statement of Sufyan is not in the narration of Ibn Qatadah. [Sound]"""
"20611","(20605) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr al-Qadi, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Isma'il ibn Muslim informed us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Mujahid, who said: \The scribe and the witness should not be harmed\"" — meaning"," he should be summoned and thereby be distracted from his estate and his market. [Da'if]"""
"20612","(20606) He said: And 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Isma'il ibn Muslim informed us, from al-Hasan, regarding His statement — Exalted is He — {And no scribe shall be harmed, nor any witness} [Al-Baqarah 282]. He said: \The scribe should not be compelled to write that which he has not been commanded to write"," and the witness should not be compelled to add to his testimony.\""\n\nHe said: And 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Sa'id informed us"," from Qatadah"," with the same meaning. [Da'if]"""
"20613","(20607) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Abu 'Amir informed us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding His statement — Exalted is He — {And bring to witness two witnesses from among your men} [Al-Baqarah 282]. He said: \From among the free men.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20614","(20608) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us; Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi informed us; Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us; Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us; Hushaym informed us; Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, saying: \I asked Mujahid about zihar (injurious comparison) from a slave woman. He said: 'It is nothing.' I said: 'Does not Allah — Glorified is He — say {And those who pronounce zihar from their wives} [Al-Mujadilah 3] — are they not among the wives?' He said: 'By Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," He says {And bring to witness two witnesses from among your men} [Al-Baqarah 282] — so is the testimony of slaves valid?' Thus Mujahid — may Allah have mercy upon him — made clear that the unqualified address pertains to free men. And Allah knows best.\""\n\nAbu Yahya al-Saji' said: It was narrated from 'Ali"," al-Hasan"," al-Nakha'i"," al-Zuhri"," Mujahid"," and 'Ata': \""The testimony of slaves is not valid.\"" Al-Bukhari — may Allah have mercy upon him — said in the translation: \""Anas said: 'The testimony of a slave is valid if he is just","' and Shurayh and Zurarah ibn Awfa permitted it. Ibn Sirin said: 'His testimony is valid"," except for a slave testifying on behalf of his master.' Al-Hasan and Ibrahim permitted it in trivial matters. Shurayh said: 'All of you are sons of slaves and slave women.'\"""""
"20615","(20609) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas — may Allah be pleased with them both — regarding the testimony of boys: \It is not valid.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20616","(20610) And Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah and Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us, saying: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us; Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us; Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us; Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, that he wrote to Ibn 'Abbas — may Allah be pleased with them both — asking him about the testimony of boys. He wrote back to him: \Indeed"," Allah — Mighty and Majestic — says {From those whom you approve of as witnesses} [Al-Baqarah 282]"," and they are not among those whom we approve. It is not valid.\"" [Sahih]"""
"20617","(20611) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me; 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-San'ani informed me in Makkah; 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us; Yazid ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Thawr informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: \I sent a message to Ibn 'Abbas — may Allah be pleased with them both — asking him about the testimony of boys. He said: 'Allah — Mighty and Majestic — says {From those whom you approve of as witnesses} [Al-Baqarah 282]"," and they are not among those whom we approve.'\""\n\nHe said: \""Then I sent a message to Ibn al-Zubayr — may Allah be pleased with him — asking him"," and he said: 'If they are asked"," they are likely to tell the truth.' He said: 'I did not see the judgment to be in accordance with anything other than what Ibn al-Zubayr said.'\"" [Sahih"," except for the story of al-Zubayr]"""
"20618","(20612) Abu Ahmad al-Mihranjani informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakka informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik informed us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, that 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr used to judge by the testimony of boys among themselves regarding wounds. [Sahih]"
"20619","(20613) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu Muhammad Ahmad ibn 'Abdillah al-Muzani informed me; 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman informed me; Shu'ayb informed me, from al-Zhi; 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdillah informed me, that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas — may Allah be pleased with them both — said: \O company of Muslims! How do you ask the People of the Book about anything"," when the Book that Allah revealed to His Messenger is the most recent of the reports from Allah — you read it purely"," without any admixture — and Allah has informed you that the People of the Book changed what Allah wrote"," altered it"," and wrote the scriptures with their own hands"," then said: 'It is from Allah","' in order to sell it for a small price? Does not the knowledge that has come to you prevent you from asking them? By Allah"," we have never seen a man among them ask you about what was revealed to you.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 2685]"""
"20620","(20614) And 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdani informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar narrated to us; 'Ubud ibn Sharik narrated to us; Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth informed us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, and he mentioned it with the same meaning.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Yaman and from Yahya ibn Bukayr. [Sahih. Previously mentioned]"
"20621","(20615) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū ʿUrubah informed us, Bundār and Ibn al-Muthannā both said, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak reported from Yaḥyā, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The People of the Book used to recite the Torah in Hebrew and explain it in Arabic to the people of Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not believe the People of the Book"," nor disbelieve them; rather say: 'We believe in Allah and what has been revealed to us' [al-Baqarah 136].\"" — the verse.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Bundār. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 4485.]"""
"20622","(20616) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, Shādhān said: I was with Sufyān al-Thawrī when I heard an old man narrating from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The adherents of two different religions do not inherit from one another"," and the testimony of one religious community is not accepted against another"," except the community of Muḥammad"," for their testimony is accepted against others.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Shādhān said: I asked some of our companions about this old man"," and he claimed that he was ʿUmar ibn Rāshid al-Ḥanafī.\n\nAnd it was narrated by Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd from al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir — and he is Shādhān — from ʿUmar ibn Rāshid. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20623","(20617) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Rabbih al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us, Baqiyyah reported from al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir al-Azdiyy from ʿUmar ibn Rāshid, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \One religious community does not inherit from another"," and the testimony of one religious community is not accepted against another"," except the testimony of the Muslims"," for it is accepted against all other religious communities.\"" And likewise al-Ḥasan ibn Mūsā narrated it from ʿUmar ibn Rāshid. [Ṣaḥīḥ. What preceded it has already been mentioned.]"""
"20624","(20618) And ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated it from ʿUmar, as Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān al-Marwazī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Rāshid al-Yamāmī reported from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) — I think he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The adherents of one religious community do not inherit from another"," and the testimony of one religious community is not accepted against another"," except my Ummah — their testimony is accepted against those other than them.\""\n\n(c) This ʿUmar ibn Rāshad is not strong. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," and others among the Imams of the people of transmission have deemed him weak.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20625","(20619) And in what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him, from Abū al-ʿAbbās, from al-Rabīʿ, from al-Shāfiʿī: Muslim ibn Khālid informed us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, that he said: \Two just"," free"," Muslim men\"" — meaning the words of Allah the Most High: \""such as you approve of as witnesses\"" [al-Baqarah 282]. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20626","(20620) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said regarding this verse — and Allah knows best the meaning of what He intended from this — \I have heard one who interprets this verse as referring to those from among the Muslims who are not of your tribe"," and he cites in support the words of Allah"," the Blessed and Most High: 'Detain them both after the prayer"," and let them both swear by Allah: \""We will not sell it for any price\""' [al-Māʾidah 106] — and the prayer is the appointed prayer of the Muslims — and the words of Allah: 'even if he be a near kinsman' [al-Māʾidah 106] — and kinship exists only between the Muslims who were with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) from among the Arabs"," or between them and the idolaters"," but not between them and the People of the Covenant. And Allah says: 'nor will we conceal the testimony of Allah"," for then we would surely be among the sinners' [al-Māʾidah 106] — and only Muslims incur sin for concealing testimony owed to Muslims"," not the People of the Covenant.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20627","(20621) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh reported from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, regarding His words: \Two just men from among you"," or two others from among those who are not of you\"" [al-Māʾidah 106]. He said: From among the Muslims — except that he says: from the tribe or from other than the tribe. Someone other than him added on the authority of al-Ḥasan: \""Do you not see that He says: 'Detain them both after the prayer' [al-Māʾidah 106]?\""\n\nAnd we have narrated from ʿIkrimah that he said: \""Or two others from among those who are not of you\"" [al-Māʾidah 106] — he said: From among the Muslims"," from other than their tribe.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And I have heard one who mentions that it is abrogated by the words of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: \""And bring to witness two just men from among you\"" [al-Ṭalāq 2]. And I have seen the jurists of the people of the Abode of Emigration and the Sunnah issuing fatwas that the testimony of non-Muslims who are just is not accepted"," and that is my position.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated in another place from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm and others that they rejected the acceptance of the testimony of the People of the Covenant.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This"," along with what has been narrated from Ibn al-Musayyab that he used to say regarding His words: \""Or two others from among those who are not of you\"" [al-Māʾidah 106] — that they are from the People of the Book — indicates that he believed in its abrogation"," or that he interpreted the verse as referring to something other than testimony"," as we shall mention"," if Allah the Most High wills. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20628","(20622) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Kāmil informed us, Muḥammad ibn Saʿd ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAṭiyyah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, my paternal uncle narrated to me, my father narrated from his father ʿAṭiyyah ibn Saʿd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding this verse, he said: It is abrogated. And among the exegetes are those who have interpreted the testimony mentioned in this verse as referring to the oath, just as the oaths of the two mutually cursing spouses are called testimony. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20629","(20623) And the meaning of the verse at that time is as Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī and Abū Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī both said, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us, Abū Khālid Yazīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me, Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf reported from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān, regarding His words: \O you who believe"," testimony is to be established among you when death approaches one of you at the time of bequest — two just men from among you\"" [al-Māʾidah 106] — He says: Two just witnesses from among you"," from the people of your religion. \""Or two others from among those who are not of you\"" [al-MāḤidah 106] — He says: Two Jews or two Christians. His words: \""If you are journeying in the land\"" [al-Māʾidah 106] — And that was concerning two Christian men from the people of Dārīn"," one of them from Tamīm and the other from ʿAdī"," who accompanied a freedman of Quraysh on a business journey. They set sail on the sea"," and with the Qurashī was a known amount of property"," which his heirs were aware of"," consisting of vessels"," garments"," and a scroll. The Qurashī fell ill and made his bequest to the two Dārīnī men. He died"," and the two Dārīnī men took possession of the property. When they returned from their trade journey"," they brought the property and the bequest and delivered it to the heirs of the deceased"," and they brought back some of his property. The people found the amount of property to be small"," so they said to the two Dārīnī men: \""Our companion went out with a great deal of property"," more than what you have brought. Did he sell something or buy something that was placed therein? Or was his illness prolonged so that he spent on themselves?\"" They said: \""No.\"" They said: \""Then you have betrayed us.\"" They seized the property and brought their matter to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). So Allah"," the Mighty and Most High"," revealed: \""O you who believe"," testimony is to be established among you when death approaches one of you\"" [al-Māʾidah 106] to the end of the verse. When it was revealed that they be detained after the prayer"," the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them"," and they stood after the prayer and swore by Allah"," the Lord of the heavens and the Lord of the earth: \""Your freedman left no property except what we have brought to you"," and we do not trade our oaths for any worldly price"," even if he be a near kinsman"," nor will we conceal the testimony of Allah"," for then we would surely be among the sinners\"" [al-Māʾidah 106]. When they had sworn"," they were released. Then afterwards they found a vessel belonging to the deceased among his belongings"," and they seized the two Dārīnī men"," and they said: \""We purchased this from him during his lifetime.\"" They lied. They were required to produce proof"," but they were unable to do so. They brought this to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," so Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," revealed: \""Then if it is discovered\"" [al-Māʾidah 107] — He says: \""if it is found out\"" — \""that they have merited the charge of sin\"" [al-Māʾidah 107] — meaning the two Dārīnī men. He says: if they have concealed a right"," \""then let two others\"" [al-Māʾidah 107] — from the heirs of the deceased — \""stand in their place from among those against whom the claim was made"," and let them swear by Allah\"" [al-Māʾidah 107] — He says: \""and let them swear by Allah: 'Our companion's property was such and such"," and what we claim against the Dārīnī men is indeed true. We have not transgressed; indeed"," we would then be among the wrongdoers'\"" [al-Māʾidah 107]. This is the statement of the two witnesses"," the heirs of the deceased"," when the treachery of the Dārīnī men was discovered. Allah the Most High says: \""That is more likely that they will give testimony in its true form\"" [al-Māʾidah 107] — meaning the Dārīnī men and the people — \""that they should return to the like of that.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20630","(20624) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Abū Saʿīd Muʿādh ibn Mūsā al-Jaʿfarī narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf reported from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān. Bukayr said: Muqātil said: \I took this tafsīr from Mujāhid"," al-Ḥasan"," and al-Ḍaḥḥāk regarding the words of Allah"," the Blessed and Most High: 'Two just men from among you"," or two others from among those who are not of you' [al-Māʾidah 106] — the verse — that two Christian men from the people of Dārīn"," one of them a Tamīmī and the other a Yamānī"," accompanied a freedman of Quraysh on a business journey. They set sail on the sea"," and with the Qurashī was a known amount of property.\"" He mentioned the meaning of what we have narrated.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The meaning of 'testimony is to be established among you' is oaths among you"," if this is the meaning — and Allah knows best.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And the meaning that Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān mentioned on the authority of the people of tafsīr has been established through a sound chain of narration from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," except that he did not preserve in it the claim of Tamīm and ʿAdī that they had purchased it"," and Muqātil preserved it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20631","(20625) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Qutaybah Salamah ibn al-Fadl al-Adami in Makkah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah al-Basri narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Ibn Abi Zā'idah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man from Banū Sahm went out with Tamim al-Dāri and 'Uddi ibn Baddā'. The Sahmi man died in a land where there was no Muslim. When they both returned with his estate, they found a silver cup inlaid with gold separated from it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) then administered an oath to them both. Later, the cup was found in Makkah, and they said, \We purchased it from Tamim and 'Uddi.\"" Two men from among the heirs of the Sahmi man stood up and swore"," \""Our testimony is more deserving than their testimony"," and the cup indeed belongs to our companion.\"" Regarding this matter"," this verse was revealed: {O you who have believed"," testimony [should be taken] when you are} [al-Mā'idah 106].\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in his Sahih"," saying: 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah — that is"," Ibn al-Madini — informed me of it.\n\nLikewise"," it was narrated from 'Atā' ibn al-Sā'ib"," from Sa'id ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)."""
"20632","(20626) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashrān informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffār narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affān narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us from Zakariyyā ibn Abi Zā'idah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Ali al-Rūdhbārī — and the wording is his — informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dāwūd narrated to us: Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Zakariyyā narrated from al-Sha'bi: A Muslim man was overtaken by death in Daqūqā, and he found no Muslim to bear witness to his testament. So he called two men from among the People of the Book to witness it. They came to al-Kūfah and went to al-Ash'ari and informed him, bringing his estate and his testament. Al-Ash'ari said, \This is a matter that did not exist after what took place in the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" So he administered an oath to them after 'Asr"," by Allah"," that they had not been treacherous"," nor lied"," nor altered"," nor concealed"," nor changed anything"," and that it was indeed the man's testament and his estate. He then accepted their testimony.\n\nThis is the hadith of Hushaym"," and the hadith of Ibn Numayr is an abridged version."""
"20633","(20627) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Sukkari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Tarīf al-Kūfi narrated to us: Abu Khālid.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu Nasr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Sarrāj narrated to us: Mutayyin narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Hammād narrated to us: Abu Khālid al-Ahmar narrated from Mujālid, from al-Sha'bi, from Jābir: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted the testimony of the Jews against one another. In the narration of Ibn 'Abdān: He permitted the testimony of the People of the Book against one another. This is how Abu Khālid al-Ahmar narrated it from Mujālid, and it is among those matters in which he erred. For others narrated it from Mujālid, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh — as his own statement and ruling, not as a marfū' (elevated) hadith."
"20634","(20628) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hārith al-Aṣbahānī, the faqīh, informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar, the hafiz, narrated to us: 'Ali ibn Mubashshir informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abādah narrated to us: Abu Usāmah narrated from 'Abd al-Wāhid, who said: I heard Mujālid mentioning from al-Sha'bi, who said: Shurayh used to permit the testimony of every religious community against its own members, but he would not permit the testimony of a Jew against a Christian, nor that of a Christian against a Jew, except in the case of Muslims, for he used to permit their testimony against all religious communities."
"20635","(20629) Abu Nasr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abu Mansur al-Naḍrawī informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansūr narrated to us: Khālid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated from Dāwūd, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, regarding His statement {or two others from among you} [al-Mā'idah 106]: When a man dies in a foreign land and finds no Muslim, and he calls two non-Muslim witnesses, their testimony is permissible. But if two Muslims come and testify to the contrary, the testimony of the Muslims is accepted and their testimony is rejected."
"20636","(20630) And Abu Nasr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abu Mansur al-Naḍrawī informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansūr narrated to us: Hushaym and Abu Mu'āwiyah narrated from al-A'mash, from Ibrāhīm, from Shurayh: He would not permit the testimony of a Jew or a Christian against Muslims, except in the matter of a testament, and he would not permit it in a testament except in the context of travel.\n\nAnd Yahya ibn Waththāb narrated: Shurayh used to permit the testimony of the People of the Book against one another."
"20637","(20631) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajānī narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Rabī'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahmān, who said: A man came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattāb (may Allah be pleased with him) from the direction of Iraq and said, \I have come to you regarding a matter that has neither head nor tail.\"" 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," \""And what is that?\"" He said"," \""False testimonies have appeared in our land.\"" He said"," \""And is that so?\"" He said"," \""Yes.\"" 'Umar ibn al-Khattāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," \""No"," by Allah — no man shall be ensnared in Islam except through upright witnesses.\""\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: \""No man shall be ensnared\"" means \""no man shall be imprisoned.\"""""
"20638","(20632) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-Walīd, the faqīh, narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyān narrated from Hibbān ibn Mūsā, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Ibn 'Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sīrīn, from Shurayh, who said: \Claim whatever you wish and bring upright witnesses"," for we have been commanded [to judge by] upright witnesses.\"" Then he asked about him and mentioned the hadith."""
"20639","(20633) Abu Hāzim al-'Abdawī, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khumayruwayh narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansūr narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Mughīrah narrated from Ibrāhīm and Yūnus, from al-Hasan and Muhammad ibn Sālim, from al-Sha'bi: They used to say regarding the testimony of a boy — if he witnessed before reaching puberty and then bore testimony upon reaching puberty; and the Christian and the Jew — if they testified while still upon their polytheism and then later became Muslim; and the slave — if he testified and then was emancipated and then bore their testimony — their testimony is permissible."
"20640","(20634) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bashrān, the 'adl in Baghdad, informed us: Abu 'Ali Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffār.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Mūsā — both said: Abu al-'Abbās Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affān al-'Āmirī narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubbāb narrated to us: Sayf ibn Sulaymān al-Makkī narrated to us: Qays ibn Sa'd narrated from 'Amr ibn Dīnār, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) rendered judgment based on a single witness and an oath.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Hajjāj recorded it in his Sahih from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Zayd ibn al-Hubbāb. And Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī recorded it in Kitāb al-Sunan from 'Uthmān ibn Abī Shaybah and al-Hasan ibn 'Ali, from Zayd ibn al-Hubbāb. And likewise, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hārith al-Makhzūmī narrated it from Sayf ibn Sulaymān."
"20641","(20635) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated from Sayf ibn Sulayman from Qays ibn Sa'd from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) adjudicated on the basis of an oath together with a witness. 'Amr said: \Concerning financial matters.\"" [Sahih. Previously cited.]"""
"20642","(20636) And Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i narrated to us; Abu Qudamah narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us, and he wrote it down for me in his own handwriting; Abu Hatim ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi narrated to us; Abu 'Abd Allah narrated to us.\n\n(And) Kaml ibn Ahmad al-Mustamli informed us; Bishr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Muzani and Fath ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Faqih narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Shami narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated it with its chain and text, and he said: \Together with a single witness.\"" Abu Qudamah said in his narration: \""Together with a witness.\"" And Ahmad said in his narration: \""'Amr said: 'Concerning financial matters.'\"" [Sahih. Previously cited.]"""
"20643","(20637) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i said: \The hadith of Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) is established from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): 'No one among the people of knowledge has rejected its like"," even if there were no other narrator alongside him"," while there are others alongside him who corroborate it.'\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20644","(20638) And Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Dahhak, Yahya ibn Zakariya, and Isma'il ibn Dawud ibn Wardan, all of them in Egypt, said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us. He said: \I heard al-Shafi'i say: 'Muhammad ibn al-Hasan said to me: \""Had I known that Sayf ibn Sulayman narrates the hadith of the oath together with a witness"," I would have declared it corrupted.\""' He said: 'So I said: \""O Abu 'Abd Allah"," if you declare it corrupted"," then it becomes corrupted.\""'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Sayf ibn Sulayman al-Makkī is trustworthy and reliable (thiqah"," thabat) according to the Imams of the people of transmission.\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20645","(20639) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad; Abu 'Amr ibn al-Sammak narrated to us; Hanbal ibn Ishaq ibn Hanbal narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Madini said: \I asked Yahya ibn Sa'id about Sayf ibn Sulayman. He said: 'He is among those who are truthful and have strong memory with us.'\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20646","(20640) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, the grandson of al-'Abbas ibn Hamzah, narrated to us; Harun ibn 'Abd al-Samad al-Rukhi narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Madini said: \And I asked him"," meaning Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan"," about Sayf ibn Sulayman. He said: 'He was"," in my estimation"," reliable (thabat)"," among those who are truthful and have strong memory.'\"" [Sahih.]"""
"20647","(20641) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi narrated to us; al-Junaydi narrated to us; al-Bukhari said: \Yahya al-Qattan said: 'Sayf ibn Sulayman lived to the age of fifty"," and he was"," in our estimation"," trustworthy (thiqah)"," among those who are truthful and have strong memory.'\""\n\nAnd 'Abd al-Razzaq and Abu Hudhayfah followed him in this narration"," both of them from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). [Sahih.]"""
"20648","(20642) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yahya and Salamah ibn Shabib said: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Muhammad ibn Muslim informed us.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah said: Abu 'Ali al-Raffa' informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Makki narrated to us; Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) adjudicated on the basis of an oath together with a witness.\n\nSalamah said in his hadith from 'Abd al-Razzaq: \'Amr said: 'Concerning rights.'\"" And those whose narrations are not cited as authoritative contradicted them regarding Muhammad ibn Muslim"," adding Tawus in its chain"," and some of them narrated it through another route from 'Amr"," adding Jabir ibn Zayd in its chain. The narration of trustworthy narrators is not invalidated by the narration of weak narrators. And that was narrated through another route from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). [Sahih.]"""
"20649","(20643) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, among a group who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated from Rabi'ah ibn 'Uthman from Mu'adh ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and another Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) whose name he mentioned but I do not recall it, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) adjudicated on the basis of an oath together with a witness. [Sahih.]"
"20650","(20644) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, among a group who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) adjudicated on the basis of an oath together with a witness.\n\n'Abd al-'Aziz said: \So I mentioned that to Suhayl. He said: 'Rabi'ah"," who is trustworthy (thiqah) in my estimation"," informed me that I narrated it to him"," though I do not retain it (in memory).'\"" 'Abd al-'Aziz said: \""An illness had afflicted Suhayl which impaired part of his intellect"," and he forgot some of his hadith. After that"," Suhayl used to narrate it on the authority of Rabi'ah"," from him"," from his father.\"" [Sahih. Previously cited.]"""
"20651","(20645) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsūs al-Sūsī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, among others, narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Nawqānī narrated to us, Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us — from Rabīʿah, from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged by the oath together with a witness. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned before.]"
"20652","(20646) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Iskandarānī narrated to us, Ziyād ibn Yūnus narrated to me, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me from Rabīʿah with his chain of narration. Sulaymān said: \I met Suhayl and asked him about this hadith"," and he said: 'I do not know it.' So I said to him: 'Rabīʿah informed me from you.' He said: 'If Rabīʿah informed you from me"," then narrate it from Rabīʿah from me.'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated by other than Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Suhayl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned before.]"""
"20653","(20647) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh in Baghdād narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-ʿĀmirī, a Madinan, trustworthy, narrated that he heard Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrating from his father, from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged by the oath together with a witness.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from another route from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned before.]"
"20654","(20648) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad ibn Bundār al-Sabbāk al-Jurjānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf, Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd, and Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥanājir narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Mubārak narrated to us, al-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) judged by the oath together with a witness. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20655","(20649) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Khurāsānī al-ʿAdl in Baghdād narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham al-Baldī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us, al-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged by the oath together with a witness. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20656","(20650) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Munīr narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ ibn Abī Nāfiʿ al-Qurashī narrated it with its chain of narration, similar to it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned before.]"
"20657","(20651) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad ibn Bundār said: \I heard Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf saying: 'Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: In this topic — meaning"," judging by the oath together with a witness — there is no hadith more authentic than this.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20658","(20652) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, al-Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad, Mālik ibn Anas, and Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed me, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to me, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar al-Madanī informed us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged by the oath together with a single witness.\n\nIsmāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar added in his narration: \And that ʿAlī (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) judged by it in Iraq.\"" Thus did a group narrate it from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad as a mursal hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20659","(20653) And ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī — and he is among the trustworthy narrators — narrated it from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, from the Prophet (ﷺ), as a connected (mawṣūl) hadith. Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and others informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us that he said to one of those who debated with him: \I said to him: 'Al-Thaqafī narrated"," and he is trustworthy"," from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad"," from his father"," from Jābir"," that the Prophet (ﷺ) judged by the oath together with a witness.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20660","(20654) Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Isfarāyinī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Razmuwayh narrated to us, Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Nasawī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged by the oath together with a witness.\n\nAl-Ḥanẓalī added in his narration: \the single witness.\"" He said: \""And my father said: 'And ʿAlī (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) judged by it in Iraq.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And it has been narrated from Ḥumayd ibn al-Aswad"," ʿAbdullāh al-ʿUmarī"," Hishām ibn Saʿd"," and others"," from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad"," likewise as a connected (mawṣūl) hadith. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20661","(20655) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to me — Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn al-Mubārak al-Mustamlī narrated to us — Abū Rajāʾ Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ḥayyah narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Jibrīl"," upon him be peace"," came to me and commanded me to decide by the oath together with the witness"," and he said: 'Indeed"," Wednesday is a day of unrelenting misfortune.'\""\n\nAnd it has also been reported from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad"," from his father"," from his grandfather"," from the Prophet ﷺ."""
"20662","(20656) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by the oath together with the witness. And he said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, decided by that as well.\n\nAnd it has also been reported from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"20663","(20657) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī narrated to us — Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated to us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by a witness and an oath, and ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, decided by that in Iraq."
"20664","(20658) And it has been reported from Shabābah, as Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us — Shabābah narrated to us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Mājishūn narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet ﷺ decided by the testimony of a single witness together with the oath of the claimant, and ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, decided by that in Iraq.\n\nAnd likewise Ḥusayn ibn Zayd narrated it from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad."
"20665","(20659) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Saʿd al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us — Isḥāq ibn Mūsā al-Anṣārī narrated to us — he said: I heard Ḥusayn ibn Zayd saying: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: that he decided by the oath together with the single witness.\n\nʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib is the grandfather of Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, and even though he did not meet ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, this chain is closer to being connected than the report of Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him."
"20666","(20660) And others besides Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Bāqir with an interrupted chain. Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us — Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us — Sulaymān, meaning Ibn Bilāl, narrated from Rabīʿah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by the oath together with the single witness."
"20667","(20661) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Khālid ibn Abī Karīmah, from Abū Jaʿfar: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by the oath together with the witness."
